      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethf26"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. f. 26</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Juel-Jensen 2, Juel-Jensen 3)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex, composite135×110 mm (weight: 282g), 24 fols, 3 quires.  Unit 1:  eighteenth–nineteenth century. Unit 2:  1930–1970.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                                The book is bound in thick wooden boards.
                              
                                The boards are flush with the bookblock without bevels.
                                The grain runs vertically. The outer surface and the head edge of both boards are polished and a finishing layer of dark colour has been added.
                                The boards show signs of reuse as an additional hole is located along the cut of the tail edge of the upper board.
                              
                                  Tackets placed at the head and the tail of each quire hold the folios together. The quires have been then stitched through the inner margin
                                   with two loops of thread connecting them to the boards. Although there are two sets of holes for the traditional attachment of
                                   the bookblock to the boards, each loop passes only through one of the holes drilled in the thickness of the boards.
                            </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Pencil foliation in the upper right corner carried out by the Bodleian Library
                                        in January 2020 (1–24).</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>It is not known how and when <fo:inline id="d1e958PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> acquired the manuscript. He assigned a shelfmark to each
                        unit of production, Juel-Jensen 2 and Juel-Jensen 3 respectively. This might
                        indicate that the two units were not bound together
                        in the moment of acquisition. Traces of a former sewing can be observed in Unit 2.</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e966PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block>3 quires. A<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2 (Fols 1r–2v)</fo:inline> – I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 3r–10v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">12+2 (Fols 11r–24v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm">Unit 1</fo:block>
         <fo:block>Parchment, 10 fols (fols 1r–10v fols 1r, 1v, 10v), eighteenth–nineteenth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e996LIT2809RepCh93">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 2r–4v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Malkǝʾ-hymn to the Church’ (​መል​ክአ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡), CAe 2809.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ለኪ፡  ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​ቅድ​ስት፡
                                     ​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ለኪ፡  ​ቤተ፡ <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline> ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡
                                    ​ቤተ፡ ​ጸሎት ፨  ​በደ​መ፡ ​መለ​ኮት፡ ​ጥል​ልት ፨
<!--                                    <hi rend="rubric">ሰላም፡</hi> ለኪ፡ ቤተ፡ ክርስቲያን፡ ቅድስት<hi rend="rubric" rendition="#partialRubric">፨</hi>
                                    <hi rend="rubric">ሰላም<supplied reason="omitted">፡</supplied></hi> ለኪ፡ ቤተ፡ ክርስቲያን፡ ቤተ፡ ጸሎት<hi rend="rubric" rendition="#partialRubric">፨</hi>-->
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​አን​ቲ፡ ​ሐሊ​ብ፡ ​ወመ​ዓር ፨  ​እስ​መ፡ ​ዘእ​ንበ​ሌኪ፡ ​አል​ብየ፡ ​ተስ​ፋ፡ ​መም​ሕር ፨ 
                                    ​ኦእ​ግዝ​እት​የ፡ ​ሰን​በተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​ቅድ​ስት፡ ​ዕቀ​ብኒ፡ ​ወሰ​ውር​ኒ፡   (fol. 4v)   ​እመ​ከራ፡ ​ሥጋ፡ ​ወነ​ፍስ፡ ​ለዓ​መት​ኪ፡
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e1038PRS13690WalattaG">
                        <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>
                                        ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡</fo:inline> ​ወለ​ጸሐ​ፊሁ፡ ​ሊተ​ኒ፡ ​ለገ​ብር<fo:inline>ከ (!)</fo:inline>፡
                                    <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>፡ ​ሃይ​ማኖ​ት፡  ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜን ፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e1060LIT2934RepCh215">
               <fo:inline>II) Fols 4v–8r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Malkǝʾ-hymn to Raphael’ (​መል​ክአ፡ ​ሩፋ​ኤል፡), CAe 2934.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ሰላ​ም፡  ​ለተ​ፈጥ​ሮት​ከ፡ ​በዕ​ለተ፡ ​እሁ​ድ፡ ​ሰን​በት፡ ​እሁ​ድ፡ ​ዘተ​ስዕ​ለ፡ ​ቅድ​መ፡ ​እም​ነፋ​ስ፡ ​ወነድ ፨
                                    ​ሩፋ​ኤል፡  ​ሊቆ​ሙ፡ ​ለፆ​ታ፡  ፫ ቱ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                    ​ነገ​ድ፡ ​ወዓ​ዲ፡ ​ተሰ​የም​ከ፡ ​በማ​ኅፀ​ነ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​ትው​ልድ፡ ​በከ​መ፡
                                    ​ይቤ፡ ​ዮሐ​ንስ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ነጐ​ድጓ​ድ፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ቅዱ​ስ፡  ​ሩፋ​ኤል፡  ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​መል​አኩ ፨  ​ዘመ​ነ፡ ​ምን​ሳዌ፡ ​ኢያ​ንጥ​የኒ፡
                                    ​ፈራ​ህኩ ፨  ​በረ​ድኤ​ትከ፡ ​ተማ​ኅፀ​ንኩ ፨ 
                                    ​ኀቤ​ከ፡ ​አስ​መኩ ፨  ​ኦአ​ምላ​ከ፡ <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ሩፋ​ኤል።  ​ዕቀ​በኒ፡
                                    ​ወአ​ድኅ​ነኒ፡   (fol. 8r)   ​ሊተ፡ ​ለዓ​መት​ከ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e1111PRS13690WalattaG">
                        <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡</fo:inline> ​ወለ​ጸሐ​ፊሁ፡ ​ሊተ​ኒ፡ ​ለገ​ብር​ከ፡ ወ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline> ​ሃይ​ማኖ​ት።  
                                    ​ለዓ​ለም፡ ​ወለ​ዓለ​መ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን። ። ።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e1129LIT2248salota">
               <fo:inline>III) Fols 8r–10r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Prayer of Thanksgiving by St Basil’ (​ጸሎ​ተ፡ ​አኰ​ቴት፡ ​ዘባ​ስል​ዮስ፡), CAe 2248.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                     <fo:inline>[////]</fo:inline> ​ለገ​ባሬ፡ ​ሠና​ያት፡ ​ላዕ​ሌነ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​መሐ​ሪ፡ ​አቡ​ሁ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​እነ፡ ​ወአ​ምላ​ክነ፡ ​ወመ​ድኃ​ኒነ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​እስ​መ፡ ​ሰወ​ረነ፡ ​ወረ<fo:inline>ደ (!)</fo:inline>​አነ፡
                                    ​ዓቀ​በነ፡ ​ወአ​ቅረ​በነ፡ ​ወተ​ወከ​ፈነ፡ ​ሀቤ​ሁ፡  ​ወተ​ማኅ​ፀነ​ነ፡ ​ወአ​ጽን​ዓነ።  ​ወአ​ብጽ​ሐነ፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ዛቲ፡ ​ሰዓ​ት፡ ​ንሰ​ዓሎ፡ ​እን​ከ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ይዕ​ቀበ​ነ፡ ​በዛ​ቲ፡ ​ዕለ​ት፡ ​ቅድ​ስት፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ኢታ​ብአ​ነ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​መን​ሱት፡ ​አላ፡ ​አድ​ኅነ​ነ፡ ​ወባ​ልሐ​ነ፡ ​እም​ኵሉ፡ ​እኩ​ይ፡ ​በጸ​ጋ፡ ​ወበ​ሣህ​ል፡ ​ዘለ​ፍቅ​ረ፡ ​ሰብ​እ፡ ዘ  (fol. 10r)  ​ለወ​ልድ​ከ፡ ​ዋህ​ድ፡ ​እግ​ዚእ​ነ፡ ​ወአ​ምላ​ክነ፡ ​ወመ​ድኃ​ኒነ፡
                                    ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​ዘቦ​ቱ፡ ​ለከ፡ <fo:inline>ስብሐተ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ወክ​ብር፡ ​ወእ​ዘዝ፡ ​ይደ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ሌሁ፡ ​ወም​ስለ፡ ​መን​ፈስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ማኅ​የዊ፡ ​ዘዕ​ሩይ፡ ​ምስ​ሌከ፡ ​ይእ​ዜኒ፡ ​በል ፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Omitted characters have been added above the line (e.g. fols 2r, 5r, 9v);
                                            a <fo:inline font-style="italic">tamallas</fo:inline>-sign is used on 8r.
                                        The ink is smudged in several places (e.g. 4v, 6r).</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 4v: The first parts of the names of the original owner and scribe have been erased. However, the name of the owner
                                            can be deciphered as <fo:inline id="d1e1353PRS13690WalattaG">Walatta Giyorgis</fo:inline>. The second part of the scribe’s name was
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሃይ​ማኖ​ት፡</fo:inline>, the first part is not decipherable, but the space it takes up makes
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ወል​ደ፡ ​ተክ​ለ፡ ​ሃይ​ማኖ​ት፡</fo:inline> a likely possibility.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 4v: Pen trial in the bottom margin.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 2r–10r: 1
                                    column (14 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 4r. The characters per line are 16-20.The horizontal ruled lines are occasionally somewhat irregular and go beyond the
                                        outer vertical line, e.g. on fols 5, 7.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            103 × 86 mm (fol. 4r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 15 mm, bottom: 27 mm, right: 12 mm, left: 4 mm (fol. 4r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible. Both primary and ruling pricks are visible. The upper and bottom lines are written above the ruling.
                                         Ruling pattern: 1A-1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 2r–10r. Eighteenth–nineteenth century.. Irregular hand with broadly spaced characters.
                                        There are changes of nib on fols 4v, 5r, 8r, but the hand is probably the same.<fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: Parts of the names of the individuals involved in the production of the manuscript; holy names;
                                        the words <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሥላ​ሴ፡</fo:inline>
                              <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሰላ​ም፡</fo:inline>; <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ይዲ</fo:inline>
                              <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ይካ</fo:inline>,
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሕዝ</fo:inline>; elements
                                        of the punctuation signs.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Abbreviations: <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="6mm"
                                             provisional-label-separation="6mm"
                                             start-indent="cm">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>1)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                            ​ሰላ and ሰ for ​ሰላ​ም፡ (e.g. fols 3r, 6r);
                                            ​ይዲ and  for ​ይቤ፡ ​ዲያ​ቆን፡ (e.g. fol. 6v);
                                            ​ይካ  for ​ይቤ፡ ​ካህ​ን፡ (e.g. fol. 6v);
                                            ​ሕዝ and for ​ሕዝ​ብ፡ (e.g. fol. 7r);
                                            ​ቡራ and for ​ቡራ​ኬ፡ (fol. 9v).
                                        </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Hole on fol. 8 from the parchment making process.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is good.This unit of production shows slight traces of use. The ink on a few folios is smudged (e.g. fols 6r),
                                        6v–7r is stained by a fluid.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>eighteenth–nineteenth century</fo:inline>
                                Unit 1 can be dated palaeographically to the eighteenth–nineteenth century.
                                The name of the original owner
                                can be deciphered as <fo:inline id="d1e1380PRS13690WalattaG">Walatta Giyorgis</fo:inline>; the second part of the scribe’s name was
                                <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሃይ​ማኖ​ት፡</fo:inline>, the first part is not decipherable, but the space it takes up makes
                                <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ወል​ደ፡ ​ተክ​ለ፡ ​ሃይ​ማኖ​ት፡</fo:inline> a likely possibility (see Varia note 4).
                            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm">Unit 2</fo:block>
         <fo:block>Parchment, 14 fols (fols 11r–24v fols 11r, 11v, 22v, 23r, 24r, 24v), 1930–1970.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e1407LIT1841Malkea">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 12ra–21vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Malkǝʾ-hymn to Emmanuel’ (​መል​ክአ፡ ​አማ​ኑኤ​ል፡), CAe 1841.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​በሰ​ሌዳ፡ ​ዝን​ቱ፡ ​ልብ​የ፡ ​አም​ጣነ፡ ​ለመ​ንክ ​ር፡ ​ተጽ​ሕፈ ፤  ​ፊደ​ለ፡
                                     ፩ ​ዱ፡ ​ፍቅ​ርከ፡ እ ​ንተ፡ ​ኢኮ​ነ፡ ​ግዱ​ፈ፤
                                    ​አማ​ኑኤ​ል፡ ​ኰና ​ኒ፡ ​ማዕ​ከላ​ተ፡ ​ወጽ​ንፈ ፨  ​ከመ፡ ​እን​ብብ፡ ​ቅድ​መ፡ ​ጉባ​ዔ፡ ​ነገ​ረ፡ ​ሥጋ​ዊከ፡
                                    ​ዘልፈ ፨  ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ሀበ​ኒ፡ ​ጥበ​በ፡ ​ወአፈ ፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡  ​ተወ​ካፌ፡ ​ስቅ​ለት፡ ​መል​ዕል​ት፡ ​ጸልቦ ፨ 
                                    ​ሥጋ​ከ፡ ​ወደ​ምከ፡ ​ምስ​ካይ፡ ​ለዘ​አጸቦ ፨  ​ረድ​ኤት​ከ፡ ​አፍ​ጥን፡ ​ፀዊ​ረከ፡
                                    ​አስቦ ፤  ​ኦእ​ግዚ​እየ፡ ​ወአ​ምላ​ኪየ፡  ​አማ​ኑኤ​ል፡  ​ዕቀ​በኒ፡ ​ወአ​ድኅነ  (b)  ​ኒ፡
                                    ​እመ​ከራ፡ ​ሥጋ፡ ​ወነ​ፍስ፡ ​ሊተ፡  ​ለገ​ብር​ከ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e1463PRS13688GabraS">​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ጻድ​ቅ። </fo:inline>
                                    ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜን ፨ ፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Colophon</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block font-family="Ludolfus">Fol. 21vb: <fo:inline/>
                        </fo:block>
                        <fo:block font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ወጸ​ሐፊ​ሁ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e1481PRS13687WaldaA">​ወል​ደ፡ ​አማ​ኑኤ​ል፡</fo:inline> ​ዘብ​ሔረ፡
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e1485LOC4898MuherI">​ምሑር</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Additional notes</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 21v: Modern colophon written within the last lines of the text in pen, partly
                                            illegible. If correct, it would point to a date of production in the 1930s or 1940s. It cannot be determined with certainty
                                        whether the hand is identical to the main hand.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">​በ፲​፱፻፴<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>ዓ<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​ምህ<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​ተጻፈ</fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 22r: Modern note.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">
                           <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​መልካ</fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 22r: Modern note.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">​ብር​ዳት ​ጡሮሞ ​ቤቱ፡ ​እኽድ ​የጸቺ ​ወን​ድም</fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 22r: Modern note.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">​ህት​ዘር፡</fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>5)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 23v: Modern note.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">​ቸር​ቤተ​ዘረር</fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>The name of the owner, mentioned in a supplication on fol. 21vb,
                                                was   <fo:inline id="d1e1676PRS13688GabraS">Gabra Ṣādǝq</fo:inline>; the name of the scribe, mentioned in the
                                                colophon, was  <fo:inline id="d1e1681PRS13687WaldaA">Walda ʾAmānuʾel</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>There are only few scribal corrections: occasionally, omitted words have been added above the line
                                            (e.g. fols 12rb, 18vb); erroneous characters have been erased or expunctuated
                                        (e.g. 16vb, 20ra).</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 12ra–21vb: 2
                                    columns (14 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 12r. The characters per line per column are are 8-11.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            98 × 77 mm (fol. 12r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 16 mm, bottom: 30 mm, right: 17 mm, left: 10 mm, intercolumn: 6 mm (fol. 12r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible. Both primary and ruling pricks are visible.  The upper line is written above the ruling. The bottom line is written above the ruling.
                                         Ruling pattern: 1A-1A-1A1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 2:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 12ra–21vb. Mid-twentieth century. (scribe: Walda ʾAmānuʾel) . Trained and regular hand. Characters are tall and slender.
                                        Walda ʾAmānuʾel is indicated as the scribe in the
                                        colophon.<fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: Groups of lines on the incipit page, alternating with black lines;
                                        the word <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሰላ​ም፡</fo:inline>;
                                    elements of numerals and of the punctuation signs.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Holes on fol. 24 from the parchment making process.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is good.The first and last folios of this unit of production are darkened and show stronger traces of use, like creases and superficial dirt.
                                        Overall, the state of preservation is good.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>1930–1970</fo:inline>
                                The name of the owner was <fo:inline id="d1e1704PRS13688GabraS">Gabra Ṣādǝq</fo:inline>.
                               The scribe, who
                                identifies himself as
                                <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e1707PRS13687WaldaA">Walda ʾAmānuʾel za-bǝḥera Mǝḥur</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>,
                                is identical to the scribe of
                                MS EMIP 989 (Mihur Gedam 14), which can be dated by mention of Patriarch <fo:inline id="d1e1713PRS2533Baselyos">Bāsǝlyos</fo:inline>
                                to <fo:inline>1956–1970</fo:inline>. The colophon added above the end of the text
                            on fol. 21v is not entirely legible, but probably points to a date of production in the
                            1930s or 1940s. This makes it certain that the date of production of this unit falls in the mid-twentieth century, probably until the
                            1940s. An original production around the church of
                                <fo:inline id="d1e1720INS0794MEN">Muhǝr ʾIyasus</fo:inline>, which also holds  MS EMIP 989 (Mihur Gedam 14), seems likely.
                            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethf26">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethf26</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
   <fo:page-sequence initial-page-number="auto-odd" master-reference="Aethiopica-master">
