      </fo:static-content>
      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethe36"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. e. 36</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Juel-Jensen 4)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex184×168 mm (weight: 390g), 60 fols, 6 quires, eighteenth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e1959LIT2000Mazmur">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 1r–60v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Psalms of David, incomplete, CAe 2000.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">
                                The text terminates abruptly in the middle of Ps 70:10 due to material loss.
                            </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ፍካ​ሬ፡ ​ዘጻ​ድቃ​ን፡ ​ወዘ​ኃጥ​አን። ​መዝ​ሙር፡ ​ዘዳ​ዊት።
                                     ​ሃሌ፡ ​ሉያ።
                                ​ብፁ​ዕ፡ ​ብእ​ሲ፡ ​ዘኢ​ሖረ፡ ​በም​ክረ፡ ​ረሲ​ዓን ፨
                                ​ወዘ​ኢቆ​መ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ፍኖ​ተ፡ ​ኃጥ​አን ፨
                                ​ወዘ​ኢነ​በረ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​መን​በረ፡ ​መስ​ተሣ​ልቃን ፨
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​አን​ተ፡ ​ረዳ​እየ፡ ​ወኃ​ይልየ ፨ 
                                ​ምላ​ዕ፡ ​አፉ​የ፡ ​ስብ​ሐተከ ፨
                                ​ከመ፡ ​እሰ​ብሕ፡ ​አኰ​ቴተከ ፨ 
                                ​ወኵ​ሎ፡ ​አሚ​ረ፡ ​ዕበ​የ፡ ​ስብ​ሐቲከ ፨
                                ​ኢት​ግድ​ፈኒ፡ ​በመ​ዋዕ​ለ፡ ​ርስ​እየ ፨
                                ​ወአ​መ፡  ​ሂ፡  ​ኃል​ቀ፡ ​ኃይ​ልየ፡ ​ኢት​ኅድ​ገኒ፡ ​አም​ላኪየ ፨
                                ​እስ​መ፡ ​ነበ​ቡ፡ ​ላዕ​ሌየ፡ ​ጸላ​እትየ ፨
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Additional notes</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 1r: ‘Come to me, David king of Israel’ (​ነዐ፡ ​ኀቤ​የ፡ ​ዳዊ​ት፡ ​ንጉ​ሠ፡ ​እስ​ራኤ​ል፡), CAe 4009.. The text, which often introduces the Psalms of David,
                                        is written in the upper margin of the folio.
                                        Some letters are barely readable due to faded ink.
                                    </fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">Incipit:  : ​ነዓ፡ ​ኀቤ​የ፡ ​ወዳ​ዊት፡ ​ንጉ​ሠ፡ ​እስ​ራኤ​ል፡ ​በዐ​ለ፡ ​መዝ​ሙር፡ ​ሠና​ይ፡ ​ወጥ​ዑመ፡ ​ቃል፡  ... 
                                        </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                                        Scribal corrections are frequent throughout the text, sometimes interlineally (e.g. on fols 46r, 47v), sometimes over erasure in black ink (e.g. 17v).
                                        Scribbles in pale or deep black ink are found, e.g. on 21v, 25v, 30r.
                                        Pen trials in pale or deep black ink are found, e.g. on 1v, 47v, 51r.
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                                        Stichometry is indicated in red ink by the word <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቃሉ፡</fo:inline> followed by a numeral:
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቃሉ፡ ​፳፯</fo:inline> (Ps 59, fol. 51v),
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቃሉ፡ ​፲፯</fo:inline> (Ps 60, fol. 51v), <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቃሉ፡ ፴</fo:inline> (Ps 61, fol. 52v),
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቃሉ፡ ​፳፬</fo:inline> (Ps 62, fol. 53r), <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቃሉ፡ ​፳፬</fo:inline> (Ps 63, fol. 53v),
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቃሉ፡ ​፴፫</fo:inline> (Ps 64, fol. 54v), <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቃሉ፡ ​፴፫</fo:inline> (Ps 65, fol. 55v),
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቃሉ፡ ​፲፭</fo:inline> (Ps 66, fol. 56r), <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቃሉ፡ ​፹፯</fo:inline> (Ps 67, fol. 58r),
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቃሉ፡ ​፸፯</fo:inline> (Ps 68, fol. 60r), <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቃሉ፡ ​፲፩</fo:inline> (Ps 69, fol. 60r).
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Short titles of the psalms are written in small script in black ink on the upper margin of many folios, e.g.
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘዳ​ዊት፡ ​ሶበ፡ ​ሰደ​ዶ፡ ​አቤ​ሴሎ​ም፡ ​ወል​ዱ፡</fo:inline> on fol. 2r (Ps 3) and
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘዳ​ዊት፡ ​ሶበ፡ ​አበ​ሰ፡ ​በብ​እሲ​ተ፡ ​ኦር​ዮ፡</fo:inline> on fols 3v (Ps 6).
                                        Other titles are found throughout the manuscript, e.g. on fols 4r, 5v, 8r.
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>A note <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">‘Bought in March 1973’</fo:inline> is written in pencil in the upper inner corner of fol. 60v,
                                        possibly by <fo:inline id="d1e2387PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline>.
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>5)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>A white sticker is glued to the lower margin of fol. 1r.
                                        The name of <fo:inline id="d1e2398PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> is printed on it
                                        (‘<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቤን​ት፡ ​ዩው​ል፡ ​የን​ሰን።</fo:inline>’) and the signature ‘MS. Aeth. e. 33’ is written in pencil.
                                        An additional sticker, with the signature ‘Ms 4’ printed on it, is glued below it.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                              The boards are missing. The binding consists of the sewing only.
                            
                             Chainstitch sewing on four sewing stations (two pairs); periodic fold pattern; Z-plied threads.
                             Between each pair of sewing stations there are two lengths of thread.
                            
                              The small holes close to the head and tail of the quires presumably are what remains of quire tackets or endbands tiedowns.
                            
                              Crimson <fo:inline id="d1e2425">leaf tab markers</fo:inline> for navigating the text are inserted in the outer margins of
                              fols 16, 24, 36, 45, 52.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Pencil foliation in the upper right corner carried out by the Bodleian Library in January 2020
                                    (1–60).</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block>6 quires. I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 1r–10v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 11r–20v)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 21r–30v)</fo:inline> – IV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 31r–40v)</fo:inline> – V<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 41r–50v)</fo:inline> – VI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 51r–60v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>1
                                    column (18 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 1r.The characters per line are 10–23.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            120 × 133 mm (fol. 1r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 24 mm, bottom: 40 mm, right: 27 mm, left: 8 mm (fol. 1r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible. Both primary and ruling pricks are visible. The upper and bottom lines are written above the ruling. Ruling pattern: 1A-1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Eighteenth century.. 
                                    Fine and trained hand. Characters are regularly spaced and slightly right-sloping. Vowel orders are clearly distinguished.
                                    The numeral ፮ has a compressed shape and the open loop.
                                <fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: 
                                    Numbers and titles of the psalms; the stichometry, indicated by the word <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቃሉ፡</fo:inline>
                                    followed by a numeral; elements of the numerals and of the punctuation signs, including text dividers.
                                </fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Abbreviations: <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="6mm"
                                             provisional-label-separation="6mm"
                                             start-indent="cm">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>1)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                        ​መ፡ for ​መዝ​ሙር፡ (e.g. fols 18r, 22r, 24v);</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>2)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                        ​ዘ፡ for ​ዘዳ​ዊት፡ (e.g. fols 18r, 22r, 24v);</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>3)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                        ​ፍ፡ or  ​ፍጻ፡ for ​ፍጻ​ሜ፡ (e.g. fols 22v, 51v, 60r).
                                    </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Holes from parchment making are found on fols 49, 52.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is deficient.
                                    The textblock is incomplete: an undetermined number of folios is missing with loss of text from Ps 70 onwards.
                                    Humidity appears to have slightly damaged the parchment, especially towards the beginning of the manuscript. Water stains are attested in the outer or inner margins of
                                    many folios, e.g. on fols 1r, 22r, 26v. Wax stains are visible on, e.g. 1r, 31v, 46r.
                                    The parchment is crumpled on 17. The boards of the binding are missing. The lowermost sewing station is damaged and the sewing is broken.
                                </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>eighteenth century</fo:inline>
                            The manuscript can be dated palaeographically to the eighteenth century.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>It was bought by <fo:inline id="d1e2444PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> in March 1973,
                            according to Varia note 4. It cannot be excluded that this manuscript is identical to the
                            ‘nice <fo:inline font-style="italic">Psalter</fo:inline>’ which Juel-Jensen acquired in
                            <fo:inline id="d1e2454LOC4244Laliba">Lālibalā (town)</fo:inline> during his first
                            visit to Ethiopia, starting in February 1973, see
                            Juel-Jensen 1977,  63.</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e2465PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Bibliography</fo:block>Juel-Jensen 1977.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethe36">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethe36</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
