      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethf24"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. f. 24</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Juel-Jensen 6)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex, composite117×91 mm (weight: 118g), 41 fols, 6 quires.  Unit 1:  nineteenth century–1912. Unit 2:  nineteenth–mid-twentieth century. Unit 3:  nineteenth–mid-twentieth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                                    The book is bound in wooden boards.
                                
                                    The front board broke and only its inner half is preserved. The preserved fragment of the front board is flush with the bookblock and has shallow external bevels.
                                    The grain runs vertically. The external surface and the edges of the board fragment are polished and a finishing layer of dark colour has been added.
                                
                                    Chainstitch sewing on two sewing stations (one pair); Z-plied thread.
                                    The sewing broke because of the insect damage and the sixth quire has been connected with the rest of
                                        the bookblock by stitching it with simple loops of thread to the chain on the spine.
                                
                                    The small pairs of holes close to the tail of the quires might be what remains of endbands or quire tackets.
                                
                                    The manuscript is provided with a leather one-piece single-walled satchel with a cord hinging strap.
                                    The satchel is equipped with two flaps extending from the side panels and a main pointed flap extending from the back to the front
                                    panel to cover the opening of the book compartment.
                                    The cord hanging strap passes through two flaps extending from the bottom panel of the case.
                                </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Pencil foliation in the upper right corner carried out by the Bodleian Library in January 2020 (1–41).</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>nineteenth–mid-twentieth century</fo:inline>
                            The manuscript probably consists of three distinct units of production: Unit 1 and Unit 2,
                            and Unit 3. Unit 3
                            consists of the addition of content on the material support of Unit 1 and Unit 2
                            and of the addition of one more quire, Quire B (corresponding to the
                            transformation model A3 according to Andrist et al. 2013,  65).
                            It is possible that Unit 1 and Unit 2
                            had been distinct units of circulation before being joined in the current unit of circulation.  Unit 3
                            might have been added at the moment of joining of the two other units or at a later date.
                            The handwriting suggests a date of production between the nineteenth and mid-twentieth century for all
                            units of production.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>It is not known how
                            and when the manuscript came into the possession of <fo:inline id="d1e5474PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e5479PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block>6 quires. A<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2 (Fols 1r–2v)</fo:inline> – I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 3r–12v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 13r–22v)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6 (Fols 23r–28v)</fo:inline> – IV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">4+5 (Fols 29r–37v)</fo:inline> – B<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">4 (Fols 38r–41v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm">Unit 1</fo:block>
         <fo:block>Parchment, 28 fols (fols 1–28), nineteenth century–1912.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e5510LIT2000Mazmur">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 3r–26r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Psalms of David, incomplete, CAe 2000.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ነዓ፡ ​ኀቤ​የ፡ ​ዳዊ​ት፡ ​ንጉ​ሠ፡ <fo:inline>ኤ፳ኤል፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                                ​በዓ​ለ፡ ​መዝ​ሙር፡ ​አመ፡ ​እወ​ድሳ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                ለ ​ማር​ያም፡  ​፩፡ ​ብፁ​ዕ፡ ​ብእ​ሲ፡ ​ዘኢ​ሖረ፡ ​በም​ክረ፡ ​ረሲ​አን ፨ 
                                ​ወዘ​ኢቆ​መ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ፍኖ​ተ፡
                                ​ኃጥ​አን ፨ 
                                ​ወዘ​ኢነ​በረ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​መን​በረ፡ ​መስ​ተሣ​ልቃ​ን። ​ዘዳ​እሙ፡ ​ሕገ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ሥም​ረቱ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​እስ​መ፡ ​ሜጥ​ዋ፡ ​ለዓ​መፃ፡ ​ላዕ​ሌየ፡ ​ወሀ​ለዩ፡ ​ምክ​ረ፡ ​እን​ተ፡ ​ኢይ​ክሉ፡ ​ዓቅ​ሞ። ​ወታ​ገብ​ዖሙ፡ ​ድኅ​ሬሆ​ሙ። ​ወታ​ስተ​ዴሉ፡ ​ገጾ​ሙ፡ ​ለጊዜ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                ​መዓ​ትከ። ​ተለ​ዓል​ከ፡ ​እግ​ዚኦ፡ ​በኃ  (fol. 26r)  ​ይል​ከ። ​ንሴ​ብሕ፡  ​ወን​ዜም​ር፡ ​ለጸን<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Additional notes</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 26r–26v: Calendaric note in Gǝʿǝz and Amharic, written by Hand 2.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">Incipit: :
                                        <fo:inline>በዘንከር፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ሀሳ​በ፡ ​ሕጉ፡ ​ወት​እዛ​ዙ፡ ​ለእ ​ግዚ ​እነ፡ ​ወአ​ምላ​ክነ፡ ​ወመድ ​ኃኒ​ነ፡
                                        ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ሀሎ​ነ፡ ​በዘ​መነ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ዮሐ​ንስ፡
                                        ​ወን​ጌላ​ዊ፡ ​ያብ​ጽሐ​ነ፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ዘመ​ነ፡ ​ማቴ​ዎስ፡ ​ዜና​ዊ፡ በ ​፶፻ ​ወበ ​፭፻  ​ዓመ​ተ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ 
                                        በ ​፲፻ ወ ​፱፻ ወ ፬  ​ኮነ፡ ​ዓመ​ተ፡ ​ምሕ​ረት፡  ​በዝ፡ ​ሠረ​ቀ፡ ​ለነ፡ ​ወር​ኃ፡ ​ነሐ​ሴ፡
                                        <fo:inline>ብሩክ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ያብ​ጽሐ​ነ፡ ​እስ​ከ፡
                                        ​ወር​ኃ፡ ​ጳጕ​ሜን፡ ... 
                                    </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 27r: ‘Protective prayer against eye disease’ (​ጸሎ​ተ፡ ​ነደ​ራ፡), incomplete, CAe 5690..
                                        The text is incomplete, breaking off after the beginning.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ፩ ​አም​ላክ፡ ​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​በእ​ንተ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                            ​ሕማ​መ፡ ​ዓይ​ነ፡ ​ወር​ቅ፡ ​ወኵ​ሎን፡ ​ሕማ​ማት።
                                            ​ጸሎ​ተ፡ ​ነድ​ራ፡ ​ወእ​ንዘ፡ ​የሐ​ውር፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ነ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ባሕ​ረ፡ ​ጥብ​ርያ​ዶስ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡
                                             ​፲ወ፪  ​አር​ዳኢሁ ፨  ​ወር​እዩ፡
                                        </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Scribal corrections by the main hand are relatively rare.
                                        Occasionally, omitted words and characters are written interlineally (e.g. fols 3r, 20v)
                                        and erroneous characters are marked for deletion with surrounding dashes (e.g. fols 8v, 11r, 18v).  </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>The titles of the psalms are written crudely by a secondary hand in the spaces left for them.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 1r, 2v: Hardly legible scribbles.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 1v–2r: Outlines of ornamental bands and text, <!--is there a better formulation for this? -->
                                        written on a page turned by 45 degrees, probably pen trials.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 3r–28v: 1
                                    column (17 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 5r.The characters per line are 17–18.Both ruling patterns are used. Horizontal ruled lines are often ruled through until the outer margin.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            88 × 71 mm (fol. 5r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 10 mm, bottom: 19 mm, right: 10 mm, left: 19 mm (fol. 5r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling is visible; pricking is partly visible. Primary pricks are visible, horizontal pricks are not visible. The upper and bottom lines are written above the ruling. Ruling pattern: 1A-1A/0-0/0-0/J.  Ruling pattern: 1A-1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 3r–26r. Nineteenth–mid-twentieth century.. Irregular and untrained hand with cursive script. The scribe often omits the word separator at the end of a line.<fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: Single or double lines on the incipit pages; holy names;
                                    elements of punctuation signs and of the numerals.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 2:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 26r–26v. 1911. Same hand as Additional note 1. The hand is more regular than that of the first hand,
                                    with a large and a very round script. Characters are broadly spaced. <fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: Two lines of the incipit; elements of the numerals.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Holes resulting from parchment making are found on fols 2, 28.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>nineteenth century–1912</fo:inline>
                            Unit 1 can be dated palaeographically to the period between the nineteenth
                            and the mid-twentieth century. The
                            calendaric note Additional note 1  (fols 26r–26v), an addition
                            to Unit 1, is dated to 1912. This date might also be close to the date of production of this
                            unit of production, and possibly of the entire manuscript.
                        </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm">Unit 2</fo:block>
         <fo:block>Parchment, 9 fols (fols 29r–37v), nineteenth–mid-twentieth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e5865LIT4711Mastabqwe">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 29r–37v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Supplications’ (​መስ​ተብ​ቍዓ​ት፡), incomplete, CAe 4711.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e5873LIT4711Mastabqwe#SupplicationNight">
               <fo:inline>I-1) Fols 29r–30v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Supplications: ​መስ​ተብ​ቍዓ​ን፡ ​ዘይ​በቍ​ዑ፡ ​ለጸ​ሎት፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​ግብ​ር፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ወካ​ዕበ፡ ​ናስ​ተበ​ቍዕ፡ ​ዘኵ​ሎ፡ ​ይእ​ኅዝ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔር<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​አብ፡
                                    ​ለእ​ግዚ​እ፡ ​ወመ​ድኃ​ኒነ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ነአ​ኵቶ፡ ​በኵ​ሉ፡
                                    ​ወበ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​እስ​መ፡ ​ከደ​ነነ፡ ​ወረ​ድአ​ነ፡ ​ሶቀ​ነ፡ ​ወአ​ብጽ​ሐነ፡ ​እስከ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ዛቲ፡ ​ሰዓ​ት፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ወአ​ምሳ​ለ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​ሕዝ​ብከ፡ ​ወተ​ረፈ፡ ​ሌሊ​ትኒ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​በኵ​ሉ፡ ​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ወዳ​ኅና፡
                                    ​ይሬ​ስየ​ነ፡ ​ነሃ​ሉ፡
                                    በ  (fol. 30v)  ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​ዘቦ​ቱ፡ ​ለከ፡ ​ምስ​ሌሁ፡ ​ወም​ስለ፡ ​ቅዱስ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​መን​ፈስ፡ ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ወእ​ኂዝ፡
                                    ​ይእ​ዜኒ፡ ​ወዘ​ልፈ​ኒ፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e5908LIT4711Mastabqwe#SupplicationSick">
               <fo:inline>I-2) Fols 30v–32v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Supplications: ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዱያ​ን።</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ወካ​ዕበ፡ ​ናስ​ተበ​ቍዕ፡ ​ለዘ​ኵሎ፡ ​ይእ​ኅዝ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ ​ር፡ ​አብ፡ <fo:inline>ለእሰግዚእ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ወመ​ድኃ​ኒነ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡
                                    ​ዱያ​ን፡
                                    አ  (fol. 31r)  ​ኃዊ​ነ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ኵሎ፡ ​ደዌ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ወኵ​ሎ፡ ​ሕማ​መ፡ ​ያሰ​ስል፡ ​እም​ኔሆ​ሙ፡
                                    ​መን​ፈሰ፡ ​ደዌ፡ ​ሥዒ​ሮ፡ ​ሕይ​ወተ፡ ​የሐ​ቦሙ፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ሀብ፡ ​ሳሕ​ተ፡ ​ወሀ​ብ፡ ​ዕረ​ፍተ፡ ​ኵሎ፡ ​ደዌ፡ ​ስደ  (fol. 32v)  ​ድ፡ ​እም​ዝን​ቱ፡ ​ቤት፡ ​ወእ​ምእ​ለ፡ ​ይፄ​ውዑ፡ ​ቅዱ​ሰ፡ ​ወቡ​ሩከ፡ ​ስመ​ከ፡ ​ወስ​እለ፡ ​ኈል​ቈ፡ ​ነፍ​ሳቲ​ነ፡ ​እን​ከ፡
                                    ​ደዌ፡ ​ፈዊ​ሰከ፡
                                    ​ፍጽ​መ፡ ​መድ​ኃኒ​ተ፡ ​ጻጕ፡ ​በ፩ ​ወል​ድከ፡ ​ዘቦቱ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e5943LIT4711Mastabqwe#SupplicationTraders">
               <fo:inline>I-3) Fols 32v–34v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Supplications: ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​እለ፡ ​ይነ​ግዱ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ወካ​ዕበ፡ ​ናስ​ተበ​ቍዕ፡  ​በእ​ንተ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​እለ፡ ​ይነ​ግዱ፡ ​አኃ​ዊነ፡
                                      (fol. 33r)   ​ወበ​እን​ተሂ፡ ​እለ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ሃለው<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> 
                                    ​ይን​ግዱ፡ ​እመ​ሂ፡ ​በባ​ሕር፡ ​ወእ​መሂ፡
                                    ​በአ​ፍላግ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                    ​ወእ​መሂ፡ ​በቀ​ላያ​ት፡ ​ወእ​መሂ፡ ​በፍ​ኖት፡ ​በዘ​ኮነ፡ ​መን ገ ​ደ፡ ​ይገ​ብሩ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ኵሎ፡
                                    ​ያብ​ጽሕ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​መር​ሶ፡ ​መድ​ኅን፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ፍጡ​ነ፡ ​ይር​ከበ​ነ፡ ​ሣህ​ልከ፡ ​እግ​ዚኦ። ​ንበ​ል፡ ​ኵል​ነ። ​እግ​ዚኦ፡ ​ተሣ​ሃለ​ነ።
                                    ​አብ​ጽሖ​ሙ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ዘመ​ድኅ​ን፡ ​መር​ሶ፡ ​አው​ፊ፡ ​ለሰ​ብኦ​ሙ፡ ​በፍ​ሥሐ፡ ​ወበ​ሀሤ​ት፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ይት​ፌሥ​ሑ፡
                                    ወ  (fol. 34v)  ​ያስ​ተፌ​ሥሑ፡ ​በ፩ ​ወል​ድከ።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e5988LIT4711Mastabqwe#SupplicationRain">
               <fo:inline>I-4) Fols 34v–36r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Supplications: ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዝና​ማት።</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ወካ​ዕበ፡ ​ናስ​ተበ​ቍዕ፡  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዝና​ማት፡ ​ከመ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ዝና​ሞ፡ ​ይፌ​ኑ፡
                                    ​ውስተ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                    ​ኀበ፡ ​ይት​ፈቀ​ድ፡ ​መካን<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ዘኵ​ሎ፡ ​ይእ​ኅዝ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​አም​ላክ​ነ። ​ጸል​ዩ፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡
​ዝና​ማት። ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡   (fol. 35r)   ​ዘኵ​ሎ፡ ​ትእ​ኅዝ፡ ​ንስ​እለ​ከ፡ <fo:inline>ወናስተበቍዓ፡ ከ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ዝና​ማቲ​ከ፡ ​ፈኑ፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​እግ​ዚኦ፡ ​ተሣ​ሀለ​ነ፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ <fo:inline>ነዳን፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ሕዝ​ብከ፡ ​ወበ​እን​ተ፡ ​ኵሎ​ሙ፡
                                    ​እለ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ይሴ​ፈው​ከ፡ ​ግበ​ር፡
                                    ​ምስ​ሌነ፡ ​በከ​መ፡ ​ምሕ​ረት​ከ፡ ​ግበ​ር፡ ​ወሴ​ሲ፡ ​ልበ​ነ፡ <fo:inline>በመለኮ፡ ተ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ትም​ህርት<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                     (fol. 36r)   ​ወበ​ለብ​ዎ፡ ​ዘእ​ምኀ<fo:inline>[ቤ]</fo:inline>​ከ፡ በ ፩  ​ወል​ድከ፡ ​ዘቦ​ቱ፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e6043LIT4711Mastabqwe#SupplicationFruit">
               <fo:inline>I-5) Fols 36r–37r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Supplications: ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ፍሬ፡ ​ምድ​ር።</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ወካ​ዕበ፡  ​ናስ​ተበ​ቍዕ፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ፍሬ፡ ​ምድ​ር፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ፍሬ​ሃ፡ ​ለም​ድር፡ ​ያል​ሕቅ፡ ​ወያ​ሥም​ር፡ ​ያብ​ጽሕ፡ ​ለዘ​ርዕ፡
                                    ​ወለ​ማዕ​ረር፡ ​ዘብ​ዑለ፡
                                    ​ጸጋ፡ ​ይጸ​ጉ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​አም​ላክ​ነ፡  ​ጸል​ዩ፡ <fo:inline>በእን (!)</fo:inline> (fol. 36v)   ​ፍሬ፡ ​ምድ​ር።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ፍጡ​ነ፡ ​ይር​ከበ​ነ፡ ​ሣህ​ልከ፡
                                    ​እግ​ዚኦ፡ ​ንበ​ል፡ ​ኵል​ነ፡ ​እግዚ  (fol. 37r)  ​ኦ፡ ​ተሣ​ሃለ​ነ፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ነዳ​ያን፡ ​ሕዝ​ብከ፡ ​ወበ​እንተ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                    ​ኵሎ​ሙ፡ ​እለ፡ ​ይፄ​ውዑ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ቅዱ​ሰ፡ ​ወቡ​ሩከ፡ ​ስመ​ከ፡
                                    ​በ፩ ​ወል​ድከ፡ ​በል።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e6079LIT4711Mastabqwe#SupplicationRivers">
               <fo:inline>I-6) Fols 37r–37v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Supplications: ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ማያ​ተ፡ ​አፍ​ላግ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The text breaks off at the end.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ወካዕ ​በ፡ ​ናስ​ተበ​ቍዕ፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ማያ​ተ፡ ​አፍ​ላግ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ያዕ​ርግ፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​መሥ​ፈር​ቶሙ፡ ​ያስ​ተፍ​ሥሕ፡
                                      (fol. 37v)   ​ገጻ፡ ​ለም​ድር፡ ​ወያ​ርዊ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ትላ​ሚሃ፡ ​ያብ​ጽሕ፡
                                    ለ<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​ርዕ፡ <fo:inline>ወለመሳረር፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                                    ​ዘብ ዑ ​ለ፡ ​ጸጋ፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Scribal corrections by the main hand are relatively rare.
                                        Occasionally, omitted words and characters are written interlineally (e.g. fols 31v, 33r)
                                        and erroneous characters are marked for deletion by means of horizontal dashes (e.g. fols 32r, 33v).</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 29r–37v: 1
                                    column (9 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 29r.The characters per line are 12–13.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            80 × 62 mm (fol. 29r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 12 mm, bottom: 23 mm, right: 17 mm, left: 10 mm (fol. 29r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic">Punctuation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block linefeed-treatment="preserve">Several supplications are divided by crudely drawn text dividers consisting
                                        of black and red grids, lines, and dots
                                        (e.g. on fols 30v, 34v, 37v).</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling is visible; pricking is partly visible. Primary pricks are visible, horizontal pricks are not visible. The upper line is written above the
                                        ruling. The bottom line is written above the
                                        ruling. Ruling pattern: 1A-1A/0-0/0-0/J.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 3:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 29r–37v. 1800–1949. Irregular and untrained hand, broad and rectangular script.
                                The scribe often omits the word separator at the end of a line. It is possible that the hand is identical
                                with hand 1, though the script differs.<fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: Incipits (double red lines, single words or groups of words);
                                    the word <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ጸል​ዩ፡</fo:inline>;
                                    elements of numerals.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>nineteenth–mid-twentieth century</fo:inline>
                            Unit 2 can be dated palaeographically to the period between the nineteenth
                            and the mid-twentieth century.
                        </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm">Unit 3</fo:block>
         <fo:block>Parchment, 4 fols (fols 38r–41v), nineteenth–mid-twentieth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e6280LIT4711Mastabqwe#SupplicationEntering">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 26v, 27r–27v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Supplications: ​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​እለ፡ ​ያበ​ውኡ፡ ​መባ​አ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Beginning of the supplication for the offerers. The text is interrupted on
                            fol. 27r by another prayer.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ወእ​ምዝ፡  ​ጸሎ​ተ፡ ​መባ​ዓ፡ ​ወካ​ዕበ፡ ​ናስ​ተበ​ቍዕ፡ ​ዘኵ​ሎ፡ ​ይእ​ኅዝ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​አብ፡ ​ለዕ​ግዚ​እ፡
                                ​ወመ​ድኃ​ኒነ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​እለ፡ ​ይበ​ውዑ፡ ​መባ​ዓ፡ ​በው​ስተ፡ ​ቅድ​ስት፡ ​አኃቲ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​እን​ተ፡ ​ላዕ​ለ፡ ​ኵሉ፡
                                ​ቤተ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​መሥ​ዋዕ​ተ፡
                                ​ቀደ​ምያ​ተ፡ ​አሥ​ራተ፡ ​ቀደ​ምተ፡ ​አኰ​ቴት፡ ​ተዝ​ካር<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ዘብ​ዙኅ፡ ​ወዘ​ኅዳ​ጥ፡
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ምሥ​ዋዕ​ተ፡ ​ቀዳ​ምያ​ተ፡ ​አሥ​ራተ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ወአ​ኰቴ​ተ፡ ​ተዝ​ካር​የ፡
                                ​ዘብ​ዙኅ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ወዘ​ኅዳ​ጥ፡ ​ዘኅ​ቡዕ፡ ​ወዘ​ገሃ​ድ፡ ​ወለ​ዕለ​ሂ፡ ​ይፈ​ቅዱ፡ ​የሀ​ቡ፡ ​አስ​ቦሙ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                ​ዘይ​ሁቡ፡ ​ተወ​ከፍ፡ ​ፍት​ወቶሙ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ሀብ፡ ​ለኵ​ሎሙ፡ ​ዓስ​በ፡ ​በረ​ከት፡ ​ክፍ​ለ፡ ​ትኵ​ን፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም።
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e6330LIT1398Fethat">
               <fo:inline>II) Fols 28r–28v, 37v–39r, 41r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Absolution of the Son’ (​ፍት​ሐት፡ ​ዘወ​ልድ፡), CAe 1398.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The text is spread through three places of the manuscript, without textual breaks.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                     <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline> ​ዘወ​ልድ፡ ​እግ​ዚእ፡ ​እግ​ዚኦ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​ወል​ድ፡ ​አብ፡
                                ​ዋህ​ድ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​አብ፡ ​ዘበ​ተከ፡ ​እም​ኔነ፡ <fo:inline>ኵ (!)</fo:inline> ​ማእ​ሠረ፡ ​ኃጣ​ውኢ​ነ፡ ​በሕ​ማማ​ቲከ፡ ​ማኅ​የዊ​ት፡ ​ዘነ​ፋሕ​ከ፡ ​ላዕለ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                ​ገጸ፡ ​አር​ዳኢ​ከ፡ ​ቅዱ​ሳን፡ ​ወላ​ዕካ​ኒከ፡
                                ​ንጹ​ሐን፡
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ወእ​ምአ​ፈ፡ ​ዚአ​የኒ፡ ​አነ፡ ​ገብ​ርከ፡ ​ሀጥእ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ወይ​ኩኑ፡ ​ፍቱ​ሐነ፡ ​ወግ​ዑዛ​ነ፡ ​ወእ​ምአ​ፉሀ፡ ​ለእ​ግዝ​እት​ነ፡
                                 ​ማር​ያም፡ 
                                ​ወላ  (fol. 41r)  ​ዲተ፡ ​አም​ላክ፡ ​ሐዳ​ስ፡ ​ምእ​ናም፡ ​ግሩ​ም፡ ​ሙዳ​የ፡ ​ስእ​ለታ​ት። ​እስ​መ፡ ​ቡሩ​ክ፡ ​ስብ​ሐተ፡ ​ስም​ከ፡  ​ኦሥ​ሉስ፡  
                                ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​አብ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ወል​ድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ይእ​ዜኒ፡ ​ወዘ​ልፈ​ኒ፡
                                ​ወለ​አለመ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​አለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን።
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e6380LIT3064RepCh344">
               <fo:inline>III) Fols 39v–41r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘I praise your grace, O Full of Grace...’ (​እሴ​ብሕ፡ ​ጸጋ​ኪ፡ ​ኦም​ልእ​ተ፡ ​ጸጋ፡), CAe 3064.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ዕሴ​ብሕ፡ <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ዕት​ጋነ​ይ፡ ​ለኪ፡ ​ኦም​ልዕ​ተ፡ ​ውዳ​ሴ፡ ​ዘከ​ርኩ፡ ​በሌ​ሊት፡ ​ንጽ​ሐ፡
                                ​ድንግ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ናኪ፡ ​ዘኢ​ረስ​ሐ፡ ​በፀ​ኒስ፡ ​ወኢ​ማሰ​ነ፡
                                <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ወሊ​ድ፡ ​እስ​መ፡ ​ቅድ​ስተ፡
                                ​ቅዱ​ሳን፡ <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ቲ፡ ​እስ​መ፡ ​ናሁ፡ ​ይፈ​ልሕ፡ ​ሞገ​ደ፡ ​ፍቅ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ኪ፡
                                ​በው​ስተ፡ ​ልብ​የ፡
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ከመ፡ ​ታድ​ኅንኒ ፤  ​በዝ፡ ​ዓለም ፤ 
                                ​እም​እደ፡ ​ሰብእ ፤  ​እኩ​ያን፡
                                ​ወበ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ይመ​ጽእ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​እም​እደ፡ ​ሰይ​ጣን ፨
                                 (fol. 41r) <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ክዩ፡ <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ፍሳ​ተ፡ ​ወይ​ስሕ​ቡ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡
                                አ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ቀጸ ፨
                                <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ን፡ ​ሰፍ​ሒ፡ ​እዴኪ ፤  ​ወባ​ርክ​ኒ፡
                                ​ለገብ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ኪ፡ ​በረ​ከተ ፤ 
                                ​ዘአ​ኪ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ወፀ​ጋ፡ ወ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ድኪ፡
                                ​ላዕለ ፤  ​ኵል​ነ፡ ​አግ​ብር​ትኪ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​አዕ​ማት​ኪ፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡
                                ​ዓለም ፨ ፨ ፨
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Scribal corrections by the main hand are very rare.
                                        Occasionally, erroneous characters are marked for deletion with surrounding dashes
                                        (e.g. fols 37v, 38r).  </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 37v–41r: 1
                                    column (14–15 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 40r.The characters per line are 17–19.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            85 × 75 mm (fol. 40r)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling is visible; pricking is not visible. The upper line is written above the
                                        ruling. The bottom line is written above the
                                        ruling. Ruling pattern: 1A-1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 4:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 26v, 27r–27v, 28r–28v37v–41v. 1800–1949. Same hand as hand 1, see the description in p1.<fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: Holy names; elements of numerals and punctuation signs.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>nineteenth–mid-twentieth century</fo:inline>
                            Unit 3 can be dated palaeographically to the period between the nineteenth
                            and the mid-twentieth century.
                            The <fo:inline font-style="italic"/> mentions <fo:inline font-style="italic"/> Mārqos and
                            <fo:inline font-style="italic"/> Yoḥannǝs in a supplication (fol. 39r). These might refer to
                            <fo:inline id="d1e6596PRS13830MarkVII">Mark VII</fo:inline> and Metropolitan <fo:inline id="d1e6598PRS10393Yohanne">Yoḥannǝs III</fo:inline>, simultaneously active in 1747–1761.
                            As this timespan seems early for the
                            production of the manuscript, the names might have been copied from the <fo:inline font-style="italic">Vorlage</fo:inline>.
                        </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethf24">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethf24</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
