      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethg30"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. g. 30</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Juel-Jensen 7)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex57×41 mm (weight: 29g), 34 fols (4 p. blank), 6 quires, nineteenth–mid-twentieth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 3r–10v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e6865">Unidentified protective prayer against the tongue of men</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Large portions of the text are illegible due to faded ink.
                                The following text is partially legible on  fol. 3r: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ልሳ​ነ፡ ​ሰብ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>.
                            </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e6881LIT5690MagicPrayer">
               <fo:inline>II) Fols 11r–23v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Protective prayer against eye disease’ (​ጸሎ​ተ፡ ​ነደ​ራ፡), CAe 5690.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Large portions of the text are illegible due to faded ink. The identification is tentative and is based on the following portion of text which is legible on
                                fol. 11v: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​እን​ዘ፡ ​ይሐ​ውር፡ ​እግ​ዚእ​ነ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ባሕ​ረ፡ ​ጥብ​ርያ​ዶስ፡  ​ወም​ስሌ​ሁ፡ ​፲ወ፪ ​አር​ዳኢ​ሁ፡ ​ርእ​ዩ፡ ​መል​ክአ፡ ​ብእ​ሲት፡ ​አረ​ጊት፡</fo:inline>.
                            </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e6896LIT2765RepCh49">
               <fo:inline>III) Fols 23v–34r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Salutations for Phanuel’ (​ሰላ​ምታ፡ ​ዘፋ​ኑኤ​ል፡), CAe 2765.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Large portions of the text are illegible due to faded ink. The identification is tentative and is based on the following portion of text which is legible on
                                fols 24r–24v: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሰላ ​ም፡ ​ለከ፡ ​ሰዳ​ዴ፡ ​ሰይ​ጣና​ት፡  ​ፋኑ ​ኤል፡
                                    ​ለእ ​ግዚ ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​እምጽ  (fol. 24v)  ​ርሑ፡</fo:inline>.
                                (cp. Worrell 1914_1915,  113). It is possible that further discrete textual units follow, but due to the faded ink, this is difficult to say with certainty.
                            </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Scribal practices are difficult to observe due to the bad condition of the manuscript, whose text is mostly illegible.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block> The name of the original owner, <fo:inline id="d1e7133PRS13686WaldaTH">Walda Takla Hāymānot</fo:inline>, is written in various supplication formulas. It is fully readable on fol. 31v
                                        and partially legible on fols 23r–23v (where only Walda is legible) and on fol. 28r (where only Walda Takla is legible).</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 2v: Illegible writings in black ink, possibly in the main hand. The ink is almost completely faded out.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>A white sticker is glued to the inner side of the front board. The name of <fo:inline id="d1e7154PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> is printed on it
                                        (‘<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቤን​ት፡ ​ዩው​ል፡ ​የን​ሰን።</fo:inline>’) and the signature ‘MS. Aeth. g. 30’ is written in pencil below it.
                                        An additional sticker, with the signature ‘Ms 7’ on it, is also glued to the inner side of the front board.
                                        The textual content and dating of the book (‘Ethiopic Prayers C 20’) is indicated in pencil in the inner side of the front board.
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                                  The book is bound in wooden boards.
                                
                                  The boards are flush with the bookblock and have shallow external bevels. The grain runs vertically.
                                  The external surface of the boards is polished and a finishing layer of dark colour was added. The inner surface and the edges are rough.
                                
                                  Chainstitch sewing on two sewing stations (one pair); Z-plied thread.
                                  In the first quire, between the sewing stations, there is one length of thread. In the rest of the quires there are double lengths.
                                  The sewing is closed in the last quire, by knotting the ends of the thread to each other.
                                
                                  The small holes close to the head of the quires are probably what remains of quire tackets.
                                
                                  The manuscript is provided with a reddish-brown leather two-piece satchel. The satchel consists of two halves that fit together to
                                  enclose the manuscript. One half is fitted on the head edge, the other on the tail edge. The case presents a blind-tooled decoration
                                  featuring a frame in which <fo:inline id="d1e7188">single straight lines</fo:inline> cross each other forming a St Andrew cross.
                                </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Pencil foliation in the upper right corner carried out by the Bodleian Library
                                    in January 2020 (1–34).</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block>5 quires. A<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2 (Fols 1r–2v)</fo:inline> – I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 3r–10v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 11r–18v)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 19r–26v)</fo:inline> – V<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 27r–34v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>1
                                    column (8 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 18r.The characters per line are 5–7</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            32 × 27 mm (fol. 18r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 8 mm, bottom: 18 mm, right: 8 mm, left: 2 mm (fol. 18r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Primary and ruling pricks have been executed on q2 #q3 (fols 3r–18v).
                                    They are not visible on the remaining quires.   Ruling lines are never visible.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Nineteenth–first half of the twentieth century.. 
                                    Mediocre handwriting. Characters are unevenly spaced and sometimes irregular in size.
                                    The graphemes ግ and ዚ in the word ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ are occasionally written with ligature
                                    (e.g. on fols 14r, 24r, 29r).
                                <fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: 
                                    Very few rubricated words are still legible, e.g. the name of <fo:inline id="d1e7106PRS7840Phanuel">Phanuel</fo:inline> on fols 24r, 24v and
                                    part of the word <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሰላ​ም፡</fo:inline>.
                                    The elements of the punctuation signs were possibly rubricated (e.g. fol. 23v).
                                </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is deficient.
                                    The entire manuscript is severely damaged by humidity, which has led to a general browning and stiffening of the parchment.
                                    Most of folios are wrinkled and stained with water.
                                    The text is for the most part illegible due to faded ink and stains of unclear origin (e.g. on fols 6v, 7r, 10v). The red ink is mostly faded out.
                                    The binding is in good condition.
                                </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>nineteenth–mid-twentieth century</fo:inline>
                            The manuscript can be dated palaeographically to the period between the
                            nineteenth and the mid-twentieth century.
                            The name of the original owner, <fo:inline id="d1e7202PRS13686WaldaTH">Walda Takla Hāymānot</fo:inline>, is written in various supplication formulas (see Varia note 2).
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>Unknown provenance.
                            The manuscript came to <fo:inline id="d1e7210PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> under unknown circumstances.</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e7215PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethg30">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethg30</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
