      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethg29"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. g. 29</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Juel-Jensen 8)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex80×62 mm (weight: 72g), 29 fols (5 p. blank), 5 quires, mid-twentieth century–1973.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e7461LIT1758Lefafa">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 1r–26v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Bandlet of Righteousness Bandlet of Justification’ (​ልፋ​ፈ፡ ​ጽድ​ቅ፡), CAe 1758.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e7469LIT1758Lefafa#FirstPart">
               <fo:inline>I-1) Fols 1r–20r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Bandlet of Righteousness: First part: revelation of the powerful names of Jesus</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ፩  ​አም​ላክ፡ ​ልፋ​ፈ፡ ​ጽድ​ቅ፡ ​ወመ​ድኃ​ኒት፡ ​ዘወ​ሀባ፡ ​አብ፡ ​በእ​ደዊ​ሁ፡
                                     ​ለእ​ግዝ​እት​ነ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡ ​እም​ቅድ​መ፡ ​ይትወ ​ለድ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​እም​ኔሃ፡ ​እን​ተ፡ ​ታበ​ውዕ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ሕይ​ወት፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ዝን​ቱ፡ ​ስም​የ፡ ​ብሂ​ል፡ ​አኀ​ዜ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​መራ​ርዮ​ን፡ ​ብሂ  (fol. 20r)  ​ል፡ ​ዘኢ​ይት​መዋ​ዕ፡ ​ለፀ​ር፡ ​ጽብ​ንዮ​ን፡ ​ብሂ​ል፡ ​መሐ​ረ፡
                                    ​በር​ሳባ​ሂል፡ ​ኵሉ፡ <fo:inline>ዘይፌርሆ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ስሙ፡ ​ለአ ​ብ፡
                                        ​ሙራ​ኤል፡ ​ስሙ፡ ​ለወ​ልድ፡ ​ምና​ቴር፡ ​ስሙ፡ ​ለመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​አብ​ያታ​ር፡ ​በዝ ​ንቱ፡ ​አስ​ማቲ​ከ፡ ​ተማ​ኅፀ​ንኩ፡ ​አነ፡ ​አመ​ትከ፡
                                    <fo:inline>[////]</fo:inline>
                                    ​ለዓ​ለ፡ ​ዓለ፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e7501LIT1758Lefafa#MangadaSamay">
               <fo:inline>I-2) Fols 20v–26v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Bandlet of Righteousness: Second part: Prayers for the heavenly journey</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ፩ ​አም ​ላክ፡ ​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​ዘመ​ንገ​ድ፡ ​ሰማ​ይ፡
                                     ​ሚካ​ኤል፡ ​ወገ​ብር​ኤል፡ ​ሱራ​ፌል፡ ​ወኪ​ሩቤ​ል፡ ​ኡራ​ኤል፡ ​ወሩ​ፋኤ​ል፡ ​አፍ​ኒን፡ ​ወራ​ጉዔ​ል፡ ወ ​ሳቁ​ኤል፡ ​መላ​እክ​ተ፡ ​ሰማ​ይ፡
                                    ​ሰአ​ሉ፡ ​ለነ፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​መሐ​ረኒ፡ ​ወተ​ሣሃ​ለኒ፡  ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡  ​ወሥ​ረይ፡ ​ኃጢ​አት​የ፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​በዛ​ቲ፡ ​ዕለ​ት፡ ​ግር​ምት፡
                                    ወ  (fol. 26v)  ​መፍ​ርህ​ት፡ ​እን​ተ፡ ​ታጠ​ውቅ፡ ​ነፍ​ሳተ፡ ​ኃጥ​አን፡ ​ወሊ​ተኒ፡ ​መሐ​ረኒ፡ ​ወተ​ሣሃ​ለኒ፡ ​ለአ​መት​ከ፡
                                    <fo:inline>[////]</fo:inline>
                                    ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                                        Erroneously omitted characters have been added above the line on fols 4r, 11r.
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Space left empty for the name of the owner in supplications
                                        is unfilled throughout (e.g. fols 6r, 14v, 25r). All supplications contain the word
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ለአ​መት​ከ፡</fo:inline>, ‘your maid’, indicating that the manuscript was produced for a
                                        woman.
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>A white sticker is glued to the inner side of the front board. The name of <fo:inline id="d1e7778PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline>
                                        is printed on it
                                        (‘<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቤን​ት፡ ​ዩው​ል፡ ​የን​ሰን።</fo:inline>’) and the signature ‘MS. Aeth. g. 29’ is written in pencil.
                                        An additional sticker, with the signature ‘Ms 8’ on it, is glued below it.
                                    The shelfmark, textual content, dating and probably place and date of acquisition
                                    of the book (‘MS Aethiop 8 <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ልፋ​ፈ፡ ​ጽድ​ቅ፡</fo:inline> Lefāfe Sedeq
                                    3rd quarter C 20 <fo:inline id="d1e7786LOC3577Gondar">Gondar</fo:inline> 1973’), barely legible,
                                        are indicated in pencil on fol. ir.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                           The book is bound in wooden boards.
                         
                           The boards are flush with the bookblock and have shallow external bevels. The grain runs vertically.
                           Both the external and internal surfaces of the boards are rough.
                         
                           Chainstitch sewing on two sewing stations (one pair). The sewing is carried out with an untwisted thread.
                           In the centrefold of the first quire, between the sewing stations, the ends of two threads are knotted together resulting
                           in a single thread length, while in the rest of the quires the thread lengths are double. In q5 the ends of the thread are left long and not knotted.
                         
                           The small holes close to the head and tail of the quires are probably what remains of quire tackets.
                         
                           The manuscript is provided with a leather two-piece satchel with a strap. The satchel consists of two halves that fit together to
                           enclose the manuscript. One half is fitted on the head edge, the other on the tail edge. A twisted leather cord passes through two
                           pockets sewn laterally on each of the two halves. The case presents a blind-tooled decoration with <fo:inline id="d1e7826">single straight lines</fo:inline>
                           and <fo:inline id="d1e7829">double circles</fo:inline>.
                         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Pencil foliation in the upper right corner carried out by the Bodleian Library in January 2020 (i–ii+1–27).</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block>5 quires. A<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2 (Fols ir–iiv)</fo:inline> – I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 1r–8v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 9r–16v)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 17r–24v)</fo:inline> – IV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2+1 (Fols 25r–27v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 1–27: 1
                                    column (10 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 9r.The characters per line are 12–13.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            62 × 49 mm (fol. 9r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 6 mm, bottom: 13 mm, right: 9 mm, left: 6 mm (fol. 9r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible. Both primary and ruling pricks are visible. The upper and bottom lines are written above the ruling.
                                     Ruling pattern: 1A-1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->1900–1973. Trained hand.<fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: Lines and groups of lines on incipit pages, alternating with black lines; holy names;
                                    the list of the names of God on fols 14v–15r; elements of the numerals.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Abbreviations: <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="6mm"
                                             provisional-label-separation="6mm"
                                             start-indent="cm">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>1)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                        ​ለዓ​ለ፡ ​ዓለ፡ or ​ለዓ፡ ​ዓለ፡
                                        for ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ (e.g. fols 20r, 24v);
                                    </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>2)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                        ​አሜ፡ for ​አሜ​ን፡ (e.g. fol. 25r).
                                    </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Decoration</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Miniatures</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Headpieces</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(4) Fol. 26v: <fo:inline>A pen-work text divider consisting of black and red dots and strokes marks the end of the text.</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Drawings</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Other</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Hairs are still attached to the bottom corner of fol. 13.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is intact.The manuscript hardly seems used.
                                    Ink is smudged on fols 7v. The sewing is a little bit loose in .</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>mid-twentieth century–1973</fo:inline>
                            The manuscript can be dated palaeographically to the twentieth century. As it
                            is in very good condition and does not seem used, it is likely that it was produced only
                            shortly before its acquisition in 1973 (see below). The manuscript was originally produced for a
                            woman, but no name has been filled in the empty spaces in supplications
                            (see Varia note 2).
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>The modern note on the first folio, ‘<fo:inline id="d1e7849LOC3577Gondar">Gondar</fo:inline>
                            1973’, very probably describes the
                            time and place of acquisition of the manuscript by <fo:inline id="d1e7855PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline>.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e7860PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethg29">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethg29</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
