      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethg28"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. g. 28</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Juel-Jensen 1)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex105×75 mm (weight: 84g), 16 fols, 3 quires, nineteenth–mid-twentieth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e8099LIT2835RepCh119">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 2r–15v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Malkǝʾ-hymn to St Michael’ (​መል​ክአ፡ ​ሚካ​ኤል፡ ), CAe 2835.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The hymn comprises 47 stanzas.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em"><!-- I would provide only the first stanza in the printed catalogue.-->
                                ​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ለዝ​ክረ፡ ​ስም​ከ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ስመ፡ ​ልዑ​ል፡ ​ዘተ ​ሳተ​ፈ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡
                                ​ያሬ​ድ፡ ​ሄኖክ ፨  ​በከ​መ፡ ​ጸሐ​ፈ፡ ​ረዳ​ኤ፡ ​ምን​ዱባ​ን፡  ​ሚካ​ኤል፡  ​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ታለ​ምድ፡ ​ዘልፈ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ለረ​ዲኦ​ትየ፡ ​ሰፊ​ሐከ፡ ​ክን​ፈ፡
<!--                                <hi rend="rubric">ሰላም<supplied resp="DR" reason="omitted"
                                        >፡</supplied></hi> ለስእርተ፡ ርእስከ፡ ዘኢይጤየቅ፡ ግዕዛ፡ <hi
                                    resp="rubric">ሚካኤል፡</hi> ሳውዕ፡ አጸን<gap reason="lost"/>
                                    ሄ፡ ሠናይ፡ ፄና፡ መዓዛ፡ <pb n="2v"/> በጺሐከ፡ ግብተ፡
                                ለልብየ፡ አመ፡ ትካዛ፡ ለነፍሰ፡ ዚአየ፡ በት<add place="above">ን</add>ባሌከ፡ ናዝዛ፡
                                እንበለ፡ ጊዜ፡ <sic>ወ</sic>ላህ፡ ኢይርሳዕ፡-->
                                ​ወሬ​ዛ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em"><!-- I would provide only the last stanza in the printed catalogue.-->
<!--                                <hi rend="rubric">ሰላም</hi>፡ ሰላም፡ ለመልክእከ፡ ኵሎን፡ በበአስማቲሆን፡ <hi
                                    rend="rubric">ሚካኤል፡</hi> ስርግው፡ በልብሰ፡ ብርሃን፡ ሠናይ፡ ተአርኮትከ፡ በኵሉ፡
                                ዘመን። ሰራ<sic resp="JK">የ</sic>፡ ኃጢ<supplied reason="omitted" resp="SH">አ</supplied>ት፡
                                አንተ፡ አርከ፡ ነፍሰ፡ ምዕመን<supplied reason="omitted" resp="DR">፡</supplied>-->
                                ​አምኃ ፡ ​ሰላ​ም፡ ​አቅ​ረብ​ኩ፡ ​ለመ​ልክ​ዕከ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​ለለ​፩፩ ​ዘበ​በክ​ፍሉ፡
                                     ​ሚካ​ኤል፡  ​ክቡ​ር፡ ​ለል​ዑል፡ ​መል​አከ፡ ​ኃይ​ሉ፡ ​ተወ​ኪፈ​ከ፡
                                ​አም​ኃየ፡ እ  (fol. 15v)  ​ምኖ​ኃ፡
                                ​ሰማ​ያት፡ ​ዘላ​እሉ፡ ​ዕሤ​ተ፡ ​ጸሎ​ትየ፡ ​ፈኑ፡ ​ወአ​ስብ​የ፡ ​ድሉ፡ ​ለገ​ብር​ከ፡  ​ወል​ደ፡
                                        <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block> Several lines with names of
                                        individuals, who were probably related to the production or ownership of the
                                        manuscript, have been erased on fol. 15v. </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Scribal corrections appear interlineally (e.g. fols 3v, 4r, 4v) or over erasures comprising
                                        several words (e.g. 12r, 13v).</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Writing exercises and crude drawings on fols 1r–1v and fols 15v–16v; scribbles
                                        and doodles in the margins throughout the manuscript;
                                        erased notes in brown ink in the lower margin of fols 9r–11r.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>A white sticker with the name of <fo:inline id="d1e8372PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> printed (<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቤን​ት፡ ​ዩው​ል፡ ​የን​ሰን።</fo:inline>), and the signatures ‘Ms.
                                        Aeth. g. 28’ and ‘Ms. Et 1’ written in pencil is glued onto
                                        the inner side of the front board. Another sticker
                                        with the signature ‘Ms 1’ is glued below it.
                                        The shelfmark, textual content and dating of the book (‘Ethiopian MS 1’, ‘Hymn to Yared’,  ‘Salutation to Mikael’, and  ‘C 20’)
                                        are indicated in pencil in the inner side of the front and back board.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                                      Bound in wooden boards.
                                    
                                
                                      The boards are cut to the same size as the bookblock and have square edges.
                                      The grain runs vertically. The outer sides of the boards have a brown finishing,
                                      while the signs left by the working tool are visible on the inner sides.
                                    
                                      The original sewing was a chainstitch on two sewing stations. It has been repaired with a different type of thread and
                                      in this occasion fol. q3 has been re-sewn on four sewing stations. Nevertheless the sewing
                                      is still in a bad state of conservation.
                                    
                                      The small holes close to the head and tail of the quires are probably what remains of quire tackets.
                                    
                                      A red <fo:inline id="d1e8410">leaf string marker</fo:inline> is attached to the upper outer prick of fol. 8
                                    </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Pencil foliation in the upper right corner (1–16).</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block>3 quires. A<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">0+1 (Fols 1r–1v)</fo:inline> – I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6+1 (Fols 2r–8v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 9r–16v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 2r–15v: 1
                                    column (13 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin
                                        dimensions taken from fol. 9r.The characters per line are 10–12.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            80 × 57 mm (fol. 9r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 4 mm, bottom: 22 mm, right: 8 mm, left: 4 mm (fol. 9r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are barely visible. Horizontal lines are visible at the bottom of fol. 3v and
                                    6r, but most folios seem to have no ruled lines. Primary pricks are visible, ruling pricks are not.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Nineteenth–mid-twentieth century.. Mediocre hand with angular script.<fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: Initial two lines on the incipit page of
                                    <fo:inline font-style="italic">Malkǝʾ</fo:inline>-hymn to St Michael; the first word of each stanza; the name
                                    of St Michael, erased names of individuals related
                                    to the production or ownership of the manuscript; elements of
                                    the punctuation signs, and numerals.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Decoration</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Miniatures</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Headpieces</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(5) Fol. 1r: <fo:inline>The manuscript contains a single interlace band on   fol. 1r. The interlace pattern appears to be coeval with the production of the manuscript
                                    and features eyes in the intersection of the twists comparable to examples found in manuscripts from the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries 
                                   (see Zanotti Eman 1992,  478).</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Drawings</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Other</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
                                      A red <fo:inline id="d1e8410">leaf string marker</fo:inline> is attached to the upper outer prick of fol. 8
                                    <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is deficient.
                                        Smudged ink on many folios, see especially on fols 15r–16v. Insect droppings and humidity stains
                                        on most folios. The original sewing is broken with the risk
                                        of leaf displacement. </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>nineteenth–mid-twentieth century</fo:inline>
                            The earliest date of production—taking into account the handwriting—can
                            be set to the nineteenth, the latest to the mid-twentieth century. Several lines with names of
                            individuals who were probably related to the production or ownership of the
                            manuscript have been erased (see Varia note 1). </fo:block>
            <fo:block>It is not known how
                            and when the manuscript came into the possession of <fo:inline id="d1e8432PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e8437PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethg28">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethg28</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
