            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e13420LIT2361somade#HolyWeek">
               <fo:inline>I-8) Fols 84va–92ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Antiphonary for Lent: Set of antiphons for the days of the Holy Week.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ምል​ጣን፡ ​ዘሠ​ርክ፡ ​ሆሣ​ዕና፡
                                        ​በዕ​ምር​ት፡ ​ዕለ​ት፡ ​በዓ​ልነ፡ ​ንፍ ​ሑ፡ ​ቀር​ነ፡ ​በጽ​ዮን፡
                                    ​ወስ​ብኩ፡ ​በደ​ብረ፡ ​መቅ​ደስ​የ፡ ​እስ​መ፡ ​ይቤ፡ ​ዛቲ፡
                                    ​ዕለ​ት፡ ​በዓ​ለ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ሆሣ​ዕና፡ ​በአ​ርያ​ም፡
                                    ​ቡሩ​ክ፡ ​አን​ተ፡ ​ንጉ​ሠ፡ ​፳ኤል ፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ዕጣ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                    በ ​፪፡ 
                                    ​ወሠ​ርከ​ሰ፡ ​አመ፡ ​ርእ​ሶ፡ ​ይሰ​ቀል፡ ​ካል​ዓ፡ ​ዕለ​ተ፡ ​ኮነ፡
                                    ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ያር​ኢ፡ ​አር​አያ፡ ​ትን​ሣኤ፡ ​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ንሰ​ብሖ፡ ​ወን​ወድ​ሶ፡
                                    ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ትን​ሣኤ ፨ 
                                    ​ተፈ​ጸመ፡ ​ጾመ፡ ​ድጓ፡ ​ሠር​ጐ፡ ​ቤተ፡
                                    ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን ​፨፨​፨፨​፨፨​፨፨​፨፨፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e13456LIT2361somade#PalmSunday">
               <fo:inline>I-8-1) Fols 84va–88ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Antiphonary for Lent: PalmSunday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>I-8-2) Fols 88ra–88va: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e13464">Monday through Wednesday in the Holy Week (?)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">This segment begins with an antiphon labelled
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዋዜ​ማ፡ ​ዘሠ​ኑይ፡</fo:inline> (<fo:inline font-style="italic">Wāzemā za-śanuy</fo:inline>,
                                        ‘<fo:inline font-style="italic">Wāzemā</fo:inline> (antiphon) for Monday’). It is appears that the
                                        segment contains material for Monday through Wednesday of the Holy Week.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e13484LIT2361somade#MaundyThursday">
               <fo:inline>I-8-3) Fols 88va–89ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Antiphonary for Lent: Liturgical instructions and set of antiphons for Maundy Thursday.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e13491LIT2361somade#GoodFriday">
               <fo:inline>I-8-4) Fols 89ra–90vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Antiphonary for Lent: Liturgical instructions and set of antiphons for Good Friday.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e13498LIT2361somade#HolySaturday">
               <fo:inline>I-8-5) Fols 90vb–92ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Antiphonary for Lent: Liturgical instructions and set of antiphons for Holy Saturday.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e13507LIT2361somade#Haleta">
               <fo:inline>I-9) Fols 92ra–93vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Antiphonary for Lent: Table of melodic variations for the Hallelujah (​አን​ቀጸ፡ ​ሃሌ​ታ፡, 
                  ʾAnqaṣa hālletā).</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                                        Omitted word(s) have been added by the hand that furnished the text with <fo:inline>mələkkət</fo:inline>
                                        in the margin (e.g. fols 6r, 7r, 8r) or interlineally (e.g. fols 29ra, 34rb, 41ra).
                                        Different type of deletions: erasures (e.g. fols 17vb, 20rb, 30va), erasures with subsequent addition of line fillers
                                        (e.g. fols 5va, 16rb, 24rb),
                                        expunctuation (fols 29ra), strike-through (fols 32vb, 66va).
                                        On fol. 45rb, a rubricated word has been corrected by writing the correct form in black on top of the rubricated letters.
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Pen trials by different hands with different inks (fols 2r–3v).
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block>10 quires. A<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2 (Fols 2r–3v)</fo:inline> – I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 4r–13v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 14r–23v)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 24r–33v)</fo:inline> – IV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">12 (Fols 34r–45v)</fo:inline> – V<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8+2 (Fols 46r–55v)</fo:inline> – VI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 56r–65v)</fo:inline> – VII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 66r–75v)</fo:inline> – VIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 76r–85v)</fo:inline> – IX<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 86r–93v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 4ra–93vb: 2
                                    columns (21–24 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 24r.There are 12–15 characters per line.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            143 × 98 mm (fol. 24r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            107 × 87 mm (fol. 24r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 12 mm, bottom: 23 mm, right: 6 mm, left: 7 mm, intercolumn: 6 mm (fol. 24r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic">Punctuation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block linefeed-treatment="preserve">
                                        One-column headbands within the textblock separate the weeks (e.g. on fols 19va, 29rb, 40ra).
                                        Chains of red and black dots occasionally separate days (e.g. on fols 17va, 19rb, 29ra)
                                        or services (e.g. on 16ra, 16rb, 16va, 24rb).
                                    </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible. Both primary and ruling pricks are often visible. The upper and bottom lines are written above the ruling.
                                     Ruling pattern (fols 5r, 89r 88r): Several different ruling patterns are attested in the manuscript: 1E!-1E!-1E!1E!/0-0/0-0/C (e.g. ), 1E!-1E!-1E!1E!/0-0/1C-1C/J (e.g. ).</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 4ra–93vb. 1700–1950. 
                                Fine hand. Characters are regularly spaced. The graphemes ግ
                                and ዚ are occasionally written as
                                a ligature, e.g. on fols 20ra, 25ra.
                            <fo:block>Ink: Black and red</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: 
                                Several groups of lines on the incipit page, alternating with black lines;
                                two lines at the beginning of a new week (e.g. fols 19va, 29rb, 40ra, ; on 64r, the rubrication has partly been extended to
                                the column b);
                                metatextual elements pertaining to the categorization of antiphons
                                (antiphon-type designations, melodic-family designations, hallelujah numbers, incipits of antiphons lacking metatextual elements), in part or completely;
                                occasionally, elements of numerals, punctuation signs, and marginal metatextual elements (<fo:inline>bet</fo:inline> designations).
                            </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Decoration</fo:block>
         <fo:block margin-top="3mm" margin-bottom="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Headbands appear to be contemporary with the making of the manuscript and to have been executed by the same hand.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Miniatures</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Headpieces</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(9) Fol. 4r: <fo:inline>Frame with uneven lines filled with a pattern of thin strings knotted by loops at its centre.
                                </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(10) Fols 19va, 29rb, 40ra, 49va, 64ra, 74rb: <fo:inline>Smaller bands, marking incipits, present small variations on the pattern found on fol. 4r.
                                </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Drawings</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Other</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Holes, from the parchment making process, are present in the folios, e.g. fols 77, 83, 84, 92. Others have been repaired by sewing, e.g.
                                    2, 9, 58, 60, 61, 72, 95.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>eighteenth–mid-twentieth century</fo:inline>
                                Unit 1 can be dated palaeographically to the period between the
                                eighteenth and the mid-twentieth century.
                            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm">Unit 2</fo:block>
         <fo:block>Parchment,  fols (), eighteenth–mid-twentieth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 94ra–95rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e13818">Three prayers</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">These prayers form part of the texts that are sometimes catalogued
                                    under the title <fo:inline>“Salutation to you, the second heaven...” (ሰላም፡ ለኪ፡ ዳግሚት፡ ሰማይ፡), CAe 2814</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>I-1) Fols 94ra–94va: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e13832">Prayer to Mary (<fo:inline font-style="italic">Salām laki dāgǝmit samāy…</fo:inline>)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ለኪ፡ ​ዳግ​ሚት፡ ​ሰማ​ይ፡ ​ሰ፡  ​ለኪ ፡ ​ሙፃ​ዓ፡ ​ፀሐ​ይ፡ ​ሰ፡
                                    ​አን​ቀጸ፡ ​መድ​ኃኒ​ት፡ ​ሰ፡ ​ሙዳ​የ፡ ​እፍ​ረት፡ ​ሰ፡ ​ገነተ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                    ​ትፍ​ሥሕ​ት፡ <fo:inline> (!)</fo:inline>​መ፡ እ ​ግዚ ​አብ​ሔር፡
                                    ፀ ባ ​ዖት፡ ​ሰ፡ ​ዘም​ስለ፡ ​ሰጊ​ድ፡ ​ንኤ​ምኃ​ኪ፡ ​ለባ​ርኮ​ትነ፡
                                    ​ስፍ​ሒ፡ ​እዴ​ኪ። ​መን​ግሥ​ተ፡ ​ንጉ​ሥ፡ <fo:inline>[////]</fo:inline> ​ባር​ኪ፡
                                        ​ወኪ​ያነ​ኒ፡ ​እሞ​ተ፡ ​ሙስ​ና፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ሰ፡ ​በከ​መ፡ ​ልማ ድ ​ኪ፡ ​በሊ፡ ​ኀበ፡ ​ወል​ድኪ፡ ​ከሃ​ሊ፡ ​ኦር​ኅሩ​ኅ፡
                                    ​ኢተ​በቃ​ሊ፡ ​ያጠ​ፍኦ​ኑ፡ ​ለስ​ዕል፡ ​ሠዓ​ሊ፡ ​ኪነ​ተከ፡ ​ዘት​ካት፡ ​ሀሊ።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>I-2) Fols 94va–95ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e13875">Prayer to Jesus Christ (<fo:inline>Səbḥat laka nəngər kʷəllo səbḥatika…</fo:inline>)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ለከ፡ ​ንን​ግር፡ ​ኵሎ፡ ​ስብ​ሐቲ​ከ፡ ​በአ​ናቅ​ጺሃ፡ ​ለጽ​ዮን፡ ​ማኅ​ደረ፡ ​ብዙ​ኅ፡ ​ሰላ​ም፡
                                    ​ዘአ​ንቃ​ሕከ​ነ፡ ​እም​ነ፡ ​ንዋ​ም፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ማ<fo:inline>[////]</fo:inline>።
                                    ​ሰ፡ ​ላዕ​ለ፡ ​ጻድ​ቃን፡ ​ወኃ​ጥአ​ን፡ ​ብር​ሃነ፡ ​ጸጋ፡ ​ምው​ቅ፡ ​ዘታ​ሠር​ቅ፡ ​ለነ፡ ​እም​ነ፡ ​ምስ​ራቅ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ፀሐ​የ፡ ​ጽድ​ቅ።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ሰ፡ ​አኰ​ቴተ፡ ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ወት​ረ፡ ​ለመ​ንግ​ሥት​ከ፡ ​ስቡ​ሕ፡ ​ጊዜ፡ ​እም​ንዋ  (fol. 95ra)  ​ምነ፡
                                    ​ንነ​ቅሕ፡ ​ወና​ቄር​ብ፡ ​ለከ፡ ​በቃ​ለ፡ ​ክላ​ህ፡ ​ወን​ፌኑ፡ ​ስብ​ሐተ፡ ​በነ​ግህ።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>I-3) Fols 95ra–95rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e13902">Prayer to the Trinity (<fo:inline>Səbḥat lakəmu səllus qəddus…</fo:inline>)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ዘስ​ላሤ፡ ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ለክ​ሙ፡ ​ስሉ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ማዕ​ምራ​ነ፡ ​ክል​ኤ፡ ​አእ​ምሮ፡ ​ለብ<fo:inline>[ር]</fo:inline>​ሃን፡
                                    ​ዓቢ​ይ፡ ​ዘፈ​ጠሮ፡ ​ቃል​ክሙ፡ ​በተ​ናግ​ሮ። ​ስብ፡ ​ሰዓ​ተ፡ ​ሌሊ​ት፡ ​ስላ​ሤ፡ ​ዘወ​ሰን​ክሙ፡
                                    ​በጎ​ህ፡ ​ወዘአ ክ ​በር​ክሙ፡ ​በጸ​ዳል፡ ​ብሩ​ህ፡ ​ፀሐ​የ፡ ​እም​ነ፡ ​ወር​ኅ።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ስ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ኀብ​ረ፡ ​ሰደ፡ ​ሥጋ​የ፡ ​አመ፡ ​በኃ​ጢአ​ት፡  (b)  ቄ ​ሐ፡ ​ኀዘ​ን፡
                                    ​ብየ፡  ​አም​ጣነ፡  ​በዝ​ሐ፡ ​ሥላ​ሴ፡ ​ዘዮ​ም፡ ​ወዘ​አሜ​ሃ፡ ​በጽ​ባሕ፡ ​ሀቡ​ኒ፡
                                    ​ፍሥሐ ​።።​።።  ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​በል፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                                            Omitted letters and, in one case, a word have been added interlineally (e.g. fols 94ra, 94va, 95rb).
                                            One letter has been marked for deletion by strokes above and under the letter (fol. 95ra).
                                        </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Throughout, there are blank spaces
                                            that were presumably intended to be filled with rubricated letters.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
                                    </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block>1 quire. X<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2 (Fols 94r–95v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 94ra–95rb: 2
                                    columns (20 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on margin dimensions taken from fol. 94r.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 11 mm, bottom: 18 mm, right: 14 mm, left: 5 mm, intercolumn: 4 mm (fol. 94r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 2:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 94ra–95rb. 1700–1950. 
                                        Irregular hand.
                                    <fo:block>Ink: Black and red</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: 
                                        Words within the first line of textual units (<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ለኪ</fo:inline>,
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ማር</fo:inline>) on fols 94r, ; elements of certain
                                        punctuation marks on fol. 95rb.
                                    </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>A hole from the parchment making process has been repaired by sewing on
                                            fol. 95.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>eighteenth–mid-twentieth century</fo:inline>
                                Unit 2 can be dated palaeographically to the eighteenth–mid-twentieth century.
                            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethe37">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethe37</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
