      </fo:static-content>
      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethd18"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. d. 18</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Juel-Jensen 16)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex, composite263×205 mm (weight: 1382g), 59 fols.  Unit 1:  1975. Unit 2:  Twentieth–twenty-first century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
                            The manuscript consists of two codicological units: Unit 1 is a codex with
                            its own binding, while
                            Unit 2 consists of one loose bifolio having a different origin and
                            placed between fol. 2 and
                            fol. 3.
                            Unit 1 was faithfully copied from another manuscript, bound together with the book of Job
                            and coming from <fo:inline id="d1e27411LOC3549Gojjam">Goǧǧām</fo:inline>,
                            belonging to the deacon <fo:inline id="d1e27414PRS12948MalakaMe">
                  <fo:inline font-style="italic">Malʿaka Mǝḥrat</fo:inline> Yāred Gǝrmāye</fo:inline>
                            from <fo:inline id="d1e27419LOC2091Calaqo">Č̣alaqot Śǝllāse</fo:inline>, south of <fo:inline id="d1e27422LOC4545Maqala">Maq̲ala</fo:inline>
                            (<fo:inline id="d1e27424LOC6569Tegray">Tǝgrāy</fo:inline>).
                            According to the colophon and to other information (cp. Juel-Jensen 1994,  189), Unit 1 was commissioned in
                            <fo:inline id="d1e27441LOC4545Maqala">Maq̲ala</fo:inline>
                            by <fo:inline id="d1e27443PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> and his wife
                            <fo:inline id="d1e27445PRS12946MaryamMary">Mary Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> in September 1974, in the house of
                            <fo:inline id="d1e27447PRS12949YohannesA">
                  <fo:inline font-style="italic">ʾAbuna</fo:inline> Yoḥannǝs</fo:inline>, Archbishop of <fo:inline id="d1e27453LOC1310Aksum">ʾAksum</fo:inline>.
                            Unit 1 was copied by the deacon
                            <fo:inline id="d1e27458PRS12944AmhaSe">ʾAmmǝḫā Śǝllāse</fo:inline> in his monastery of <fo:inline id="d1e27461LOC4505Manawe">Manāwe</fo:inline>
                            in <fo:inline id="d1e27464LOC5882Tamben">Tamben</fo:inline>, and was completed in the month of January 1975.
                            It costed 100 Ethiopian birr, and the binding costed 5 birr extra.
                            As far as Unit 2 is concerned, a connection to
                            <fo:inline id="d1e27471LOC3659GurAmb">Gʷǝrāmbā</fo:inline> can be established on the
                            basis of some of the
                            documents contained therein.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e27477PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm">Unit 1</fo:block>
         <fo:block>Parchment263×205 mm, 59 fols (fols 1–59 fols 1r, 1v, 2r, 2v, 59r, 59v), 8 quires, 1975.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e27494LIT1340EnochE">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 3ra–56rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Book of Enoch, CAe 1340.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e27500LIT1340EnochE#Watchers">
               <fo:inline>I-1) Fols 3ra–12vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">(Ethiopic Book of) Enoch: Book of the Watchers</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ክፍ​ል፡ ፩ ​ቃለ፡ ​በረ​ከት፡ ​ዘሄ​ኖክ፡ ​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ባረ​ከ፡
                                        <fo:inline>ኀሩያነ፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                                     ​ወጻ​ድቃ​ነ፡  ​እለ፡ ​ሀለ​ዉ፡ ​ይኩ​ኑ፡ ​በዕ​ለተ፡ ​ምን​ዳቤ፡ ​ለአ​ሰስ​ሎ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​እኩ​ያን፡ ​ወረ​ሲዓ​ን፡ ​ወአ​ውሥ​አ፡
                                    ​እን​ከ፡ ሄ ​ኖክ፡ ​ወይ​ቤ፡ ​ብእ​ሲ፡ ​ጻድ​ቅ፡ ​ዘእ​ምኃ​በ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ አ ​ዕይ​ንቲ​ሁ፡ ​ክሡ​ታት፡ ​ወይ​ሬኢ፡ ​ራእ​የ፡ ​ቅዱ​ሰ፡ ​ዘበ​ሰማ​ያት፡ ​ዘአ​ርአ​ዩኒ፡ ​መላ​እክ​ት፡
                                    ​ወሰ​ማዕ​ኩ፡ ​እም​ኃቤ​ሆሙ፡ ​ኵሎ፡ ወ ​አእ​መር​ኩ፡ ​አነ፡ ​ዘእ​ሬኢ፡ ​ወአ​ኮ፡ ​ለዝ፡ ​ትው​ልድ፡ ​ርኁ​ቃን፡ ​አላ፡ ለ ​ዘይ​መጽ​እ፡ ​ትው​ልድ፡ ​ርኁ​ቃን፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡
                                        <fo:inline>ኀሩያን። (!)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ወሶ​በ፡ ​ርኢ​ኩ፡ ​ባረ​ኩ፡ ​ወበ​ኲሉ፡ ​ጊዜ፡ ​እባ​ርክ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​አ፡
                                        <fo:inline>ሰብሐት፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                                     ​ዘገ​ብረ፡ ​ተአ​ምራ​ተ፡ ​ዓቢ​ያነ፡ ​ወስ​ቡሐ​ነ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ያር​ኢ፡ ​ዕበ​የ፡ ​ግብ​ሩ፡ ​ለመ​ላእ​ክቲ​ሁ፡ ​ወለ​ነፍ​ሳተ፡ ​ሰብ​እ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ይሰ​ብሑ፡ ​ግብ​ሮ። ​ወኲ​ሉ፡ ​ተግ​ባሩ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ይር​አዩ፡ ​ግብ​ረ፡
                                    ​ኃይ​ሉ፡ ​ወይ​ሰብ​ሕዎ፡ ​ለግ​ብረ፡ ​እደ​ዊሁ፡ ​ዓቢ​ይ፡ ​ወይ​ባር​ክዎ፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ለዓ​ለም።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e27532LIT1340EnochE#Parables">
               <fo:inline>I-2) Fols 12vb–27va: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">(Ethiopic Book of) Enoch: Book of the Parables</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ክፍ​ል፡  ​፴፬ ​ራእ​ይ፡ ​ዘር​እየ፡ ​ካል​ዕ፡ ​ራእ​የ፡ ​ጥበ​ብ፡ ​ዘር​እየ፡ ​ሄኖ​ክ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ያሬ​ድ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​መላ​ልኤ​ል፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ቃይ​ናን፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ሄኖ​ስ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ሴት፡ ​ወል​ደ፡
                                   ​አዳ​ም። ​ወዝ​ርእ​ሱ፡ ​ለነ​ገረ፡ ​ጥበ​ብ፡ ​ዘአ​ንሣ​እኩ፡ ​እት​ናገ​ር፡ ​ወእ​ብል፡ ​ለእ​ለ፡ ​የሐ​ድሩ፡ ​ዲበ፡ ​የብ​ስ፡ ​ስም​ዑ፡ ​ቀደ​ምት፡ ​ወር​እዩ፡ ​ደኃ​ርያ​ን፡ ​ነገ​ረ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡
                                   ​ዘእ​ነግ​ር፡ ​ቅድ​መ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ፡ ​መና​ፍስ​ት፡ ​እሉ፡ ​ቀዳ​ሚ፡ ​ይኄ​ይስ፡ ​ብሂ​ል፡ ​ወደ​ኃው​ያን​ሂ፡ ​ኢን​ከል​እ፡ ​ርእ​ሳ፡ ​ለጥ​በብ፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ወም​ስሌ​ከ፡ ​ይከ​ውን፡ ​ማኅ​ደሪ​ሆሙ፡ ​ወም​ስሌ​ከ፡ ​ክፍ​ሎሙ፡ ​ወእ​ምኔ​ከ፡ ​ኢይ​ትሌ​ለዩ፡ ​ለዓ​ለም፡ ​ወለ​ዓለ​መ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፤ ​ወከ​መዝ፡ ​ይከ​ውን፡ ​ኑኃ፡ ​መዋ​ዕል፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​እጓ​ለ፡
                                    ​እመ​ሕያ​ው። ​ወሰ​ላም፡ ​ይከ​ውን፡  ለ ​ጻድ​ቃን፡ ​ወፍ​ኖቱ፡ ​ርቱ​ዕ፡ ​ለጻ​ድቃ​ን፡   (fol. 27va)   ​በስ​መ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ፡ ​መና​ፍስ​ት፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም። ። ።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e27558LIT1340EnochE#Luminaries">
               <fo:inline>I-3) Fols 27va–35vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">(Ethiopic Book of) Enoch: Book of the Luminaries</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ክፍ​ል፡ ​፷ወ፱ ​መጽ​ሐፈ፡ ​ሕይ​ወተ፡ ​ብር​ሃና​ተ፡ ​ሰማ​ይ፡ ​፩፩ ​ዘከ​መ፡  ​ሀለ​ዉ፡ ​በበ​ሕዘ​ቢሆ​ሙ፡ ​፩፩ ​በበ​ሥል​ጣኖ​ሙ፡ ​ወበ​በዘ​መኖ​ሙ፡ ​፩፩
                                        ​በበ​ስሞ​ሙ፡ ​ወሙ​ላዳ​ቲሆ​ሙ፡ ​ወበ​በአ​ውራ​ሂሆ​ሙ፡ ​ዘአ​ርአ​የኒ፡  ​ኡር​ኤል፡  ​መል​አክ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ዘሀ​ሎ፡ ​ምስ​ሌየ፡ ​ዘው​እቱ፡
                                        ​መራ​ሂሆ​ሙ፡ ​ወኲ​ሎ፡ ​መጽ​ሐፎ​ሙ፡ ​በከ​መ፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​አር​አየ​ኒ።
                                    </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        
                                        ​ወእ​ሉ፡ ​እሙ​ንቱ፡ ​ስሞ​ሙ፡ ​ወሥ​ርዓ​ቲሆ​ሙ፡ ​ወመ​ራኅ​ያኒ​ሆሙ፡ ​እለ፡ ​መት​ሕቲ​ሆሙ፡ ​ለእ​ሉ፡ ​ጊዳ​ኤያ​ል፡ ​ወሲ​ኤል፡ ​ወሂ​ኤል፡ ​ወስ​ሙ፡ ​ለዘ​ይት​ዌሰ​ክ፡
                                        ​ምስ​ሌሆ​ሙ፡ ​ርእ​ሰ፡ ​፲፻ ​አስ​ፋኤ​ል፤ ​ወተ​ፈጸ​መ፡ ​መዋ​ዕለ፡ ​ሥል​ጣነ፡ ​ዚአ​ሆሙ ።
                                    </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e27582LIT1340EnochE#DreamVisions">
               <fo:inline>I-4) Fols 35vb–45rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">(Ethiopic Book of) Enoch: Book of the Dream Visions</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ክፍ​ል፡  ፹ ​ወይ​እዜ​ኒ፡ ​አር​እየ፡ ​ወል​ድየ፡ ​ማቱ​ሳላ፡ ​ኵሎ፡ ​ራእ​ያተ፡ ​ዘር​ኢኩ፡ ​ወበ​ቅድ​ሜከ፡ ​እነ​ግር፡ ፪ ​ራእ​ያተ፡ ​ርኢ​ኩ፡ ​እን​በለ፡ ​እን​ሣእ፡ ​ብእ​ሲተ፡ ​ወ፩​ሂ፡ ​እም​ኔሆ​ሙ፡ ​ኢይ​ትማ​ሰል፡
                                    ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ካል​ኡ፡ ​ቀዳ​ማየ፡ ​አመ፡ ​እት​መሐ​ር፡   (fol. 36ra)   ​መጽ​ሐፈ፡ ​ወካ​ልአ፡ ​ዘእ​ንበ​ለ፡ ​እነ​ሥኣ፡ ​ለእ​ምከ፡ ​እድ​ና። ​ርኢ​ኩ፡ ​ራእ​የ፡ ​ጽኑ​ዐ፡ ​ወበ​እን​ቲአ​ሆሙ፡ ​አስ​ተብ​ቋዕ​ክዎ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​እ፡ ​ስኩ​በ፡
                                    ​ኮን​ኩ፡ ​በቤ​ተ፡ ​መላ​ልኤ​ል፡ ​እም​ሔው​የ፡ ​ርኢ​ኩ፡ ​በራ​እይ።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ወእ​ምኔ​ሁ፡ ​በከ​ይኩ፡ ​ብካ​የ፡  ​ዓቢ​የ፡ ​ወአ​ንብ​ዕየ፡ ​ኢቆ​መ፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ኢክ​ህል​ኩ፡
                                        <fo:inline>ተአግሦተ፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                                    ​ሶበ፡ ​እሬ​ኢ፡ ​ይወ​ርዱ፡ ​ዲበ፡ ​ዝኩ፡ ​ዘር​ኢኩ፡ ​እስ​መ፡ ​ኲሉ፡ ​ይመ​ጽእ፡ ​ወይ​ትፌ​ጸም። ​ወኲ​ሉ፡ ​በበ​ክፍ​ሉ፡ ​ምግ​ባረ፡ ​ሰብ​እ፡ ​ተር​እየ፡ ​ሊተ፤ ​ወበ​ይእ​ቲ፡
                                    ​ሌሊ​ት፡ ​ተዘ​ከር​ክዎ፡ ​ለሕ​ልም​የ፡ ​ቀዳ​ማዊ። ​ወበ​እን​ቲአ​ሁ፡ ​በከ​ይኩ፡ ​ወተ​ሀወ​ኩ፡ ​እስ​መ፡ ​ርኢ​ኩ፡ ​ውእ​ተ፡ ​ራእ​የ።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e27607LIT1340EnochE#Epistle">
               <fo:inline>I-5) Fols 45rb–56rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">(Ethiopic Book of) Enoch: Book of the Epistle</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ክፍ​ል፡  ፺ ​ወይ​እዜ​ኒ፡ ​ወል​ድየ፡ ​ማቱ​ሳላ፡ ​ጸው​እ፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​ኲሎ፡ ​አኃ​ዊከ፡ ​ወአ  (fol. 45va)  ​ስተ​ጋብ​እ፡ ​ዘን​ተ፡ ​ኲሎ፡
                                    ​ደቂ​ቀ፡ ​እም​ከ፡ ​እስ​መ፡ ​ቃል፡ ​ይጼ​ውአ​ኒ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ሰ፡
                                    ​ተክ​ዕወ፡ ​ዲቤ​የ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​አር​ኢክ​ሙ፡ ​ኲሎ፡ ​ወይ​በጽ​ሐክ​ሙ፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ለዓ​ለም። ​ወእ​ምኔ​ሁ፡ ​ሖረ፡ ​ማቱ​ሳላ፡ ​ወጸ​ውዖ​ሙ፡ ​ለኲ​ሎሙ፡ ​አኃ​ዊሁ፡ ​ኀቤ​ሁ፡
                                    ​ወአ​ስተ​ጋብ​ኦሙ፡ ​ለአ​ዝማ​ደ፡ ​ዚአ​ሁ። ​ወተና<fo:inline>[ገ]</fo:inline>​ሮሙ፡ ​ለኲ​ሎሙ፡ ​ውሉ​ዱ፡ ​ጽድ​ቀ።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ወይ​ትወ​ሀው​ሁ፡ ​በአ​ዝማ​ን፡ ​ዘአ​ልቦ፡ ​ኊል​ቊ። ​እስ​መ፡ ​ጽድ​ቅ፡ ​ኲነ​ኔሁ፡ ​ለአ​ምላ​ክ። ​እስ​መ፡ ​ለመ​ሃይ​ምና​ን፡ ​ይሁ​ብ፡ ​ሃይ​ማኖ​ተ። ​በማ​ኅደ​ረ፡ ​ፍና​ዋት፡ ​ርቱ​ዓት፡ ​ወይ​ሬእ​ይዎ​ሙ።
                                    ​ለእ​ለ፡ ​ተወ​ልዱ፡ ​በጽ​ልመ​ት፡ ​ይት​ወደ​ዩ፡ ​በጽ​ልመ​ት፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ይት​ወሐ​ውሁ፡ ​ጻድ​ቃን፡ ​ወይ​ጸር​ሑ፡ ​ወይ​ሬእ​ይዎ​ሙ፡ ​ኃጥ​አን፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ይበ​ርሁ፡ ​ወየ​ሐው​ሩ፡ ​እሙ​ንቱ​ሂ፡ ​በኀ​በ፡
                                    ​ተጽ​ሕፈ፡ ​ሎሙ፡ ​መዋ​ዕል፡ ​ወአ​ዝማ​ን። ​ተፈ​ጸመ፡ ​መጽ​ሐፈ፡ ​ሄኖ​ክ፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e27634NAR0101Moon">
               <fo:inline>II) Fols 56va–58rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">, CAe 0101.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Astronomical tables have been drawn in black and red ink on fols 56v, 57r: each folio accommodates three columns in red ink filled
                                    with astronomical terms and digits which indicate the <fo:inline font-style="italic">kekros</fo:inline>.
                                    Areas between columns host drawing of the lunar phases. Text on 56v is written upside down.
                                    A table showing the lunar phases, perhaps incomplete, is also drawn on 56rb.
                                </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ሠረ​ቀ፡ ​ሚያ​ዝያ፡  ​በኆ​ህት፡ ​ራብ​ዕ፡ ​፪። ​በኃ​ምስ፡ ​ኅህ​ት፡ ​፰። ​በሳ​ድስ፡ ​ኆኅ​ት፡ ​፰። ​በኃ​ምስ፡ ​ኆኅ​ት፡ ​፩። ​በራ​ብዕ፡ ​ኆኅ​ት፡ ​፩፡ ​በሣ​ልስ፡ ​ኆኅ​ት፡ ​፪።
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Colophon</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block font-family="Ludolfus">Fol. 58va: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">The colophon states that the manuscript was commissioned by <fo:inline id="d1e27685PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> and his wife <fo:inline id="d1e27687PRS12946MaryamMary">Mary Juel-Jensen</fo:inline>.
                                It was completed on the 25th Tāḫśāś of the year of mercy 1967 EC, corresponding to the 18th January 1975.
                                The scribe was the deacon <fo:inline id="d1e27692PRS12944AmhaSe">ʾAmmǝḫā Śǝllāse</fo:inline> from the monastery of <fo:inline id="d1e27695LOC4505Manawe">Manāwe</fo:inline>
                                in <fo:inline id="d1e27699LOC5882Tamben">Tamben</fo:inline>.
                            </fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline>1975</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                        <fo:block font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዝን​ቱ፡ ​መጽ​ሐፍ፡ ​ዘአ​ጽሐ​ፎ፡ ​ዶክ​ተር፡ <fo:inline id="d1e27666PRS5782JuelJen">​ቤን​ት፡ ​ኢ፡ ​የው​ል፡ ​የን​ሰን፡</fo:inline>
                            ​ወም​ስለ፡ ​ብእ​ሲቱ፡ ​ወይ​ዘሮ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e27670PRS12946MaryamMary">​ማር​ያም፡ ​ሜሪ፡</fo:inline>
                            ​ዝመ​ጽሐ​ፍ፡ ​ተፈ​ጸመ፡ ​በወ​ርኃ፡ ​ታህ​ሣሥ፡ ​በ፳​ወ፭ ​መዓ​ልት፡  ​በ፲​ወ፱​፻፷​ወ፯ ​ዓመ​ተ፡ ​ምሕ​ረት፡  ​ወጸ​ሐፊ​ሁ፡ ​ዲያ​ቆን፡
                            <fo:inline id="d1e27677PRS21944AmhaSe">​አም​ኃ፡ ​ሥላ​ሴ፡</fo:inline> ​ገ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​ዘብ​ሔረ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e27680LOC4505Manawe">​ተም​ቤን፡ ​መነ​ዌ፡ ​ገዳ​ም።</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>The codicological unit contains no scribal corrections.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Chapter numbering is erroneously given from 12 onwards.
                                        Chapters 11, 27, 32, 46 are not numbered.
                                        Numbering of chapter 68 (which corresponds to ch. 71) is omitted.
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>A white sticker is glued on fol. 1r. The name of <fo:inline id="d1e27981PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> is printed on it
                                        (‘<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቤን​ት፡ ​ዩው​ል፡ ​የን​ሰን።</fo:inline>’) and the signature ‘MS. Aeth. d. 18’ is written in pencil.
                                        An additional sticker, with the signature ‘Ms 16’ on it, is glued below it.  The textual content
                                        of the book in Gǝʿǝz and in English (‘<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ኄኖክ</fo:inline>’, ‘The book of Henok’) is indicated in pencil in small script
                                        on 1r.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                                    The book is bound in wooden boards covered with orange blind-tooled leather. The front and back board are decorated with  inlays.
                                
                                    The boards are cut to the same size as the bookblock and present square edges.
                                
                                    Full orange leather cover.
                                    The turn-ins have been trimmed out and at the corners they form butt mitres. An <fo:inline id="d1e28015">additional leather patch</fo:inline>
                                    has been added along the inner margin of the boards to fill the gap between the turn-ins.
                                    The front and back covers and the turn-ins are decorated with blind-tooled ornaments.
                                    The cover sides present a design consisting of three concentric rectangular frames
                                    surrounding a central panel featuring a Latin cross. The frames are composed by the repetition of single tools
                                    enclosed between <fo:inline id="d1e28018">single straight lines</fo:inline> arranged in groups of three. The frame between the
                                    decorated ones is left blank.
                                    The outer frame presents <fo:inline id="d1e28021">criss-cross</fo:inline> motifs and the inner one <fo:inline id="d1e28024">curve strapwork</fo:inline> elements.
                                    The cross is formed by bands of <fo:inline id="d1e28027">X-form</fo:inline> motifs between single straight lines.
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e28031">Corniform</fo:inline> motifs and three <fo:inline id="d1e28034">double circles</fo:inline> decorate the
                                    ends of the arms of the cross.
                                    In the blank areas, the straight lines form cross- and square-shaped patterns decorated with <fo:inline id="d1e28037">double circles</fo:inline>
                                    at the intersections.
                                    The two square patterns flanking the foot of the cross are surmounted by a triangular shape each.
                                
                                  <fo:inline id="d1e28043">Slit-braid</fo:inline> orange endbands are present.
                                
                                    Chainstitch sewing on four sewing stations (two pairs) carried out with two tightly Z-plied threads, starting from
                                    the centre of the first quire. Their ends are knotted in the centrefold of the last quire.
                                
                                    Two lines of running stitches close to head and tail, are visible on the back cover. They are part of the attachment system
                                    of the endbands.
                                    The spine covering extends slightly beyond the endbands forming two caps.
                                </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Pencil foliation in the upper right corner (1–59).</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm">
                                        Decorated quire marks are written in the upper margin of the first folio of each quire.
                                    </fo:block>
         <fo:block>8 quires. A<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2 (Fols 1r–2v)</fo:inline> – I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 3r–10v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 11r–18v)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 19r–26v)</fo:inline> – IV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6+2 (Fols 27r–34v)</fo:inline> – V<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 35r–42v)</fo:inline> – VI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 43r–50v)</fo:inline> – VII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6+3 (Fols 51r–59v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 3ra–58va: 2
                                    columns (26 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 35r. The characters per line are 12–14.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            257 × 203 mm (fol. 35r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            189 × 162 mm (fol. 35r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 25 mm, bottom: 44 mm, left: 14 mm, right: 26 mm, intercolumn: 11 mm (fol. 35r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible. Both primary and ruling pricks are visible.  The upper and the bottom lines are written above the ruling. Ruling pattern: 1A-1A-1A1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->1975 (scribe: ʾAmmǝḫā Śǝllāse) . 
                                    Fine handwriting.
                                    ʾAmmǝḫā Śǝllāse is indicated as the scribe in the colophon (fol. 58va).
                                <fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: 
                                    Several groups of lines on the incipit page, alternating with black lines;
                                    first two lines of the Book of the
                                        Luminaries; incipit of each monthly section of the Book of the Parables;
                                    holy names; name of the individuals mentioned in the colophon; the word <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ክፍ​ል፡</fo:inline>;
                                   elements of the punctuation signs, text dividers, and numerals, included quire marks.
                                </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Decoration</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Miniatures</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Headpieces</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(11) Fols 3r, 56r: <fo:inline>The start and end of the manuscript on  fol. 3r and  fol. 56r are marked by two horizontal bands filled 
                                    with polychrome interlace placed respectively at the top and, 
                                    more unusually, bottom of the page. These were probably executed at the time the manuscript was commissioned by its former owner.</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Drawings</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Other</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Tears repaired on fols 1, 16, 43, 53.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is good.
                                The manuscript appears to have hardly been used and displays only slight deformation of the parchment.
                                </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Bibliography</fo:block>Juel-Jensen 1992; Juel-Jensen 1994.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm">Unit 2</fo:block>
         <fo:block>Parchment, 2 fols (fols i–ii fol. ivv), 1 quires, Twentieth–twenty-first century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols ir–iir: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e28118">Land records and various documents</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">
                                    The documents are written in Amharic, with some formulas in Gǝʿǝz.
                                    Some documents (Land records 1–4) mention <fo:inline id="d1e28125LOC3659GurAmb">Gʷǝrāmbā</fo:inline>.
                                    Several local individuals holding various honorific titles are mentioned, in particular <fo:inline font-style="italic">malʾaka ṣahay</fo:inline>,
                                    <fo:inline font-style="italic">liqa ṭabbabt</fo:inline>, <fo:inline font-style="italic">bālāmbā rās</fo:inline>, etc.
                                    Single texts are divided with black lines.
                                </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>I-1) Fol. ir: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e28142">Documentary text 1</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">
                                    ​ከች፡ የ<fo:inline font-style="italic">​መል​አከ፡</fo:inline> ​ፀሐ​ይ፡ ​ሣህ​ሉ፡ ​፩ጋ​ሽ፡ ​የች​ዋይ፡ ​፩ም፡ ​ባድ​ማው፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ወይ​መከ​ይ፤
                                    ​፩ም፡ ​የሰ​ጊ፡ ​የዶ​ንቾ፡ ​ባድ​ማ፤ ​፩ም፡ ​ሰር​ዳሆ፡ ​ያያ​ን፡ ​ባፍ​ማ፤
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>I-2) Fol. ir: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e28155">Documentary text 2</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">
                                        ​ከች፡ የ<fo:inline font-style="italic">​ባለ​አም​ባ፡ ​ራስ፡</fo:inline> ​ረም​ሃ፡ ​የጋ​ሽ፡ ​እኩ፡ ​ያባ​ይ፡ ​ባድ​ማው፤ ​፩ም፡ ​ማተ​ቦጊ፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ቀይ፡ ​አፈ​ር፤
                                        ​፩ም፡ ​ኵር​ቢላ​ሃ፡ ​፩ም፡ ​አም​ባው፡ ​የጨ​ጓር፡ ​ባድ​ማ፡ ​፪ም፡ ​ዘን​ተይ​ጌ፡ ​፩ም፡ ​ስን​ኰር​ኵራ፡ ​፩ም፡ ​ደኪ፡ ​አር​ዋ፡ ​፩ም፡ ​ሰሎ​ግ፡ ​፩ም፡ ​ኳር​ዌና፡
                                    </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>I-3) Fol. ir: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e28169">Documentary text 3</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">
                                        የ<fo:inline font-style="italic">​ብላ​ቴን፡ ​ጌታ፡</fo:inline> ​ለታ፡ ​፩ጋ፡ ​ደዝ​ቢሆ​ን፡ ​፩ም፡ ​ፉራ፡ ​ወል​ዱ፡ ​አስ​ከ፡ ​፩ም፡ ​ስጉ​ደ፡ ​የከ​ቴ፡ ​አስ​ከ፡ ​፩ም፡ ​ላይ፡
                                        ​ፉራ፡ ​የከ​ብቴ፡ ​አስ​ከ፡ ​፩ም፡
                                    </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>I-4) Fol. ir: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e28182">Documentary text 4</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">
                                        በ<fo:inline font-style="italic">​መል​አከ፡ ​ፀሐ​ይ፡</fo:inline> ​ሣህ​ሉና፡ በ<fo:inline font-style="italic">​ሊቀ፡ ​ጠበ​ብት፡</fo:inline> ​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ሥሉ​ስ፡
                                        ​ሹመ​ት፡ የ<fo:inline font-style="italic">​ወይ​ዘሮ፡</fo:inline>
                                        ​ሣህ​ሉ፡ ​ልጅ፡ ​ሰይ​ፈ፡ ​ሩፋ​ኤል፡ ​በ፲፪ ​ወቄ​ት፡ ​ወር​ቅ፡ ​የቍ​ስቋ​ምን፡ ​አሪ​ም፡ ​ከይ​ብተ​ሮች፡
                                    </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>I-5) Fol. ir: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e28201">Documentary text 5</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">
                                        በ<fo:inline font-style="italic">​መል​አከ፡ ​ፀሐ​ይ፡</fo:inline> ​ሣህ​ሉና፡ በ<fo:inline font-style="italic">​ሊቀ፡ ​ጠበ​ብት፡</fo:inline> ​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ሥሉ​ስ፡
                                        ​ሹመ​ት፡ ​ጻፊ፡ ​ፈን​ታ፡ ​በላ​ስ፡ ​፩ም፡ ​እም​ቡሪ​ፍ፡ ፪ ​ጭየ፡ ​የቄ​ስ፡ ​አደ​ነት፡ ​በወ​ቄት፡ ​ወር​ቅ፡
                                    </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>I-6) Fol. iv: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e28217">Land record 1</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">
                                        ​የሊ​ቄ፡ ​ኃይ​ሉ፡ ​ሪም፡ ​በይ​ዴም። በ<fo:inline id="d1e28221LOC3659GurAmb">​ጕራ​ምባ፡</fo:inline> ፪ ​ምድ​ር፡ ​ከጸ​ባሕ​ተ፡ ​ወል​ድ፡
                                        ከ<fo:inline font-style="italic">​ባል​አም​በራ​ስ፡</fo:inline> ​ረም​ኃ፡ ​ምድ​ር፡ ​በጸ​ገብ​ና፡ ​ከብ​ርጭ​ቆ፡ ​ደጅ፡ ​፩ም፡ ​ባድ​ማ፤ ​፩ም፡ ​ከማ​ሪቺ​ን፡
                                    </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>I-7) Fol. iv: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e28233">Land record 2</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">
                                        በ<fo:inline id="d1e28237LOC3659GurAmb">​ጕራ​ምባ፡</fo:inline> ​የጽ​ራግ፡ ​ማሰ​ሬ፡ ​ዜና፡ ​ዘጸ​ረመ​ኒ። ​ሪም፡ ​ከመ​ርቆ​ረዎ​ስ፡ ​ያ፬​ጬን፡ ​ምደ​ር።
                                        ፩ ​ምድ​ር፡ ​ያባ፡ ​ጌት​የ። ፪ ​ምድ​ር፡ ​ዋል​ዋል​ታ። ​የሙ​ዙ። ፩ ​ምድ​ር፡ ​አኽ​ያ፡
                                    </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>I-8) Fol. iv: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e28246">Land record 3</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">
                                        በ<fo:inline id="d1e28250LOC3659GurAmb">​ጕራ​ምባ፡</fo:inline> ​የወ​ልደ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ቀጸ​ለ፡ ​ሪም። ​በ፫​ጨን፡ ​ምድ​ር፡ ​ተሰ​ርተ​ውበ​ታል፡
                                    </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>I-9) Fol. iir: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e28260">Land record 4</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">
                                        ​በዘ​መነ፡ <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ዮሐን ​ስ፡  ​በሐ​ምሌ፡  በ<fo:inline font-style="italic">​መል​አከ፡
                                            ​ፀሐ​ይ፡</fo:inline> ​ሣህ​ሉ፡ ​አለ​ቅነ​ት፡
                                        በ<fo:inline font-style="italic">​ሊቀ፡ ​ጠበ​ብት፡</fo:inline> ​እን​ግዳ፡ ​ሹመ​ት፡ ከ<fo:inline id="d1e28277LOC3659GurAmb">​ጕራ​ምባ።</fo:inline> ​፲፫​ቱን፡
                                        ​ጫን፡ ​የዘ​ይቱ​ን፡ ​ሰቤ​ተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​ይሁ​ን፡ ​ብለ​ው፡ ​ተገ​ዝተ​ው፡ ​ሰጥ​ቶ፡ ​አሉ፡ ​መል​አከ፡ ​ፀሐ​ይ፡
                                        ​ሣህ​ሉ፡ ​ሊቀ፡ ​ጠበ​ብት፡ ​እን​ግዳ፡ ​አለ​ቀ፡ ​አስ​ቡ፡ ​ግራ​ጌታ፡ ​ሰሎ​ሞን፡
                                    </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The bifolio is not foliated. Its folios are referred to in this description as fols i–ii.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block>1 quire. VIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2 (Fols ir–iiv)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>1
                                    column (36 written lines)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 2:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols ir–iir. Twentieth–twenty-first century.. Uneven and untrained handwriting, possibly executed by several hands.
                                    <fo:block>Ink: Black.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is good.
                                      A portion of the lower margin of fol. ii is cut out.
                                    </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>Twentieth–twenty-first century</fo:inline>
                                Unit 2 can be dated palaeographically to the period between the
                                twentieth and the twenty-first century.
                                <fo:inline id="d1e28370">Some of the documents contained display a certain connection to <fo:inline id="d1e28372LOC3659GurAmb">Gʷǝrāmbā</fo:inline>.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethd18">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethd18</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
