      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethf29"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. f. 29</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Juel-Jensen 19)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex165×99 mm (weight: 570g), 123 fols (5 p. blank), 14 quires, 1841–1861.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e33057LIT2296Sayfas">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 4r–80r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Sword of the Trinity’ (​ሰይ​ፈ፡ ​ሥላ​ሴ፡), CAe 2296.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e33063LIT2296Sayfas#Introduction">
               <fo:inline>I-1) Fols 4r–15r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Sword of the Trinity: Introduction</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                     (fol. 4r) 
                                    ​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ ​ስ፡ ​፩አ​ምላ​ክ፡ ​በቅ​ድስ​ት፡
                                    ​ሥላ​ሴ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡  ​አአ​ምን፡ ​ወእ​ትመ​ሐፀ​ን፡ ​እክ​ህደ​ከ፡ ​ሰይ ​ጣን፡
                                    ​በቅ​ድመ፡ ​ዛቲ፡ ​እም​የ፡ ​ቅድ​ስት፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​እን ​ተ፡ ​ይእ​ቲ፡
                                        ​ስም​ዕየ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡ ​ጽዮ​ን፡ ​ለዓ ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም። ​ተማ​ኅፀ​ንኩ፡ ​ብክ​ሙ፡ አ  (fol. 4v)  ​ነ፡ ​ገብ​ርክ​ሙ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e33083PRS13017GabraMar">{​ገብ​ረ፡}
                                        ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ተማ​ኅፀ​ንኩ፡ ​በሥ​ጋሁ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ወበ​ደሙ፡ ​ክቡ​ር፡ ​በዘ  (fol. 15r)  ​ወሀ​ቦ፡ ​ለሰ​ብእ፡ ​መድ​ኃኒ​ተ፡ ​አው​ገዝ​ኩ፡ ​ወኃ​ተም​ኩ፡ ​እለ፡ ​ይገ​ብሩ፡ ​ሥራ​የ፡
                                    ​ወኃ​ይለ፡ ​ጸላ​ዒ፡ ​ወእ​ምሰ​ብእ፡ ​እም​ማኤ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ኢይ​ቅረ​ቡ፡ ​ኀቤ​የ፡ ​ወኀ​በ፡ ​ቤት​የ፡ ​ወሰ​ብእ​የ፡
                                    ​ወእ​ንስ​ሳየ፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​ለገ​ብር​ከ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e33101PRS13017GabraMar">{​ገብ​ረ፡}
                                        ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline> ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን።
                                    ​ወለ​ጸሐ​ፊሁ፡  ​ገብ​ረ፡ <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>፡ 
                                     ​ማር​ያም
                                    ​።ዘ​ነብ።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e33131LIT2296Sayfas#Monday">
               <fo:inline>I-2) Fols 15v–26v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Sword of the Trinity: Praise for Monday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                 (fol. 15v) 
                                ​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ እ ​ነቅ​ሕ፡ ​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡
                                ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ። ​እት​ነሣ​እ፡ ​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡
                                 ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​አአ​ትብ፡ ​ገጽ​የ፡ ​በት​እም​ርተ፡ ​መስ​ቀል፡ </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​በከ​መ፡ ​ባረ​ከ፡ ​ያዕ​ቆብ​ሃ፡ ​ወደ​ቂቆ፡ ​ለከ፡ ​ስብሐ  (fol. 26v)  ​ት፡ ​ወአ​ኰቴ​ት፡ ​ወኃ​ይል፡ ​ወመ​ንግ​ሥት፡ ​ለአ​ብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ይእ​ዜኒ፡
                                ​ወዘ​ልፈ​ኒ፡ ​ወለ​ዓለ​መ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን። ​ዕቀ​ቡኒ፡ ​ለገ​ብር​ክሙ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e33152PRS13017GabraMar">{​ገብ​ረ፡}
                                    ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e33170LIT2296Sayfas#Tuesday">
               <fo:inline>I-3) Fols 27r–35v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Sword of the Trinity: Praise for Tuesday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                 (fol. 27r) 
                                ​አአ​ትብ፡ ​ገጽ​የ፡ ​በመ​ለኮ​ተ፡ ​ሥሉ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​አአት ​ብ፡ ​ፍጽ​ምየ፡
                                ​በመ​ለኮ​ተ፡ ​ሥሉ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​አኃ ​ትም፡ ​ከዋ​ላየ፡ ​በመ​ለኮ​ተ፡ ​ሥሉ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡
                                    ​አኃ ​ትም፡ ​የማ​ንየ፡ ​በመ​ለኮ​ተ፡ ​ሥሉ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​አኃ​ትም፡ ​ፀጋ​ምየ፡ ​በመ​ለኮ​ተ፡ ​ሥሉ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ ​ስ፡
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ወኢ​ለዜ​ንዎ፡ ​ዕመ​ቀ፡ ​ህላ​ዌሆ​ሙ፡ ​ብሑ​ታነ፡ ​ሕሉ​ና፡ ​ዘእ​ንበ​ለ፡ ​ጥን​ት፡
                                    በ ​ሥላሴ ​ሆሙ፡ ​እን​በለ፡ ​ፍል​ጠት፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡
                                    <fo:inline>ሀ (!)</fo:inline>​ላው​ያን፡ ​ዘእ​ንበ​ለ፡ ​ጥን​ት፡ ​ወኢ​ተፍ​ጻሜ​ት፡ በ ​ሥላሴ ​ሆሙ፡ ​ዘእ​ንበ​ለ፡ ​ፍል​የት፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓ፡ ​አ፡ ​ወአ፡ ​ለይ​ኵ፡ ​ለይ። ​በዝ​ቃል​ክሙ፡ ​ዕቀ​ቡኒ፡
                                ​እመ​ከራ፡ ​ሥጋ፡ ​ወነ​ፍስ፡ ​ለገ​ብር​ክሙ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e33200PRS13017GabraMar">{​ገብ​ረ፡}
                                    ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e33219LIT2296Sayfas#Wednesday">
               <fo:inline>I-4) Fols 36r–45r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Sword of the Trinity: Praise for Wednesday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                 (fol. 36r) 
                                ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ኅቡ​ራነ፡ ​ህላ ​ዌ፡ ​በ፩​መን​በር። ​ህላ​ዌ፡
                                ​አብ፡ ​ኢይ​ትሌ​ለይ፡ ​እም​ህላ​ዌ፡ ​ወል​ድ፡ ​ወመን ​ፈስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ። ​ህላ​ዌ፡ ​ወል​ድ፡
                                    ​ኢይ​ትፈ​ለጥ፡ እ ​ምህ​ላዌ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ። </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ግዕ​ዘ፡ ​መን​ፈስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​፩ም​ስለ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወም​ስለ፡ ​ወል​ድ። ​በዝ​ንቱ፡  ​ሥላ​ሴ፡  ​ኅቡ​ር፡ ​ተማ​ኅፀ​ንኩ፡ ​ወአ​ማኅ​ፀን​ኩ፡ ​ነፍ​ስየ፡ ​ወሥ​ጋየ፡ ​ከመ፡
                                ​ይም​ሐረ​ኒ፡ ​ወይ​ሣሃ​ለኒ፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡  ​ሥላሴ ​ሁ፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​ገብ​ሩ፡
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e33244PRS13017GabraMar">{​ገብ​ረ፡}
                                    ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline> ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን፡ ​ወአ​ሜን፡
                                ​ለይ፡ ​ለ። </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e33262LIT2296Sayfas#Thursday">
               <fo:inline>I-5) Fols 45v–55r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Sword of the Trinity: Praise for Thursday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                 (fol. 45v) 
                                ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​በግ​ፃዌ፡ ​ሥሉ​ስ፡  ​በሥ​ላሴ፡ ​ግጽ​ው፡
                                ​ዋህ​ድ፡ ​አም​ላክ፡ ​፫አ​ዕማ​ደ፡  ​ብር​ሃን፡ ​፩አ​ምጣ​ኖሙ፡ ​ወ፩​ስኖ​ሙ፡
                                ​፫መ​ባርቅ ​ት፡ </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​በዝ​ንቱ፡ ​ስመ፡  ​ሥላ​ሴ፡  ​ተማ​ኅፀ​ንኩ፡
                                ​ከመ፡ ​ይክ​ፍለ​ኒ፡  ​ሥላ​ሴ፡  ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​እም​ተስ​ፋ፡ ​ቅዱ​ሳን፡ ​እን​ተ፡ ​ይእ​ቲ፡
                                ​ደብ​ተራ፡ ​ጽድ​ቅ፡ ​ጽዮ​ን፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​ገብ​ርከ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e33287PRS13017GabraMar">{​ገብ​ረ፡}
                                    ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e33305LIT2296Sayfas#Friday">
               <fo:inline>I-6) Fols 55v–66r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Sword of the Trinity: Praise for Friday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                 (fol. 55v) 
                                ​ዓይ፡ ​ልሳ​ን፡ ​ወዓ​ይ፡ ​ከና​ፍር፡ ​ዘይ​ክል፡ ​ነቢ​በ፡  ​ዕበ​የ፡ ​ክብ​ሩ፡
                                ​ለሥ​ላሴ፡ ​ዓይ፡ ​ልቡ​ና፡ ​ወዓ​ይ፡ ​ሰሚ​ዕ፡ ​ዘይ​ክል፡ ​አእም ​ሮ፡ ​ህላ​ዌሆ​ሙ፡
                                    ​ለሥ​ላሴ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                     <fo:inline>ስብሐ፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                                ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​ሰብ​እ፡ ​ወመ​ላእ​ክት፡   (fol. 66r)   ​ኢየ​አም​ርዎ፡ ​ለም​ክሩ፡ ​ወለ​ምሥ​ጢሩ። ​ለዓ​ለመ፡
                                ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን። ​ወአ​ሜን፡ ​ለይ​ኵን፡ ​ለይ​ኩን። ​ዕቀ​በኒ፡ ​ወአ​ድኅ​ነኒ፡ ​እመ​ከራ፡ ​ሥጋ፡ ​ወነ​ፍስ፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​ለገ​ብር​ከ፡
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e33327PRS13017GabraMar">{​ገብ​ረ፡}
                                    ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>​ወለ​ጸሐ​ፊሁ፡  ​ገብ​ረ፡ <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>
                                 ​ማር​ያም
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e33354LIT2296Sayfas#Saturday">
               <fo:inline>I-7) Fols 66v–73v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Sword of the Trinity: Praise for Saturday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                 (fol. 66v) 
                                ​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ለፍ​ቅረ፡ ​መለ​ኮት፡ ​በት​ስብ​እቱ፡ ​ዘጸ​መ።  ​እን​በይ​ነ፡ ​ዚአ​ነ፡
                                ​አር​አያ​ሁ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​የሀ​በነ።  ሰ ​ላም፡ ​ለፍ ​ቅረ፡
                                    ​መለ​ኮት፡ ​ዘይ​ፄዓ​ን፡ ​ላዕ​ለ፡ ​ሠረ​ገላ፡ ​ኪሩ ​ቤል፡ ​በት​ስብ​እቱ፡ ​ተፅ​ዕነ፡ ​ዲበ፡
                                ​ዕዋ​ል።</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ለ ​ሥላ​ሴ፡  ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡
                                ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ምሉ​ዕ፡ ​በኵ​ለሄ፡ ለ ​ሥላ​ሴ፡  ​ይደ​ሉ፡ ​ስባ​ሔ፡ ​እዉ​ድ፡
                                ​በሱ​ራኄ፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን። ​ወአ​ሜን፡ ​ለይ​ኵን፡ ​ለይ​ኩን።</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e33388LIT2296Sayfas#Sunday">
               <fo:inline>I-8) Fols 74r–80r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Sword of the Trinity: Praise for Sunday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                 (fol. 74r) 
                                ​አኃ​ሥሥ፡ ​ጽድ​ቀ፡ ​እም​ኀቤ​ከ፡ ​ኦቀ​መረ፡ ​ጽድ​ቅ።  ​አኃ​ሥሥ፡ ​ጥበ​በ፡
                                ​እም​ኀቤ​ከ፡ ​ኦሙ​ዳየ፡ ጥ<fo:inline>ብ (!)</fo:inline>​ብ።  ​ኦሥ​ሉስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡
                                    ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ቅ ​ዱስ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ዛቲ፡ ​ክር​ታስ፡ ​ሲሳ​ይ፡ ​መን​ፈሳ​ዊት፡ ​ለዘ​ቦ፡ ​ሃይ​ማኖ​ት፡
                                ​በደ​ኃሪ​ት፡ ​ዕለ​ት፡ ት  (fol. 80r)  ​ባል​ሕ፡ ​እሞ​ት፡ ​አሜ​ን፡ ​ወአ​ሜን፡ ​ለይ​ኩን፡ ​ለይ​ኩን። ​ወአ​ድኅ​ነኒ፡
                                ​ወባ​ልሐ​ኒ፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​ለኃ​ጥእ፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​ገብ​ርከ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e33411PRS13017GabraMar">{​ገብ​ረ፡}
                                    ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>​ወለ​ጸሐ​ፊሁ፡ ​መሐ​ሮ፡ ​ወዕ​ቀቦ፡ ​ለገ​ብር​ከ፡
                                     ​ገብ​ረ፡ <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>
                                ​ወለ<fo:inline id="d1e33431PRS13021WaldaMik">​ወል​ደ፡
                                        ​ሚካ​ኤል</fo:inline>​ኒ፡ ​ዕቀ​ቦ፡ ​ወአ​ድኅ​ኖ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e33441LIT2736RepCh20">
               <fo:inline>II) Fols 80v–95r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Image of the Trinity’ (​መል​ክአ፡ ​ሥላ​ሴ፡), CAe 2736.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The hymn comprises 47
                                stanzas.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                 (fol. 80v) 
                                ​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ለህ​ላዌ​ክሙ፡ ​ዘይ​መው​ዕ፡ ​ህላ​ዌያ​ተ። ​ለረኪ ​በ፡ ​ስሙ፡ ​ኅቡ​ዕ፡ ​አመ፡
                                ​ወጠ​ንኩ፡ ​ተም​ኔተ። ​እምግ ​ብር​ክሙ፡ ​ሥላ​ሴ፡ ​ሶበ፡ ​ረከ​ቡ፡ ​አስ​ማተ።
                                ​መለኮ ​ተ፡ ​ለለ​፩ዘ​ዚአ​ክሙ፡ ​ገጻ​ተ። ​እን​በለ፡ ​ትድ​ምር​ት፡ ​እሰ​ሚ፡ ​ወእ​ሁብ፡ ​ትድ​ምር​ተ።  ​ሰላ ​ም፡ ​ለዝ​ክረ፡ ​ስም​ክሙ፡ ​ዘኢ​ትጋ​ባዕ፡ ​እም​ተከ​ፍሎ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ለዘ​በነ ​ጊድ፡ ​አቅ​ረብ​ኩ፡ ​መካ​ልየ፡ ​ልሳ​ን፡ ​ስብ​ሐታ​ተ። ​መጠ​ነ፡ ​ራብ​ዕ፡ ​አሥ​ር፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​አተ​ሉ፡
                                ​፯ተ። ​ህየ​ንተ፡ ​፩ሥ​ላሴ፡ ​እለ፡ ​ትፈ​ድዩ፡ ​፻ተ። ​ጸግ​ወኒ፡
                                <!--(before was written:
                                    ጸግውኒ፡)-->
                                ​ለገ​ብር​ክሙ፡ ​ንዋ​የ፡ ​ገጽ፡ ​ትፍ​ሥሕ​ተ። ​ወዲ​በ፡ ​፲አ​ኅጉ​ር፡   (fol. 95r)   ​ሀቡ​ኒ፡ ​ሢመ​ተ። ​ለገ​ብር​ክሙ፡
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e33470PRS13017GabraMar">{​ገብ​ረ፡}
                                    ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline>[////]</fo:inline>
                                ​መል​ዓ፡  ​መን​ፈስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​በላ​ዕለ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e33488PRS13017GabraMar">{​ገብ​ረ፡}
                                    ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e33506LIT2285Saqoqa">
               <fo:inline>III) Fols 95v–111v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Lament on the Virgin’ (​ሰቆ​ቃወ፡ ​ድን​ግል፡), CAe 2285.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                 (fol. 95v) 
                                ​በስ​መ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ሥሉ​ስ፡ ​ኅፀ​ተ፡ ​ግፃ​ዌ፡ ​ዘአ​ልቦ።  ​ሰቆ​ቃወ፡
                                ​ድን​ግል፡ ​እጽ​ሐፍ፡ ​በቀ​ለመ፡ ​ዓን​ብዕ፡  ​ወአን ጠ ​ብጥ​ቦ። ​ወይ​ሌ፡ ​ወላ​ህ፡ ​ለይ​በል፡ ​ለዘ​ንበ​ቦ።  ​ከማ​ሃ፡ ​ኃዘ​ን፡ ​ወተ​ሰዶ፡ ​ኀበ፡
                                ​በኵ​ለሄ፡ ​ረኪ​ቦ። ​ርእ​ዮ፡ ​ለይ​ብኪ፡ ​ዓይ​ነ፡  ​ልበ፡ 
                                ​ዘቦ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሶበ፡  ሐ<fo:inline>ይ (!)</fo:inline>​ለይ​ኩ፡ ​ፍል​ሰት​የ፡ ​ርኁ​ቅ፡ ​ብሔ​ረ። ​ወሑ​ረት​የ፡ ​እም​ዝ፡ ​ኀበ፡
                                ​ኢይ​ገብ​ዕ፡ ​ድኅ​ረ። ​ብካ​የ፡ ​ንግ​ደት​ኪ፡ ​ድን​ግል፡ ​ኮነ​ኒ፡ ​መዝ​ሙረ። ​ረሰ​ይኒ፡ ​ወት​ረ፡  ​ማር​ያም፡
                                 (fol. 111v)   ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​አፉ​ኪ፡ ​ዝኩ​ረ። ​በሕ​ሊና​ኪ፡ ​ህል​ወ፡ ​ወበ​ልብ​ኪ፡ ​ኅዱ​ረ። ​እስ​መ፡ ​ዘእ​ንበ​ሌኪ፡
                                ​ባዕ​ደ፡ ​አል​ብየ፡ ​ማዕ​ምረ። ​ኦእ​ግዝ​እት​የ፡  ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ዕቀ​ብኒ፡ ​እመ​ከራ፡
                                ​ሥጋ፡ ​ወነ​ፍስ፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​ለገ​ብር​ኪ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e33545PRS13017GabraMar">{​ገብ​ረ፡}
                                    ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e33563LIT4963Naahabeya">
               <fo:inline>IV) Fols 112r–114v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Come to me, o my Lord Jesus Christ’ (​ነዓ፡ ​ኀቤ​የ፡ ​ኦእ​ግዚ​እየ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡), CAe 4963.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                 (fol. 112r) 
                                ​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​፩አ​ምላ​ክ፡ ​ነዓ፡ ኀ ​ቤየ፡
                                ​እግ​ዚእ​የ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ሕያ​ው፡ ​ወወ​ልደ፡  ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ስግ​ው። ​በመ​ብረ​ቀ፡ ​መለ​ኮት፡ ​መደ​ንግ​ፅ፡ ፍ ​ሕመ፡
                                    ​መለ​ኮት፡ ​ብቁ​ፅ፡ ​ሐፀ፡ ​መለ​ኮት፡ ​ርው​ጽ፡
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​እጼ​ለል፡ ​ሳዶ​ር፡ ​አላ​ዶር፡
                                ​ዳና​ት፡ ​አዴ​ራ፡ ​ሮዳ​ስ። ​በዝ  (fol. 114v)  ​ንቱ፡ ​አስ​ማት፡ ​ቅን​ዋተ፡ ​መስ​ቀሉ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​እነ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡
                                ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​ቦቱ፡ ​ለስ​ሐ፡ ​ኅም​ዙ፡ ​ለሞ​ት፡ ​ወተ​ቀጥ​ቀጠ፡ ​ኃይ​ሎሙ፡ ​ለሰ​ይጣ​ናት፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ኢይ​ቅረ​ቡ፡ ​ኀበ፡ ​ነፍ​ሱ፡
                                ​ወሥ​ጋሁ፡ ​ለገ​ብረ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር። <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>
                     <!--Homoioteleuton (compare MNC-010)
                            ወተቀጥቀጠ፡ ኃይሎሙ፡ ለሰይጣናት፡
                                         ከማሁ፡ ይልሳሕ፡ ሕምዞሙ፡ ለአጋንንት፡ ወይትቀጥቀጥ፡ ኃይሎሙ፡ ለሰይጣናት፡
                                                     ከመ፡ ኢይቅረቡ፡-->
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e33600LIT3051RepCh331">
               <fo:inline>V) Fols 114v–118r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘In the name of the Trinity, I believe in this Trinity with praise’ (​በስ​መ፡ ​ሥላ​ሴ፡
               ​አአ​ምን፡ ​ዘን​ተ፡ ​ሥላ​ሴ፡ ​ዘም​ስለ፡ ​ሰብ​ሖ፡), CAe 3051.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                 ​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ፩ ​አም​ላክ፡ ​በስ​መ፡  ​ሥላ​ሴ፡
                                ​አአ​ምን፡ ​ዘን​ተ፡ ​ሥላ​ሴ፡ ​ዘም​ስለ፡ ​ሰብ​ሖ፡ ​ለዘ​ይፃ​ረረ​ኒ፡ ​ተመ​ኪሆ፡ ​ቃለ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ይን​ጽሖ፡ ​በሰ​ይፈ፡
                                ​መለ​ኮት፡ ​በሊ​ህ፡ </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">፫ ​ገጽ፡ ​ዘኢ​ይት​ከፈ​ል፡ ፩ ​ራዕ​ይ፡
                                ​ወ፩ ​አካ​ል፡ ​ዕሩ​ያነ፡ ​አም​ሳል፡ ​ቡሩ​ካነ፡ ​ቃል፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ዋህ​ድ፡ ​በአ​ካሉ፡ ​ወም​ሉዕ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> 
                                ​እም​ቅድ​መ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡
                                    ​ህል ው  ​እስ​ከ፡ <fo:inline>ለዓም፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ይሄ​ሉ፡ ​ትጉ​ሃነ፡
                                ​ሰማ​ይ፡ ​ኪያ​ሁ፡ ​ይስ​እሉ፤ ​ቅዱ​ስ፤ ​ቅዱ​ስ፤ ​ቅዱስ ፡  ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ጸባ​ዖት፡ ​ይብ​ሉ፡ ​ወስ​ብሐ​ቲሁ፡ ​ይመ​ልዕ፡
                                ​በኵ​ሉ፡ ​ለገ​ብር​ከ፡ <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e33636LIT5962PrayerThreeNames">
               <fo:inline>VI) Fols 118r–118v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Prayer to the three names to defeat the
                    enemy, CAe 5962.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The entire text is reproduced below.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                 ​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ፩ ​አም​ላክ፡ በ ​ስመ፡ ፫ ​አስ​ማት፡
                                ​አአ​ትብ፡  (fol. 118v)   ​ገጽ​የ፡ ​አአ​ትብ፡ ​ድኅ​ሬየ፡ ​በዘ​ቦቱ፡ ​ተወ​ኪል​የ፡ ​ዕመ​ውዕ፡ ​ፀር​የ፡ ​በስ​መ፡ ፫
                                ​አስ​ማት፡ ​አአ​ትብ፡ ​የማ​ንየ፡ ​በስ​መ፡ ፫ ​አስ​ማት፡ ​አአ​ትብ፡ ​ፀጋ​ምየ፡ ​በዘ​ቦቱ፡ ​ተወ​ኪል​የ፡ ​ዕመ​ውዕ፡ ​ፀር​የ፡ ​ወጸ​ላዕ​ትየ፡
                                ​በስ​መ፡ ፫ ​አስ​ማት፡ ​ገደ​ፍኩ፡ ​ነፍ​ስየ፡ ​ወሥ​ጋየ፡ ​ወበ​ስመ፡ ፫ ​አስ​ማት፡ ​ገደ​ፍኩ፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ርእ​ስየ፡ ​በዘ​ቦቱ፡ ​ዕመ​ውዕ፡
                                ​ፀር​የ፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን። ​ኦእ​ግዚ​ኦ፡ ​ዕቀ​በኒ፡ ​ለገ​ብር​ከ፡ <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e33657PRS13017GabraMar">​ገበ​ረ፡ ​ማር​ያም።
                                </fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Additional notes</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 119r–120v: Nicene Creed, CAe 3308.
                                        . The text is written by Hand 2.
                                    </fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        Incipit:  :
                                            ​በአ​ሀዱ፡ ​አም​ላክ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​አብ፡ ​አኀ​ዜ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​ገባ​ሬ፡ ​ሰማ​ያት፡
                                            ​ወም​ድር፡ ​ዘያ​ስተ​ርኢ፡ ​ወዘ​ኢያ​ስተ​ርኢ።  ... 
                                    </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 120v: Praise to God, incomplete, CAe 5991.
                                        . The text is written by Hand 2.
                                        It is incomplete: it breaks off in the middle of a word on the bottom of fol. 121v. </fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        Incipit:  :
                                            ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ጸባ​ዖት፡ ​ፍጹ​ም፡ ​ምሉ​እ፡ ​ሰማ​ያተ፡
                                            ​ወም​ድረ፡ ​ቅዱ​ሳተ፡ ​ስብ​ሐቲ​ከ። ​እሰ​ግድ፡ ​ለአ​ብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​፫ቱ፡ ​፩ዱ፡ ​ወእ​ንዘ፡
                                            ​፩ዱ፡ ​፫ቱ፡ ​እሰ​ግድ፡ ​ለአ​ብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡
                                         ... 
                                    </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block> Scribal corrections occur occasionally over erasure (e.g.
                                        fols 112r here comprising several lines)
                                        or interlineally (e.g. 28v, 31v), also
                                        made in a secondary hand (e.g. 29v, 40v, 88v, 114r). Spaces (after erasure)
                                        were filled with an interlaced band on 50r, 72r and with several thin lines on
                                        fols 66v, 79v. The scribe wrote the last
                                        two lines of the reading for Tuesday in small script in
                                        order to complete the section on the same folio (35v). Writing exercises were executed on
                                        123r and upside down on fols 121v, 122v. The name <fo:inline id="d1e34239PRS13017GabraMar">Gabra Māryām</fo:inline> is written on 3r (the rest of the entire folio is
                                        blank).
                                        The name of the scribe was erased in all
                                        supplication formulas he had dedicated to himself (15r, 66r, 80r), only the first part of his name
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ገብ​ረ፡</fo:inline> being preserved.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Aids for identifying weekday readings are written in the
                                        upper margin on the incipit page of each section of ms_i1 in red ink
                                        <!--framed by ornamental bands @Jacopo--> (the scribe used a
                                        different nib for the reading references than for the main
                                        text): <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘሰ​ኑይ</fo:inline> (fol. 15v)
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘሠ​ሉስ</fo:inline> (fol. 27r), <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘረ​ቡዕ</fo:inline> (fol. 36r), <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘሐ​ሙስ</fo:inline> (fol. 45v), <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘዓ​ርብ</fo:inline> (fol. 55v), <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘቀ​ዳሚት</fo:inline> (fol. 66v), <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘዘ​ወትር</fo:inline> (fol. 72r, in
                                        black), <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘእ​ኁድ</fo:inline> (fol. 74r).
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>An English note is written in pencil, possibly by <fo:inline id="d1e34308PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline>, on  fol. 1r.
                                        It indicates the main content of the book:
                                    <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">‘Book of prayers and praises inscribed with the
                                        name of one Gabra Maryam. 19th century. Ethiop Ms 19’.</fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>An English note is written in black or dark blue pen on fol. 2r. It states the circumstance of acquisition of this manuscript.
                                        The first word, possibly the name of the owner of the manuscript, is uncertain due to the cursory handwriting.
                                    <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">‘<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>
                                        82nd Regt.
                                        
                                        Looted at Maqdala 13th Apl 1868’.</fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>5)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 2r: A turquoise and gold label of the textile trading company
                                        A.H. Huschke &amp; Co with a leaping horse is sewn onto
                                            fol. 2v. This India-based company was
                                        active in the nineteenth century until its founder, August Henry
                                        Huschke of Swiss-German family background, died in 1866 and
                                        his company was sold. A.H. Huschke &amp; Co acquired a high
                                        ‘reputation for luxury cottons’ and other ‘quality goods for
                                        the fashion market’ (see: <inline xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Format">Nenadic 2019</inline>).</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>6)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 1v, 2v:  A white sticker, with the name of <fo:inline id="d1e34357PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> (<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቤን​ት፡
                                            ​ዩው​ል፡ ​የን​ሰን።</fo:inline>) printed on it, and the signatures
                                        ‘Ms. Aeth. f. 29’ written in pencil, is respectively glued
                                        on fol. 1v and on fols 2v .
                                        Other two stickers with the signature ‘Ms 19’ printed on
                                        them are glued on fol. 1v.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>7)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                                        This manuscript and MS Gāntā ʾAfašum, ʾAbrǝqo Māryām, QMA-005 share, beside the identical handwriting, particular
                                            scribal practices. They show similar elements for the visual
                                            organisation: an almost identical ornamental band on the incipit
                                            page of the first text (more elaborated in the Bodleian manuscript than in MS Gāntā ʾAfašum, ʾAbrǝqo Māryām, QMA-005; in the latter,
                                            other reserved spaces for ornamental bands do exist but were not
                                            filled) and a very similar way of rubricating the incipit pages of
                                            texts and their sections (at the top: two red lines followed by two
                                            black and another two red lines; at the bottom: two red lines and
                                            two black lines). The name of the patron or scribe or owner,
                                            originally written in red ink throughout both manuscripts, was
                                            deleted. There is only one instance, found in MS Gāntā ʾAfašum, ʾAbrǝqo Māryām, QMA-005 (see, e.g. fol. 86v), where
                                            the original text layer is still (but barely) readable. This text
                                            passage points to the original name of <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ገብ​ረ፡
                                                ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline> (in this case, this original name was replaced in
                                            the Bodleian manuscript with one and the same
                                            name, see below).
                                        In addition to the attested similar scribal practices, both
                                            codices share also physical peculiarities. Both have a quite
                                            particular, slender book format (more pronounced in MS Gāntā ʾAfašum, ʾAbrǝqo Māryām, QMA-005). Each cover shows a fine and careful
                                            blind-tooled decoration. Both have threads inserted into folios for
                                            navigation through the multiple-text manuscripts; MS Gāntā ʾAfašum, ʾAbrǝqo Māryām, QMA-005 has also marks painted in red to indicate
                                            the incipit page of a text or of a section. Extremely striking are
                                            two labels of two textile companies, one is glued into the inner
                                            part of the front board in MS 
                                                Gāntā ʾAfašum, ʾAbrǝqo Māryām, QMA-005
                                             and
                                            the other is sewn onto fol. 2v in the Bodleian manuscript (see Varia
                                                    note 5). Gāntā ʾAfašum, ʾAbrǝqo Māryām, QMA-005 shows the label
                                        of ‘W&amp;I
                                            Peel’, the (later) company of the successful textile industrialist
                                            Robert Peel (1723–1795), widely known as Parsley Peel (the label displays the Peel arms including
                                            a shuttle held by a lion, below a bee and the family motto
                                            ‘Industria’; it is the same as provided in Wikipedia (, accessed
                                                on 25 May 2020). Both labels are related most probably to
                                            the silk or cotton inlays in the two manuscripts.
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                                  The book is bound in wooden
                                  boards covered with blind-tooled .
                                  The back board is decorated with a textile <fo:inline id="d1e34434">inlay</fo:inline>.
                                
                                  The boards project beyond the edges of the textblock and have a steep internal bevel
                                  that stops to the size of the bookblock.
                                  A niche possibly for a <fo:inline id="d1e34440">Mirror</fo:inline> is carved into the inner side of
                                  the front board (the mirror is lost, but traces of adhesive are still visible).
                                  The inner side of the back board is decorated with a silk inlay coloured gold, blue, and
                                  red of Indian provenance (see Crill 2026,  169–170).
                                  The connection with an Indian-based textile trading company is testified by Varia note 5).
                                
                                  Full reddish-brown leather cover.
                                  The turn-ins have been trimmed out and, at the corners, they form butt mitres.
                                  <fo:inline id="d1e34454">Additional leather patches</fo:inline> reduce the size
                                  of the area between the turn-ins.
                                  Blind-tooled ornaments decorate the cover in full, including turn-ins, edges,
                                  and spine.
                                  The cover sides present a slightly different design consisting of a rectangular frame of <fo:inline id="d1e34457">criss-cross</fo:inline>
                                  motifs between <fo:inline id="d1e34460">triple straight lines</fo:inline> and
                                  <fo:inline id="d1e34463">double straight lines</fo:inline>, enclosing a central panel
                                  with a star. In the areas above and below the star are triangular-shaped patterns formed by superimposed
                                  <fo:inline id="d1e34466">V-form</fo:inline> motifs with <fo:inline id="d1e34470">double circles</fo:inline> at the top.
                                  The star is formed by V-form motifs and double circles (see Winslow 2015,  235; 239). The back board presents a 4-pointed star while
                                  the upper board an 8-pointed one with the addition of <fo:inline id="d1e34480">mother of water</fo:inline> motifs.
                                  <fo:inline id="d1e34483">Triple straight lines</fo:inline> run along the edges of the boards.
                                  Four-fold straight lines form rectangular panels on the spine and outline the borders of the the turn-ins.
                                  Groups of four double circles fill in the empty spaces and are stamped at the intersection of the lines.
                                
                                  The endbands are not extant but their internal tiedowns are visible in the centrefolds of the quires.
                                
                                  Chainstitch sewing on four sewing stations (two pairs).
                                  Two Z-plied threads have been used. Their ends are knotted in the centrefold of the last quire.
                                
                                  Two lines of running stitches close to head and tail are visible on the back cover, they are part of the attachment system
                                  of the endbands.
                                
                                  Coloured <fo:inline id="d1e34502">leaf string markers</fo:inline> are inserted
                                    in the outer margin of folios to indicate the incipit pages of
                                    the sections of ms_i1 and the incipit pages of
                                    ms_i2 #ms_i3 #ms_i4 (on fols 16, 27, 36, 45, 55, 66, 74, 82, 95, 111).
                                </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Pencil foliation in the upper right corner (1–123).</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm">
                                        Undecorated quire marks are written in the upper inner margin of the first folio of most quires, with the exception of
                                        the first two and last three quires.
                                        The quire mark on fol. 72 (<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">፰</fo:inline>) was added later, still by the main hand.
                                    </fo:block>
         <fo:block>14 quires. A<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2+1 (Fols 1r–3v)</fo:inline> – I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 4r–13v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 14r–23v)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 24r–33v)</fo:inline> – IV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 34r–43v)</fo:inline> – V<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 44r–53v)</fo:inline> – VI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 54r–61v)</fo:inline> – VII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 62r–71v)</fo:inline> – VIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 72r–81v)</fo:inline> – IX<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 82r–91v)</fo:inline> – X<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 92r–101v)</fo:inline> – XI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 102r–111v)</fo:inline> – XII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6+2 (Fols 112r–119v)</fo:inline> – B<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">4 (Fols 120r–123v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 4r–119v: 1
                                    column (16 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin
                                        dimensions taken from fol. 20r.The characters per line are 8–10.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            159 × 93 mm (fol. 20r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            106 × 63 mm (fol. 20r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 19 mm, bottom: 35 mm, right: 21 mm, left: 10 mm (fol. 20r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 120r–120v: 1
                                    column (20 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin
                                        dimensions taken from fol. 120r.The characters per line are 10–13.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            159 × 93 mm (fol. 20r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            107 × 72 mm (fol. 120r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 19 mm, bottom: 36 mm, right: 11 mm, left: 8 mm (fol. 120r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible. Primary pricks are visible. Ruling pricks are mostly visible. The upper and the bottom lines are written above the
                                        ruling. Ruling is visible; pricking is visible. Primary pricks are visible. Ruling pricks are mostly visible. The upper line is written above the
                                        ruling. The bottom line is written above the
                                        ruling.  The ruling pattern is clearly different on
                                            fols 121v–123v: three ruled lines above,
                                        three lines in the middle, and three lines below. The same
                                        pattern, barely visible, is probably ruled on fols 1r–2v. Ruling pattern (fols 3r–119v): 1A-1A/0-0/0-0/C.  Ruling pattern (fols 120r–121r): 1A-1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 4ra–118v. First half of the nineteenth century.. Trained hand. The handwriting is regular with broadly spaced
                                    characters. The scribe also copied MS 
                                        Gāntā ʾAfašum, ʾAbrǝqo Māryām, QMA-005
                                     (see History).<fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: One or more groups of lines on
                                    the incipit pages of the Sword of the Trinity (<fo:inline font-style="italic">Sayfa Śǝllāse</fo:inline>), all its
                                    sections and the following texts;
                                    holy names (names of the members of the Trinity are written
                                    alternating with red and black on fols 21v), names
                                    (mostly erased) of individuals related to the production of the
                                    manuscript;
                                    names of the Hebrew letters on fol. 13v;
                                    some words in the Sword of the Trinity, in full or in part:
                                    <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሰላ​ም፡</fo:inline>,
                                    <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​እኵ​ት፡</fo:inline>; <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ስብ​ሐት፡</fo:inline>; the first word of each
                                    verse in the Lament on the Virgin (<fo:inline font-style="italic">Saqoqāwa dǝngǝl</fo:inline>);
                                    elements of the punctuation marks, text dividers, and numerals.
                                </fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Abbreviations: <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="6mm"
                                             provisional-label-separation="6mm"
                                             start-indent="cm">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>1)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                        ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓ፡ ​አ፡ ​ወአ፡ ​ለይ​ኵ፡ ​ለይ። or
                                        ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡
                                            ​አሜ​ን፡ ​ወአ​ሜን፡ ​ለይ፡ ​ለ። for ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን፡
                                                ​ወአ​ሜን፡ ​ለይ​ኵን፡ ​ለይ​ኩን። (fols 27r–45r); </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>2)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                        ስ or ​ስብ or ​ስብሐ for
                                        ​ስብ​ሐት (fols 55v–66r);</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>3)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                        ​ሰላ፡ ​ለፍቅ or ​ሰላ​ለፍ or
                                        ​ሰ፡ ​ለፍ for ​ሰላ​ም፡
                                            ​ለፍ​ቅረ (fols 66v–73v);</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>4)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                        ሰ or ​ሰላ for ​ሰላም 
                                        (fols 80v–95r).</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 2:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 119r–120v. Mid-nineteenth century. Poor hand, executed by an inexperienced scribe who tends to scribal
                                    errors and to a rushed script.<fo:block>Ink: Black.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Decoration</fo:block>
         <fo:block margin-top="3mm" margin-bottom="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Monochrome interlace bands in the ‘Menelik style’ mark
                                           the incipit pages of the Sword of the Trinity (<fo:inline font-style="italic">Sayfa Śǝllāse</fo:inline>):
                                         fols 4r, 15v, 27r, 36r, 45v, 55v, 66v.
                                         Such bands are not present on fols 72r, 74r, 80v, 95v, 119r even though
                                             the scribe left a few lines above the page for them to be inserted.
                                             Most of these bands are topped by indications for the reading days of the week
                                         which are encircled by smaller decorative frames drawn by using a different
                                         ink. The fact that such readings are also indicated when the interlace bands are absent
                                         strongly suggests that they were not added by the illustrator.
                              </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Miniatures</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Headpieces</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(15) Fols 4r, 15v, 27r, 36r, 45v, 55v, 66v: <fo:inline>Monochrome interlace bands.</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Drawings</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Other</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
                                  Coloured <fo:inline id="d1e34502">leaf string markers</fo:inline> are inserted
                                    in the outer margin of folios to indicate the incipit pages of
                                    the sections of ms_i1 and the incipit pages of
                                    ms_i2 #ms_i3 #ms_i4 (on fols 16, 27, 36, 45, 55, 66, 74, 82, 95, 111).
                                <fo:block>A hole on fols 54 from parchment
                                        making. A tear carefully amended on 42.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is deficient.A rectangular piece
                                    of parchment has been cut out from fols 121 at the
                                    bottom. All edges were re-trimmed.
                                    Occasionally smudged ink, e.g. on 19r, 69v, 80v.
                                    The sewing broke at the connection with the upper board.
                                    As a result, the 1, 2, 3 are detached from the textblock with the risk of their displacement.
                                    Head and tailband are missing (tiedowns are
                                        visible in the centrefolds of all quires).
                                </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>1841–1861</fo:inline>
                            The manuscript was produced by the same scribe who manufactured <fo:inline/> which belongs to the church of
                            <fo:inline id="d1e34524INS0175QMA">ʾAbrǝqo Māryām</fo:inline> in <fo:inline id="d1e34526LOC3293GantaA">Gāntā ʾAfašum</fo:inline>, <fo:inline id="d1e34528LOC5932Tegray">Tǝgrāy</fo:inline> and was
                            reasonably dated to 1841–1861. We therefore may conclude that <fo:inline/> and <fo:inline/>
                                were manufactured around the same time, somewhen between 1841–1861,
                                in the area of <fo:inline id="d1e34536LOC3293GantaA">Gāntā ʾAfašum</fo:inline>, <fo:inline id="d1e34538LOC5932Tegray">Tǝgrāy</fo:inline> in Ethiopia by a
                                professional scribe with connections to foreign traders or at least
                                to imported goods (see Varia note 5).
                            The name of
                            the original patron or donor (introduced as <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ገበ​ርከ፡</fo:inline> ‘your servant’) of <fo:inline/> was erased from the supplication
                            formulas throughout the manuscript. Only the first part of his name
                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ገብ​ረ፡</fo:inline> survived. His name was
                            replaced by that of <fo:inline id="d1e34553PRS13017GabraMar">Gabra Māryām</fo:inline>. The name of
                            <fo:inline id="d1e34555PRS13021WaldaMik">Walda Mikāʾel</fo:inline> written by the main hand is
                            mentioned only once, on fol. 80r.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>
                            The manuscript must have come into the possession of the church of
                            <fo:inline id="d1e34562INS0101MadhaneAlam">Maqdala Madḫāne ʿĀlam</fo:inline> at a
                            certain time in its history from where it was looted on 13 April 1868
                            (see Varia note 4) and brought to England. It is unknown
                                how and when the manuscript came into the possession of <fo:inline id="d1e34571PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline>.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e34576PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Bibliography</fo:block>Winslow 2015; Crill 2026.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethf29">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethf29</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
