      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethf31"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. f. 31</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Juel-Jensen 21, Phillipps 23451)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex117×103 mm (weight: 280g), 82 fols (1 p. blank), 11 quires, eighteenth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e35661LIT1693John">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 3ra–75rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Gospel of John (Collection), CAe 1693.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ብስ​ራተ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ትሩ​ፍ፡ ​ረድ<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​ገረ፡ ​በመ​ለኮ​ት፡ ​ዮሐ​ንስ፡ ​ወን​ጌላ​ዊ፡
                                ወ ​ልደ፡ ​ዘብ​ዴዎ​ስ፡ ​ፍቁ​ረ፡ እ ​ግዚ ​እን​ተ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡  ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ገብ​ሩ፡
                                <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline> ​በዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን።
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e35687LIT2715John">
               <fo:inline>I-1) Fols 3ra–75ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Gospel of John, CAe 2715.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ቀዳ​ሚሁ፡ ​ሀለ​ወ፡  ​ቃል፡ ​ወው​እቱ፡  ​ቃል፡ ​ኀበ፡ ​እግዚ ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ወእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ቃል።
                                    ​ወዝ​ንቱ፡ ​እም​ቀዳ​ሚሁ፡ ​እም​ቀዲ​ሙ፡ ​ኀበ፡ ​እግ​ዚኣ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ሀለ​ወ፡ ​ወኵ​ሉ፡ ​ቦቱ፡ ​ኮነ፡ ​ወዘ​እን​በሌ​ሁሰ፡   (b)  ​አል​ቦ፡ ​ዘኮ​ነ፡
                                        ​ወኢም ​ንት​ኒ፡ ​እም​ዘ፡ ኮ ​ነ። ​ወቦ​ቱ፡ ​ኮነ፡ ​ሕይ ​ወት።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ወሶ​በ፡ ​ተጽ​ሐፈ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​በበ፡ ​አሐ​ዱ፡ ​እም​ኢያ​ግመ​ሮ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​ጥቀ፡ ​መጻ​ሕፍ​ቲሁ። ​ዘተ​ጽሕ​ፈ፡ ​አሜ​ን፡ ​ወአ​ሜን።   (fol. 75r)   ​ወኵ​ሉ፡ ​ቃሉ፡ ​በወ​ንጌ​ለ፡
                                    ​ጽድ​ቅ፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​እም​ጥን​ቱ፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ተፍ​ጻሜ​ቱ፡ ​ለሊ​ሁ፡ ​ወል​ድ፡ ​ተና​ገረ።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e35721LIT1693John#Postscript">
               <fo:inline>I-2) Fols 75ra–75rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Gospel of John (Collection): Colophon of the Gospel of John</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm"> The subscription is separated from the explicit of the text by means of two chains of black and red dots.
                                    <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​መል​አ፡ ​ጽሕ​ፈተ፡ ​ብስ​ራቱ፡ ​ለዮ​ሐን​ስ፡ ​ዜና​ዊ።  ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ዘብ​ዴዎ​ስ፡ ​ሐዋ​ርያ፡ ​፩እ​ም፲​ወ፪ ​ሰባ​ክያ​ን። ​ወጸ​ሐፋ፡ ​እን​ከ፡ ​በል​ሳነ፡
                                    ​ዮና​ናው​ያን፡ ​ለሰ​ብአ፡ ​ሀገ​ረ፡ ​ኤፌ​ሶን። ​እም​ድኅ​ረ፡ ​ዕር​ገቱ፡   (b)   ​ለእ​ግዚ​እነ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ሰማ​ይ፡ ​በሥ​ጋ፡ ፴ ​አመ​ት፡ ​ወበ​፲ወ፫ ​እመ​ንግ​ሥቱ፡
                                    ​ለሄ​ሮድ​ስ፡ ​ንጉ​ሠ፡ ​ሮም። ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​ወላ​ዕለ፡ ​ይኩ​ን፡ ​ምሕ​ረቱ፡ ​ለዓ​ለም፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e35739LIT4614Salam">
               <fo:inline>II) Fols 75va–76ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Hymn to Our Lady Mary, CAe 4614.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ሃሌ፡ ​ሉያ፡ ​ሃሌ፡ ​ሉያ፡ ​ንሰ​ግድ፡ ለ ​አብ፡ ​ብር​ሃና​ት፡ ​ወለ​ወል​ዱ፡ ​ዋህ​ድ፡ ​ወለ​መን​ፈስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ <fo:inline>ጰራቅሊሊጦስ፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                                ​ሥሉ​ስ፡ ​ዕሩ​ይ። ​ሰላ​ም፡  ​ለማ​ርያ​ም፡  ​ንግ​ሥት፡ ​ወአ​ፀድ፡ ​ዘበ​ግዕ፡ ​ወዑ​ፅፍ​ት፡ ​በዝ​ንቱ፡ ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ዐቢ​ይ፡
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ንዑ፡ ​ትነ​ጽሩ፡ ​ኀበ፡ ​ዛቲ፡ ​መር​ዓት፡ ​ወሥ​ርጉ​ት፡ ​ዘበ​ግዕ፡ ​ዘኢ​ተገ​በር​ዋ፡ ​ተረ​ክበ፡ ​አስ​ካለ፡ ​በረ​ከት፡ ​ዛቲ፡ ​ይእ​ቲ፡ ​ጽዮ​ን፡ ​ሐዳ​ስ፡ ​ኃደ​ረ፡ ​ላዕ​ሌሃ፡
                                ​ዘኃ​ደረ፡ ​አም​ላክ​ነ፡ ​ፍሥ​ሐ፡ ​ኵሎ​ሙ፡ ​ነቢ​ያት፡ ​ቅዱ​ሳን።
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e35764LIT3022RepCh302">
               <fo:inline>III) Fols 76ra–79rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Rejoice Mary, the Pascha of Adam’ (​ተፈ​ሥሒ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡ ​ለአ​ዳም፡ ​ፋሲ​ካሁ፡), CAe 3022.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm"/>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ተፈ​ሥሒ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ለአ​ዳም፡   (b)   ​ፋሲ​ካሁ፡ ​ወማ​ዕይ​ታ፡ ​ለሔ​ዋን፡ ​እን​ተ፡ ​ይእ​ቲ፡ ​አመ፡ ​ገባ​ሁ።
                                ​እስ​መ፡ ​ግዕ​ዛኖ​ሙ፡ ​ኮነ፡ ​ለወ​ልድ​ኪ፡ ​በት​ንሣ​ኤሁ።
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ሴሰ​ይኒ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ለጸ​ማድ​ኪ፡ ​ርሁ​ብ፡ ​ኅብ​ስተ፡ ​አእ​ምሮ፡ ​ሠና​ይ፡ ​ወወ​ይነ፡ ​ጥበ​ብ፡ ​እመ​ኒ፡ ​እድ​ፋደ፡ ​ኃጢ​አት​የ፡
                                ​እም​ኅዝ​ብ፡ ​ተዘ​ከሪ፡ ​እግ​ዝዕ​ትየ፡ ​በር​ኅራ​ኄኪ፡ ​ዕፁ​ብ፡ ​በከ​መ፡ ​አስ​ተይ​ኪዮ፡ ​ማየ፡ ​ለጽ​ሙዕ፡ ​ከል​ብ፡
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e35791LIT3100RepCh380">
               <fo:inline>IV) Fols 79rb–82vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘
                     Malkǝʾ -hymn to St George’ (​መል​ክአ፡ ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡), CAe 3100.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ኦፍ​ጡነ፡ ​ረድኤ ​ት፡ ​ለጽ​ኑዕ፡ ​ወለ​ድኩ​ም፡ ​ለነ​ፍሰ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​ቃው​ም፡  ​ጊዮር<fo:inline>[​ጊስ፡]</fo:inline>
                                ​የዋ​ህ፡ ​እን​በለ፡ ​መስ​ፈር​ት፡ ​ወዓ​ቅም፡ ​ከመ፡ ​እግ​ዝእ​ትከ፡ ​ቡር​ክት፡  ​ለማ​ርያ​ም፡  ​ርኅ​ሩኃ፡ ​ልብ፡ ​እም​በቀ​ል፡ ​ወቁ​ም።
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ሠና​ያተ፡ ​ኵሎ፡ ዕ<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​ተ፡ ​ሞት​ሰ፡ ​ድል​ው፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​ባሕ​ቱ፡ ​ለን​ስሐ፡
                                ን<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​ሕኒ፡ ​ንስ​ሐተ፡  ​ናዘ ​ዚት​የ፡ ​እም​ኀዘን
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Additional notes</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 1v–2v: Book of the Funeral Ritual: Tenth Blessing of ʾabbā Sāmuʾel. The text is written in a poor hand in dark brownish ink.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        Incipit:  :
                                            ​ይት​ባረ​ክ፡ ​ስሙ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​ቡሩ​ክ፡ ​ይት​አኮ​ት፡ ​እኩ​ት፡ ​ይት​ቀደ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ይሴ​ባሕ፡ ​ስሙ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡
                                        ​ስቡ​ሕ፡ ​ይዕ​በይ፡ ​ስሙ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​ዓቢ​ይ፡ ​ይት​ለዓ​ል፡ ​ስሙ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​ልዑ​ል፡ ... 
                                    </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Many corrections are executed over erasure (e.g. on fols 10ra, 20va, 38va), sometimes in small script to accommodate multiple lines (e.g.
                                        23rb, 31rb, 40va). Many corrections, executed either over erasure or interlineally, are written in the same hand as that of the
                                            aids for identifying weekday readings. The spaces left after erasures are sometimes marked with thin lines (e.g. on 11rb).
                                        Erasures are also found in the upper margins in correspondence of the incipit of the weekday readings (e.g. on 16vb, 40vb, 69rb).
                                        The name of an individual, indicated as <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ገብ​ሩ፡</fo:inline> ‘his servant’ (probably either the owner, the patron or the donor of
                                        the manuscript), has been erased on 3r. Few words are washed out on 46va, 53vb, 64vb.
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Aids for identifying weekday readings are written in the upper margin within a frame, probably in the same hand as that of a1:
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘስ​ኑይ</fo:inline> (fol. 3r), <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                           <fo:inline>ዘቀዳም (!)</fo:inline>
                        </fo:inline> (fol. 16vb),
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘሠ​ሉስ</fo:inline> (fol. 20vb), <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘረ​ቡዕ</fo:inline> (fol. 40va),
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘሐ​ሙስ</fo:inline> (fol. 48vb), <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘዓ​ርብ</fo:inline> (fol. 61va),
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘእ​ሁድ።</fo:inline> (fol. 69ra).
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                                        A <fo:inline font-style="italic">tamallas</fo:inline>-sign in the shape of a cross indicates on fol. 49vb the omission of a portion of text,
                                        which is written in the upper margin. Both the <fo:inline font-style="italic">tamallas</fo:inline>-sign and the omitted text are written in the same hand as
                                        that of the aids for the weekday readings and of many corrections.
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>There are some writings in pencil on fol. 1r: ‘Brought from
                                        <fo:inline id="d1e36276PRS13027Sturt">
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Capt.</fo:inline> Sturt</fo:inline> from
                                        <fo:inline id="d1e36281LOC3010Ethiop">Ethiopia</fo:inline>’ and
                                       ‘Gospel of John’. The titles of the manuscript contents are indicated in the same handwriting in pencil in the upper margin of
                                        3r (‘Gospel of John’) and fol. 75v (‘Hymns to the Virgin’).
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>5)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>A white sticker is glued to the inner side of the front board. The name of <fo:inline id="d1e36295PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> is printed on it
                                        (‘<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቤን​ት፡ ​ዩው​ል፡ ​የን​ሰን።</fo:inline>’) and the signature ‘MS. Aeth. f. 31’ is written in pencil.
                                        An additional sticker, with the signature ‘Ms 21’ on it, is glued below it.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                                  The book is bound in wooden boards partially covered with reddish-brown leather.
                                
                                  The boards are few millimeters larger than the bookblock and have external shallow bevels. The grain runs vertically.
                                  On the inner surface of both boards, along the inner margin, leather fibres and traces of glue are present.
                                
                                  The boards and the spine are partially covered with plain reddish-brown leather.
                                  The front board is almost entirely covered, while only half of the back board is. The turn-ins are not well adhered and are partially detached from the boards.
                                  The irregular cut, its smaller size compared to the bookblock and the absence of decoration suggest that the cover was a hasty, posthumous addition to the binding.
                                
                                  Brown <fo:inline id="d1e36329">slit-braid</fo:inline> endbands are present.
                                
                                  The bookblock was originally sewn on four sewing stations (two pairs) with S-plied threads resulting in a periodic fold pattern.
                                  However, the original sewing is not preserved and only the marks left by the threads in the quires, the holes in the boards and in the quires remain.
                                  As of today, each quire is stitched through the inner margin in correspondence of the uppermost and lowermost sewing stations.
                                
                                  Vertical short stitches pierce the leather on the spine in two points at the head and tail of each quire, thus fixing the endbands to the cover.
                                
                                  The manuscript is provided with a leather two-piece satchel with a strap. The inner case is single-walled and equipped with long flaps
                                  extending from the side panels and a main tapered flap extending from the back to the front panel, to cover the opening of the book compartment.
                                  The outer case slides along the hanging strap to fit over the inner case. The strap used to pass through two pouches
                                  sewn to the lateral panels of the inner case and the top panel of the outer case but it is now fixed just to the inner case.
                                  A sticker with the inventory number ‘23451’ is glued onto one side of the case.
                                  Threads of various origin are inserted in the outer margins in correspondence of the incipit of the weekday readings.
                                  More specifically, a bright red <fo:inline id="d1e36348">leaf string mark</fo:inline> is inserted in the outer margin of fol. 16 and
                                  a piece of textile of the same type is inserted on fol. 17ra. Other coloured or uncoloured <fo:inline id="d1e36355">leaf string markers</fo:inline>
                                  are inserted in the outer margins of fols 20, 40, 61.
                                  A fragment of the same bright red textile used as a leaf tab marker is placed between fol. 16 and fols 17.
                                  A straw from a plant is placed between fol. 68 and fol. 69.
                                </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
                                    Pencil foliation in the upper left corner (1–82).
                                </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block>11 quires. A<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2 (Fols 1r–2v)</fo:inline> – I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 3r–12v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8+2 (Fols 13r–22v)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 23r–32v)</fo:inline> – IV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8+2 (Fols 33r–42v)</fo:inline> – V<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8+2 (Fols 43r–52v)</fo:inline> – VI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 53r–62v)</fo:inline> – VII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 63r–70v)</fo:inline> – VIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6 (Fols 71r–76v)</fo:inline> – IX<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">4 (Fols 77r–80v)</fo:inline> – X<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2 (Fols 81r–82v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 3ra–82vb: 2
                                    columns (13–17 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 21r. The characters per line are 7–11.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            112 × 99 mm (fol. 21r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            72 × 82 mm (fol. 21r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 12 mm, bottom: 23 mm, right: 10 mm, left: 8 mm, intercolumn: 5 mm (fol. 21r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible. Both primary and ruling pricks are visible. The upper and bottom lines are written above the ruling.
                                        The vertical ruling is sometimes crudely executed, e.g. on fols 39r, 40r, 41r.
                                     Ruling pattern: 1A-1A-1A1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 3ra–75rb. Eighteenth century.. Mediocre handwriting. It becomes less accurate towards the end (e.g. on fols 74ra).
                                    The scribe does not always follow the vertical ruling (e.g. on 40r, 57v).
                                    The last ruled line has not been written on 13vb.
                                <fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: 
                                    Few lines on the incipit page of the Gospel of John, alternating with black lines;
                                    the chapters, indicated with the term <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ምዕ​ራፍ፡</fo:inline>, and the first two or three lines of each chapter;
                                    elements of the numerals and of the punctuation signs, including the text dividers.
                                </fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Abbreviations: <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="6mm"
                                             provisional-label-separation="6mm"
                                             start-indent="cm">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>1)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                        ​ም፡ or ​ምዕ፡ for ​ምዕ​ራፍ፡ (e.g. on fols 7ra, 16vb, 45vb).
                                    </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 2:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 75va–82vb. Eighteenth century.. The handwriting is mediocre, uneven and somewhat irregular in spacing the letters.
                                    It is not clear whether it is the same hand as Hand 1.
                                <fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: 
                                    The first two lines of the incipit page of the <fo:inline font-style="italic">Malkǝʾ</fo:inline>-hymn known as
                                    ms_i2;
                                    the first two words and the first letter or word of each
                                    stanza of the two <fo:inline font-style="italic">Malkǝʾ</fo:inline>-hymns;
                                    holy names (those of <fo:inline id="d1e36125PRS6819Mary">Mary</fo:inline> and of <fo:inline id="d1e36128PRS4585Georgeo">George</fo:inline>);
                                    elements of the numerals and of the punctuation signs.
                                </fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Abbreviations: <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="6mm"
                                             provisional-label-separation="6mm"
                                             start-indent="cm">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>1)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                        ​ጊዮ​ር፡ or ​ጊዮ​ርጊ፡ for ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡ (e.g. on fols 79va, 79vb).
                                    </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
                                  Threads of various origin are inserted in the outer margins in correspondence of the incipit of the weekday readings.
                                  More specifically, a bright red <fo:inline id="d1e36348">leaf string mark</fo:inline> is inserted in the outer margin of fol. 16 and
                                  a piece of textile of the same type is inserted on fol. 17ra. Other coloured or uncoloured <fo:inline id="d1e36355">leaf string markers</fo:inline>
                                  are inserted in the outer margins of fols 20, 40, 61.
                                  A fragment of the same bright red textile used as a leaf tab marker is placed between fol. 16 and fols 17.
                                  A straw from a plant is placed between fol. 68 and fol. 69.
                                <fo:block>A hole from parchment making is found on fol. 54.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is good.
                                    The manuscript shows traces of intensive use.
                                    Some folios have been damaged by humidity and present water stains, especially towards the end of the manuscript. More generally, the conditions of the
                                    manuscript and the readability of the text deteriorate towards the end. The ink is occasionaly smudged (e.g.fols 36, 68, 77).
                                    There are insect holes on the inner side of the upper board, the first and the last folios (fols 1, 82). Insect droppings are also present.
                                    A small loss, possibly a burn, is found on 54. The parchment is deformed on 12 and torn on fol. 26.
                                </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>eighteenth century</fo:inline>
                            The manuscript can be dated palaeographically to the eighteenth century.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>
                            The manuscript was acquired by the collector <fo:inline id="d1e36383PRS13883PhillippsT">Thomas Phillipps</fo:inline> in 1871 from
                            <fo:inline id="d1e36387PRS13027Sturt">
                  <fo:inline font-style="italic">Captain</fo:inline> Sturt</fo:inline>,
                            who had brought it from <fo:inline id="d1e36392LOC3010Ethiop">Ethiopia</fo:inline> in 1868 after <fo:inline id="d1e36398PRS7484Napier">Napier</fo:inline>’s expedition
                            (cp. also e2). It was then assigned ‘23451’ as an inventory number and is described under this number
                            in [Phillipps] 1837,  432.
                           It was purchased by <fo:inline id="d1e36408PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> at auction on 27 November 1974,
                            according to the Sotheby’s sale receipt (lot 642), through the bookseller <fo:inline id="d1e36412PRS13559Thomas">Alan G. Thomas</fo:inline>
                            (cp. Juel-Jensen 1981,  65).
                            The manuscript, including its binding, seems to match the description of the ‘Gospel of John’ offered for sale in
                            Quaritch 1893,  13, but an identification remains speculative.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e36428PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Bibliography</fo:block>Juel-Jensen 1981; [Phillipps] 1837.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethf31">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethf31</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
