               <fo:inline>I-3-23) Fols 141vb–143rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of St George: A pagan woman takes the
                    Eucharist and dies an agonizing death How a pagan woman who received the Eucharist
                    died, CAe 6236.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፳፪፡ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡
                                        <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                                         (b)   ​ወሀ​ለወ​ት፡ ​በሀ​ገር፡ ​እን​ተ፡ ​ዘከ​ርና​ሃ፡ ​ቀዲ​ሙ፡ ​ብእ​ሲት፡ ​አረ​ማዊ​ት፡
                                        ​ወሰ​ይጣ​ን፡ ​ቦአ፡ ​ውስ​ቴታ። ​ወይ​እቲ፡ ​መጽ​አት፡ ​ኀበ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ወዘ​ከመ፡ ​ሞተ​ት፡ ​በዐ​ቢይ፡ ​ምን​ዳቤ።
                                        ​ወእ​ሙን​ቱሰ፡ ​ሶበ፡ ​ሰም​ዑ፡ ​ዘን​ተ፡ ​ኵሎ፡ ​አን​ከሩ፡ ​ጥቀ። ​ወሰ​ብሕ​ዎ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​ስቡ​ሕ፡
                                        ​ወል​ዑል። ​ወለ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ  (b)  ​ስ፡ 
                                        ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡ ​ወበ​ረከ​ቱ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e37925LIT6267MGChurchDoor1">
               <fo:inline>I-3-24) Fols 143rb–144va: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of St George: St George opens the door of
                    his church while the keeper sleeps How St George opened the door of his chapel while
                    the keeper slept, CAe 6267.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፳ወ​፫። ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡ ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡ ​ማር፡ ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ዘገ​ብረ፡
                                        ​በመ​ርጡ​ል፡ ​እን​ተ፡ ​አቅ​ደም​ነ፡ ​ዘክ​ሮታ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                                         (c)   ​ወሀ​ሎ፡ ​በው​እቱ፡ ​ሀገ​ር፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ሳዊ። ​ወፈ​ቀደ፡ ​ያው​ስብ፡ ​ብእ​ሲተ፡
                                        ​ወአ​ስተ​ጋብ​አ፡ ​ብዙ​ኃ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ሥዕ​ሉ፡ ​ብሉ​ይ፡ ​ዘአ​ንበ​ርዎ፡ ​ህየ፡ ​አመ፡
                                        ​ጊዜ፡ ​ሕን​ጸታ፡ ​ለቤ​ተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያኑ። ​ወአ​ንከ​ሩ፡ ​ጥቀ፡ ​እን​በይ​ነ፡ ​ዘር​እዩ፡ ​ወሰ​ብሕ​ዎ፡
                                        ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​ስቡ​ሕ፡ ​ወል​ዑል። ​ወለ​ሰማ​ዕቱ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡ ​ወበ​ረከ​ቱ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e37957LIT6267MGChurchDoor2">
               <fo:inline>I-3-25) Fols 144va–145ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">, CAe 6267.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፳ወ​፬፡ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡
                                        <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline> ​ወሀ​ሎ፡ ​ቤቱ፡ ​ለኤ​ጲስ፡ ​ቆጶ​ስ፡ ​በዛ​ቲ፡
                                        ​መር​ጡል፡ ​ኀበ፡ ​ዴዴ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​ወበ​አሐ​ቲ፡ ​ዕለ​ት፡ ​ረስ​ዑ፡ ​ላዕ​ካኒ​ሁ፡ ​አጺ​ወ፡ ​ኃዋ​ኅወ፡
                                        ​ቤት፡ ​በጊ​ዜ፡ ​ምሴ​ት፡ ​ወኖ​ሙ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ወአ​እመ​ሩ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ሰማ​ዕት፡ ​ኅዱ​ር፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡
                                        ​መር​ጡሉ፡ ​ወኢ​ተፈ​ልጠ፡ ​እም​ኔሃ። ​ወአ​ነ፡ ​አአ​ምሮ፡ ​ለዝ​ንቱ፡ <fo:inline>አ (!)</fo:inline>​ጲስ፡ ​ቆጶ​ስ፡ ​ወው​እቱ፡ ​እም​አዝ​ማድ​የ፡ ​ወሞ​ተ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ሀሎ​ኩ፡ ​አነ፡ ​በህ​የ።
                                        ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡ ​ለዝ​ንቱ፡ ​ሰማ​ዕት፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e37991LIT6269MGSamuel">
               <fo:inline>I-3-26) Fols 145ra–148ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of St George: St Samuel of the monastery of
                    Qalǝmon, and the translation of St George’s body at the time of ʾAbbā Gabriel,
                    Patriarch of Alexandria Concerning Samuel of the monastery of Qalamon, the
                    monks, who used to bring hosts to the church of St George, and the translation
                    of his body at the time of ʾAbbā Gabriel, Patriarch of Alexandria, CAe 6269.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፳፭፡ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡
                                        <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline> ​ወሶ​በ፡ ​ሞተ፡ <fo:inline>ኢ (!)</fo:inline>​ጲስ፡ ​ቆጶ​ስ፡ ​ዘዘ​ከር​ናሁ፡ ​ቀዲ​ሙ፡ ​ተሠ​ይመ፡ ​ህየ​ንቴ​ሁ፡ ​ቀሲ​ስ፡ ​ሚካ​ኤል፡
                                        ​ዘጸ​ሐፍ​ነ፡ ​ስሞ፡ ​ውስ​ተዝ፡ ​መጽ​ሐፍ፡ ​እም​ቀዲ​ሙ። <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                                         (b)   ​ወወ​ሰድ​ዎ፡ ​ኀበ፡ ​ደብ​ረ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ዐቢ​ይ፡ ​መስ​ተጋ​ድል፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ሃይ​ማኖ​ተ፡
                                            ​ኦር​ቶዶ​ክስያ  (c)  ​ዊ፡ ​አባ፡ ​ሳሙ​ኤል፡ ​ዘገ​ዳመ፡ ​ቀል​ሞን፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ወዝ​ንቱ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​ዘኮ​ነ፡ ​በመ​ዋዕ​ለ፡ ​ርስ​ዕና​ሁ፡
                                        ​ለአ​ብ፡ ​ክቡ​ር፡ ​ሊቀ፡ ​ጳጳ​ሳት፡ ​አባ፡ ​ገብ​ርኤ​ል፡ ​ዘው​እቱ፡ ​፹ወ  (c)  ፰ ​በው​ስተ፡
                                        ​ኍላ​ቌሆ​ሙ፡ ​ለአ​በው፡ ​ሊቃ​ነ፡ ​ጳጳ​ሳት። <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                                        ​በሀ​ገረ፡ ​ሳሕ​ረዝ​ት፡ ​ወሀ​ገረ፡ ​ድፍ​ራ። ​ወእ​ምድ​ኅረ፡ ​ሞተ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ሀሎ​ኩ፡ ​አነ፡ ​በህ​የ፡ ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡
                                        ​ለዝ​ንቱ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  የ  (fol. 148ra)  ​ሀሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e38043LIT6272MGChurchInva">
               <fo:inline>I-3-27) Fols 148ra–149rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of St George: Pagans invade a church of St
                    George How pagans invaded the chapel of St George, CAe 6272.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፳፮ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡
                                        <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline> ​ወወ​ሀሎ፡ ​መኰ​ንን፡ ​ዐቢ​ይ፡ ​ዘእ​ምታ​ሕተ፡
                                        ​ንጉ​ሥ። ​ወሖ​ረ፡ ​እም​ጽር​ሐ፡ ​ንጉ​ሥ፡ ​ወቤ​ተ፡ ​ቅሩ​በ፡ ​ቤቱ፡ ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡ ​ማር፡ ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡ ​ወቦ​አ፡
                                            ​ሰይጣ  (b)  ​ን፡ ​ላዕ​ለ፡ ፩ ​ብእ​ሲ፡ ​እም​አረ​ሚ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ወሜ​ጠ፡ ​ሎሙ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያኖ​ሙ፡ ​ወለ​ዕሉ​ሰ፡
                                        ​አረ​ሚ፡ ​ዘበ​ጦሙ፡ ​ወአ​ስተ​ፀዓ​ኖሙ፡ ​ዲበ፡ ​አግ​ማል፡ ​ወአ​ዖዶ​ሙ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ሀገ​ር፡   (b)  
                                        ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ይብ​ል፡ ​ዓዋ​ዲ፡ ​ቅድ​ሜሆ​ሙ፡ ​ዝን​ቱ፡ ​ፍዳ፡ ​ዘይ​ኄይ​ሱ፡ ​ወይ​ብል፡ ​ርኢ​ኩ፡ ​ራእ​የ፡
                                        ​ወእ​ትኔ​በይ፡ ​ትን​ብል​ናሁ፡ ​ለዝ​ንቱ፡ ​ሰማ​ዕት፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e38076LIT6273MGOldChurch">
               <fo:inline>I-3-28) Fols 149rb–149vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of St George: An old church of St George is
                    being replaced with a newly built one but it is immediately destroyed by a
                    storm How the priests of an old church of St George asked
                    the governor to restore it and how he built a new one which was
                    destroyed, CAe 6273.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፳፯ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡
                                        <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                                         (c)   ​ወሀ​ለወ​ት፡ ​አሐ​ቲ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ሕ ን ​ጽት፡ ​በስ​መ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ወይ​እቲ​ሰ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​በል​የት፡
                                        ​ወማ​ሰነ​ት።</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​መጽ​አ፡ ​መን​ፈሰ፡ ​ዐው​ሎ፡ ​ፅኑ​ዕ፡ ​ወገ​ፍዖ፡
                                        ​ለው​እቱ፡ ​ቤት፡ ​ወወ​ዘር​ዎ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ዓየ​ር፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​ቅፅ​ሩ፡ ​ወአ​ልቦ፡ ዘ  (b)  ​ተር​ፈ፡ ​ምን​ትኒ፡ ​እም​ኔሁ፡ ​ወኢ​ተረ ክ ​በ፡
                                        ​ዓሠ​ሩ። ​ወኵ​ሎሙ፡ ​እለ፡ ​ርእ​ዩ፡ ​ተአ​ምረ፡ ​ዘገ​ብረ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​አን​ከሩ፡ ​ወሰ​ብሕ​ዎ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​ስቡ​ሕ፡ ​ወል​ዑል፡ ​ወወ​ደስ​ዎ፡
                                        ​ለሰ​ማዕ​ቱ፡ ​ኃያ​ል፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡
                                            <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e38123LIT6274MGFireHouse">
               <fo:inline>I-3-29) Fols 149vb–150ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of St George: The house of a monk is saved
                    from fire How the house of a monk was saved from fire, CAe 6274.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፳፰ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡
                                        <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                                         (c)   ​ወኮ​ነ፡ ​በ፩​እመ<fo:inline>[ዋ]</fo:inline>​ዕል፡ ​አው​ዓየ፡ ​እሳ​ት፡ ​ቤቶ፡ ​ለ፩​ብእ​ሲ፡ ​በጎ​ሩ፡ ፩ ​መነ​ኮስ።
                                        ​ወተ​መይ​ጠ፡ ​እሳ​ት፡ ​መን​ገለ፡ ​ቤቱ፡ ​ለው​እቱ፡ ​መነ​ኮስ፡ ​ወለ​ወለ​ወ፡ ​ልሳ​ኖ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ወአ​ልዓ​ለ፡ ​በት​ሮ፡ ​ወዘ​በጦ፡ ​ለነ​በል​ባለ፡ ​እሳ​ት፡ ​ወሜ​ጦ፡
                                        ​ፍጡ​ነ፡ ​ወር​እየ፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​መነ​ኮስ፡ ​ወብ​እሲ​ኒ፡ ​ዘው​ዕየ፡ ​ቤቱ። ​ወአ​ንከ​ሩ፡ ​አድ<fo:inline>[ኅ]</fo:inline>​ኖቶ፡ ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡ ​ወበ​ረከ​ቱ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e38160LIT6275MGHeathenArmy">
               <fo:inline>I-3-30) Fols 150ra–150va: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of St George: A governor sees in a dream
                    how he defeats an army of the heathens How the saint helped a Christian chief during a
                    battle against pagans, CAe 6275.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፳፱ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡
                                        <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                                         (b)   ​ወኮ​ነ፡ ​በ፩ ​እመ​ዋዕ​ል፡ ​መጽ​ኡ፡ ​አረ​ሚ፡ ​ብሔ​ረ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​ከመ፡
                                        ​ይጽ​ብዕ​ዎሙ። ​ወር​እየ፡ ፩ ​መኰ​ንን፡ ​በሕ​ልሙ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ወሞ​ቱ፡ ​በኵ​ናት፡ ​ወበ​ጸድ​ፍ፡ ​ወተ​ዘከ​ረ፡
                                        ​ሕል​ም። ​ወአ​እኰ​ቶ፡   (fol. 150va) 
                                         ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ትን​ብል​ናሁ፡
                                        ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e38196LIT6276MGChurchkeeper">
               <fo:inline>I-3-31) Fols 150va–151rc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of St George: A serpent fights with a
                    church keeper How the keeper of a new church was healed after
                    being bitten by a serpent, CAe 6276.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ፴ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡
                                        <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                                         (b)   ​ወሀ​ለወ​ት፡ ​አሐ​ቲ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​ሐዳ​ስ፡ ​እን​ተ፡ ​ሐነ<fo:inline>ጸ (!)</fo:inline>​ዋ፡ ​በስ​መ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ውስ​ተ፡
                                        ​መካ​ን፡ ​ዘነ​በረ፡ ​ማሪ​ት። ​ወበ፩ ​እመዋ<fo:inline>[ዕ]</fo:inline>​ል፡ ​መጽ​አ፡ ​ከይ​ሲ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ወው​እቱ​ሰ፡ ​በዓ​ለ፡ ​ማሪ​ት፡ ​ሞተ፡   (c)   ​በሣ​ልስ​ት፡ ​ዕለ​ት፡ ​በእ​ኩይ፡ ​ሞት፡ ​ወአ​ንከ​ሩ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​ሰብ​አ፡ ​ዕበ​የ፡ ​ኃይ​ሉ፡
                                        ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e38244LIT6277MGSerpentStone">
               <fo:inline>I-3-32) Fols 151rc–151vc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘’ (Miracle of St George: A boy kills a serpent with a
                    stone), CAe 6277.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፴፩ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡
                                        <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                                         (fol. 151va) 
                                         ​ወካ​ዕበ፡ ​በ፩ ​እመ​ዋዕ​ል፡ ​መጽ​አ፡ ​ከይ​ሲ፡ ​ዐቢ​ይ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ይእ​ቲ፡ ​ቤተ፡
                                        ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን። ​ወፀ​ጕረ፡ ​ርእ​ሱ፡ ​ይመ​ስል፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ቈና​ዝዓ፡ ​ብእ​ሲ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ወኮ​ነ፡ ​ኑኁ፡ ​፲ወ፭ ​በእ​መት፡ ​ወስ​ፍሑ፡ ፫ ​በእ​መት፡
                                        ​ወነ​ሥእ​ዎ፡ ​ወሰ​ቀል​ዎ፡ ​ዲበ፡ ​ኦም፡ ​በአ​ፍአ፡ ​እም​ሐፁ​ረ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን። ​ወኵ​ሎሙ፡ ​እለ፡
                                        ​ርእ​ዩ፡ ​ኃይ​ሎ፡ ​ወተ​አም​ሪሁ፡ ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡
                                        ​ወበ​ረከ​ቱ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡<fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e38277LIT6293MGBeerCont">
               <fo:inline>I-3-33) Fols 151vc–152rc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of St George: A beer container falls down a
                    precipice without shattering and without losing a drop How a Christian who was carrying gifts to the
                    church of St George fell without breaking the vessels, CAe 6293.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፴፪ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡
                                        <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                                         (fol. 152ra) 
                                         ​ወሀ​ለወ​ት፡ ​አሐ​ቲ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​ሕን​ጽት፡ ​በስ​ሙ፡ ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ወጥ​ቃሃ፡ ​ለቤ​ተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​ሀሎ፡ ​ዐቢ​ይ፡
                                        ​ጸድ​ፍ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ወል​ሕኵ​ቱሂ፡ ​ኢተ​ጐድ​ዓ። ​ወዓ​ዲ፡ ​ኢተ​ርኅ​ወ፡
                                        ​ማኅ​ተሙ፡ ​ወም​ዝሩ፡ ​ኢተክ ዕ ​ወ፡ ​ወኢ​ሂ፡ ​ነጠ​በ፡ ​ንስ​ቲተ። ​ወሶ​በ፡ ​ርእ​ዩ፡ ​ዘን​ተ፡ ​መን​ክረ፡
                                        ​አስ​ተብ​ፅዕ​ዎ፡ ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡ ​ወበ​ረከ​ቱ፡
                                        ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e38316LIT6294MGWetDream">
               <fo:inline>I-3-34) Fols 152rc–152vc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of St George: How St George takes away his
                    image from a monk who wears it on his neck after a wet dream How St George tore his image from a monk who used
                    to wear it on his neck, after a wet dream, CAe 6294.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፴፫ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡
                                        <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline> ​ወሀ​ሎ፡ ​፩፡ ​መነ​ኮስ፡ ​ወአ​ጥረ​የ፡ ​ሎቱ፡
                                        ​ሥዕ​ለ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ወኮ​ነ፡ ​ይፀ​ውሮ፡ ​ለው​እቱ፡
                                        ​ሥዕ​ል፡ ​መዓ​ልተ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ክሳ​ዱ፡ ​ወሌ​ሊተ፡ ​ይሰ​ቅሎ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ማኅ​ደሩ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ወይ​ቤሉ፡ ​በበ​ይና​ቲሆ​ሙ፡ ​እም​ይእ​ዜሰ፡
                                        ​ንተ​ዓቀ​ብ፡ ​እም​ፀዊ​ረ፡ ​ሥዕ​ል፡   (c)   ​ዘእ​ንበ​ለ፡ ​ነጺ​ሐነ፡ ​ወፈ​ቲነ​ነ፡ ​ርእ​ሰነ፡
                                        ​በተ​ጠና​ቅቆ። ​ትን​ብል​ናሁ፡ ​ለዝ​ንቱ፡ ​ሰማ​ዕት፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ወት​ረ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e38350LIT6295MGEgypKing">
               <fo:inline>I-3-35) Fols 152vc–153vc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of St George: St George strikes down an
                    Egyptian king after he came with his wife to make abode in a new church devoted to
                    the saint How an Egyptian king who usurped a church of St
                    George died after the saint appeared to him, CAe 6295.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፴፬ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡
                                        <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                                         (fol. 153ra) 
                                        ​ወሀ​ሎ፡ ፩ ​ብእ​ሲ፡ ​በም​ድር፡ ​ግብ​ጽ፡ ​ዘያ​ፈቅ​ሮ፡ ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​እም​ኵሉ፡ ​ልቡ፡ ​ወእ​ምብ​ዝኃ፡ ​ፍቅ​ሩ፡ ​ሐነ​ጸ፡
                                        ​ሎቱ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​ዐባ​የ፡ ​ወሠ​ናይ​ተ፡ ​ጥቀ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ወእ​ምዝ፡ ​አብ​ኡ፡ ​ታቦ​ተ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ቤተ፡
                                        ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​እን​ተ፡ ​ተሐ​ንጸ​ት፡ ​በስ​መ፡ ​ሰማ​ዕት፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​በፍ​ሥሐ፡ ​ወበ​ሐሤ​ት፡ ​ወበ​ማኅ​ሌት፡ ​ወበ​ዝማ​ሬ። ​ወሰ​ብሕ​ዎ፡
                                        ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​ዘአ​ርአ​የ፡ ​ኃይ​ሎ፡   (c)   ​በእ​ደ፡ ​ሰማ​ዕት፡ ​ኃያ​ል፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ትን​ብል​ናሁ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e38392LIT6296MGLampWave">
               <fo:inline>I-3-36) Fols 153vc–154vc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of St George: A lamp reaches the church on
                    a wave whereupon the head of the army entrusts himself to the saint and wins the
                    battle How a lamp promised to the church of St George
                    moved from a boat and floated to the keeper of the church, CAe 6296.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፴፭ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡ ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡ ​ማር፡ ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ዘገ​ብረ፡ ​ይእ​ዜ፡
                                        ​በቤ​ተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​ዘብ​ላ፡ ​ኀበ፡ ​ሥጋ​ሁ። <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                                         (fol. 154ra) 
                                        ​ወበ<fo:inline>[አ]</fo:inline>​ሐቲ፡ ​እመ​ዋዕ​ል፡ ​ወጽ​አ፡ ​ርእ​ሰ፡ ​ሠራ​ዊት፡ ​ዘን​ጉሥ፡ ​ግብ​ጽ፡ ​ከመ፡
                                        ​ይፃ​ባዕ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ጸላ​እቱ። ​ወም​ስሌ​ሁ፡ ፶ ​አህ​ማር፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ወዓ​ዲ፡ ​ንግ​ር፡ ​ለነ፡ ​ለን​ጉሥ፡ ​ንሕ​ንጽ፡
                                        ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​ዘቅ​ዱስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ወወ​ሀቦ​ሙ፡
                                        ​ምድ​ረ፡ ​ዘአ​ጥረ​የ፡ ​ለር​እሱ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ይዝ​ርኡ፡ ​ወይ​ሕየ​ው፡   (c)   ​ባቲ፡ ​ወሀ​ለወ​ት፡
                                        ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ዮም፡ ​ትን​ብል​ናሁ፡ ​ለዝ​ንቱ፡ ​ሰማ​ዕት፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e38435LIT6297MGFishernet">
               <fo:inline>I-3-37) Fols 154vc–155rc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of St George: St George and St Behnam help
                    a fisherman pulling his net full of fish How St George and Mar Behnam repaired the net of a
                    fisherman, CAe 6297.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፴፮፡ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡
                                        <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                                         (fol. 155ra) 
                                        ​ወሀ​ሎ፡ ፩ ​ብእ​ሲ፡ ​መሠ​ግረ፡ ​ዓሣ፡ ​ወወ​ደየ፡ ​መር​በብ​ቶ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ባሕ​ር፡
                                            ​ወተ<fo:inline>[እ]</fo:inline>​ኅዘ፡
                                        ​ዓሣ፡ ​ብዙ​ኅ። ​ወሶ​በ፡ ​ሰሐ​በ፡ ​ተበ​ትከ፡ ​መሥ​ገር​ቱ፡ ​ወከ​ልሃ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ይብ​ል፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​መር​ምህ​ናም፡
                                        ​ርድ​አኒ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ወር​እየ፡ ​ኃይ​ለ፡ ​ረድ​ኤቱ፡ ​ወፈ​ድፋ​ደ፡ ​ክብ​ሩ፡
                                        ​ለሰ​ማዕ​ት፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​በከ​መ፡ ​ይት​ፌኖ፡
                                        ​ረድ​ኤት፡   (c)   ​ኀበ፡ ​ጸው​ዕዎ​ሙ፡ ​ለካ​ልአ​ኒሁ፡ ​ሰማ​ዕታ​ት፡ ​ወዘ​ከመ​ሂ፡ ​አዕ​በዮ፡
                                        ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​መር​ምህ​ናም፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ይብ​ል፡ ​እግ​ዚእ​የ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡ ወ<fo:inline>[በ]</fo:inline>​ረከ​ቱ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e38481LIT6298MGMostVenerated">
               <fo:inline>I-3-38) Fols 155rc–156ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of St George: A virtuous monk witnesses
                    that St George is the most venerated of all saints How a monk saw St George in golden shoes, CAe 6298.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፴፯ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡
                                        <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                                         (fol. 155va) 
                                        ​ወኮ​ነ፡ ​በ፩ ​እመ​ዋዕ​ል፡ ​ተበ​ሃሉ፡ ​ሰብ​እ፡ ​መሃ​ይም​ናን፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዜና​ሆሙ፡
                                        ​ለቅ​ዱሳ​ን፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ተና​ገሩ፡ ​ዕበ​ያቲ​ሁ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​አማ​ንኬ፡ ​ይደ​ልዎ፡ ​አሣ​ዕነ፡ ​ወር​ቅ፡
                                        ​ለባ​ሕቲ​ቱ፡ ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ህየ​ንተ፡ ​አሣ​ዕነ፡
                                            ሐ  (fol. 156ra)  ​ፂን፡ ​ዘአ​ስተ​ሰዓ​ንዎ፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ተመ​ትረ፡ ​አሥ​ራወ፡
                                        ​እገ​ሪሁ፡ ​ወተ​ክዕ​ወ፡ ​ደሙ፡ ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡ ​ወበ​ረከ​ቱ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e38520LIT6299MGEgg">
               <fo:inline>I-3-39) Fols 156ra–156rc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of St George: During the decoration of St
                    George’s church, an egg falls from the top without breaking  How during the decoration of St George’s church an
                    egg fell from the top and did not break, CAe 6299.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፴፰ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡
                                        <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline> ​ወኮ​ነ፡ ​በ፩ ​እመ​ዋዕ​ል፡   (b)   ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ይሥ​ዕሉ፡ ​ሥዕ​ላተ፡ ​ወያ​ሠረ​ግው፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያኑ፡ ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ወ፩፡ ​ብእ​ሲ፡ ​ወሀ​በ፡ ​ዶር​ሆ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ወሠ​ፈሩ፡ ​ኒኆ፡ ​ለው​እቱ፡ ​ተስ​ላስ፡ ​እም​ኀበ፡ ​ወድ​ቀ፡ ​ወኮ​ነ፡
                                        ​ኑኁ፡ ​እም​ድር፡ ፭ ​እመ​ተ፡ ​ሥዝ​ረ፡ ​ወስ​ፍሑ፡ ፫ ​አፃ​ብዓ፡ ​ወአ​ንከ​ሩ፡ ​ኃይ​ለ፡ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡ ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡
                                        ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡ ​ወበ​ረከ​ቱ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e38554LIT6300MGPainter">
               <fo:inline>I-3-40) Fols 156rc–156vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of St George: A painter falls from the top
                    of the church and remains unharmed and his colour container intact How a man who was decorating the church fell and
                    was not injured, CAe 6300.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፴፱ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡
                                        <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                                         (fol. 156va)   ​ወካ​ዕበ፡ ​በአ​ሐቲ፡ ​ዕለ​ት፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ይእ​ቲ፡ ​ቤተ፡
                                        ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​ዓር​ገ፡ ​ዲበ፡ ​ተስ​ላስ፡ ​ልዑ​ል፡ ​ብእ​ሲ፡ ​መስ​ተገ​ብረ፡ ​ሥዕ​ል፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ያሰ​ኒ፡ ​ግብ​ረ፡ ​እደዊ<fo:inline>ሆሙ (!)</fo:inline>። ​ወተ​ሰብ​ረ፡ ​ዕፀ፡ ​ተስ​ላስ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ተን​ሥአ፡ ​ፍጡ​ነ፡ ​ወኢ​ነክ​ዮ፡ ​ምን​ተኒ፡ ​ወን​ዋየ፡ ​ቀለ​ምሂ፡
                                        ​አል​ቦ፡ ​ዘተ​ጐድ​ዓ። ​ወአ​ንከ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ብእ​ሲ፡ ​ወኵ​ሎሙ፡ ​እለ፡ ​ርእ​ዩ፡ ​አድ​ኅኖ​ቶ፡ ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡ ​ወበ​ረከ​ቱ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e38597LIT6301MGNewChurch">
               <fo:inline>I-3-41) Fols 156vb–157va: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of St George: A newly built church does not
                    correspond to the will of the saint and is replaced How a church built in honour of St George was
                    rebuilt by a miracle, CAe 6301.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፵፡ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡  ​ወበ፩ ​እመ​ዋዕ​ል፡ ​ሐነ​ጹ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡
                                        ​ዐባ​የ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                                         (c)   ​በስ​መ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡ ​ወፈ​ጸመ፡ ​በሠ​ናይ፡ ​ፃሕ​ቅ፡ ​እስ​መ፡ ​ርኡ​ሰ፡ ​ይእ​ቲ፡
                                        ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​መስ​ተሐ​ምም፡ ​ጥቀ፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​ግበ​ሪሁ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ወእ​መሂ፡ ​ምድ​ራ፡ ​ወእ​መሂ፡ ​ካህ​ናቲ​ሃ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡
                                        ​ይብ​ሉ፡   (fol. 157va)   ​ይኩ​ን፡ ​መክ​ፈል​ቱ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ሲሞ​ን፡ ​መሠ​ርይ፡
                                        ​ወይ​ሁዳ፡ ​ረሲ​ዕ። ​ወተ​ዘከ​ረ፡ ​ውእ​ተ፡ ​ራእ​የ፡ ​ወአ​እኰ​ቶ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​ስቡ​ሕ፡ ​ወል​ዑል፡
                                        ​ወቅ​ዱስ​ሰ፡ ​ማር፡ ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡ ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡ ​ወበ​ረከ​ቱ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e38628LIT6302MGGold">
               <fo:inline>I-3-42) Fols 157va–162rc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of St George: A priest and his son rebuild
                    an old church of St George and find gold hidden in the old building, CAe 6302.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፵፩፡ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡
                                        <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                                         (b)   ​ወሀ​ሎ፡ ፩ ​ብእ​ሲ፡ ​ካህ​ን፡ ​ዘእ​ምቤ​ተ፡ ​ካህ​ናት፡ ​ዘይ​ትአ​መን፡ ​በእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡
                                        ​ወበ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡ ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ወይ​ሴፎ፡ ​ወት​ረ፡
                                        ​ረድ​ኤቶ፡ ​በፍ​ሥሐ​ሁ፡ ​ወበ​ምን​ዳቤ​ሁ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ወእ​ምይ​እቲ፡ ​ዕለ​ት፡ ​ኮነ፡ ​ይሁ​ብ፡ ​ንጉ​ሥ፡ ​መባ​ዓ፡ ​ለካ​ህን፡
                                        ​ከመ፡ ​ይግ​በር፡ ​በዓ​ሎ፡ ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ርእ​ዩኬ፡
                                        ​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ድኅ​ኑ፡ ​ደቂ​ቀ፡ ​ካህ​ን፡ ​በጸ​ሎቱ፡ ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡ ​ብፁ​ዓዊ፡ ​ማር፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  ​ምእ​መን። ​ከማ​ሁ፡ ​ያድ​ኅኖ፡ ​እመ​ሥገ​ርተ፡ ​እኩ​ያት፡ ​ለፍ​ቁሩ፡ <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e38666LIT6303MGJoseph">
               <fo:inline>I-3-43) Fols 162rc–162vc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of St George: Joseph, a young man from
                    Mount Lebanon, is being rescued by St George near Beirut, incomplete, CAe 6303.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The miracle stops abruptly on fol. 162vc in
                                        the middle of a word.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​፵፪፡ ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሁ፡
                                        <fo:inline>(...)</fo:inline>
                                         (fol. 162va)   ​ወሀ​ሎ፡ ፩ ​ብእ​ሲ፡ ​ዘስ​ሙ፡ ​ዮሴ​ፍ፡ ​ወስ​መ፡ ​አቡ​ሁ፡
                                        ​ስዑ​ድ፡ ​ዘበ​ትር​ጓሜ​ሁ፡ ​ክቡ​ር፡ ​ብሂ​ል፡ ​ወስ​መ፡ ​ለእ​ሙ፡ ​ጌን​ያ፡ ​ዘበ​ትር​ጓሜ​ሁ፡ ​ባዕ​ልት፡ ​ብሂ​ል።
                                        ​ወየ​ኃድ​ሩ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​አድ​ባረ፡ ​ሊባ​ኖስ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Additional notes</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 4r: Ownership note written in black ink in the
                                        upper margin, stating that the manuscript belonged to
                                            <fo:inline id="d1e39647INS0101MadhaneAlam">Madḫāne ʿĀlam</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ገድ​ለ፡ ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡ ​ዘቅ​ዱስ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e39652INS0101MadhaneAlam">​መድ​ኃኔ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡</fo:inline>
                        </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Scribal corrections by the main hand are rare. The scribe
                                        occasionally added a missing word interlineally (e.g. fol. 136rc), he marked a dittographical error
                                        with thin strokes above and below the words on fol. 106rb (in the same way as the numerals are
                                        marked). Other corrections were most likely made by later
                                        hands. Superfluous words were washed out carelessly at the
                                        beginning of the codex (e.g. on 5vc, 6ra, 6vc). Missing characters and words
                                        were interlineally inserted, sometimes with a thin nib (e.g.
                                            fols 51va, 110vc, 146rb). Words or
                                        passages erroneously written twice (dittographies) were
                                        encircled with a thin line (e.g. 40vc, 133va, 134ra). Erased words in the upper margin of 149va.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Spaces left for rubricated names were occasionally left unfilled
                                        (as on fols 118rv,  or on 126vc).</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Writing exercise by the main hand in yellow paint on fol. 52vc.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 1r, :  A white sticker, with the name of <fo:inline id="d1e39699PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> (‘<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቤን​ት፡
                                            ​ዩው​ል፡ ​የን​ሰን።</fo:inline>’) printed, is glued on fol. ir. Other stickers displaying the signature
                                        ‘Ms 2’ are glued below (probably a sticker with another
                                        number 2, once resulting in 22, is fallen off). A note ‘No
                                        41. Georges’ is written in pencil (?) below.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                                    The book is bound in wooden boards covered with reddish-brown blind-tooled leather. The inner sides of the front and back boards are decorated with silk textile <fo:inline id="d1e39725">inlays</fo:inline>
                                    of Indian origin with floral pattern in blue, white, yellow, and red colour (Crill 2026,  172).
                                  
                                    The boards are cut to the same size as the bookblock and present external shallow bevels.
                                  
                                    Full reddish-brown leather cover.
                                    The turn-ins have been trimmed out and at the corners they form butt mitres.
                                    An <fo:inline id="d1e39742">additional leather patch</fo:inline> has been added along the inner margin of the boards to fill the gap between the turn-ins.
                                    Between the bookblock and the back board is a fragment of brown leather decorated with criss-cross motifs, which does not belong
                                    to this binding.
                                    On the back board, an additional leather patch has been added to increase the width of the narrow fore-edge turn-in.
                                    The cover shows a fine blind-tooled decoration, identical on both sides of the cover. The turn-ins and the edges are also decorated.
                                    The decoration consists of nine concentric frames surrounding a central rectangular panel featuring a Latin cross.
                                    Frames composed by the repetition of single tools, enclosed between <fo:inline id="d1e39745">triple straight lines</fo:inline>,
                                    alternate with empty ones.
                                    Proceeding from the outer to the inner frame, the repeating decoration motifs are <fo:inline id="d1e39748">criss-cross</fo:inline> (in two variants),
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e39751">wavy lines</fo:inline>, <fo:inline id="d1e39754">curve strapwork</fo:inline>, and <fo:inline id="d1e39758">straight strapwork</fo:inline> elements.
                                    The cross is formed by <fo:inline id="d1e39761">X-form</fo:inline> motifs between <fo:inline id="d1e39764">single straight lines</fo:inline>.
                                    At the ends of the arms of the cross there are pairs of <fo:inline id="d1e39767">crescents</fo:inline> disposed to resemble a corniform motif,
                                    and three <fo:inline id="d1e39770">double circles</fo:inline>.
                                    Double circles are also stamped at the intersections of the triple straight lines.
                                    In the areas at the foot of the cross, the triple straight lines form two triangles each surmounted by three double circles.
                                    Triple straight lines arranged diagonally decorate the turn-ins. On the spine, they cross each other diagonally, forming a diamond pattern
                                    which encloses double circles. Double circles decorate the edges of the boards as well.
                                  
                                    Brown <fo:inline id="d1e39776">slit-braid</fo:inline> endbands are present.
                                  
                                    Chainstitch sewing on four sewing stations (two pairs); periodic fold pattern; Z-plied threads.
                                    Between each pair of sewing stations there are two lengths of thread.
                                  
                                    The spine is formed by two overlapping layers of leather. The endbands are sewn through the first layer so that
                                    the tie-downs are hidden under the second layer.
                                  </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Pencil foliation in the upper right corner (1–163). The first folio is not foliated. It is referred to as
                                    fol. i in this description.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm">
                                        Quire marks are written in the upper inner margin of
                                        the recto of the first folio of each quire with black ink,
                                        with the exception of the first quire mark, which is written in red. Some quire marks are
                                        decorated in a simple manner, partly with red elements.
                                    </fo:block>
         <fo:block>22 quires. A<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2+2 (Fols ir–3v)</fo:inline> – I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 4r–11v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 12r–19v)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6 (Fols 20r–25v)</fo:inline> – IV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">4+3 (Fols 26r–32v)</fo:inline> – V<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 33r–40v)</fo:inline> – VI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 41r–48v)</fo:inline> – VII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 49r–56v)</fo:inline> – VIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 57r–64v)</fo:inline> – IX<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 65r–72v)</fo:inline> – X<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 73r–80v)</fo:inline> – XI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 81r–88v)</fo:inline> – XII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 89r–96v)</fo:inline> – XIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 97r–104v)</fo:inline> – XIV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 105r–112v)</fo:inline> – XV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 113r–120v)</fo:inline> – XVI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 121r–128v)</fo:inline> – XVII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6 (Fols 129r–134v)</fo:inline> – XVIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 135r–142v)</fo:inline> – XIX<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6 (Fols 143r–148v)</fo:inline> – XX<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 149r–156v)</fo:inline> – XXI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6+1 (Fols 157r–163v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 4ra–162vc: 3
                                    columns (20 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin
                                        dimensions taken from fol. 52r.The characters per line are 7–9.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            395 × 332 mm (fol. 52r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            266 × 255 mm (fol. 52r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 50 mm, bottom: 91 mm, right: 60 mm, left: 25 mm, intercolumn: 25 mm (fol. 52r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible
                                        (except on fols 1r–2v). Primary pricks are visible. Ruling pricks are mostly visible.  The upper and bottom lines are written above the
                                        ruling. Ruling pattern (fols 1r–2v fols 4r–163v): and 1A-1A-1A1A-1A1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Mid-eighteenth–mid-nineteenth century.. Trained handwriting, characterised by finely
                                    shaped, slender, and regularly spaced characters. Presumably due
                                    to the change of nib, the writing appears somewhat irregular
                                    from fol. 144v onward.<fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: 
                                    Several groups of lines on the incipit pages of all texts; initial two lines
                                    of the sections of all parts; the names of <fo:inline id="d1e39080PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline> and
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e39083PRS6819Mary">St Mary</fo:inline>; names of
                                    individuals related to the production of the manuscript;
                                    the words <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ክፍ​ል፡</fo:inline> and <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ምዕ​ራፍ፡</fo:inline> in the <fo:inline font-style="italic">Vita</fo:inline> of St George;
                                    elements of the punctuation marks, text dividers, and numerals
                                    on some folios (e.g. fols 19v–22r and more
                                    regularly from fols 128r onward) partly executed in
                                    a darker tone of red (cp. fol. 150rb).
                                </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Decoration</fo:block>
         <fo:block margin-top="3mm" margin-bottom="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">
  The manuscript contains 39 framed miniatures in the <fo:inline id="d1e39111">Zamana Masāfǝnt Style</fo:inline>
  that appear to have been executed by the same hand. The style of the miniatures bears comparison with that of manuscripts
  such as <fo:inline/> and <fo:inline/>
  that can be dated to a period between <fo:inline>1730 and 1847</fo:inline>.
  This piece is part of a group of manuscripts, which includes <fo:inline/>,
  that are extensively illustrated with scenes inspired by the life and miracles of St George (<inline xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Format">‘George of Lydda: Iconography of St. George in Ethiopia’, <inline font-style="italic">EAe</inline>, II (2005), 764b–766b (E. Balicka-Witakowska)</inline>;
  Bosc-Tiessé 2008,  145–169).
  These manuscripts await systematic study, but the iconographic similarities between them and this piece appear quite limited after a preliminary survey.
  The identification of the miniatures that accompany the Miracles (fols 86ra–162vc).
  is hindered by the lack of captions and by the fact that the scenes do not always appear
  to be directly related to the texts they illustrate. Further difficulties arise from the inconsistent use of attributes:
    <fo:inline id="d1e39133PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline>, for example, at times has no halo,
  whereas in other scenes the halo is rendered with a pattern of dots or a plain line. Evil characters are consistently shown in profile.
  There is a great variety of layouts, with some images taking up a full-page and others only half of one of the three columns of text
  (e.g. fols 97v, 118r). Moreover, some of the full-page miniatures feature more than one episode while others present a single iconic portrait.
  Most of the miniatures were at some time protected by curtains, but only fragments of fabric survive (fols 139v, 147r).
  A horse is crudely drawn on fol. iv, whereas a well-trained hand has drawn a scene with <fo:inline id="d1e39143PRS5684JesusCh">Jesus Christ</fo:inline> on fol. 3r.
</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Miniatures</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(27) Fol. 11r: <fo:inline>
     The miniature is divided into three episodes. In the upper register a group of figures mourn over the shrouded body,
     presumably the father of St George. Below, to the right,
       <fo:inline id="d1e39154PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline> is enthroned like a bishop to signal his rank; to the left
     the saint travels with an armed entourage (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(28) Fol. 14r: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e39167PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline>  on horseback slays the dragon (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(29) Fol. 22v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e39179PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline>
     and his followers travelling in a boat to meet <fo:inline id="d1e39182PRS3283Dadyanos">Dādyānos</fo:inline> (two-column).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(30) Fol. 24v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e39192PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline> bound to a tree and pierced by nails (two-column).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(31) Fol. 29r: <fo:inline>
     The miniature presents three episodes and is divided in half.
     In the left half eight men roll a pillar over <fo:inline id="d1e39204PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline>.
     In the upper register of right half two men scourge the fettered saint; in the lower register he is thrown
     on a fiery gridiron (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(32) Fol. 29v: <fo:inline>
     The miniature features four separate episodes. In the first, <fo:inline id="d1e39215PRS2215Athanasi">Athanasius the magician</fo:inline> splits
     an ox into two perfect halves in front of <fo:inline id="d1e39217PRS3283Dadyanos">Dādyānos</fo:inline>. In the second, he gives
       a poisonous cup to  <fo:inline id="d1e39219PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline>. In the third, he is baptized
     as a result of seeing the saint unharmed by his potion. In the fourth, he is martyred by decapitation (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(33) Fol. 35r: <fo:inline>
     To the left the governors in a palace look at <fo:inline id="d1e39230PRS7049Michael">St Michael</fo:inline> who has gathered
       the severed body parts of <fo:inline id="d1e39233PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline>. The saint appears to the right of the scene,
     he is bound upside down to a tree and has a rock attached to his neck (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(34) Fol. 35v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e39244PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline> is boiled in a cauldron and
     then torn into pieces, but at night he has a vision of <fo:inline id="d1e39247PRS5684JesusCh">Jesus Christ</fo:inline>
     in a cloud (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(35) Fol. 38v: <fo:inline>
       The miniature features three episodes. First, <fo:inline id="d1e39257PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline>
         has a vision of <fo:inline id="d1e39260PRS5684JesusCh">Jesus Christ</fo:inline> in a cloud; then, he is mauled by men holding adzes;
         and, finally, his head is set ablaze (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(36) Fol. 42r: <fo:inline>
       Above, two torturers hit <fo:inline id="d1e39270PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline>
      with spiked instruments; below, two men hammer metal rods into his head (two-columns).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(37) Fol. 42v: <fo:inline>
       To the left, two torturers carry <fo:inline id="d1e39282PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline>
      by means of a pole inside a palace; while to the right the saint prays while comforted by <fo:inline id="d1e39285PRS5684JesusCh">Jesus Christ</fo:inline> (two-columns).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(38) Fol. 46v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e39295PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline> has miraculously transformed the wooden pillar of the house
      of a poor widow into a tree and, with the help of <fo:inline id="d1e39298PRS7049Michael">St Michael</fo:inline>,
       has filled her table with food. The poor woman stands to the right with her child in her arms (two-columns).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(39) Fol. 50r: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e39309PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline> appears twice upon a mountain. Below, he is burned
      by a fiery furnace, while two men scatter his ashes to the wind; above, the saint, risen up from the dead,
      confronts the king’s four evil attendants (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(40) Fol. 50v: <fo:inline>
       There are three episodes. Above, <fo:inline id="d1e39320PRS5684JesusCh">Jesus Christ</fo:inline> has brought <fo:inline id="d1e39322PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline>
       back to life. Below, to the left, St George baptizes the four jailers turned Christian after his miraculous recovery
       in a pool at the foot of a hill surmounted by a Gondarene castle; to the right, an executioner has cut off their heads (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(41) Fol. 53r: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e39333PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline> is subjected to further torturers (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(42) Fol. 63v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e39344PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline>, accompanied by the son
      of the poor widow who can now miraculously walk, casts the statue of Apollo into the pit of Hell under the gaze of
      <fo:inline id="d1e39347PRS3283Dadyanos">Dādyānos</fo:inline> and other pagan kings (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(43) Fol. 90r: <fo:inline>
     A man, presumably
       <fo:inline id="d1e39358PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline>, is boiled in brazen ox and sawn in half. He appears a third time before <fo:inline id="d1e39361PRS5684JesusCh">Jesus Christ</fo:inline> (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(44) Fol. 93v: <fo:inline>
     A man, presumably
       <fo:inline id="d1e39371PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline>, is tortured inside a building. He appears a second time before <fo:inline id="d1e39374PRS5684JesusCh">Jesus Christ</fo:inline> (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(45) Fol. 94v: <fo:inline>
     A couple of donors, probably to be identified
     as the children of <fo:inline id="d1e39387PRS13193Giyorgis">Giyorgis</fo:inline>,
     pray towards the scene on the opposite page (half-column).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(46) Fol. 95r: <fo:inline>
       There are three scenes. In the first, <fo:inline id="d1e39397PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline> is impaled; in the second he
     beholds <fo:inline id="d1e39400PRS5684JesusCh">Jesus Christ</fo:inline>; in the third he is stabbed by daggers. A pair of
     <fo:inline id="d1e39402">donors</fo:inline>, presumably <fo:inline id="d1e39405PRS13193Giyorgis">Giyorgis</fo:inline> and his wife <fo:inline id="d1e39407PRS13194AmataSell">ʾAmata Śǝllāse</fo:inline>, lie in proskynesis at the bottom of the page (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(47) Fol. 97v: <fo:inline>
     A couple of donors, probably to be identified
     as <fo:inline id="d1e39420PRS13193Giyorgis">Giyorgis</fo:inline> who embraces his child <fo:inline id="d1e39422PRS13196WaldaMik">Walda Mikāʾel</fo:inline>,
     pray towards the scene on the opposite page (half-column).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(48) Fol. 98r: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e39432PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline> is trampled by a horse;
    an icon-like panel above the scene shows <fo:inline id="d1e39435PRS5684JesusCh">Jesus Christ</fo:inline> embracing a soul (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(49) Fol. 99v: <fo:inline>
       The kings observe buds sprouting from one of their thrones on which <fo:inline id="d1e39446PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline>
    is seated (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(50) Fol. 103r: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e39457PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline> converses with a king shown in profile, this may be the episode where he fools
     <fo:inline id="d1e39460PRS3283Dadyanos">Dādyānos</fo:inline> into believing that he will sacrifice to his gods (two-columns).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(51) Fol. 103v: <fo:inline>
       There are two scenes. In the upper register <fo:inline id="d1e39470PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline> converses with a figure shown in profile;
     in the lower register a naked and bleeding woman with a loincloth is dragged by a mounted king. This is probably a representation of the
     conversion and martyrdom of <fo:inline id="d1e39473PRS12089Alexandra">Alexandra</fo:inline> (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(52) Fol. 105v: <fo:inline>
     Three enthroned kings observe the hanging of <fo:inline id="d1e39483PRS12089Alexandra">Alexandra</fo:inline> (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(53) Fol. 109v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e39493PRS12089Alexandra">Alexandra</fo:inline> is beheaded (two-columns, L-shaped frame).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(54) Fol. 105v: <fo:inline>
     A woman is baptized by an unidentified figure. <fo:inline id="d1e39503PRS5684JesusCh">Jesus Christ</fo:inline>
     observes the scenes from above. A second woman in an attitude of prayer observes the scene in the company
     of a smaller figure with a beard who holds onto her robe. His features and attire are similar to those of the donor
     on fol. 97v
      (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(55) Fol. 113v: <fo:inline>
     An angel gazes from the clouds upon a figure in prayer, probably St George, to bottom left of the scene. The same figure appears
     a second time to the right with blood pouring out of his mouth
      (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(56) Fol. 118r: <fo:inline>
     A couple of unidentified donors
     turn their gaze towards the scene on the verso (half-column).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(57) Fol. 118v: <fo:inline>
       The scene features two episodes. Below an angel collects the severed head of <fo:inline id="d1e39534PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline>.
      Above, the saint is welcomed in heaven by <fo:inline id="d1e39537PRS5684JesusCh">Jesus Christ</fo:inline> who crowns him.
     A group of angels in the clouds surround the pair, while six more crowns hover in the sky behind
     St George to indicate his years of torture (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(58) Fol. 122r: <fo:inline>
     Two unidentified figures stand inside a church, these could be donors or figures connected
     with the miracles of St George (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(59) Fol. 122v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e39556PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline>  on horseback
      interacts with a standing and unidentified figure in prayer (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(60) Fol. 127r: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e39568PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline> blinds the Emperor
        <fo:inline id="d1e39571PRS3581Diocleti">Diocletian</fo:inline>
       (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(61) Fol. 127v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e39582PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline> and
      <fo:inline id="d1e39585PRS7049Michael">St Michael</fo:inline>
      crown <fo:inline id="d1e39588PRS3175Constant">Constantine I</fo:inline> emperor
       (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(62) Fol. 138r: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e39598PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline> leads a youth
      into a church, probably that of Bǝbā (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(63) Fol. 139v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e39609PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline> and another
      saint on horseback ride forth from a church towards a blind person (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(64) Fol. 142r: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e39620PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline> rescues a group
      of people on a boat (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(65) Fol. 147r: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e39631PRS4585Georgeo">St George</fo:inline> kills a pagan as punishment
       for breaking a lamp in his church in Cairo (full-page).
   </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Headpieces</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Drawings</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Other</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Holes resulting from parchment making have been carefully repaired by sewing, e.g. on fols 1, 38, 123.
                                    Smaller holes have not been repaired, e.g. on 10, 30, 120.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is good.
                                  The manuscript has a few losses along the margins of the leaves and deformations caused by humidity.
                                  Some folios have water stains (e.g. fols 41r–42v, , 108r–121r). The
                                  headband is broken, the tailband torn off. The leather cover is torn on the spine.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
                          <!--SH proposed 1600 as lowest starting date, but JG
                          assuming that miniatures are near coeval, would
                          consider 1750-1850 (and ca. 1800 esp) more likely.
                        -->
               <fo:inline>mid-eighteenth–mid-nineteenth century</fo:inline>
                            The
                            date of production – taking into account the handwriting and the
                            style of the miniatures – can
                            be set to the period between the mid-eighteenth and mid-nineteenth century. The name of <fo:inline id="d1e39802PRS13193Giyorgis">Giyorgis</fo:inline> is mentioned in the supplication formulas
                            throughout the manuscript following the phrase <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ገብ​ርከ፡ </fo:inline> ‘your servant’. This person was either the patron,
                            the owner, the donor or the scribe of the manuscript. Names of members
                            of his family are often stated along with him: his wife <fo:inline id="d1e39808PRS13194AmataSell">ʾAmata Śǝllāse</fo:inline> and his children
                                <fo:inline id="d1e39812PRS13195GadlaGiyorgis">Gadla Giyorgis</fo:inline>,
                                <fo:inline id="d1e39815PRS13196WaldaMik">Walda Mikāʾel</fo:inline>, and
                                <fo:inline id="d1e39818PRS13197WalattaMik">Walatta Mikāʾel
                            </fo:inline>.</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript must have come into the possession of the church
                            of <fo:inline id="d1e39824INS0101MadhaneAlam">Maqdala Madḫāne ʿĀlam</fo:inline> at a certain
                            time in its history from where it was probably looted on 13 April 1868
                            (see Additional note 1) and brought to England. It seems to match the description
                             of the  ‘Acts of St. George the Martyr’ offered for sale in the catalogue of the London bookseller
                            <fo:inline id="d1e39833INS0525Quaritch">Bernard Quaritch Ltd</fo:inline>
                            (Quaritch 1893,  12).
                            It is unknown how and when the manuscript came into the possession of <fo:inline id="d1e39841PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline>.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e39846PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Bibliography</fo:block>Crill 2026; Thomas 1990.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethb4">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethb4</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
