      <fo:static-content flow-name="xsl-footnote-separator">
         <fo:block space-before="5mm" space-after="5mm">
            <fo:leader leader-length="30%" rule-thickness="0pt"/>
         </fo:block>
      </fo:static-content>
      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethf32"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. f. 32</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Juel-Jensen 26)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex98×72 mm (weight: 128g), 86 fols (5 p. blank), 9 quires, eighteenth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e46431LIT1099Anapho">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 5r–82r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Anaphora of Our Lady Mary by Cyriacus of Behnesa, CAe 1099.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​አኰ​ቴተ፡ ​ቍር​ባን፡ ​ዘእ​ግዚ ​እት​ነ፡  ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ዘደ​ረሰ፡ ​አባ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ሕር​ያቆ​ስ፡
                                ​ኤጲ ​ስ፡ ​ቆጶ​ስ፡ ​ዘሀ​ገረ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ብሕ​ንሳ፡
                            </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ጸሎታ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ወበ​ረከ​ታ፡ ​የሃ  (fol. 5v)  ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ገብ​ራ። <fo:inline>[////]</fo:inline> ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡  አ ፤
                            </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ጐሥ​ዓ፡ ​ልብ​የ፡ ​ቃለ፡ ​ሠና​የ፡ ጐ ​ሥዓ፡ ​ልብ​የ፡ ​ቃለ፡ ​ሠና​የ፡ ​ጐሥ​ዓ፡ ​ልብ​የ፡ ​ቃለ፡ ​ሠና  (fol. 6r)  ​የ፡ ​ወአ​ነ፡ ​አየ​ድዕ፡ ​ቅዳ​ሴሃ፡
                                 ​ለማ​ርያ​ም፡
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​እስ​መ፡  ​ማር​ያም፡ ​እግ​ዝእ​ትነ፡ ቅ  (fol. 81v)  ​ድስ​ት፡ ​ድን​ግል። ​ይእ​ቲ፡ ​ወት​ረ። ​በሰ​ማይ፡ ወ በ ​ምድ​ር፡
                                ​በረ​ከተ፡ ​ጸሎ​ታ፡ ​ወሀ​ብተ፡ ​ረድ​ኤታ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ገብ​ራ። ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡  ​አሜ።  ​ወአ​ሜን፡   (fol. 82r)   ​ለይ​ኩን።
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Additional notes</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 2r–3r: Anaphora of Our Lady Mary by Cyriacus of Behnesa, CAe 1099.Excerpt from the , written in the main hand.
                                        The note reproduces the same text found on fols 61r–62v and corresponds to the text in
                                        Petrus Ethyops 1548,  172va, last line–172vb, l. 12.
                                        Liturgical directives in abbreviation and elements of the punctuation signs are rubricated.
                                    </fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        Incipit: :
                                            <fo:inline>...</fo:inline>​የ፡ ​ትዜ​ንዉ።  ​ይካ፡  ​ኦእ​ግዚ​ኦ፡ ​በከ​መ፡ ​አሜ​ሃ፡ ​ዘን​ተ፡ ​ኅብ​ስተ፡ ​ባር​ክ። ​ወፈ​ትት፡
                                        ​ወሀ​ብ፡ ​እግ​ዚኦ፡ ​በከ​መ፡ ​አሜ​ሃ፡ ​ዘን​ተ፡ ​ጽዋ​ዓ፡ ​ዕቀ​ብ። ​ወቀ​ድስ፡ ​ወመ​ጡ።
                                         ... 
                                    </fo:inline>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                                        Corrections are infrequent. They mostly consist of interlinear additions (e.g. fols 17r, 21v, 65v) and corrections through dashes above and below
                                        the letters (e.g. fols 15r, 43v, 75r).
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 1r–1v: Scribbles and pen trials in blue or violet ink.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 86r–86v: Crude drawings of human figures in red ink or blue pencil.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 81v–82r: Several names of individuals have been added in blue pencil or violet ink in a very inaccurate handwriting.
                                        The names of <fo:inline id="d1e46885PRS13885GabraHe">Gabra Ḥǝywat</fo:inline> (spelled once as Gabra Ḥaywat), <fo:inline id="d1e46887PRS13886GabraIy">Gabra ʾIyasus</fo:inline> (spelled once as Gabra ʾƎyasus),
                                        <fo:inline id="d1e46889PRS13887WaldaGa">Walda Gabrǝʾel</fo:inline> (spelled as Walda Garʾel), and <fo:inline id="d1e46891PRS13888WalattaGa">Walatta Gabrǝʾel</fo:inline> are still legible.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>5)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>A white sticker is glued on the inner side of the front board. The name of <fo:inline id="d1e46900PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> is printed on it
                                        (‘<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቤን​ት፡ ​ዩው​ል፡ ​የን​ሰን።</fo:inline>’) and the signature ‘MS. Aeth. f. 32’ is written in pencil.
                                        Some writings have been added in pencil on fol. 1r by the hand of <fo:inline id="d1e46907PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline>. On the upper margin is written
                                        an amount of money which presumably indicates the price of sale of the manuscript (‘£ 120’); below are found
                                        information on the dating and the decorations <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">"C 18 - 2 miniatures"</fo:inline>, as well as the signature of the book <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">"Ms Aeth. J-J 39"</fo:inline>.
                                        Furthermore, the title of the book in English <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">"Praise for the Holy Communion of Our Mother Mary written
                                            <fo:inline>[by]</fo:inline> Aba Hariyaqos of Bhansa"</fo:inline> is written on the lower margin of fol. 1r.
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                                  The book is bound in wooden boards.
                                
                                  The boards are flush with the bookblock and have shallow external bevels. The grain runs vertically.
                                  The external surface of the boards is polished, while the inner surface exhibits signs of the working tool.
                                  The boards were reused, as testifies the inscription on the back board where the
                                  writing <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">"Profumeria 20555 Extra Mil"</fo:inline> (?) is still legible, together with decorative interlaces.
                                  Part of the writing is now lost.
                                
                                  Chainstitch sewing on two sewing stations (one pair). The original sewing with S-plied thread has been repaired with a
                                  white colour thread, visible in Quire 1. The ends of the original thread are knotted in the centrefold of the last quire and a pink ribbon is attached
                                  to them.
                                
                                  The manuscript is provided with a leather two-piece satchel with a strap. The inner case is double-walled and the back panel overlaps over the front.
                                  The satchel is equipped with long flaps extending from the side panels and a main rounded flap extending from the back to the front
                                  panel to cover the opening of the book compartment.
                                  The outer case slides along the hanging strap and fits over the inner case. The strap is formed by a thick cord which passes through two flaps
                                  extending from the bottom panel of the inner case and the top panel of the outer case.
                                </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Pencil foliation in the upper right corner (1–86).</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block>9 quires. A<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">4 (Fols 1r–4v)</fo:inline> – I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 5r–14v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 15r–24v)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 25r–34v)</fo:inline> – IV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">12 (Fols 35r–46v)</fo:inline> – V<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8+2 (Fols 47r–56v)</fo:inline> – VI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 57r–66v)</fo:inline> – VII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 67r–76v)</fo:inline> – VIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 77r–86v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 2r–82r: 1
                                    column (8 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 26r. The characters per line are 5–9.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            92 × 69 mm (fol. 26r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            62 × 48 mm (fol. 26r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 9 mm, bottom: 26 mm, right: 10 mm, left: 8 mm (fol. 26r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible. Both primary and ruling pricks are visible. The upper and bottom lines are written above the ruling. Ruling pattern: 1A-1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Eighteenth century. 
                                    Mediocre handwriting. Slant and spacing of the characters vary throughout the manuscript.
                                <fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: 
                                    Some lines on the incipit page, alternating with black lines; few lines on fols 62v, ;
                                    the title of the Prayer of the breaking of the bread on 64v, ; holy names;
                                    liturgical directives in abbreviation; few letters, alternating with black lines, of single words or groups of words on 63v, 71v;
                                    elements of the punctuation signs and numerals.
                                </fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Abbreviations: <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="6mm"
                                             provisional-label-separation="6mm"
                                             start-indent="cm">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>1)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                          <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ይዲ</fo:inline> for <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ይበ​ል፡ ​ዲያ​ቆን፡</fo:inline> (e.g. fols 15r, 17v, 18v);
                                    </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>2)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                          <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ይካ</fo:inline> or <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ይ፡ ​ካህ፡</fo:inline> for <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ይበ​ል፡ ​ካህ​ን፡</fo:inline> (e.g. fols 17v, 20r, 68v);
                                    </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>3)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                          <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ይሕ</fo:inline> for <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ይበ​ል፡ ​ሕዝ​ብ፡</fo:inline> (e.g. fols 47v, 71v, 73r);
                                    </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>4)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                          <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">ቅ</fo:inline> for <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቅዱ​ስ፡</fo:inline> (e.g. fol. 53v).
                                    </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Decoration</fo:block>
         <fo:block margin-top="3mm" margin-bottom="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">The miniatures are a later addition, and probably date to
                              the second half of the 20th century. </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Miniatures</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(71) Fol. 4v: <fo:inline>The Virgin and Child.</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(72) Fol. 57r: <fo:inline>St George and the dragon.</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Headpieces</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Drawings</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Other</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Tears from the parchment making process have been repaired by sewing on fols 1, 43, 71.
                                       The small holes present on 61, 62 have not.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is deficient.
                                    The entire manuscript is slightly damaged by humidity. Dirt is present especially in the upper and outer corners of the folios.
                                    Stains are found on fols 76v, 77r.
                                    The readability of text deteriorates towards the end of the book: the text is barely legible due to faded ink (81r, 81v).
                                    The sewing, despite having been repaired over time, is broken in many points with the risk of leaves displacement.
                                </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>eighteenth century</fo:inline>
                    The manuscript can be dated palaeographically to the eighteenth century.
                    The names of several persons (<fo:inline id="d1e46966PRS13885GabraHe">Gabra Ḥǝywat</fo:inline>, <fo:inline id="d1e46968PRS13886GabraIy">Gabra ʾIyasus</fo:inline>,
                            <fo:inline id="d1e46970PRS13887WaldaGa">Walda Gabrǝʾel</fo:inline> and <fo:inline id="d1e46972PRS13888WalattaGa">Walatta Gabrǝʾel</fo:inline>), possibly secondary
                            owners, have been added at a later date to the manuscript
                    (see Varia note 4).
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>Unknown provenance.
                            The manuscript was put up for sale on 9 July 1979 at
                            Sotheby’s (‘Fine Oriental Manuscripts’, lot 73) and acquired
                            by <fo:inline id="d1e46983PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> through
                            the bookseller <fo:inline id="d1e46985PRS13559Thomas">Alan G. Thomas</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e46990PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethf32">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethf32</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
