      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLjj29"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian shelfmark missing</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Juel-Jensen 29)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment leaf383×335 mm, 1 fols, mid-seventeenth–eighteenth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e49944LIT3596Miracle">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 1ra–1vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Miracle of Mary: Miracle of the youth Zechariah, from Rome Mary Crowned with Roses The young man who used to bring roses to the icon of St Mary The Virgin Mary and the youth Zachary (Zakāryās), incomplete, CAe 3596.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The beginning and the end are missing.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                 (fol. 1ra)  
                                ​ያን፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ይጸሊ ፤  ​ወነ​ጸረ፡ ​ሥዕ​ላ፡ ​ለእ​ግዝ​እት​ነ፡ ​ቅድ​ስት፡
                                ​ድን​ግል፡ ​በክ​ልኤ፡  ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ወላ​ዲተ፡ ​አም​ላክ ፨ 
                                ​ወአ​ደመ​ቶ፡ ​ፈድ​ፋደ፡ ​ወው​ዕየ፡ ​ልቡ፡ ​በፍ​ቅረ፡ ​ዚአሃ ፨  ​ወሐ​ለየ፡ ​ወይ​ቤ፡   (b)   ​ምን​ተ፡ ​አም​ኃ፡ ​እሁ​ባ፡ ​ላቲ፡
                                ​ዘያ​ሠምራ ፨
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ወቆ​መ፡ ​ቅድ​መ፡ ​ሥዕ​ላ፡ ​ለእ​ግዝ​እት​ነ፡   (b)   ​ቅድ​ስት፡
                                ​ድን​ግል፡ ​በክ​ልኤ፡  ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ወላ​ዲተ፡ ​አም​ላክ ፨ 
                                ​ወይ​ቤላ፡ ​ኦእ​ግዝ​እት​የ፡ ​ፍቅ​ርት፡ ​እስ​መ፡ ​አን​ቲ፡ ​ተአ​ምሪ ፤ 
                                ​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ኀለ​ፈ፡ ​መዋ​ዕለ፡ ​ጽጌ፡ ​ረዳ ፨  ​ወባ​ሕቱ፡ ​አነ፡ ​እኤ​ምኅ፡ ኵ</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>There are no scribal corrections.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 1r: Italian note in pencil in the lower margin.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">Secolo XVIII</fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 1r: Note in pencil in the lower right corner.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block/>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 1r: An incomplete dating (with the actual date missing) and the shelfmark (‘C MS 29’) are indicated in pencil in the lower left corner.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The leaf is not foliated. In this description, the recto is referred to as
                                    fols 1r, , the verso as 1v.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 1ra–1vb: 2
                                    columns (11 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 1r.The characters per column are 7–9.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            235 × 240 mm (fol. 1r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 50 mm, bottom: 98 mm, right: 65 mm, left: 30 mm, intercolumn: 20 mm (fol. 1r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible. Primary and ruling pricks are visible. The upper line is written below the ruling while
                                    the bottom line is written above it. Ruling pattern (fols 1ra–1vb): 1A-1A-1A1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Mid-seventeenth–eighteenth century.     
                                    Fine and regular hand, gʷǝlḥ-script. Characters are broadly spaced and very large, with a height of more than
                                    one centimetre.
                                <fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: The name of <fo:inline id="d1e50103PRS6819Mary">St Mary</fo:inline>; the numeral <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">፶</fo:inline>; elements of punctuation signs.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is good.The upper outer corner is stained by humidity. The lower margin shows slight traces of use.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>mid-seventeenth–eighteenth century</fo:inline>
                            The manuscript can be dated palaeographically to the period between the
                            mid-seventeenth and the eighteenth century.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>In January 2020, the leaf had been inserted into <fo:inline/>, looted
                            from <fo:inline id="d1e50167INS0101MadhaneAlam">Madḫāne ʿĀlam</fo:inline>, but it is not known whether this was already the case
                            when <fo:inline/> 
                            The manuscript was put up for sale on 22 April 1980 (lot
                            251) <!--in
                                file<date>9 July 1979</date>, now updated according to intro--> at Sotheby’s and acquired by 
                            <fo:inline id="d1e50176PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> through the bookseller <fo:inline id="d1e50178PRS13559Thomas">Alan G. Thomas</fo:inline>.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e50183PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLjj29">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLjj29</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
