         </fo:block>
      </fo:static-content>
      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethg36"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. g. 36</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Juel-Jensen 30)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm">Prayer of Our Lady Mary on Mount Golgotha, Teaching of Mysteries (<fo:inline font-style="italic">Tǝmhǝrta ḫǝbuʾāt</fo:inline>)</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex, composite89×78 mm (weight: 98g), 54 fols (1 p. blank), 7 quires.  Unit 1:  mid-nineteenth–mid-twentieth century. Unit 2:  mid-nineteenth–mid-twentieth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                                    The book is bound in wooden boards.
                                
                                    The boards are flush with the bookblock and have square edges. The grain runs vertically.
                                    Both the external and inner surfaces of the boards are polished. On the external surface a finishing layer of dark colour has been added.
                                    The board attachment is uncommon. It only consists of two holes drilled through the thickness of the boards.
                                
                                    Chainstitch sewing on three sewing stations; continuous fold pattern; S-plied thread.
                                    The bookblock was probably sewn on four sewing stations and has been resewn on three, also substituting the boards. On the folios, the holes and the marks left by the previous sewing are present.
                                    The ends of the thread are knotted in the centrefold of the first quire.
                                    Fols 53,  is stitched through the inner margin directly to 54.
                                
                                    A piece of folded parchment protects the spine and is linked to the bookblock by stitching it to the holes for board attachment and the chains that the sewing forms on the spine.
                                    A yellow thread emerges from the tail edge of the bookblock.
                                </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Pencil foliation in the upper right corner carried out by the Bodleian Library
                                    in January 2020 (1–54).</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Unknown provenance. According to Varia note 1, the manuscript was
                            bought by Mesraq in <fo:inline id="d1e50620LOC1216AddisA">ʾAddis ʾAbabā</fo:inline> and given to <fo:inline id="d1e50622PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> before
                            1950. Unit 2 is a single leaf sewn onto a leaf in Unit 1 at an
                            unknown point in time.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e50633PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block>7 quires. I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 1r–8v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 9r–16v)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 17r–24v)</fo:inline> – IV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 25r–32v)</fo:inline> – V<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 33r–42v)</fo:inline> – VI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 43r–50v)</fo:inline> – VII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">3+1 (Fols 51r–54v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm">Unit 1</fo:block>
         <fo:block>Parchment, 53 fols (fols 1–52,  fol. 54), mid-nineteenth–mid-twentieth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e50652LIT2246salotz">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 1r–40r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">The prayer of Our Lady Mary which she prayed at Golgotha on 21 Sane, CAe 2246.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​በስ​መ፡ <fo:inline>አብብ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ፩ ​አም​ላክ፡ <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>
                                ​ጸሎ ት ፡ ​ዘእ​ግዝ​እት​ነ፡  ​ማር​ያም<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                ​ወላ​ዲተ፡ ​አም​ላክ፡ ​ቅድ​ስት፡ ​ድን​ግል<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​እሙ፡ ​ለብ​ርሃ​ን፡ ​እን​ተ፡ ​ጸሐ​ፋ፡
                                ​አብ​ሮክ​ሮስ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ረድ​ኣ፡ ​ዮሐ​ንስ፡
                            </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                     <fo:inline>ጸሎት፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ወበ​ረከ​ታ፡ ​ወኃ​ይለ፡ ​ረድ​ኤታ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ነፍ​ሰ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e50689PRS14730Gabra">
                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">​አቡ​ነ፡</fo:inline> ​ገብ​ረ፡ <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>
                     </fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e50696PRS14731braSeyon">
                        <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ብረ፡ ​ጽዮ​ን፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ዘጸ​ለየ​ት፡ ​ባቲ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> አ  (fol. 1v)  መ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline>፳መ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​፩፡ ​ለወ​ርኃ፡ ​ሰኔ፡ ​በደ​ብረ፡ ​ጎል​ጎታ፡ ​ዝው​እቱ፡ ​መቃ​ብረ፡ ​እግ​ዚእ​ነ፡ <fo:inline>ኢየሱ፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline>ክርስቶ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​እን​ዘ፡
                                ​ትብ​ል፡ ​ኦእ​ግዚ​እየ፡ ​ወአ​ምላ​ኪየ፡ ​ወመ​ድኃ​ንየ፡ ​ወን​ጉሥ​የ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ <fo:inline>ክርቶስ። (!)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ወፈ​ጺሞ፡ ​እግ​ዚእ​ነ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​ነጊ​ሮታ፡ ​ለእ​ሙ፡ ​ወወ​ሀባ፡ <fo:inline>ሰለመ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ወአ​ርገ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ሰማ​ያት፡ ​ወይ​እቲ​ኒ፡
                                ​አተ​ወት፡ ​ቤታ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ተአ​ኵቶ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን።
                            </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ኦእ​ግዝ​እት​የ፡  ​ማር​ያም ፡ ​ዕቀ​ብኒ፡ ​ለገ​ብር​ኪ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e50739PRS14734GabraMikael">​ገብ​ረ፡
                                    <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>
                     </fo:inline>
                                 (fol. 40r)   ​ወጸ​ሐፊ​ሁ፡ ​ኃጥ​ዕ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e50749PRS14735GabraGiyorgis">​ገብ​ረ፡  ​ሚካ​ኤል።</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e50762LIT2444Temher">
               <fo:inline>II) Fols 40r–52v, 54r–54v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Teaching of Mysteries Doctrine of Mysteries’ (​ትም​ህር​ተ፡ ​ኅቡ​ኣት፡), CAe 2444.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ትም​ህር​ተ፡ <fo:inline>ኀ (!)</fo:inline>​ቡአ​ት፡
                                    ​ቅድ​መ፡ ዘ ​ትት​ነገ​ር፡ ​እም<fo:inline>ጰ (!)</fo:inline>​ርስ​ፎራ፡ ​ለም​እመ​ናን፡ ​ህቡ​አት ፨
                            </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ትም​ሕር​ተ፡ ​ህቡ​አት​ሰ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ዝን​ግር፡ ​ዘቅ​ድመ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                ሀ ሎ ፡ ወ ይ ​ሄሉ፡ ​ዘመ​ፅአ፡ ዘ  (fol. 40v)  ​ሐመ፡
                                ​ወሞ​ተ፡ ​ወተ​ቀብ​ረ፡ ​ወተ​ንሥ​አ፡ ​ፃዕ​ረ፡ ​ዘሞ​ት፡ ​ፈት​ሐ፡ ​ወዘ​እሙ​ታን ፨  ​ተን​ሥአ ፨
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​በከ​መ፡ <fo:inline>ቤይ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ሙሴ፡ <fo:inline>ዳባዕዳንሂ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ነቢ​ያት፡ ​ንሕ​ነሂ፡
                                ​አኃ​ውየ፡ ​ቦቱ፡ ​ተወ​ኪለ​ነ፡ ​ነሀ​ብ፡ ​ሎቱ፡ ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ወጽ​ንዕ፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም።​።።
                            </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ዕቀ​ብኒ፡ ​ወአ​ድኅ​ንኒ ፨  ​እመ​ከራ፡ ​ሥጋ፡ ​ወነ​ፍስ፡
                                ​ሀጥ<fo:inline>[እ]</fo:inline>፡ ​ወድ​ኩም፡
                                ​ለገ​ብርከ ፨
                                <fo:inline id="d1e50829PRS14730Gabra">​ገብረ ፨
                                    <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ን፡ ​ስ።</fo:inline>
                                ​ወፀ​ሃፊሁ ፨
                                <fo:inline id="d1e50842PRS14729KidanaMaryam">​ኪዳ​ነ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​፨፨​፨፨
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Omitted letters and words have been added, most often interlineally (e.g. fols 23r, 28v, 45r),
                                but once in the upper margin with a <fo:inline>tamallas</fo:inline> sign in the text
                                (45r).
                                There are different type of deletions: erasures (e.g. 1r, 5v, 38v),
                                erasures with subsequent addition of line fillers
                                (e.g. 13r, 25v),
                                marking with over- and underlining (e.g. fols 4r, 20r, 32r),
                                marking with over- and underlining with subsequent erasure (e.g. fols 20v, 28r, 30r),
                                    blotting out (e.g. 12r, 13r, 25v).</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 1–52, 54: 1
                                    column (12 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 33r.There are 8–12 characters per line.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            94 × 71 mm (fol. 33r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            73 × 55 mm (fol. 33r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 5 mm, bottom: 15 mm, right: 5 mm, left: 10 mm (fol. 33r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible. Primary pricks are visible and ruling pricks are mostly visible. The upper line is mostly written above the
                ruling, but occasionally under it (e.g. fols 41–44). The bottom line is written above the
                ruling. Ruling pattern: 1E!-1E!/0/0/B.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 1r–52v, 54r–54v. 1850–1950. 
                                Irregular hand, but characters are regularly spaced.
                            <fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: 
                                Initial introductory formula; two lines on the incipit page fol. 40r;
                                the initial word(s) of sections of prayers
                                (e.g. <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​አም​ሕለ​ከ፡</fo:inline> or an abbreviation thereof
                                on 3v–12r; <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​መሐ​ልኩ፡ ​ለኪ፡</fo:inline> or an abbreviation thereof
                                on 33r–38r, ; different words on 40v–54r); holy names;
                                names of owners; elements of numerals and punctuation signs.
                                </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Decoration</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Miniatures</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Headpieces</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(18) Fol. 40r: <fo:inline>Single band filled with a pattern of interlocked black and red triangles.
                            </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Drawings</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Other</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Holes on fols 18, 32 from the parchment making process.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>mid-nineteenth–mid-twentieth century</fo:inline>
                                Unit 1 can be dated palaeographically to the period between the
                                mid-nineteenth and the mid-twentieth century.
                            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm">Unit 2</fo:block>
         <fo:block>Parchment, 1 fols (fol. 53), mid-nineteenth–mid-twentieth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e51044LIT6011FeastsList">
               <fo:inline>I) Fol. 53ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">List of commemorations for the Apostles and the Evangelists, incomplete, CAe 6011.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The entire text is reproduced below.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
            ​ሠረ​ቀ፡ ​መስ​ከረ​ም፡ ​በ፩ ​በር​ተሎ​ሜዎ​ስ፡ ​ሠረ​ቀ፡ ​ጥቅ​ምት፡ ​በ፲​ወ፪ ​ማቴ​ዎስ፡ ​በ፳​ወ፪ ​ሉቃ​ስ፡ ​ሠ፡ ኅ
            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 53r: 1
                                    column (5 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Five lines of text in the upper part of the folio.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are only partly visible.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 2:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fol. 53r. 1850–1950. 
                    Regular hand with regularly spaced characters.
                <fo:block>Ink: Black.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: 
                    No rubrication.
                </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>mid-nineteenth–mid-twentieth century</fo:inline>
            Unit 2 can be dated palaeographically to the period between the
            mid-nineteenth and the mid-twentieth century.
        </fo:block>
