      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethd17"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. d. 17</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Juel-Jensen 31)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex237×201 mm (weight: 1963g), 139 fols (6 p. blank), 18 quires, mid-seventeenth–mid-eighteenth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e51341LIT2505Weddas">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 4ra–139ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Praise of God’ (​ውዳ​ሴ፡ ​አም​ላክ፡), CAe 2505.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e51349LIT2505Weddas#Incipit">
               <fo:inline>I-1) Fols 4ra–4rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Praise of God: Incipit of the work</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The entire text is reproduced below.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em"> (fol. 4ra) 
                                    ​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​አሐ​ዱ፡ ​አም ​ላክ። ​በስ​መ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡
                                    ​ዘይ​ትወ​ሐድ፡ ​በመ​ለኮ ​ቱ፡ ​ኅቡ​ረ፡ ​ህላ​ዌ፡ ​ወዕ​ሩየ፡ ​መለ​ኮት፡ ​እስ​ከ።  ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡
                                    ​አሜ​ን። ​ንወ​ጥን፡ ​በረ​ድኤ​ተ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ጽሒ​ፈ፡ ​ስእ​ለት፡ ​ወአ​ስተ​ብቍ​ዖት፡ ​እን​ተ፡ ​ነበ​በ፡ ​ባቲ።
                                    ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ባስ​ልዮ​ስ፡  ​ኤጲ​ስ፡ ​ቆጶ​ስ፡ ​ዘቂ​ሳር​ያ፡
                                    ​በእ​ንተ፡ ፯ ​ዕለ​ታት፡ ​ዘመ​ፍት​ው፡ ​ይጸ​ልዩ፡ ​ባቲ። ​ለለ​ኵሉ፡
                                    ​ዕለ​ት። ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡ ​ወበ​ረከ​ቱ፡ ​ወሀ​ብተ፡ ​ረድ​ኤቱ፡ ​ለአ​ቡነ፡   (b)   ​ባስ​ልዮ​ስ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ገብ​ሩ፡
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e51366PRS12973Rehr">​ርኅ​ሩኅ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡
                                    </fo:inline> ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን።</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e51376LIT2505Weddas#Monday">
               <fo:inline>I-2) Fols 4rb–19rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Praise of God: Monday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ቀዳ​ሚ፡ ​ስእ​ለት፡  ​ዘይ​ትነ​በብ፡
                                        ​በዕ​ለተ፡ ​ሰኑ​ይ። ​ኦእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡  ​እግ​ዚእ​የ፡ ​ሰራ​ዬ፡ ​ኃጢ​አት​የ። ​አን​ተ፡ ​ተአ​ምር፡ ​ኵሎ፡
                                    ​ኃጢ​አተ፡ ​እን​ተ፡ ​ገበ​ርክ​ዋ፡ ​ጽሚ​ተ። ​አን​ተ፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ዘተ​አም​ር፡ ​ውሣ​ጥያ​ተ። ​ወት​ፈት​ን፡ ​ልበ፡ ​ወኵ​ልያ​ተ።
                                    ​አን​ተ፡ ​ተአ​ምር፡ ​ሕሰ​መ፡ ​ምግ​ባር​የ፡ ​እኪ​ት።</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                     ​ተወ​ከፍ፡ ​ስእ​ለት​የ፡ ​ድክ​ምተ፡ ​ወኅ​ሥር​ተ፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​ለገ​ብር​ከ፡
                                        <fo:inline id="d1e51390PRS12973Rehr">​ርኅ​ሩኅ፡
                                            ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡</fo:inline> ​በዕ​በየ፡ ​አፍ​ቅሮ​ትከ፡ ​እን​ተ፡ ​አል​ባቲ፡ ​ወሰ​ን፡
                                    ​እስ​መ፡ ​ለከ፡ ​ይደ​ሉ፡ ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ወክ​ብር፡ ​ወተ​ጋን​ዮ፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e51401LIT2505Weddas#Tuesday">
               <fo:inline>I-3) Fols 19va–45rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Praise of God: Tuesday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                     (fol. 19va) 
                                    ​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​ወስ​እለ​ት፡ ​ዘዕ​ለተ፡ ​ሰሉ​ስ፡ ​እም​ድር​ሳነ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡
                                    <fo:inline font-style="italic">​ማሪ፡</fo:inline> ​ኤፍ​ሬም፡ ​ሶር​ያዊ፡ ​አፈ፡ ​በረ​ከት፡ ​ወበ​ቍዔ​ት።
                                         ​በረ​ከቱ፡ <fo:inline> ቅዱስት፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ወጸ​ጋ፡ ​ረድ​ኤቱ፡ ​የሃ​ሉ፡
                                        ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ገብ​ሩ፡
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e51423PRS12973Rehr">​ርኅ​ሩኅ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡</fo:inline> ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡
                                    ​አሜ​ን። ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ለከ፡ ​ኦመ​ስተ​ዓግ​ሥ። ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ለከ፡ ​ኦጸ​ዋሪ፡ ​ወጸ​ናሂ። ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ለከ፡ ​ኦተ​መያ​ጢ፡
                                    ​ላዕ​ለ፡ ​ሰብ​እ። ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ለከ፡ ​ኦኄ​ር። ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ለከ፡ ​ኦጠ​ቢብ፡ ​ባሕ​ቲት​ከ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                     ​ወአ​ንጽ​ሕ፡ ​መን​ፈስ​የ። ​ወእ​ፃእ፡ ​በፍ​ሥሐ፡ ​ለቀ​በላ​ከ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡
                                    ​እሴ​ብሕ፡ ​ወእ​ባር​ክ፡ ​መር​ዓዌ፡ ​ዘኢ​ይመ​ውት። ​እኩ​ን፡ ​ድል​ወ፡ ​ወእ​ኩን፡ ​ሱታ​ፌ፡ ​ለቅ​ዱሳ​ን፡ ​እለ፡
                                    ​አሥ​መሩ​ከ፡ ​እስ​መ፡ ​ለከ፡ ​ይደ​ሉ፡ ​ስብ​ሐት። ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን። </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e51437LIT2505Weddas#Wednesday">
               <fo:inline>I-4) Fols 45ra–64vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Praise of God: Wednesday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​ወስ​እለ​ት፡ ​ወአ​ስተ​ብቍ​ዖት፡ ​ዘዕ​ለተ፡ ​ረቡ​ዕ፡  ​እም​ድር​ሳነ፡
                                    ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ <fo:inline font-style="italic">​ማሪ፡</fo:inline> ​ኤፍ​ሬም፡ ​ካዕ​በ። ​ኦእግ ​ዚእ​የ፡ ​አም​ላኪ​የ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ። ​ወል​ደ፡ ​እግ ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር።
                                    ​ሶበ፡ ​እዜ​ከር፡ ​ምጽ​አተ​ከ፡ ​ግሩ​መ፡ ​ለኰ​ንኖ፡ ​ፍጥ​ረት​ከ፡ ወ  (b)  ​ፍዳ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​ለለ​፩ዱ፡ ​በከ​መ፡ ​ምግ​ባሩ። ​ትት​ሀወ​ክ፡ ​አዕ ​ጽም​ትየ፡
                                    ​ወይ​ትመ​ተር፡ ​ኃይ​ለ፡ ​ነፍ​ስየ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ሥ ​ጋየ።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ከመ፡ ​አሥ​ምሮ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​በብ​ሔረ፡ ​ሕያ​ዋን። ​ወረ​ስየ​ኒ፡
                                    ​ድል​ወ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​እስ​ማዕ፡ ​ቃለ፡ ​ዘይ​ብል። ​ዝን​ቱ፡ ​ወል​ድየ፡ ​ሞተ​ሂ፡ ​ወሐ​ይወ፡ ​ተሐ​ጕለ​ሂ፡ ​ወተ​ረክ​በ።
                                    ​እስ​መ፡ ​ለከ፡ ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ወክ​ብር፡ ​ወእ​ዘዝ፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን። </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e51471LIT2505Weddas#Thursday">
               <fo:inline>I-5) Fols 65ra–89vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Praise of God: Thursday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                     (fol. 65ra) 
                                    ​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​ራብ​ዕ፡ ​ዘዕ​ለተ፡ ​ሐሙ​ስ፡ ​እን​ተ፡ ​ተጋ​ብአ​ት፡  ​እም​ቃለ፡
                                    ​አረ​ጋዊ፡ ​መን​ፈሳ​ዊ። ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ዮሐ​ንስ፡ ​ጸሎ ​ቱ፡ ​ወበ​ረከ​ቱ፡ ​የሃ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡
                                        ​ፍቁ​ሩ፡
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e51488PRS12973Rehr">​ርኅ​ሩኅ፡ ክ
                                        ር ​ስቶ​ስ።</fo:inline> ​ብሩ​ክ፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​አቡ​ሁ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​እነ፡ ​ወመ​ድኃ​ኒነ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡
                                    ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ። ​ዘከ​ሠተ፡ ​ምሥ​ጢረ፡ ​አፍ​ቅሮ​ቱ፡ ​ለነ​ፍሳ​ቲነ። <fo:inline> ወሥረቀ፡  (!)</fo:inline> ​ልቡ​ና፡ ​ጸጋ​ሁ፡
                                    ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​አል​ባቢ​ነ። ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ለዘ​አሥ​ረቀ፡ ​ስብ​ሐቲ​ሁ፡ ​ወገ​ብረ፡ ​ኃይ​ላቲ​ሁ፡ ​ወም​ሥጢ​ራቲ​ሁ፡ ​ለኑ​ዛዜ፡ ​እለ፡
                                    ​ይስ​እል​ዎ። </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ወባ​ቲ፡ ​ይኩ​ን፡ ​ግብ​ርነ፡ ​ወአ​ንብ​ቦት​ነ፡ ​በዛ​ቲ፡ ​ዘመ​ን፡
                                    ​ሙስ​ንት፡ ​ዘወ​ሀብከ<fo:inline>ከ (!)</fo:inline>​ነ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ትፍ​ትን፡ ​ግዕዛ  (b)  ነ<fo:inline>ነ (!)</fo:inline>፡ ​ወን​ብጻ​ሕ፡ ​ቦቱ፡ ​በሞ​ገስ፡ ​ኀቤ​ከ፡ ​በብ​ዝኃ፡ ​ምሕ​ረት​ከ፡ ​ወሣ​ህል​ከ።
                                    ​ወበ​ጸሎ​ተ፡ ​ዝን​ቱ፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ። ​መን​ፈሳ​ዊ፡ ​ዮሐ​ንስ፡ ​ዕቀ​ቦ፡ ​ለገ​ብር​ከ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e51506PRS12973Rehr">​ርኅ​ሩኅ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡</fo:inline> ​እስ​መ፡ ​ለከ፡
                                    ​ይደ​ሉ፡ ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ወክ​ብር። ​ዕበ​ይ፡ ​ወተ​ጋን​ዮ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​አቡ​ከ፡ ​ኄር፡ ​መሓ​ሪ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡
                                    ​ማኅ​የዊ። ​ይእ​ዜኒ፡ ​ወዘ​ልፈ​ኒ፡ ​ወለ​ዓለ​መ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን። ​ወአ​ሜን፡ ​ለይ​ኩን፡ ​ለይ​ኩን።</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e51516LIT2505Weddas#Friday">
               <fo:inline>I-6) Fols 90ra–109rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Praise of God: Friday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e51522LIT2505Weddas#FridayShenute">
               <fo:inline>I-6-1) Fols 90ra–100rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Praise of God: Friday: Prayer of Shenute</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                         (fol. 90ra) 
                                        ​ጸሎ​ተ፡ ​አባ፡ ​ሲኖ​ዳ፡ ​አር​ሳይ፡ ​መት​ርያ​ድስ፡ ​ዘማ​ኅበ​ር፡  ​እን​ተ፡
                                        ​ይት​ነበ​ብ፡ ​ዕለ​ተ፡ ​ዓር​ብ። ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡  ​ወበ​ረከ​ቱ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡
                                            ​ገብ​ሩ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e51537PRS12973Rehr">​ርኅ​ሩኅ፡
                                                ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡</fo:inline> ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን። ​እግ​ዚኦ፡ ​በመ​ዓት​ከ፡
                                        ​ኢት​ቅሥ​ፈኒ፡ ​ወበ​መቅ​ሠፍ​ትከ፡ ​ኢት​ገሥ​ጸኒ። ​አን​ሰ፡ ​እሬ​ኢ፡ ​በዓ​ይነ፡ ​ልቡ​ናየ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ዕሩ​ቅ፡
                                        ​ወክ​ሡት፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​እቀ​ውም፡ ​ቅድ​መ፡ ​ዝን​ቱ፡ ​መን​በር፡ ​መፍ​ርህ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​እደ​ንን፡ ​ርእ​ስየ፡
                                        ​በፍ​ርሃ​ት፡ ​ወረ​ዓድ፡ ​በቅ​ድሜ​ከ፡ </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​እስ​መ፡ ​ናሁ፡ ​ሰም​ዓ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ቃለ፡ ​ብካ​ይየ፡
                                        ​ወሰ​ምዓ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ስእ​ለት​የ። ​በር​ስዓ​ን፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ተው​ከፍ፡ ​ጸሎ​ትየ፡ ​ይት​ኃፈ​ሩ፡
                                        ​ወይ​ኅሠ​ሩ፡ ​ኵሎ​ሙ፡ ​ጸላ​እት​የ፡ ​ወይ​ግብ​ኡ፡ ​ድኅ​ሬሆ​ሙ፡ ​ወይ​ትሐ​ፈሩ፡ ​ፈድ​ፋደ፡
                                        ​ፍጡ​ነ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e51551LIT2505Weddas#FridayPachomius">
               <fo:inline>I-6-2) Fols 100rb–109rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Praise of God: Friday: Prayer of Pachomius</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​ዘአ​ባ፡ ​ጳኵ​ሚስ፡ ​አበ፡ ​ግር​ገታ​ተ፡ ​እን​ተ፡ ​ይእ​ቲ፡ ተ ​ፍጻ​ሜተ ፡ ​ለዛ​ቲ፡ ​ዕለ​ት፡ ​ዐባ​ይ፡ ​ስብ​ሐት፡
                                        ​ለአ​ብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ። ​ሥላ​ሴ፡ ​በተ​ዋህ​ዶ፡ ​ወተ​ዋህ​ዶ፡ ​በሥ​ላሴ፡   (fol. 100va)   ​እግ​ዚኦ፡ ​ሥረ​ይ፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​እስ​መ፡ ​አበ​ስኩ፡ ​ለከ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ሰብ​እ። </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​ኦአ​ምላ​ኪየ፡ ​እስ​እለ​ከ፡ ​ከመ፡ ት  (b)  ​ምት​ር፡ ​አመ​ክን​ዮት​የ፡ ​በዘ​ይደ​ሉ፡ <fo:inline>ለአመክንዮከ፡
                                         (!)</fo:inline> ​በላ​ዕሌ​የ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ትስ​ረይ፡ ​ኃጢ​አት​የ፡ ​ወት​ትዓ​ደው፡ ​አበ​ሳየ፡ ​ወጌ​ጋይ​የ፡ ​ሊተ፡
                                        ​ለኃ​ጥእ፡ ​ገብ​ርከ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e51574PRS12973Rehr">
                        <fo:inline>ርኅሩኅ፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                     </fo:inline> ​በም​ሕረ​ትከ፡ ​ወስ​ብሐ​ት፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​ኣብ​ሔር፡
                                        ​ለዓ​ለም፡ ​አሜ​ን።</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e51584LIT2505Weddas#Saturday">
               <fo:inline>I-7) Fols 109ra–123rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Praise of God: Saturday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​ሳድ​ሲት፡ ​ዘዕ​ለተ፡ ​ሰን​በተ፡ ​አይ​ሁድ፡ ​ዘአ​ስተ ​ጋብ​አ፡
                                    ​እማ​ኀል​የ፡ ​ቅብ​ጢ፡ ​አቡ​ነ፡ ​አት​ናት​ዮስ፡
                                     ​ሊቀ፡ ​ጳጳ​ስ፡ ​ዘሀ​ገረ፡ ​እለ፡ ​እስ​ክን​ድር​ያ። ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡ ወ ​በረ​ከቱ፡ ​ቅድ​ስት፡ ​ትኩ​ን፡
                                    ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ገብ​ሩ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e51596PRS12973Rehr">​ርኅ​ሩኅ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡</fo:inline>
                                    ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን። ​ወት​ብል፡ ​ከመ​ዝ፡ ​ኃሠ​ሥኩ​ከ፡   (b) 
                                    ​እማ​ዕም​ቀ፡ ​ልብ​የ። ​ኦእ​ግዚ​እየ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡  ​ርድ​አኒ፡
                                    ​አን​ተ፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ረዳ​ኢ፡  ​ወፍ​ትሐ​ኒ፡  ​እማ​ዕሥ​ረ፡ ​ኃጢ​አት። ​ኦእ​ግዚ​እየ፡
                                        ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡  ​ርድ​አኒ፡ ​አን​ተ፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ረዳ​ኢ፡ ​ለአ​ድኅ​ኖት​ነ፡ ​ኂሩ​ትከ፡ ​ይር​ከበ​ኒ፡
                                    ​ፍጡ​ነ፡ ​ወጸ​ልለ​ኒ፡ ​ታሕ​ተ፡ ​ጽላ​ሎተ፡ ​ክነ​ፊከ፡ ​በሰ​ዱስ፡   (fol. 109va) 
                                     ​ዕለ​ት፡ ​ፈጠ​ርከ​ነ፡ ​ኵሎ፡ ​ዓለ​መ። </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ብሩ​ክ፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ሥሉ​ስ፡
                                    ​ፍጹ​ም። ​ንስ​ግድ፡ ​ሎቱ፡ ​ወን​ሰብ​ሖ፡ ​ሎቱ፡ ​ይደ​ሉ፡ ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​እም​አፈ፡ ​መላ​እክ​ት፡ ​ወሰ​ብእ፡ ​ወእ​ምአ​ፈ፡
                                    ​ኵሉ፡ ​ፍጥ​ረት፡ ​እለ፡ ​ሀለ​ው፡ ​በም​ድር፡ ​ወበ​ሰማ​ያት። ​በባ​ሕር​ኒ፡ ​ወበ​ቀላ​ያት፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e51623LIT2505Weddas#Sunday">
               <fo:inline>I-8) Fols 123ra–139ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Praise of God: Sunday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ጸሎ​ተ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ቄር​ሎስ፡
                                        ​አቡ ​ነ፡ ​ሊቀ፡ ​ጳጳ​ሳት፡ ​ዘሀ​ገረ፡ ​እለ፡  ​እስ​ክን​ድር​ያ፡
                                    ​ዘዕ​ለተ፡ ​ሰን ​በት፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​በረ​ከቱ፡ ​ቅድ​ስት፡ ​ትኩ​ን፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡
                                    ​ገብ​ሩ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e51638PRS12973Rehr">
                        <fo:inline>ርኅሩኅ፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                     </fo:inline>
                                    ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም። ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ለአ​ብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ። ​ቦሙ፡ ​አአ​ምን፡ ​ወእ​ትአ​መን፡ ​እስ​ከ፡
                                    ​ነፍ​ስ፡ ​ደኃ​ሪት። ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ለከ፡ ​ኦእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡
                                      (b)  ​ስብ​ሐት። ​አቄ​ርብ፡ ለ ​ከ፡ ​በአ​ማን፡ ​ዘይ​ደሉ፡
                                        ​ለዕበ ​የ፡ ​ቅድ​ምና​ከ።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​እጽ​ናዕ፡ ​በፍ​ቅር​ከ። ​ወእ​ትወ​ከል፡ ​በብ​ዝኃ፡
                                    ​ምሕ​ረት​ከ። ​በጸ​ጋከ፡ ​ወሣ​ህል​ከ፡ ​ኀቤ​ከ፡ ​እስ​እል፡ ​እግ​ዚኦ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ትም​ርሃ​ኒ፡ ​ፍኖ​ተ፡ ​ዘነ​ሐው​ር፡ ​ባቲ።
                                    ​እን​ተ፡ ​ይእ​ቲ፡ ​ፍኖ​ተ፡ ​ጻድ​ቃን፡ ​ርት​ዕት። ​እስ​ከ፡   (fol. 139ra) 
                                    <fo:inline>ከ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ነፍ​ስ፡ ​ደኃ​ሪት፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን፡ ​ወአ​ሜን። </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Scribal corrections are rare (fols 91va, 106va, , only on 123ra comprising several
                                        lines). Missing characters are written interlineally here
                                        and there (fols 4va, 17rb, 33ra, 72vb: very
                                        thin and small characters), probably by a different hand;
                                        one correction over erasure clearly by a later hand on
                                        fol. 96ra (in deep black ink).</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>The name of <fo:inline id="d1e52095PRS12973Rehr">Rǝḫruḫ Krǝstos</fo:inline> is mentioned in the
                                        supplication formulas throughout the manuscript following the phrase
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ገብ​ርከ፡</fo:inline> ‘your servant’. This person
                                        was either the patron, the owner, the donor or the scribe of the
                                        manuscript.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block> A white sticker with the name of <fo:inline id="d1e52107PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> printed (‘<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቤን​ት፡ ​ዩው​ል፡ ​የን​ሰን።</fo:inline>’), and the signatures ‘Ms.
                                        Aeth. d. 17’ and ‘Ms. Et 31’ written in pencil is glued onto
                                        the inner side of the front board. Another sticker
                                        with the signature ‘Ms 31’ is glued below it.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                                The book is bound in wooden boards, once fully covered with brown blind-tooled leather.
                              
                                The boards are cut to the same size as the bookblock. The grain runs vertically.
                              
                                Full brown blind-tooled leather cover. The turn-ins have been trimmed out and they form butt mitres at the corners.
                                <fo:inline id="d1e52136">Additional leather patches</fo:inline> had been added along the inner margin of the boards
                                to fill the gap between the turn-ins, but later they have been removed probably to access the sewing and repair it.
                                Only the turn-ins and part of the back cover have been preserved. The back cover shows a fine blind-tooled decoration.
                                The turn-ins and the spine are also decorated.
                                The decoration consists of five concentric frames surrounding a central rectangular panel featuring a Latin cross.
                                Frames composed by the repetition of single tools, enclosed between <fo:inline id="d1e52139">double straight lines</fo:inline>,
                                alternate with empty ones.
                                Proceeding from the outer to the inner frame, the repeating decoration motifs are <fo:inline id="d1e52142">criss-crosses</fo:inline> (in two variants) and
                                <fo:inline id="d1e52145">straight strapwork</fo:inline> elements.
                                A third variant of criss-cross motifs between double straight lines forms the cross.
                                At the ends of the arms of the cross there are pairs of <fo:inline id="d1e52148">crescents</fo:inline> disposed to resemble a corniform motif,
                                and three <fo:inline id="d1e52152">double circles</fo:inline>. Dotted
                                  lines surmounted by a double circle intersect at the centre of the
                                  cross forming a <fo:inline font-style="italic">crux decussata</fo:inline>.
                                At the foot of the cross, the same criss-cross motif used in the first frame functions as a pedestal surrounded by five double circles.
                                Concentric frames of double straight lines decorate the turn-ins.
                              
                                The endbands are missing, but their tie-downs have been preserved.
                              
                               Chainstitch sewing on four sewing stations (two pairs); periodic fold pattern; Z-plied threads.
                               Between each pair of sewing stations there are two thread lengths, except in the first quire where there is one length.
                              
                                At the head and tail are preserved the short horizontal stitches used to pierce the leather on the spine
                                (at the head and tail), thus fixing the endbands to the cover. Two sets of holes are visible close to the head: at c.10 mm and
                                c.25 mm from the head. Another set is visible at c.10 mm from the tail.
                              
                                According to the auction catalogue (Sotheby's), the manuscript was sold in a leather satchel.
                                The manuscript, however, is currently not kept in a book case.
                              
                                Coloured <fo:inline id="d1e52177">leaf tab markers</fo:inline> are inserted in the outer margin of
                                folios with the incipit page of the days on fols 19, 45, 65, 109. The threads for Friday (fol. 90) and Sunday (fols 123) are
                                probably lost (a hole is visible on each of those folia). A
                                loose piece of red textile is kept on fol. 20r.
                              </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Pencil foliation in the upper right corner (1–139).</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm">Quire marks are written in black ink in the upper inner margin of the recto of the first folio of most quires.
                                        The first, the thirteenth and the last two quires are unmarked.
                                        Quires 14–16 are indicated as <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">፪</fo:inline>,
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">፫</fo:inline>, and <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">፬</fo:inline>, respectively.
                                       </fo:block>
         <fo:block>18 quires. A<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2+1 (Fols 1r–3v)</fo:inline> – I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 4r–11v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 12r–19v)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 20r–27v)</fo:inline> – IV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 28r–35v)</fo:inline> – V<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 36r–43v)</fo:inline> – VI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 44r–51v)</fo:inline> – VII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 52r–59v)</fo:inline> – VIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 60r–67v)</fo:inline> – IX<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 68r–75v)</fo:inline> – X<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 76r–83v)</fo:inline> – XI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6 (Fols 84r–89v)</fo:inline> – XII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 90r–97v)</fo:inline> – XIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 98r–105v)</fo:inline> – XIV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 106r–113v)</fo:inline> – XV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 114r–121v)</fo:inline> – XVI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 122r–131v)</fo:inline> – XVII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 132r–139v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 4ra–139ra: 2
                                    columns (19 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin
                                        dimensions taken from fol. 52r.The characters per line are 10–12.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            237 × 199 mm (fol. 52r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            147 × 153 mm (fol. 52r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 32 mm, bottom: 57 mm, right: 29 mm, left: 17 mm, intercolumn: 12 mm (fol. 52r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible. Primary pricks are visible. Ruling pricks are mostly visible. The upper and bottom lines are written above the
                                        ruling. Ruling pattern (fols 3ra–139vb): 1A-1A-1A1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Mid-seventeenth–mid-eighteenth century.. Trained hand. The handwriting remains uniform throughout the
                                    manuscript. It is characterized by finely shaped, regularly spaced
                                    characters with a very few archaic features (e.g. the
                                    characters ፅ and ዕ are usually “cone-shaped” , downward
                                    oriented).<fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: Several groups of lines on
                                    the incipit page of the text (fol. 4r) as well as
                                    of each section (the other six days); regularly two lines of
                                    subsections; the name of <fo:inline id="d1e52026PRS6819Mary">St Mary</fo:inline>; a few
                                    repeatedly occurring words within the reading for Monday (on
                                    13rb–15ra: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​አመ​ንኩ፡</fo:inline>, <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ስረ​ይ፡</fo:inline>,
                                    <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​መሐ​ረኒ፡</fo:inline>); the name <fo:inline id="d1e52040PRS12973Rehr">Rǝḫruḫ Krǝstos</fo:inline>; elements of
                                    the punctuation marks, text dividers, and numerals.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Decoration</fo:block>
         <fo:block margin-top="3mm" margin-bottom="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">The decorative frame on fol. 4r marks
                        the incipit and is painted in a style associated with works produced in the historical region
                      of Lasta around 1700 by the manuscript’s former owner (<inline xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Format">Juel-Jensen 1977</inline>).
                      It appears to be contemporary with the production of the manuscript. In contrast, the drawing in the volume is difficult to date.
                      </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Miniatures</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Headpieces</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(19) Fol. 4r: <fo:inline>The horizontal band is filled zig-zag pattern and topped by triangles and horn-shaped elements. Two lateral pendants filled with small squares and diagonal crosses
                            reach down to the last text line of the page.</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Drawings</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(3) Fol. 139r: <fo:inline>Small drawing of a grazing hippopotamus.</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Other</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
                                      Holes resulting from parchment making have been repaired by sewing, e.g. on fols 31, 94, 110. Others have not been repaired, e.g. on 26, 70, 105.
                                    </fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is good.
                                  Many folios are damaged by humidity, especially on the upper margin fols 65r–137r,
                                  resulting in deformations and stains.
                                  Insect droppings are present on fols 72v–73r and fols 106v–107r.
                                  The leather cover is torn off from
                                  the spine and the front board but its turn-ins are preserved. The inner
                                  corners of the back cover and the endbands are missing.
                                  The sewing is broken at the attachment with the boards.
                                </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>mid-seventeenth–mid-eighteenth century</fo:inline>
                            The
                            date of production, taking into account the handwriting and the frame on fol. 4r,
                            falls probably within the period between the mid-seventeenth and mid-eighteenth century.
                            A person called <fo:inline id="d1e52201PRS12973Rehr">Rǝḫruḫ Krǝstos</fo:inline> is mentioned in the
                            supplication formulas throughout the manuscript and
                            was either the patron, the owner, the donor or the scribe of the
                            manuscript (see Varia note 2).</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript was bought by <fo:inline id="d1e52210PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> at Sotheby’s
                            (Sotheby Parke Bernet &amp; Co.) on 13 October 1980 (lot
                            86) through the bookseller <fo:inline id="d1e52214PRS13559Thomas">Alan G. Thomas</fo:inline>, according to the
                            auction catalogue.</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e52219PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethd17">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethd17</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
