               <fo:inline>I-7-29-5) Fol. 211ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Salām-hymn to the companions of Tewodros</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e65002LIT4035SenkessarDL#Yakk29">
               <fo:inline>I-7-30) Fols 211ra–211rc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: 
                        29th Yakkātit
                        
                     </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e65008LIT4035SenkessarDL#Yakk29Christ">
               <fo:inline>I-7-30-1) Fol. 211ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Commemoration of the birth of Christ</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e65016LIT4035SenkessarDL#Yakk29Bolikarbos">
               <fo:inline>I-7-30-2) Fols 211ra–211rc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Commemoration of Bolikārbos</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e65024LIT4035SenkessarDL#Yakk29SalChrist">
               <fo:inline>I-7-30-3) Fol. 211rc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Salām-hymn to the birth of Christ</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e65033LIT4035SenkessarDL#Yakk29SalBolikarbos">
               <fo:inline>I-7-30-4) Fol. 211rc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Salām-hymn to Bilkiryos</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e65042LIT4035SenkessarDL#Yakk30">
               <fo:inline>I-7-31) Fols 211rc–212rc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: 
                        30th Yakkātit
                        
                     </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e65048LIT4035SenkessarDL#Yakk30Yohannes">
               <fo:inline>I-7-31-1) Fols 211rc–211va: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Commemoration of the invention of the head of St John the Baptist
                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e65056LIT4035SenkessarDL#Yakk30Yohannes2">
               <fo:inline>I-7-31-2) Fols 211va–212rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Discourse of John Chrysostom on John the Baptist</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e65064LIT4035SenkessarDL#Yakk30Minas">
               <fo:inline>I-7-31-3) Fols 212rb–212rc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Commemoration of ʾabbā Minās</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The entire text is reproduced below.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ​ወበ​ዛቲ፡ ​ዕለ​ት፡ ​ካዕ​በ፡ ​ተዝ​ካሩ፡  ​ለአ​ባ፡ ​ሚና​ስ፡ ​ሊቀ፡ ​ጳጳ​ሳት፡ ​ዘሀ​ገረ፡ ​እስ​ክን​ድር​ያ፡ ​ክብ​ርት፡
                                            ​እም​ነ፡ ​አህ​ጉራት ፨
                                            ​በረ​ከቱ፡ ​ቅድ​ስት፡ ​ትኩ​ን፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ፍቁ​ሩ፡
                                                <fo:inline id="d1e65081PRS13077TaklaM">​ተክ​ለ፡  ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline> ​ወም​ስለ፡ ​ኵል​ነ፡ ​ሕዝ​በ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡
                                                አ  (c)  ​ሜን ፨
                                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e65098LIT4035SenkessarDL#Yakk30SalYohannes">
               <fo:inline>I-7-31-4) Fol. 212rc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Salām-hymn to John the Baptist</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The entire text is reproduced below.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ​ሰላ​ም፡  ​እብ​ል፡ ​ለር​እስ​ከ፡ ​ክቡር ፨ 
                                            ​ዘተ​ረክ​በ፡ ​ዮም፡ ​በን​ዋይ፡ ​ጽቡር ፨ 
                                            ​ዮሐ​ንስ፡ ​ሰራ​ሪ፡ ​ንጉ​ሠ፡ ​አዕ​ዋፍ፡ ​ንስር ፨ 
                                            ​ንሥ​አኒ፡ ​በክ​ነፊ​ከ፡ ​ወአ​ዕድ​ወኒ፡ ​ለገ​ብር ፨ 
                                            ​ከመ፡ ​ኢያ​ስቆ​ቁ፡ ​ቀዊ​ምየ፡ ​በር​እሳ፡ ​ለባ​ሕር ፤
                                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e65133LIT4035SenkessarDL#YakkSubscription">
               <fo:inline>I-7-32) Fol. 212rc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Subscription for Yakkātit</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The entire text is reproduced below.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            Fol. 212rc ​ተፈ​ጸመ፡ ​ወር​ኃ፡ ​የካ​ቲት፡ ​ቡሩ​ክ፡ ​በሥ​ምረ​ተ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ኢ ​የሱ​ስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​ሎቱ፡ ​ስብ​ሐት፡
                                        ​ወላ​ዕሌ​ነ፡ ​ይኩ​ን፡ ​ሣህ​ሉ፡ ​ወም​ሕረ​ቱ፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜን ፨</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e65153LIT4035SenkessarDL#YakkSupplication">
               <fo:inline>I-7-33) Fol. 212rc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Supplication for Yakkātit</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The entire text is reproduced below.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        
                                        ​ለዘ​ጸሐ​ፎ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e65162PRS13094GabraKr">​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡</fo:inline> ​ወለ​ዘአ​ጽሐ​ፎ፡
                                        <fo:inline id="d1e65166PRS13077TaklaM">​ተክ​ለ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e65170PRS13078NewayaM">​ወን​ዋየ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline> ​በፈ​ቃደ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ኅቡ​ረ፡ ​ይም​ሐሮ​ሙ፡ ​በመ​ንግ​ሥተ፡ ​ሰማ​ያት፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን፤
                                    </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Colophon</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block font-family="Ludolfus">Fols 212rc–212rb: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">The colophon begins in column c and continues in
                                    columns a and b. It states that the manuscript was completed in
                                    the time of King <fo:inline id="d1e65184PRS10473Yostos">Yosṭos</fo:inline> (r. 1711–1716)
                                    and Patriarch <fo:inline id="d1e65186PRS6777Marqos">Mārqos IV</fo:inline>.
                                    The date of beginning is given as Wednesday, 30 Ḫǝdār, and the date of completion as
                                    Thursday, 30 Sane. If these dates are correct, its completion would have taken
                                a year and half, from 30 Ḫǝdār 1712 to 30 Sane 1714. The supplication mentions the
                                people of ‘Lǝggāt’.</fo:inline>
                           <!--according to https://cal.ethiopicist.com/-->
                        </fo:block>
                        <fo:block font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘተ​ወጥ​ነ፡  ​አመ፡  ፴ ​ሁ፡
                                    ​ለኅ​ዳር<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​በዕ​ለተ፡
                                ​ረቡ​ዕ፡ ​ተፈ​ጸመ፡ ​አመ፡  ፴ ​ሁ፡ ​ለሰ​ኔ፡ ​በዕ​ለተ፡ ​ሐሙ​ስ፡ በ  (a)  ​ጊዜ፡  ፱ ​ሰዓ​ት፡ ​በሠ​ርቀ፡ ​ሌሊ​ት፡  ፲ ወ ፱ ፡ ​በሠ​ርቀ፡ ​መዓ​ልት፡  ፴ ፡ ​በመ​ንግ​ሥተ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e65220PRS10473Yostos">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​ንጉ​ሥ፡</fo:inline> ​ዮስ​ጦስ፡</fo:inline>
                                 (b)   ​ወጳ​ጳስ​ነ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e65228PRS6777Marqos">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​አባ፡</fo:inline> ​ማር​ቆስ ፨</fo:inline>
                                ​ወይ​ምሐ​ሮሙ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ለኵ​ሎሙ፡ ​ሰብ​አ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e65237LOC7348Legat">​ልጋ​ት፡</fo:inline> ​ለዓ​ለመ፡
                                        ​ዓለ ፤</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>The manuscript contains numerous scribal corrections throughout. Corrections are added
                                        interlineally (e.g. fols 7vb, 10rb), in
                                        the margins (e.g. 14rb, 28ra), or written above deletions (e.g. 8rb,, 108vb).
                                        Erroneous text is expunctuated with dashes above and
                                        below (e.g. 108vc). <fo:inline font-style="italic">Tamallas</fo:inline>-signs in the margins point to scribal corrections (e.g.
                                        158v, 206v) or to the place in which sentences have been omitted, which have been then added
                                        in the margin (e.g. 109va). The function of all <fo:inline font-style="italic">tamallas</fo:inline>-signs is not always immediately
                                        clear (e.g. 72r, 150v). Occasionally,  commemorations or
                                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">salām</fo:inline>-hymns have been
                                        added in the margins (e.g. 48vb, 143v).
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>The name of the scribe <fo:inline id="d1e65814PRS13094GabraKr">Gabra Krǝstos</fo:inline> is mentioned throughout in supplications and
                                        at the beginning of several quires. <fo:inline id="d1e65816PRS13115SelaKr">Śǝʿla Krǝstos</fo:inline> is
                                        mentioned as scribe in one supplication on fol. 102rc. The
                                        patron was <fo:inline id="d1e65820PRS13077TaklaM">Takla Māryām</fo:inline>, whose brother <fo:inline id="d1e65822PRS13078NewayaM">Nǝwāya Māryām</fo:inline> is also mentioned in supplications (fol. 78vc). <fo:inline id="d1e65827PRS13101ZamanfasQ">Zamanfas Qǝddus</fo:inline> is mentioned
                                        more rarely (fols 33ra, 158va).
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 1v–2r: Several pen trials, one of which contains the name of <fo:inline id="d1e65839PRS13094GabraKr">Gabra Krǝstos</fo:inline>.
                                    Three longer pen trials contain the beginning of the Sǝnkǝsār, excerpts from the Psalms of David and
                                    a liturgical prayer.
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 3v, 21r: Scribbles or pen trials.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>5)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 4r, 79r, 109r:  The decorated names of the months Maskaram, Ḫǝdār and
                                        Tāḫśāś are written in the upper margin.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>6)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 4r, 129r: The word <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ጥራ​ዝ፡</fo:inline>, i.e. ‘quire’, written in the lower margin
                                        (see collation) is
                                        followed by the name of the scribe, <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዝዘ<fo:inline id="d1e65873PRS13094GabraKr">​ገብ​ረ፡
                                                ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡</fo:inline>
                        </fo:inline> (fol. 4r),
                                        resp. <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">ዘ<fo:inline id="d1e65880PRS13094GabraKr">​ገብ​ረ፡
                                            ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡</fo:inline>
                        </fo:inline> (fol. 129r).
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>7)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 91v: A cross in black ink, possibly by a European hand, in the
                                        upper outer corner.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>8)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 1r: A white sticker with the name of <fo:inline id="d1e65900PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> printed (‘<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቤን​ት፡ ​ዩው​ል፡ ​የን​ሰን።</fo:inline>’), and the signatures ‘Ms.
                                        Aeth. b. 5’ and ‘Ms. Et 32’ written in pencil is glued on the page.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                              The book is bound in wooden boards covered with reddish-brown blind-tooled leather. The inner sides of the boards are decorated with blue textile <fo:inline id="d1e65924">inlays</fo:inline>.
                              
                              The boards are cut to the same size as the bookblock and present external shallow bevels.
                            
                              Full reddish-brown blind-tooled leather cover.
                              The turn-ins are irregular but at the corners they are trimmed to form butt mitres.
                              An <fo:inline id="d1e65933">additional leather patch</fo:inline> has been added along the inner margin of the boards to fill the gap between the turn-ins.
                              Other leather patches have been added in trying to pair the margins of the turn-ins.
                              On the back board, pieces of leather are stitched together to form the cover.
                              The cover shows a trembling blind-tooled decoration, hastily executed identically just with minor variations on both sides of the cover. The edges are also decorated.
                              The decoration consists of six concentric frames surrounding a central rectangular panel featuring a Latin cross.
                              Frames composed by the repetition of single tools, enclosed between <fo:inline id="d1e65936">double straight lines</fo:inline>,
                              alternate with empty ones.
                              Proceeding from the outer to the inner frame, the repeating decoration motifs are <fo:inline id="d1e65939">X-forms</fo:inline>,
                              <fo:inline id="d1e65942">straight strapwork</fo:inline>, and <fo:inline id="d1e65945">curve strapwork</fo:inline> elements.
                              The cross is formed by <fo:inline id="d1e65949">curve strapwork</fo:inline> elements between double straight lines.
                              At the ends of the arms of the cross there are three <fo:inline id="d1e65952">double circles</fo:inline>.
                              Double circles are also stamped at the intersections of the straight lines and in the empty spaces.
                              The straight lines delimit six areas in the central panel. In each
                              area they cross each other forming on the upper board a <fo:inline font-style="italic">crux decussata</fo:inline>
                              and on the lower board an eight-pointed star.
                              A double straight line and double circles decorate the edges of the boards.
                            
                             Brown and white <fo:inline id="d1e65961">slit-braid</fo:inline> endbands are present.
                            
                             Chainstitch sewing on four sewing stations (two pairs); periodic fold pattern; Z-plied threads.
                             Between each pair of sewing stations there are two lengths of thread.
                            
                              The manuscript is provided with a one-piece, double-walled satchel.
                              The satchel is equipped with a main pointed flap extending from the back to the front panel to cover the opening of the book compartment.
                              The stitching holding together the satchel has become undone.
                            </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Pencil foliation in the upper right corner (1–214). One folio each after fol. 141 and fol. 142 had been skipped in the original foliation.
                                    The sequence has been corrected to 141a, 141b, 142a, 142b.
                                    An empty
                                    folio between 212 and fol. 213, of which two thirds are cut off, has not been foliated.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm">Decorated quire marks are written in the upper and lower margins of the recto of the first folio of all quires, except for the
                                        protective quires. Quire marks are also written in the upper and lower margins of the verso
                                        of the first folio of quires 2–4.
                                        All quire marks are written in red and black, are decorated with dots and lines and are occasionally surrounded by four nine-dot signs.
                                        Moreover, the word <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ጥራ​ዝ፡</fo:inline>, i.e. ‘quire’,
                                        written in red or black and decorated with dots and lines,
                                        is written in the lower margin (e.g. fol. 4r)
                                        or both in the lower and upper margin of the recto of the first folio of
                                        all quires, except for the protective quires (e.g. fols 14r, 24r, 34r). It is also
                                        written on fol. 79r and fol. 118v, the second and last page of a quire respectively.
                                     </fo:block>
         <fo:block>24 quires. A<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2+1 (Fols 1r–3v)</fo:inline> – I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 4r–13v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 14r–23v)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 24r–33v)</fo:inline> – IV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8+2 (Fols 34r–43v)</fo:inline> – V<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10+2 (Fols 44r–55r)</fo:inline> – VI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10+2 (Fols 56r–67v)</fo:inline> – VII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8+2 (Fols 68r–77v)</fo:inline> – VIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8+2 (Fols 78r–87v)</fo:inline> – IX<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6+2 (Fols 88r–95r)</fo:inline> – X<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 96r–103v)</fo:inline> – XI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">4+1 (Fols 104r–108v)</fo:inline> – XII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 109r–118v)</fo:inline> – XIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 119r–128v)</fo:inline> – XIV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8+2 (Fols 129r–138v)</fo:inline> – XV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8+2 (Fols 139r–146v)</fo:inline> – XVI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8+2 (Fols 147r–156v)</fo:inline> – XVII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8+2 (Fols 157r–166v)</fo:inline> – XVIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 167r–174v)</fo:inline> – XIX<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8+1 (Fols 175r–183v)</fo:inline> – XX<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 184r–193v)</fo:inline> – XXI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8+2 (Fols 194r–203v)</fo:inline> – XXII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8+1 (Fols 204r–212v)</fo:inline> – B<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2 (Fols 213r–214v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 4ra–212rc: 3
                                    columns (30–38 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin
                                        dimensions taken from fol. 44r.The characters per line per column are 13–17.Line endings are very irregular.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            378 × 327 mm (fol. 44r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            262 × 262 mm (fol. 44r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 32 mm, bottom: 75 mm, right: 43 mm, left: 21 mm, intercolumn: 17 mm (fol. 44r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible. Primary pricks are visible. Ruling pricks are mostly visible. The upper and bottom lines are written above the
                                        ruling. Ruling pattern (fols 2ra–214vc): 1A-1A-1A1A-1A1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->1711–1716 (scribe: Gabra Krǝstos) . Written by a trained hand, but slightly irregular. The characters are also spaced
                                    irregularly.
                                    Gabra Krǝstos is mentioned as scribe in supplications throughout the
                                    manuscript.
                                    Śǝʿla Krǝstos is mentioned as scribe in
                                    supplications on fols 102rc, 106vc. It cannot be excluded that more than one scribe were involved in the copying,
                                    but no clear discontinuities in hand can be observed.
                                <fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: Incipits (alternating with black lines at
                                    the top and bottom of the page for months, two continuous lines
                                    for days, one to two continuous lines for commemorations);
                                    the word <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሰላ​ም፡</fo:inline>;
                                    the full names of persons involved in the
                                    production of the manuscript (fols 33ra, 78vc)
                                    or, more often, only the holy names <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline> and
                                    <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡</fo:inline> which form part of their name;
                                    paratextual elements (names of the months and of the scribe);
                                    elements of punctuation signs and quire marks  (see Winslow 2015,  134; 136–137).
                                </fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Abbreviations: <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="6mm"
                                             provisional-label-separation="6mm"
                                             start-indent="cm">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>1)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                          <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሰ፡</fo:inline> for
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሰላ​ም፡</fo:inline> (e.g. fol. 65ra).</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Decoration</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Miniatures</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Headpieces</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(20) <fo:inline>The manuscript contains some small penwork dividers created by alternating patterns of 
                                     black and red dots or lines. For instance, on fols 46ra–46rb, two double lines divide the first and second columns into two. 
                                     Each pair of lines is filled with three cross-shaped elements that are rendered as the punctuation
                                     marks in the rest of the manuscript and are thus certainly coeval with the main production unit. 
                                     Similar variations on this pattern appear elsewhere in the manuscript: dot patterns can be found
                                     at the bottom of the column on fol. 65vb, , 78vc, , 
                                     108va–108vc, , 183va–183vc,
                                     and fol. 212r, and
                                     in between the columns 108rb–108rv, , 141ra,
                                     and fols 143va–143vc; and line patterns are found on
                                     fol. 134vb and fol. 135ra.</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(21) <fo:inline>Small Tau-shaped elements are occasionally found on the margins of the pages
                                     (e.g. on fol. 72r).</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Drawings</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Other</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Frequent holes resulting from parchment making have been repaired by sewing, e.g. fols 30, 73, 162. Smaller holes have not been repaired, e.g. 50, 61, 208.
                                        The larger part of an empty <!--blank?-->folio between 212 and fol. 213 has been cut off.
                                    </fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is good.
                                  The trimming of the bookblock caused minimal loss
                                  of text on fol. 143v. The folios are occasionally stained by
                                  humidity and their lower margin is slightly stained by dirt.
                                  The leather cover is abraded and worn. The stitching of the slip-case has become undone.
                                </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>1712–1714</fo:inline>
                            The colophon states that the manuscript was completed during the reign of
                            King <fo:inline id="d1e65984PRS10473Yostos">Yosṭos</fo:inline> (r. 1711–1716). The weekdays on which
                            the manuscript was begun and completed would point to a production between
                            1712–1714.
                            The colophon mentions <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሰብ​አ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e65988LOC7348Legat">​ልጋት</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline> and
                            supplications mention <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ደቂ​ቀ፡ ​ቂር​ቆስ፡</fo:inline>
                                (fols 53vbc, 143vc),
                            which points to a church of Qirqos in Lǝggāt as place of origin. The current village of
                            <fo:inline id="d1e65996LOC7348Legat">Lǝggāt</fo:inline> is located not far from <fo:inline id="d1e65999INS0017UM">ʿUrā Qirqos</fo:inline>, which might point
                            to this church or a scribal community connected to it being the place of production of the manuscript.
                            The name of the scribe <fo:inline id="d1e66001PRS13094GabraKr">Gabra Krǝstos</fo:inline> is mentioned throughout;
                            <fo:inline id="d1e66003PRS13115SelaKr">Śǝʿla Krǝstos</fo:inline> is
                            mentioned as scribe in one supplication (see Varia note 2). The
                            patron was <fo:inline id="d1e66008PRS13077TaklaM">Takla Māryām</fo:inline>, whose brother <fo:inline id="d1e66010PRS13078NewayaM">Nǝwāya Māryām</fo:inline> is also mentioned in supplications;
                            <fo:inline id="d1e66013PRS13101ZamanfasQ">Zamanfas Qǝddus</fo:inline> is mentioned
                            more rarely (see Varia note 2).</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript was bought by <fo:inline id="d1e66021PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline>
                            at Sotheby’s in 28 April 1981 (‘Sotheby’s Western
                            Manuscripts’, lot 213) through the bookseller <fo:inline id="d1e66025PRS13559Thomas">Alan G. Thomas</fo:inline>, according to the sale receipt.</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e66030PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Bibliography</fo:block>Winslow 2015.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethb5">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethb5</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
