      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethg40"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. g. 40 (R)</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Juel-Jensen 37)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment scroll1902×62–74 mm (weight: 24g),  fols, 1960s–
                                1970s.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e73539LIT1763Legend">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 1r1–1r121: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Legend of St Susǝnyos and Wǝrzǝlyā (general record), CAe 1763.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The legend of Susǝnyos proper is framed by lengthy protective
                            supplications.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​በስ​መ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ሕያ​ው፡ ​ነባ​ቢ፡ ​ወተ​ናጋ​ሪ፡ ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡ ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡ ​ሱስ​ንዮ​ስ፡ በ ​እን​ተ፡
                            ​አሰ​ስሎ፡ ​ደዌ፡ ​እም​ሕፃ​ናት፡ ​እለ፡ ​ይጠ​ብው፡ ​ጥበ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​እሞ​ሙ፡ ​እም​ኵሉ፡
                                ​ደዊያ<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>፡ ​ዓዲ፡ ​ጸሐ​ፍኩ፡ ​ለብ​እሲ ሲ ​ት፡ ​ሐሐ​ዋ፡ ​ዘየ​ሐዩ፡
                                ​ደዌ<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline> ​ወት​ስቅ​ሎ፡ ​ላዕ​ሌሃ፡ <fo:inline>ወይበቁዕ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​በረ​ድኤ​ተ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ልዑ​ል፡ ​ወክ​ቡር፡
                            ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን፡</fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                     <fo:inline>ቱ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ወበ​ረከ​ቱ፡ ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡ ​ሱስ​ንዮ​ስ፡ ​ያድ​ኅና፡ ​እም​ሕማ​መ፡ ​ዓይ​ነጥ​ላ፡ ​ወዓ​ይነ​ናስ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                ​ዓይ​ነና​ስ፡ ​ዓይ​ነ፡ ​ዛር፡ ​ወዓ​ይነ፡ ​ጠቢ​ብ፡ ​ወቡ​ዳ፡ ​ዓይ​ነ፡ ​ባርያ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ወሌ​ጌዎ​ን፡ ​ድድ​ቅ፡ ​ወጋ​ኔነ፡ ​ቀት​ር፡ ​ምች፡ ​ወተ​ላዋ​ሽ፡
                                ​ቁራ​ኛ፡ ​ወተ​ያያ​ዥ፡ ​ዕጀ፡ ​ሰብ​እ፡ ​ወጽ​ላወ​ጊ፡ ​ደም፡ ​ወሽ​ተላይ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                ​ለዓ​መትከ ፨
                                <fo:inline id="d1e73578PRS13860HawituA">​ሐዊቱ ​አሊ፡</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e73583PRS13861WalattaH">​ወለ​ተ፡ ​ሕይ​ወት</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ወሀሎ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ፩ 
                            ​ብእ​ሲ፡ ​ዘስ​ሙ፡ ​ሱስ​ንዮ​ስ፡ ​ወአ​ውሰ​በ፡ ​ብእ​ሲተ፡ ​ወወ​ለደ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ትባ​ዕተ፡ ​ወአ​ንስ​ተ፡ ​ወበ​ቀዳ​ማይ፡ ​ወል​ዳ፡ ​ቦዓ​ት፡ ​ውር​ዝል​ያ፡ ​ጋኔ​ን፡
                                <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ወቀ​ተለ​ቶ፡ ​ለወ​ልዳ፡ ​ወበ​ከየ​ት፡ ​እሙ፡ ​ወይ​ቤላ፡ ​ኦብ​እሲ​ቶ፡ ​ምን​ት፡ <fo:inline>ያበከየኪ፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ወት​ቤ፡ ​ይእ​ቲ፡ ​አን​ሰ፡ ​ኢየ​ኃው​ር፡ ​ኀበ፡ ​ሀሎ፡ ​ስም​ከ፡ ​ፍኖ​ተ፡ ​ውስ​ቴታ፡ ​ወኢ​ይቀ​ርብ፡ ​ኀበ፡ ​ሀሎ፡ ​ስም​ከ፡ ​ፍኖ​ተ፡ ​ወኀ​በ፡ ​ይፀ​ውራ፡ ​ለዛ​ቲ፡ ​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​እመ​ሂ፡
                            ​አን​ስት፡ ​ወእ​መሂ፡ <fo:inline>አንስት፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ወወ​ተባ​ዕት፡ ​ወእ​መሂ፡ ​አዕ​ሩግ፡ ​ወሕ​ፃና​ት፡ ​ወወ​ሬዛ፡ ​ልሂ​ቅ፡ ​ኢይ​በጽ​ሕ፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ለአ​ለም፡ ​ወእ​ምድ​ኅረ​ዝ፡ ​ሶበ፡ ​ኮነ፡ ​ሰማ​ዕተ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ሱስ​ንዮ​ስ፡ ​በስ​መ፡
                                ​እግ​ዚእ​ነ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡  ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​ሎቱ፡ ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​አለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን።</fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ኦአ​ምላ​ከ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ሱስ​ንዮ​ስ፡ ​አድ​ኅና፡ ​እም​ሕማ​መ፡ ​ዓይ​ነጥ​ላ፡ ​ወዓ​ይነ​ናስ፡ ​ወዓ​ይነ​ናስ፡ ​ዓይ​ነ፡ ​ዘር፡ ​ወው​ላጅ፡ ​ዓይ​ነጠ​ቢብ፡ ​ወቡ​ዳ፡
                                ​ዓይ​ነ፡ ​ባርያ ያ ፡ ​ወሌ​ጌዎ​ን፡ ​ድድ​ቅ፡ ​ወጋ​ኔነ፡ ​ቀት​ር፡ ​ምች፡ ​ወተ​ላዋ​ሽ፡ ​ቁራ​ኛ፡ ​ወተ​ያያ​ዥ፡ ​ደም፡
                                ​ወሸ​ተላ​ይ፡ ​መገ​ኛ፡ ​ወጕ​ሥም​ት፡ ​ውጋ​ት፡ ​ወቁ​ርጥ​ማት፡ ​ፍል​ጸት፡ ​ሥራ​ይ፡ ​ወድ​ግም​ት፡ ​ወቁ​ርጸ​ት፡ ​ፌራ፡ ​ዘደ​ጋ፡ ​ንዳ​ድ፡ ​ዘቆ​ላ፡ ​ወእ​ምኵ​ሉ፡ ​ደዌ​ያት፡
                            ​ከመ፡ ​ኢይ​ቅረ​ቡ፡ ​እም​ላዕ​ለ፡ ​ዓመ​ትከ ፨ <fo:inline id="d1e73618PRS13860HawituA">​ወይ​ዘሮ ​ሃዋ</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e73622PRS13861WalattaH">​ወለ​ተ፡ ​ሕይ​ወት</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e73632LIT5690MagicPrayer">
               <fo:inline>II) Fols 1r122–1r219: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Protective prayer against eye disease’ (​ጸሎ​ተ፡ ​ነደ​ራ፡), CAe 5690.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ፩ ​አም​ላክ፡ ​ጸሎ​ተ፡ ​ነዲ​ራ፡ ​ዝው​እቱ፡ ሕ ​ማመ፡
                                ​ዓይ​ነት፡ ​እኪ​ት፡ ​ወእ​ንዘ፡ ​የኃ​ውር፡ ​እግ​ዚእ​ነ፡ ​ውስተ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ባሕ​ረ፡ ​ጥብ​ርያ​ዶስ፡
                                ​ወምስ ​ሌሁ፡ ​፲ወ፪ ​አር​ዳኢ​ሁ፡
                            ​ወሶ​በ፡ ​ርዕ​ዩ፡ ​መል​ክዓ፡ ​ብእ​ሲት፡ <fo:inline>ኀራጊት፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​እን​ተ፡ ​ትነብ ​ር፡ ​በማ​ዕዶ​ተ፡ ​ፈለ​ግ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​አድ​ኅና፡ ​እም​ሕማመ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ደም፡ ​ወሾ​ተላ​ይ፡ ​ለዓ​መተ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔር<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e73657PRS13860HawituA">​ሐዊቱ ​አሊ</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e73661PRS13861WalattaH">​ወለ​ተ፡ ​ሕይ​ወት፡</fo:inline>
                                ​ሊስ፡ ​አፍ​ሊስ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​መሊ​ስ፡ ​ማላ​ሊስ፡ ​መላ​ልዮ​ስ፡ ​በኃ​ይለ፡ ​ዝን​ቱ፡ ​አስ​ማቲ​ከ፡ ​ዘአ​ርጋ​ዕከ፡ ​ኀይ​ለ፡ ​በረ​ድ፡ ​ወነ​ፋስ፡ ​ከማ​ሁ፡ ​አር​ግዕ፡ ​ደማ፡
                                ​ወአ​ፅገ​ዕ፡ ​ፍሬ፡ ​ማኅ​ፀና፡
                                ​እስከ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ትወ​ልድ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​በጊ​ዜሃ፡ ​ለዓ​መትከ ፨
                                <fo:inline id="d1e73676PRS13860HawituA">​ሐዋ</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e73680PRS13861WalattaH">​ወለ​ተ፡ ​ሕይ​ወት</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e73690LIT6739PPDam">
               <fo:inline>III) Fols 1r219–1r230: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Protective prayer against hemorrhage ( ḥǝmāma dam ),
                    containing  ʾasmāt 
                , CAe 6739.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The entire text is reproduced below.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ሕማ​መ፡ ​ደም፡ <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>
                                ​ተላ​ይ፡ ​ማሎ​ክ፡ ​ሉሎ​ክ፡ ​አፍ​ላሎ​ክ፡ ​በእ<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline> ​አስ​ማቲ​ከ፡ ​ዘአ​ንሳ​እከ፡ ​ለዓ​ልአ​ዛር፡ ​እም<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​ሰ፡ ​መቃ​ብር፡ ​ከማ​ሁ፡
                                ​አን​ሥዓ፡ ​እም​ሕማ​መ፡ ​ደም፡ ​ወወ​ሊድ፡ ​ወዕ​ግዲ​ሕል​ጅ፡ ​ለዓ​መተ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔር ፨
                                <fo:inline id="d1e73708PRS13860HawituA">​ሓዊቱ</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e73712PRS13861WalattaH">​ወለ​ተ፡ ​ሕይ​ወት</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e73722LIT6740PPWegat">
               <fo:inline>IV) Fols 1r230–1r240: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Protective prayer in Gǝʿǝz and Amharic against
                    stomach ache ( wǝgāt 
                    and  qurṣat ), containing  ʾasmāt 
                , incomplete, CAe 6740, in Gǝʿǝz and Amharic.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The text breaks off at the end due to material damage. The entire
                                preserved text is reproduced below.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ሕማ​መ፡ ​ውጋ​ት፡  ​ወቁ​ርጸ​ት፡ ​ድሜ​ጥር​ስ፡ ​ድሜ​ጥር​ስ፡ ​ድሜ​ጥር​ስ፡
                                ​ጋይ​ስጦ​ስ፡ <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​ስጦ​ስ፡ ​ጋይ​ስጦ​ስ፡ <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​ታው፡ ​ሰቈ​ታው፡ ​ሰቆ<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​ው፡
                                <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">​የል​ብ፡
                                ​ውጋ​ት፡ ​የሆ​ድ፡ ​ቁር​ጸጥ፡ ​ሸገ​ር፡ <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​ሸገ​ር፡ ​ጪጪ<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>V) Fol. 1v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e73750"
                                font-family="Ludolfus"
                                letter-spacing="0.5pt"
                                font-size="0.9em">Largely illegible text on the verso of the scroll</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>The verso contains traces of a miniature (Miniature 3) and a text (Textual unit V), both of which are
                                        now hardly visible.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>There are few scribal corrections. Rarely, characters are marked for deletion with strokes above and below
                                        or are striked through.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>The last visible line contains <fo:inline font-style="italic">Brillenbuchstaben</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>The name of the owner, mentioned in supplications throughout, was <fo:inline id="d1e73960PRS13860HawituA">Ḥawitu ʾAli</fo:inline>.
                                        The name <fo:inline id="d1e73962PRS13861WalattaH">Walatta Ḥǝywat</fo:inline>, possibly a later owner, has been added in different ink interlineally.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>5)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Order of textual units and miniatures: Recto: Miniature 1,
                                        Textual unit I, Miniature 2, Textual units II–IV; Verso:
                                        Miniature 3, Textual unit V.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>The three parchment strips are sewn together with narrow parchment strips.There is a small hole in the middle of the upper part of the scroll, maybe pointing
                                to a thread that once was attached there.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>1
                                    column (121 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Number of characters per line: 12–15.The left margin is delimited by a black line.There are no side margins.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            673 × 68–72 mm ()</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 1–2 mm, bottom: 1–2 mm ().
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>1
                                    column (119 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Number of characters per line: 11–12.The left margin is delimited by a black line.There are no side margins. The manuscript is damaged at the bottom.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            772 × 62–68 mm ()</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 1 mm ().
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Pricking and ruling are not visible. Pricking and ruling are not visible.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Twentieth century.. Probably a trained hand, but slightly irregular. Broad and
                                    cursive script. The characters are widely spaced. Some
                                    characters, e.g. ጥ with
                                    rounded strokes, give a slightly older impression.<fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: Incipits (groups of rubricated lines alternating with groups of black lines or
                                    pairs of rubricated lines); several groups of lines within the main body of the Legend of St Susǝnyos and Wǝrzǝlyā and
                                    ms_i2;
                                    the name of <fo:inline id="d1e73884PRS5684JesusCh">Jesus</fo:inline>; names of the owners; elements of numerals and punctuation signs.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Decoration</fo:block>
         <fo:block margin-top="3mm" margin-bottom="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">The two illustrated panels of this scroll are highly unusual and were
                                 likely produced (or subsequently added) around the 1960s or 1970s for the tourist market,
                                 close in time to when the scroll was purchased by its former owner 
                                 <fo:inline id="d1e73897PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline>. 
                                 This is further supported by the presence of synthetic colours to paint the background behind
                                 the figure at the centre of the scroll. Bands, filled with interlace or floral motifs mark the 
                                 upper and lower boundaries of the illustrated panels.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Miniatures</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(176) <fo:inline>A variation of the net of Solomon motif, with a 3 × 3 grid featuring a face at its centre, 
                                 and four different types of crosses at its corners. There are bands above and below it featuring 
                                 respectively interlaced snakes and crosses. A bird sits atop the
                                 composition and pecks at the snakes, 
                                 while a second pair of snakes face each other in the space above it.</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(177) <fo:inline>An unidentified person in prayer.</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Headpieces</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Drawings</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Other</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is good.Small losses are present in the upper part of the parchment support, likely caused by insects.
                                The parchment is very stiff, and at the lowest part of the scroll, it has apparently broken off,
                                with loss of text. As the text has been written without leaving a margin, many characters at the beginning and end
                                of a line are not legible anymore. Only traces remain of a drawing and text on the verso of the scroll. It is not
                                clear whether this has been intentionally erased or has worn out due to its location on the exterior of the
                                rolled up scroll.
                                The stitching that joins strip 2 and strip 3 has become
                                partly undone.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>1960s–
                                1970s</fo:inline>
                            The manuscript can be dated palaeographically and by the style of the
                            miniatures to the 1960s to 1970s.
                            The name of the original owner was <fo:inline id="d1e73993PRS13860HawituA">Ḥawitu ʾAli</fo:inline>; the name of
                            <fo:inline id="d1e73995PRS13861WalattaH">Walatta Ḥǝywat</fo:inline>, probably a later owner, has been added interlineally
                            (see Varia note 4).
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>The provenance of the manuscript is unknown.</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e74005PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethg40">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethg40</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
