      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethe38"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. e. 38</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Arch. O. e. 13, Juel-Jensen 41, Lady Meux 4)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex183×129 mm (weight: 785g), 83 fols (5 p. blank), 10 quires, 1775–1815.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>I) <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true"/>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e82124LIT1460Gadlah">
               <fo:inline>II) Fols 11ra–69rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Vita of Anne’ (​ገድ​ለ፡ ​ሐና፡), CAe 1460.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e82130LIT1460Gadlah#Prologue">
               <fo:inline>II-1) Fols 11ra–12ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Vita of Anne: Prologue</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​በስ​መ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​አብ፡ ​ገባ​ሬ፡  ​ሰማ​ያት ፤  ​ወም​ድር፡ ​ህላ​ዌሁ፡ ​ዘኢይ ​ትአ​መር፡ ​እም​ልበ፡ ​መዋ​ቲ፡
                                            ​ስው​ር፡  ​ወዘ​ኢይ​ትከ​ሀል፡ ​ይበ​ልዎ፡ ​እም​ዝ፡ ​ለዝ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ዝ፡ ​በጥ​ንተ፡ ​ነገር ፨ 
                                    ​ዳዕ​ሙ፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ህላ​ዌሁ፡ ​የአ​ምር ፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ሊተ​ኒ፡ ​ያፈ​ትወ​ኒ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​እን​ግር፡ ​ዕበ​ያ፡ ​ለይ​እቲ፡ ​ገነ​ት፡ ​ወም​ድር ፨ 
                                    ​ምድ​ርሂ፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡  ​ሐና፡  ​ወገ​ነት​ሂ፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​እግ​ዝእ​ትነ፡
                                     ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ወፍ​ሬሃ​ኒ፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ወል​ዳ፡ ​እግ​ዚእ​ነ፡ ​ወመ​ድኃ​ኒነ፡  ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡  ​ሎቱ፡ ​ስብ​ሐት፡
                                     ​ጸሎ​ታ፡ ​ለቅ​ድስ​ት፡  ​ሐና፡  ​ያድ​ኅኖ፡
                                        ለ<fo:inline id="d1e82175PRS12983GabraMa">​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline> ​ለዓ፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡
                                            ​ዓ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አ። ​አሜ​ን።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e82195LIT1460Gadlah#Monday">
               <fo:inline>II-2) Fols 12rb–26ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Vita of Anne: Reading for Monday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ ​ስ፡  ፩  ​አም​ላክ፡ ​በጸ​ሎታ፡ ​ለቅድ ​ስት፡ ​ሐና፡ ​ያድ​ኅኖ፡
                                        ለ<fo:inline id="d1e82209PRS12983GabraMa">​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline> ​እዌ​ጥን፡ ​በረ​ድኤ​ተ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ወጸ​ጋሁ፡ 
                                    ​ዘተ​ውህ​በ፡
                                    ​ለለ ​፩፩ ፡ ​ለለ​ኵሉ፡ ​በበ​መሥ​ፈር​ተ፡ ​ሀብ​ቱ፡ ለ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡  ​ዘዓ​ርገ​ሂ፡
                                    ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ወዘ​ወረ​ደሂ፡ ው  (fol. 12va)  ​እቱ፡ ​ወዘ​ሀሎ፡
                                    <fo:inline>መልዕተ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ሰማ​ያት፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ይፈ​ጽም፡ ​ኵሎ፡ ​በቀ​ዳሚ፡ ​ዘነ​ቢያ​ት፡ ​ወበ​ዳግ​ም፡ ​ዘሐዋ ር ​ያት፡ ​ወበ​ሣል​ስ፡ ​ዘሊ​ቃው​ንት ፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​አነ​ኒ፡ ​እቤ፡ ​ከማ​ሁ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​ዘአ​ርኰ​ሰ፡ ​ስመ፡  ​ማር  (fol. 26ra)  ​ያም፡  ​ድን​ግል፡ ​ወቡ​ርክ​ት፡ ​ወለ​ተ፡ 
                                     ​ሐና፡ 
                                    ወ ​ኢያ​ቄም፡  ​እሙ፡ ለ ​አማ​ኑኤ​ል፡  ​አም​ላክ​ነ፡ ​ለይ​ሙት፡ ​ሞተ፡ ​በነ​ፍሱ፡ ​ወሥ​ጋሁ፡
                                    ​ወኢ​ይር​ከብ፡ ​ጥዒ​ና፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜን ፨ ፨ ፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e82266LIT1460Gadlah#Tuesday">
               <fo:inline>II-3) Fols 26ra–35ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Vita of Anne: Reading for Tuesday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዝን​ቱ፡ ​ነገ​ር፡ ​ንዑ፡ ​ንወ​ድሳ፡ ​ለሐ​ና፡  ​እስ​መ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ወደ​ሳ፡ ​ወበ​ውዳ​ሴሁ፡ ​ኃደ​ረ፡ ​ለወ​ለተ፡
                                     ​ሐና፡  ​በከ​ርሣ ፨ 
                                    ​ንዑ፡ ​ናዕ​ብያ፡ ለ ​ሐና፡  (b)   ​እስ​መ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​አዕ​በያ፡
                                    ​እም​ሔው​ቱ፡ ​ይእ​ቲ፡ ​እመ​ንገ​ለ፡ ​ሥጋ። ​ይእ​ቲ፡ ​ትት​በደ​ር፡ ​እም​ነ፡ ​ወር​ቅ፡ ​ወብ​ሩር፡ ​ወት​ኄይ​ስ፡ ​ፈድ​ፋደ፡ ​እም​ነ፡ 
                                     ፲ ወ ፪  ​አዕ​ናቍ፡
                                    ​ዘዘ​ዚአ​ሁ፡ ​ኅብ​ሮን፡ ​ወት​ሤኒ፡ ​እም​ፀሐ​ይ፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ወአ​ዕረ​ፈት፡ ​ወፈ​ለሰ​ት፡ ​በወ​ርኃ፡ ​ግዕ​ዝ፡ ​አመ፡ ​፲ወ ​፩፡  ​ለኅ​ዳር ፨ 
                                    ​ወበ​ወር​ኃ፡ ​ዕብ​ራው​ያን፡ ​ዳግ​ማይ፡ ​ታስ​ሪን ፨ 
                                    ​ወበ​ሮሜ፡ ​ናኦ​ብሮ​ስ፡ ​አመ፡  ፮  ​ዕረ​ፍታ፡ ወ  (fol. 35ra)  ​ቀበ​ርዋ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​መቃ​ብረ፡ 
                                    ​አበ​ዊሃ፡ ​በከ​መ፡ ​ሐጎ​ሙ፡ ​ለው​ሉደ፡ ​አሮ​ን፡ ​እስ​ከ፡
                                    ​ማጣ​ት፡ ​አቡሃ ፨  ​ጸሎ​ታ፡ ​ወበ​ረከ​ታ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ገብ​ራ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e82318PRS12983GabraMa">​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                                    ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜን ፤
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e82331LIT1460Gadlah#Wednesday">
               <fo:inline>II-4) Fols 35ra–45ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Vita of Anne: Reading for Wednesday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ወዝ​ንቱ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​ኮነ፡ ​ዕረ​ፍታ፡ ​ለሐ​ና፡ ​እን ​ዘ፡ ​ሀለ​ወት፡ ​እግ​ዝእ​ትነ፡  ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ቤተ፡
                                    ​መቅ​ደስ፡ ​ወነ​ገር​ዋ፡ ​ከመ፡   (b)   ​አዕ​ረፈ​ት፡  ​ሐና፡  ​እማ፡ ​ወሰ​ሚዓ፡ ​እግ​ዝእ​ትነ፡  ​ማር​ያም፡ 
                                    ​በከ​የት፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ትብ​ል፡ ​ወይ፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​አሌ፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​እም​የ፡ ​ኃደ​ገተ​ኒ፡ ​ትክ​ዝተ፡ ​ወይ፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​አሌ፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​እመ፡ ​መኑ፡ ​ይከ​ውነ​ኒ፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​ከማ​ኪ፡
                                    ​ወለ​መኑ፡ ​ኃደ​ግኒ፡ ​ወይ፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​አሌ፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​እም​የ፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ወይ​ቤ፡ ​ብፁ​ዕ፡  ​ኢያ​ቄም፡  ​ናሁ፡ ​አእ​መር​ኩ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​መሀ​ረኒ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ወተ​ወክ​ፈኒ፡ ​ወራ​እይ​ኒ፡ ​ዘአ​ስተ​ርአ​የኒ፡ ​እሙ​ነ፡
                                    ​ውእቱ ፨  ​ወተ​መይ​ጠ፡  ​ኢያ​ቄም፡  ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ቤቱ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ይሴ​ብሖ፡ 
                                    ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​በፍ​ሥሐ፡ ​ወበ​ሐሴ​ት፡ ​ለዘ​ሎቱ፡ ​ይደ​ሉ፡
                                    ​ክብ​ር፡ ​ወስ​ብሐ​ት፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ ፤  ​ዓለም ፤  ​አሜን ፤
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e82382LIT1460Gadlah#Thursday">
               <fo:inline>II-5) Fols 45rb–54ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Vita of Anne: Reading for Thursday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ናይ​ድዕ፡ ​ባህ​ለ፡ ​ነቢ​ያት፡ ​ስማ​ዕ፡ ​ዘይ​ቤሎ፡  ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔር ፤  ​ለአ​ቡነ ፤  ​አዳም ፤  ​እመ ​ጽእ፡ ​አነ፡ ​ለል​የ፡ ​በ፭፡
                                                    ​ዕለ​ተ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ቀ፡  ​ዕለ​ት፡ ​እት​ወለ​ድ፡ ​እም​ወለ​ትከ ፨ 
                                    ​አሜ​ሃ፡ ​እም​ህረ​ከ፡ ​ወእ​ሣሃ​ለከ፡ ​በብ​ዝኃ፡ ​ምሕ​ረትየ ፨  ለ ​፶፻  ​ዓመ​ታት፡ 
                                    ​ረሰ​ዮን፡ ​ከመ፡  ፭  ​ዕለ​ታት፡
                                    ​ወለ ​፭፻  ​ዓመ​ታት፡
                                    ​ረሰ​ዮን፡ ​ከመ፡  ፮ 
                                    ​ሠዓ​ተ፡ ​ዕለት ፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​መጽ​ሐፈ፡ ​ኃጢ​አቱ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ወለ​ታ፡ ​እግ​ዚእ​ነ፡  ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡  ​ይደ​ምስ​ስ፡ ​ወይ​ስጥ​ጥ፡ ​ወይ​ክፍ​ሎ፡ ​ቁመ​ተ፡ 
                                      (fol. 54ra)  
                                    ​ምስ​ሌሃ፡ ​በየ​ማነ፡ ​መን​ግሥ​ቱ፡ ​ዘኢ​ይሠ​ዓር፡ ​ወኢ​ይት​ዌለጥ ፨ 
                                    ​ለዓ​ለም፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን፡ ​ወአ​ሜን፡ ​ለይ​ኩን፡ ​ለይ​ኩን ፨ ፨ ፨ ፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e82459LIT1460Gadlah#Friday">
               <fo:inline>II-6) Fols 54ra–60va: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Vita of Anne: Reading for Friday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​በስ​መ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​አብ፡ ​ለሰ​ማይ፡  ​ዘረ​በቦ ፨ 
                                    ​ወበ​ስመ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ወ ​ልድ፡ ​ዋሕ​ድ፡ ​ዘአ​ምጽ​አ፡ ​ዓለ​መ፡
                                        ​እም​ኀበ፡  ​አልቦ ፨  ​ወበ​ስመ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​መን​ፈስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ 
                                    ​ጰራ  (b) <fo:inline>[ቅ]</fo:inline>​ሊጦ​ስ፡
                                    ​መን​ፈሰ፡ ​አለ​ብዎ፡ ​ወአ​ጥብቦ ፨  ​ናን​ብብ፡ ​ዘን​ተ፡ ​ድር​ሳነ፡
                                    ​ዘክ​ቡረ፡ ​ስም፡ ​ወል​ዑለ፡ ​ዝክ​ር፡  ​ኢያ​ቄም፡  ​አቡ​ሃ፡ ​ለእ​ግዝ​እት​ነ፡ ​ወላ​ዲተ፡ ​አም​ላክ፡  ​ማር​ያም፡ 
                                    ​ድን​ግል፡ ​በቍ​ዔት፡ ​ለዘ​ያነ​ብቦ ፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ኦ ​ክቡ​ር፡  ኦ ​ልዑል ፤ ኦ ​ስቡሕ ፤
                                    ኦ ​ጻድቅ ፤
                                    ኦ ​ኅሩይ ፤ ኦ ​ትሩፍ ፤ ኦ ​ኄር ፤  ​እም​ኄራ​ን፡  ​ኢያቄ  (fol. 60va)  ​ም፡ 
                                    ​ሰአ​ል፡ ​ወጸ​ሊ፡ ​ለዘ​ያፈ​ቅረ​ከ፡ ​ፈድ​ፋደ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e82547PRS12983GabraMa">​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline> ​ኅር​ቱም፡ ​ለገ​ቢረ፡
                                    ​ሠና​ይ፡ ​ወጽ​ድቅ፡ ​ድኩ​ም፡ ​ይት​ከዐ​ው፡ ​በረ​ከት​ከ፡ ​ላዕ​ሌሁ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ዝና​ም፡ ​እም​ይእ​ዜ፡ ​ወእ​ስከ፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለም ፤ አ ፨ ​አሜ​ን።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e82567LIT1460Gadlah#Saturday">
               <fo:inline>II-7) Fols 60va–65vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Vita of Anne: Reading for Saturday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ንት​መየ​ጥ፡ ​ካዕ​በ፡ ​ንወ​ድሳ፡ ​ለወ​ለተ፡ ​ኢያ​ቄም፡ ​ወሐ​ና፡ ​ድን ​ግል፡
                                    ​መፆ​ረ፡ ​ነበ​ልባ​ል፡ ​ዘስ​ሙ፡ ​አማ​ኑኤል ፨  ​ወን​ዜኑ፡   (b)  
                                    ​ክብ​ረ፡ ​ልደ​ታ፡ ​እም​ነ፡ ​ክቡ​ር፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ፡ ​ጻድ​ቅ፡ ​ወን​ጹሐ፡ ​ምግ​ባር፡ ​ወት​ጉህ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​መላ​እክት ፨  ​ሠና​ይኬ፡ ​ተዜ​ያን​ዎ፡ ​ልደ​ታ፡ ​ለእ​ግዝ​እት​ነ፡
                                     ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ወላ​ዲተ፡ ​አም​ላክ፡ ​ድን​ግል፡ ​ዘይ​ጥዕ​ም፡ ​ጥቀ፡ ​እመ​ዐር፡ ​ወሦ​ከር፡ ​ወከ​መ፡ ​ወይ​ን፡ ​መዓ​ርዒር ፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ወእ​ምድ​ኅረ፡ ​ኅዳ​ጥ፡ ​መዋ​ዕል፡ ​ይቤ​ሎሙ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ለደ​ቂቀ፡ ​እስ​ራኤ​ል፡ ​ሶበ፡ ​አም​ዕዕ​ዎ፡ ​አየ​ኑ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​ተሐ​ንፁ፡ ​ለም​ዕራ​ፍየ፡ ​ወአ​የኑ፡ ​መካ​ነ፡ ​ለማ​ኅደ​ርየ ፨ 
                                    ​ነያ፡   (b)   ​ማኅ​ደር​የሰ፡ ​እን​ተ፡ ​አመ​ጽኣ፡ ​ዘእ​ድ፡ ​ኢገ​ብራ፡ ​ዘት​ከው​ን፡ ​መድ​ኃኒ​ተ፡  ለ ​አዳ​ም፡ 
                                    ​ወለ​ደቂቁ ፨ ፨ ፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e82620LIT1460Gadlah#Sunday">
               <fo:inline>II-8) Fols 65vb–69rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Vita of Anne: Reading for Sunday</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ዝን​ቱ፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​መጽ​ሐፈ፡ ​ዜና፡ ​ልደ​ታ፡ ​ለእ ​ግዝ​እት​ነ፡  ​ማር​ያም፡  
                                    ​ወለ​ተ፡  ​ኢያ​ቄም፡ 
                                    ​ወል​ደ፡  ​ዳዊ​ት፡  ​ንጉ​ሥ፡  ​ሰሎ​ሞን፡  ​ወለ​ዶ፡ ​ለና​ታን፡ ​ወና​ታን፡ ​ወለ​ዶ፡ ​ለሌ​ዊ፡ ​ወሌ​ዊ፡ ​ወለ​ደ፡ 
                                    ​ማጣ​ትሃ፡
                                    ​ወቅ​ስራ​ሃ፡ ​ወቅ  (fol. 66ra)  ​ስራ፡ ​ወለ​ደ፡  ​ኢያ​ቄም ​ሃ፡ ​አቡ​ሃ፡ ​ለእ​ግዝ​እት​ነ፡
                                     ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ድን​ግል፡ ​ቅድ​ስት፡
                                    ​ወማ​ጣት፡ ​ወለ​ደ፡  ፫ ት ፤ ፡ ​አዋ​ልደ፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ወከ​ማሃ፡ ​ክመ፡ ​መጽ​ኡ፡ ​ብዙ​ኃን፡ ​ሕሙ​ማን፡ ​ወገ​ሠሥ​ዋ፡ ​ወተ​ፈወ​ሱ፡ ​ወሐይ  (b)  ​ዉ፡ ​እም​ደዌ​ሆሙ፡ ​ወኮ​ነ፡ ​ዕፁ​በ፡ ​ዝ፡ ​ግብ​ር፡ ​በኀ​በ፡ ​ኵሎ​ሙ፡
                                    ​ሊቃ​ናተ፡ ​እስ​ራኤል ፨  ​ጸሎ​ታ፡ ​ወስ​እለ​ታ፡ ​ወጸ​ሎተ፡  ​ኢያ​ቄም፡  ​ምታ፡ ​ይክ​ድኖ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ሥሙ​ር፡ ​ወል​ታ፡ ​ለገ​ብራ፡
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e82672PRS12983GabraMa">​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline> ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን፡
                                    ​ወአ​ሜን፡ ​ለይ​ኩን፡ ​ለይ​ኩን ፨ ፨ ፨
                                </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ለዛ​ቲ፡ ​መጽ​ሐፍ፡  ​ዜና​ሃ፡ ​ለብ​ፅዕ​ት፡  ​ሐና፡  (fol. 69ra)   ​ወዜ​ና፡ ​ውዳ​ሴ፡ ​ልደ​ቱ፡ ​ለክ​ቡር፡
                                     ​ኢያ​ቄም፡  ​ዘአ​ጽሐ​ፋ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e82704PRS12983GabraMa">​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                                    ​ነዳ​ይ፡ ​ወም​ስኪ​ን፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ያስ​ተዋ​ጽእ፡ ​እም​ጥሪ​ቱ፡ ​ይጽ​ሐፍ፡ ​ስሞ፡ ​እግ​ዚእ​ነ፡  ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡  ​በቀ​ለመ፡ ​ብር​ሃን፡
                                    ​ዘኢ​ይደ​መሰ​ስ፡ ​ወለ​ጸሐ​ፊሁ​ኒ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e82711PRS12986GabraKr">​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡</fo:inline> ​ኃጥ​እ፡ ​ወእ​ቡስ ፨ 
                                    ​እም​ፍኖ​ተ፡ ​ኃጢ​አት፡ ​ርኩ​ስ፡ ​ዘኢ​ይት​ገሠ​ሥ፡   (b)   ​ያድ​ኅኖ​ሙ፡ ​ትን​ብል​ናሆ​ሙ፡ ለ ፪ ​ሆሙ፡ ​እመ፡ ​ዕለ​ተ፡ ​ፍዳ፡ ​ወኂ​ስ፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡
                                    ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን፡ ​ወአ​ሜን፡ ​ለይ​ኩን፡ ​ለይ​ኩን ​፨=፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e82733LIT5917TaammeraHa">
               <fo:inline>III) Fols 69rb–72vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Miracles of Anne’ (​ተአ​ምረ፡ ​ሐና፡), CAe 5917.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ተአ​ምሪ​ሃ፡ ​ለቅ​ድስ​ት፡ ​ወብ​ፅዕ​ት፡ ​ሐና፡  ​እመ ፤
                                    ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ወላ​ዲተ ፤  ​አም​ላክ ፤ 
                                    ​ጸሎታ ፤  ​ወበ​ረከታ ፤
                                     (fol. 69va)   ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ገብ​ራ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e82765PRS12983GabraMa">​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline> ​ለዓ​ለመ፡
                                    ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜን ፨  ​ወሀ​ሎ፡
                                     ፩ ፡ ​ብእ​ሲ፡ ​እም​ዘመ​ደ፡ ​ይሁ​ዳ፡ ​ወይ​ሰመ​ይ፡  ​ኢያ​ቄም፡  ​ወአ​ውሰ​በ፡ ​ብእ​ሲተ፡ ​እም​አዋ​ልደ፡
                                    ​ካህ​ናት፡ ​ወት​ሰመ​ይ፡  ​ሐና፡  ​ወክ​ልዔ​ሆሙ፡ ​ኄራ​ን፡ ​ወሥ​ሙራ​ን፡ ​ወይ​ሄል​ዉ፡ ​በሕ​ገ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔር ፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ወይ​ቤል​ዋ፡  ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ለኪ፡ ​ኦብ​ፅዕ​ት፡ ወ ​ኅሪ ​ት፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡
                                    ​ወነ​ሥእ​ዋ፡ ​ወሐ​ቀፍ​ዋ፡ ​ወአ​ብዕ​ዋ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​መቅ​ደስ፡ ​አመ፡ ሠ  (b)  ​ሉሱ፡ ​ለታ​ኅሣ​ሥ፡ ​በሰ​ላመ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔር ፨ 
                                    ​ጸሎ​ታ፡ ​ወበ​ረከ​ታ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ገብ​ራ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e82802PRS12983GabraMa">​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                                    ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜን ፨
                                    ፨ ፨ ፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e82823LIT2897RepCh178">
               <fo:inline>IV) Fols 72vb–75va: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Malkǝʾ-hymn to St Anne, CAe 2897.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ለዝ​ክረ፡ ​ስም​ኪ፡ ​እም​ዝክ​ረ፡  ​ማኅ​ሌት ፤  ​አዳም ፤  ለ ​ምግ​ባር ​ኪ፡ ​ሰላም ፤
                                ​ወለ​ስእ​ርተ፡ ​ርእ​ስኪ፡ ​ጸሊ​ም። ​እመ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡ ​ሐና፡ ወ  (fol. 73ra)   ​ሕይ​ወተ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​ዓለም ፨ 
                                ​ብኪ፡
                                ​ተሣ​ረሩ፡ ​እለ፡ ​ዘሥ​ጋ፡ ​ወደም ፨  ​ወመ​ላእ​ክት፡ ​ዘል​ዑል፡ ​አር​ያም ፨
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ስብ​ሐት፡  ​ይደ​ሉ፡ ለ ​ማር​ያም፡ 
                                ​በሰ​ጊድ፡ ​ወዝ​ማሬ ፨  ​ዘም​ስለ፡
                                 ፪ ​ሆን፡ ​በኁ​ባሬ ፨ 
                                ​እመ፡  ​ማር​ያም፡ ​ሐና፡  ​ዕን​ቈ፡ ​ሶም፡ ​ወወ​ራውሬ ፨  ​ይደ  (fol. 75va)  ​ምሰ​ሱ፡ ​ፀረ፡ ​ዚአ​የ፡ ​ወኢ​ይት​ርፉ፡
                                ​ለፍሬ ፨  ​ከመ፡ ​ተደ​ምሰ​ሱ፡ ​ደቂ​ቁ፡ ​ለቆሬ ፨
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e82905LIT5919SalamHa">
               <fo:inline>V) Fols 75va–76rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Salāmta-hymn to St Anne, CAe 5919.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ለኪ፡  ​ጥዕ​ምተ፡ ​ስም፡ ​ወዝ​ክረ፡ ​ለፄ​ወ፡ ​መለ​ኮት፡ ​ቅሱም ፨
                                ​ሐና፡  ​ቅድ​ስት፡
                                ​እመ፡  ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ዘነ​ገሥ​ኪ፡ ​በአ​ርያም ፨
                                ​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ለኪ፡ ​ሐና፡  ​ጽባ​ሕ፡
                                 ​ወማ​ርያ​ም፡  ​ሰማይ ፨ 
                                ​እን​ተ፡ ​ወለ​ደቶ፡ ለ  (b)  ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡  ​ፀሐይ ፨ 
                                ​ዘያ​ውዒ፡ ​ሦከ፡ ​ጌጋይ ፨
                                ​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ለኪ፡  ​ዘኪ​ልቂ​ዶን፡  ​ሐና፡  ​ወዘ​ባሕ​ርይ፡ ​ፅዱል ፨
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ለኪ፡ ​ሐና፡  ​ንጽ​ሕት፡ ወ ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ጳጦስ ፨ 
                                ​እን​ተ፡ ​ወለ​ደቶ፡
                                ለ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡  ​ንጉሥ ፨  ​ኃጢ​አተ፡ ​ዘይ​ደመ​ስስ ፨
                                 (b)  ​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ለኪ፡ 
                                ​አመ​ኒ፡ ​መጽ​አኒ፡ ​መል​አከ፡ ​ሞት፡ ​መስጢ ፤  ​እም​ኔየ፡  ​ሐና፡  ​ኢት​ትፈ​ለጢ ፨ 
                                ​መጽ​ሐፈ፡ ​ዕዳ​የ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡
                                ​ትሠ​ጥጢ ፨  ​ወላ​ህየ፡ ​በሐ​ሤት፡
                                ​ወልጢ ​፨=፨
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e83007LIT5918TaammeraHaIy">
               <fo:inline>VI) Fols 76va–78va: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Miracles of Anne and Joachim’ (​ተአ​ምራ​ቲሆ​ሙ፡ ​ለሐ​ና፡ ​ወኢ​ያቄ​ም፡), CAe 5918.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ተአ​ምራ​ቲሆ​ሙ፡ ​ለሐ​ና፡ ወ ​ኢያ​ቄም፡ ​ዘወ​ለድ​ዋ፡ ለ ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ወላ​ዲተ፡ ​ሰማ​ያዊ፡
                                ​ወም​ድራ​ዊ፡ ​ጸሎ​ቶሙ፡ ​ወበ​ረከ​ቶሙ፡ ​የሃ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ፍቁ​ሮሙ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e83020PRS12983GabraMa">​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                                ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜን ፨ 
                                ​ናሁ፡ ​ተብ​ህለ​ት፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ነበ​ረት፡   (b)  ​ሐና፡ ​ብፅ​ዕት፡ ​ብእ​ሲተ፡ ​ኢያ​ቄም፡ 
                                ​በብ​ዙኅ፡ ​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​ወወ​ሀባ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ዘር​ዓ፡ ​ቡር​ክተ፡ ​ወእ​ምድ​ኅረ፡  ፯  ​ወር​ህ፡ ​ተዓ​ውቀ፡ ​ፅን​ሳ፡ ለ ​ሐና፡ 
                                ​ወሰ​ምዑ፡ ​አዝ​ማዲ​ሃ፡ ​ወአ​ዝማ​ደ፡ ​ምታ፡ ​ወመ​ጽኡ፡ ​ኀቤ​ሃ፡
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ወይ​ቤሎ​ሙ፡ ለ ​ሐና፡  ​ወኢ​ያቄ​ም፡ ​ተን​ሥኡ፡ ​ክቡ​ራነ፡ ​ዘመ​ድ፡ <fo:inline>ወወወዶሙ፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                                ​ደብ​ረ፡ ​ወሰ​ወሮ​ሙ፡ ​ወተ​ወል​ደት፡ ​በህ​የ፡  ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ስማ፡ ​ምል​ዕተ፡ ​ሞገ​ስ፡ ​ወግ​ርማ፡ ​ወለ​ነኒ፡ ​ታድ​ኅነ​ነ፡ ​እመ​ሥገ​ርተ፡
                                ​አር​ዌ፡ ​መስ​ቲማ ፨  ​ጸሎ​ቶሙ፡ ​ወበ​ረከ​ቶሙ፡   (b)   ለ ​ሐና፡  
                                ወ ​ኢያ​ቄም፡  ​የሃ​ሉ፡
                                ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ፍቁ​ሮሙ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e83070PRS12983GabraMa">​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                                ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜን ፨ ፨ ፨ ፨
                            </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​በረ​ከታ ቲ ​ሆሙ።  ​ለሐ​ና፡ ​ወኢ​ያቄ​ም፡  ​ዘወ​ለድ​ዋ፡
                                 ​ለማ​ርያ​ም፡  ​መራ​ን፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ያድ​ኅነ​ነ፡ <fo:inline>እመሥገርት፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​አር​ዌ፡ ​ርጉ​ም፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜን ፨ 
                                ሃ ​ሌ፡ ​ሉያ፡ 
                                ​በብ​ዝሖ፡ <fo:inline>ኂሩትክም፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ኢያ​ቄም፡ ወ  (fol. 78va)  ​ሐና፡  ​ሰው​ሩነ፡ ​እም​ሰይ​ጣን፡ ​መከ​ራ፡ ​ለዛ​ቲ፡ ​መጽ​ሐፍ፡
                                ​ዘአ​ንበ​ባ፡ ​ወዘ​ተር​ጐማ፡ ​ኢት​ርስ​ኡኒ፡ ​አቡ​ነ፡ ​ዘበ​ሰማ​ያት፡ ​ዘአ​ንበ​ብክ​ዋ።
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Colophon</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block font-family="Ludolfus">Fols 10r–10v: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">The colophon is written in Gǝʿǝz and Amharic.
                                It states that the manuscript was commissioned by <fo:inline id="d1e82075PRS12983GabraMa">
                                 <fo:inline font-style="italic">ʾAbbā</fo:inline> Gabra Māryām</fo:inline>,
                                son of the deacon <fo:inline id="d1e82080PRS12985AmdaSe">ʾAmda Ṣǝyon</fo:inline>,
                                at the time of <fo:inline id="d1e82082PRS9978Waldase">
                                 <fo:inline font-style="italic">rās</fo:inline> Walda Śǝllāse</fo:inline>.
                                The colophon also states that the manuscript was copied by <fo:inline id="d1e82087PRS12986GabraKr">Gabra Krǝstos</fo:inline> and illustrated by
                                <fo:inline id="d1e82089PRS12987HabtaGa">Habta Gabrǝʾel</fo:inline>.
                                Other individuals are mentioned: <fo:inline id="d1e82092PRS12981WaldaGa">
                                 <fo:inline font-style="italic">ʾAbbā</fo:inline> Walda Garimā</fo:inline>,
                                <fo:inline id="d1e82097PRS12982Ananiqos">
                                 <fo:inline font-style="italic">ʾAbbā</fo:inline> ʾAnāniqos</fo:inline>,
                                <fo:inline id="d1e82102PRS12984TasfaMi">Tasfā Mikāʾel</fo:inline>,
                                and <fo:inline id="d1e82104PRS12988WaldaSe">
                                 <fo:inline font-style="italic">ʾAbbā</fo:inline> Walda Śǝllāse</fo:inline>.
                                According to the colophon, the book was written in the monastery of <fo:inline id="d1e82109LOC2297DabraL">Dabra Libānos</fo:inline>, in <fo:inline id="d1e82111LOC5597Sawa">Šawā</fo:inline>.
                                Two short <fo:inline font-style="italic">salām</fo:inline>-hymns in honour of Anne and
                                Joachim are embedded in the colophon.
                                They are separated with chains of red and black dots or with black and red lines.
                                </fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                        <fo:block font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ዘተ​ጽሕ​ፈት፡ ​በም​ድረ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e81903LOC5597Sawa">​ሻዋ፡</fo:inline> በ<fo:inline id="d1e81906LOC2297DabraL">​ደብ​ረ፡ ​ሊባ​ኖስ፡</fo:inline>
                            ​በም​ድረ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e81909PRS9162TaklaHa">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​አቡ​ነ፡</fo:inline> ​ተክ​ለ፡ ​ሃይ​ማኖ​ት፡</fo:inline> ​አል​ቦ፡
                            ​ዘየ​ዓቢ፡ ​እም​ክብ​ራ፡ ለ<fo:inline id="d1e81916LOC2297DabraL">​ደብ​ረ፡ ​ሊባ​ኖስ፡</fo:inline> ​ዘእ​ንበ​ለ፡
                              ​መቃ​ብረ፡ ​መድ​ኅን።</fo:block>
                        <fo:block font-family="Ludolfus">
                           <fo:inline id="d1e81925PRS12981WaldaGa">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​አባ፡</fo:inline> ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ገሪ​ማ፡</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline id="d1e81932PRS12982Ananiqos">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​አባ፡</fo:inline> ​አና​ኒቆ​ስ፡</fo:inline>
                            ​እን​ዴት፡ ​አላ​ችሁ፡ ​አሉ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e81939PRS12983GabraMa">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​አባ፡</fo:inline> ​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline id="d1e81946PRS12984TasfaMi">​ወተ​ስፋ፡ ​ሚካ​ኤል።</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline id="d1e81950PRS9978Waldase">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​ራስ፡</fo:inline> ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ሥላ​ሴ፡</fo:inline>
                            ለ<fo:inline id="d1e81958LOC1310Aksum">​አኵ​ስም፡</fo:inline> ​አድ​ርሱ፡ ​ታቦ​ት፡ ​ጠባ​ቂ፡ ​ይድ​ገማ​ት፡ ​ይህ​ችን፡ ​መጽ​ሐፍ፡ ​ለመ​ጣ፡
                            <fo:inline id="d1e81961PRS9978Waldase">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​ራስ፡</fo:inline> ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ሥላ​ሴ፡</fo:inline> ​ወቄ​ት፡ ​ይስ​ጡ፡ ​ስለ፡ ​ጽላ​ተ፡ ​ሙሴ።
                                    
                                    
                                     ​ሰላ​ም፡  ​ለኪ፡ ​እመ፡  ​ማር​ያም፡ ​ሐና፡  ​ዘወ​ለድ​ኪ፡ ​አፈ፡ ​ብር​ጋና ፨ 
                                    ​ሰአ​ሪተ፡ ​መር​ገም፡ ​ሰዓ​ሪተ፡ ​ሙስና ፨ ​ሰላ​ም፡  ​ለኪ ፨ ፨ ​ሰላ​ም፡  ​ለከ፡ ኢ ​ያቄ​ም፡  ​አረ​ጋዊ ፨ 
                                    ​ወላ​ዴ፡  ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ወለ​ተ፡ ​ዳዊ​ት፡ ​ዕን​ቃዊ ፨ ​ሰላ፡ 
                            ​ም፡ ​ሳይ​ሆን፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ይፍ​ታች​ሁ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ትር​ከቡ፡ ​እሤ​ተ፡ ​በወ​ለታ፡ ​ፍቃ​ዳች​ሁ፡</fo:block>
                        <fo:block font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                 ​ዝመ​ጽሐ​ፍ፡ ዘ ​ኢያ​ቄም፡ ​ወሐ​ና፡  ​ትብ​ጻሕ፡ ​ኀበ፡ ​ገበ​ዘ፡
                                <fo:inline>አኩስም፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ርእ​ሰ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ 
                                ​ታቦ​ታት ፨  ​ኵሉ፡ ​የሐ​ልፍ፡ ​ዘኢ​ተሐ​ልፍ ፨ 
                                
                            ​ዘአ​ጽሐ​ፋ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e82027PRS12983GabraMa">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​አባ፡</fo:inline> ​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                                ​ዘወ​ለድ​ዎ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e82034PRS12985AmdaSe">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​ዲያ​ቆን፡</fo:inline> ​አም​ደ፡ ​ጽዮን ፨</fo:inline> ​የመ​ምሕ​ር፡ ​ተጠ​ምቀ፡ ​መድ​ኅን፡ ​ልጅ ፨ 
                            ​ዘጸ​ሐፋ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e82044PRS12986GabraKr">​ገብ​ረ፡  ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡</fo:inline>
                            ​ዘሰ​አላ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e82049PRS12987HabtaGa">​ሐብ​ተ፡  ​ገብ​ርኤ​ል፡</fo:inline>
                            ​ዘአ​ስላ፡ ​ወዘ​አጽ​ሐፈ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e82054PRS12983GabraMa">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​አባ፡</fo:inline> ​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                            ​ወዘ​ፃራ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e82062PRS12988WaldaSe">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​አባ፡</fo:inline> ​ወል​ደ፡  ​ሥላ​ሴ፡</fo:inline> ​ጥቡ​ዕ፡ ​መና​ኒ።
                            ​ወዘ​ምራ​ን፡ <fo:inline id="d1e82069LOC1310Aksum">​አኩ​ስም፡</fo:inline> ​ማኅ​ሌተ፡ ​ኢታ​ኅጕ​ሉ፡ ​በዓ​መታ፡</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Additional notes</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 3r: Unidentified text written in Gǝʿǝz and Amharic. The end of the note is barely legible due to a water stain.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                           <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus"/>
                                        ​ዕፁ​በ፡ ​ግብ​ረ፡ ​ወመ​ድም​መ፡ ​ኢር​ኢኩ፡ ​ወኢ​ሰማ​ዕኩ፡ ​ከዳ​ዊት፡ ​ከሰ​ሎሞ​ን፡ ​ከዛ​ቲ፡ ​ዘመ​ን፡ ​ንጉ​ሥ፡ ​ለስ​ደት፡ ​ንጉ​ሥ፡ ​መሸ​ኃዳ​ር፡ ​ኢር​ኢኩ፡ ​ወኢ​ሰማ​ዕኩ፡
                                        ​ገዳ​ማተ፡ ​ትግ​ሬ፡ ​ወኢ​ትዮ​ጵያ፡ ​ብክ​ያ፡ ​ወላ​ህዋ፡ ​እም​ሥራ​ቅ፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ምዕ​ራብ፡ ​መን​ግሥ​ት፡ ​እና​ጥፋ፡ ​አሉ፡ ​መሳ ፍ ​ንት፡
                                        ​ወመ​ኳን​ንት፡ ​ዕፁ​በ፡ ​ግብ​ረ፡ ​ወምድ  (3rb)  ​ምመ፡ ​ኢር​ኢኩ፡ ​ወኢ​ሰማ​ዕኩ፡ ​ንጉ​ሥ፡ ​ለስ​ደት፡ ​ንጉ​ሥ፡ ​መሸ​ኃዳ​ር፡ ​ኢር​ኢኩ፡ ​ወኢ​ሰማ​ዕኩ፡
                                        ​ገዳ​ማተ፡ ​ትግ​ሬ፡ ​ወኢ​ትዮ​ጵያ፡ ​ብክ​ያ፡ ​ወላ​ህዋ፡
                                    </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 78va: Unidentified text, possibly a divinatory note, crudely written in Gǝʿǝz and Amharic.
                                        The first two lines are rubricated.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                           <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus"/>
                                        ​ሐሳበ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                           ​ፍካ​ሬሁ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                            ​ለዳ​ዊት<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ስምአ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                            ​ሞተ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                        ​ምሕ​ረት<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ወን​ጌላዊ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ወር​ህን<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                        ​በመ​ቶታ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​፶ግ​ደፍ፡ ​ደግ​ሞሞ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                        ​ሐባ​ርን<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                        ​ሰምን<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​፻፶ ​ግደ​ፍ፡ ​የወ​ጸው​ን፡ ​የዳ​ዊቱን
                                    </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 78vb–80rb: ‘Miracle of Jesus Christ’ (​ተአ​ምረ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡), CAe 5992..
                                        The text, hastily written, mentions <fo:inline id="d1e83835PRS12983GabraMa">Gabra Māryām</fo:inline>.
                                    </fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        Incipit: :
                                        ​ተአ​ምረ፡ ​ዘገ<fo:inline>[ብ]</fo:inline>​ረ፡  ​እግ​ዚእ​ነ፡ ​ወአ​ምላ​ክነ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡
                                            ​ክር​ስቶ<fo:inline>[ስ]</fo:inline>
                                        ​በኃ​ይለ፡ ​ሞቱ፡ <fo:inline>ማኀየዊ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ይም​ሐሮ፡ ለ ​ገብ​ሩ፡ ​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡ ​ወሀ​ሎ፡ ፩ ​ድው​ይ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡
                                            ​ይግ ዕ ​ር፡
                                        ​ወየ​አው​ዩ፡ ፲ ፪  ​ዓመ​ተ፡ ​ወዘ​ረከ​ቦ፡ ​በብ​ዝኃ፡ ​ኃጢ​አቱ፡ ​ወተ​ፈት​ነ፡ ​በእ​ሳት፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ወር​ቅ፡ ​ወብ​ሩር፡ ​መዓ​ልተ፡ ​ወሌ​ሊተ፡  ... 
                                    </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 80va–80vb: Salām-hymn to Dabra Libānos, incomplete, CAe 5921..
                                        Part of the text is hardly readable due to faded ink. Spaces for rubrication have been left unfilled.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        Incipit:  :
                                            ​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ለኪ፡ ​ደብ​ረ፡ ​ሊባ​ኖስ፡ ​ግነ​ት፡ ​ፄና፡ ​መዓ​ዛኪ፡ ​ዕፍ​ረት፡ ​ዘአ​ዕረ​ፈ፡ ​ብኪ፡ ​ተክ​ለ፡ <fo:inline>ሃማኖተ፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                                        ... 
                                    </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Corrections over erasure on fols 12ra, 39rb, 44rb.
                                        Erasures marked with thin black lines are e.g. on 73vb, 74va.
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Aids for identifying weekday readings are written in the upper margin within a frame decorated in black and red:
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘሠ​ሉስ።</fo:inline> (fol. 26ra), <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘረ​ቡዕ።</fo:inline> (fol. 35ra),
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘሐ​ሙስ።</fo:inline> (fol. 45rb), <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘዓ​ርብ።</fo:inline> (fol. 54ra),
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘቀ​ዳሚ​ት።</fo:inline> (fol. 60va), <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘእ​ሑድ።</fo:inline> (fol. 66vb).
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Writings in pencil are drawn up on the recto side of the protective bifolio glued to the front cover.
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">81 folios. 10 full page paintings. 2 sketches. size 7" x 5"</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>A white sticker is glued to the inner side of the front board. The name of <fo:inline id="d1e83947PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> is printed on it
                                        (‘<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቤን​ት፡ ​ዩው​ል፡ ​የን​ሰን።</fo:inline>’) and the signatures ‘MS. Aeth. e. 38’ and ‘MS. Aethiop. J-J. 41’ are written in
                                        pencil. Below is glued an additional sticker with the signature ‘Ms 41’ on it.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                                The book is bound in wooden boards. An older blind-tooled leather, perhaps contemporary with the majority of the manuscript's content,
                                covers them entirely and a new leather <fo:inline id="d1e83968">quarter cover</fo:inline> has been added on top.
                              
                                The boards are flush with the bookblock and have internal shallow bevels. The inner sides of the boards could not be examined
                                because a parchment bifolio has been glued to them.
                              
                                The earlier blind-tooled cover is preserved, despite deteriorated, under the present one. The decoration is partially
                                legible on the edges, where it shows a pattern of double circles.
                                The present reddish-brown leather is blind-tooled as well but covers only the spine and partially the boards.
                                On its surface bands of two <fo:inline id="d1e83977">single straight lines</fo:inline> intersect
                                forming a column of juxtaposed panels. Within each panel, the lines cross each other forming a <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">crux decussata</fo:inline> and at the intersections of the lines,
                                <fo:inline id="d1e83983">double circles</fo:inline> are stamped. The back features only straight single lines outlining its perimeter.
                                The edges of the thick leather cover are nailed to the boards and decorated with double circles.
                              
                                Brown <fo:inline id="d1e83989">slit-braid</fo:inline> endbands are present.
                              
                                Chainstitch sewing on four sewing stations (two pairs); periodic fold pattern. Two S-plied threads are used.
                                The sewing starts from the first quire where, for each pair of sewing stations, there is one length of thread.
                                In the rest of the quires the lengths are two. The ends of the thread are knotted in the last quire.
                              The stitches of four endband chains are sewn into the leather of the spine, two being close to the head and two to the tail.
                                A blue <fo:inline id="d1e84005">leaf tab marker</fo:inline> for navigating the text is inserted in the upper corner of
                                fols 54 (incipit page of the reading for Friday), fol. 60 (incipit page of the reading for Saturday),
                                and fol. 65 (incipit page of the reading for Sunday).
                              </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
                                    Pencil foliation in the upper right corner (10–79).
                                    The first nine and last two folios are not foliated; the foliation begins with the number 10
                                    on fols 10. The unfoliated folios are referred to as 1–9 and fols 80–81
                                    in this description.
                                    A protective bifolio has been glued to the front and back cover and has not been considered in the foliation.
                                </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm">
            <fo:footnote>
               <fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">311</fo:inline>
               <fo:footnote-body text-align="justify" text-indent="0">
                  <fo:list-block>
                     <fo:list-item>
                        <fo:list-item-label>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline vertical-align="text-top" font-size="9pt">311</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-label>
                        <fo:list-item-body>
                           <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                                     space-before="0.45cm"
                                     font-size="9pt"
                                     line-height="11pt"
                                     margin-left="0.45cm">
                                            Quire marks are written in the upper inner margin of the first folio of quires 4–8, respectively marked with
                                            Ethiopic numerals as 2–6. All quire marks are written in black and red ink and are surrounded by four nine-dot signs, also executed in red and black ink.
                                        </fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-body>
                     </fo:list-item>
                  </fo:list-block>
               </fo:footnote-body>
            </fo:footnote>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>10 quires. A<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2+1 (Fols 1r–3v)</fo:inline> – I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6+1 (Fols 4r–10v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 11r–20v)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 21r–30v)</fo:inline> – IV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 31r–40v)</fo:inline> – V<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 41r–49v)</fo:inline> – VI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 50r–59v)</fo:inline> – VII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 60r–69v)</fo:inline> – VIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 70r–79v)</fo:inline> – B<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2 (Fols 80r–81v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 11ra–80rb: 2
                                    columns (15–17 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 31r. The characters per line are 6–9.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            180 × 127 mm (fol. 31r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            116 × 96 mm (fol. 31r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 19 mm, bottom: 43 mm, right: 19 mm, left: 11 mm, intercolumn: 9 mm (fol. 31r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible. Both primary and ruling pricks are visible. The upper and bottom lines are written above the ruling. Ruling pattern: 1A-1A-1A1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->1775–1815 (scribe: Gabra Krǝstos) . Fine and regular handwriting, slightly deteriorating towards the end (e.g. fols 76v–78v).
                                    Gabra Krǝstos is indicated as the scribe in the Colophon (10v).
                                <fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: 
                                    Several groups of lines on the incipit page of History of Anne and of the opening sections for each weekday, sometimes alternating with black lines;
                                    holy names and the names of the individuals involved in the production of the book, both in the colophon and in the supplication formulas throughout the
                                    manuscript; the words <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሰላ​ም፡</fo:inline> in the colophon and
                                    <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ለኪ፡</fo:inline> in <fo:inline font-style="italic">Malkǝʾ</fo:inline>-hymns to Anne;
                                    elements of the punctuation, including text dividers, and numerals, including the quire marks.
                                </fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Abbreviations: <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="6mm"
                                             provisional-label-separation="6mm"
                                             start-indent="cm">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>1)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                          <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ለዓ፡ ​ዓ፡ ​አ፡</fo:inline> for <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን፡</fo:inline> (fol. 12ra);
                                    </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>2)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                          <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​አ፡</fo:inline> for <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​አሜ​ን፡</fo:inline> (fol. 60va).
                                    </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Decoration</fo:block>
         <fo:block margin-top="3mm" margin-bottom="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">The manuscript contains a prefatory cycle of full-page miniatures (fols 4v–9r),
                         which include two uncommon representations of <fo:inline id="d1e83438PRS5687Joachim">Joachim</fo:inline> and
                         <fo:inline id="d1e83441PRS1948Anne">Anna</fo:inline>.
                         The images in this volume were first described by Budge, who described them
                         as ‘archaic’ and mistakenly attributed them to the fifteenth century
                         (Budge 1922,  vii). In fact, the miniatures actually belong to the turn of the
                         19th century and are painted in the Šawān style (Chojnacki 1983,  469–524).
                          These images must be more or less contemporary with the production of the manuscript since one of them features its patron,
                           <fo:inline id="d1e83454PRS12983GabraMa">Gabra Māryām</fo:inline>. The style and poses of the figures in the miniatures, as well as the palaeography of their captions,
                           are almost identical to those seen in a set of miniatures found at the end of EMML 2349.
                           The name of the scribe who worked on the EMML manuscript (Getatchew Haile and Macomber 1982,  414)
                           is different from that who authored this example. This suggests that in at least one, if not both examples, the scribe and illuminator
                           were different individuals, thus confirming the information provided in the colophon on fol. 10v that identifies the artist
                           as <fo:inline id="d1e83466PRS12987HabtaGa">Habta Gabrǝʾel</fo:inline>.

                           The manuscript also contains several headpieces. They are inserted in empty lines, which suggests they were planned as additions,
                           during the writing, but they are slightly different from the decorations that appear in EMML 2349,
                           which leads to the question about whether or not they were painted by the artist responsible for the figurative cycle of illuminations.
                     </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Miniatures</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(200) Fol. 4v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e83478PRS5687Joachim">Joachim</fo:inline> and
                              <fo:inline id="d1e83481PRS1948Anne">Anna</fo:inline> praying in an orans
                              pose for a child.
                               <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                     <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ወኢ​ያቂ​ም፡ ​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ጸለ​ዩ፡ <fo:inline>በኃጢ (!)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(201) Fol. 5r: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e83497PRS5687Joachim">Joachim</fo:inline> with a staff and dove and
                              <fo:inline id="d1e83500PRS1948Anne">Anna</fo:inline> carrying Mary on her back.

                               <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሐና፡ ​ወኢ​ያቂ​ም፡ ​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ወለ​ድዋ፡ ​ለማ​ርያ​ም፡ ​በጸሎ<fo:inline>[ቶ]</fo:inline>​ሙ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(202) Fol. 5v: <fo:inline>
                                St. <fo:inline id="d1e83519PRS4585Georgeo">George</fo:inline>
                              on horseback slaying the dragon.
                            </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(203) Fol. 6r: <fo:inline>
                              The Virgin and Child,
                              flanked by the archangels <fo:inline id="d1e83533PRS7049Michael">Michael</fo:inline>
                                and <fo:inline id="d1e83536PRS4377Gabriel">Gabriel</fo:inline>. The manuscript’s patron, <fo:inline id="d1e83539PRS12983GabraMa">Gabra Māryām</fo:inline>,
                              is shown in proskynesis before them.

                               <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ፍቁ​ር፡ ​ወል​ዳ፡</fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e83546PRS7049Michael">​ሚካ ኤ ​ል፡</fo:inline> ወ<fo:inline id="d1e83552PRS4377Gabriel">​ገብ​ርኢል</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘተ​ማኅ​ፀነ፡ ​አባ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e83557PRS12983GabraMa">​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(204) Fol. 6v: <fo:inline>

                              The Crucifixion with <fo:inline id="d1e83569PRS6819Mary">Mary</fo:inline> and <fo:inline id="d1e83572PRS5695John">John</fo:inline>
                              weeping at the sides of the cross.

                              <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ስእ​ለ፡ ​ስቅ​ለት፡</fo:inline>
                              On the cross: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e83579PRS5684JesusCh">​ኢያ​ሱስ፡</fo:inline> ​ናዝ​ራዊ፡ ​ንጉ</fo:inline>
                              On the cross: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e83584PRS5684JesusCh">​ኢያ​ሱስ፡</fo:inline> ​ናዝ​ራዊ፡ ​ንጉ​ሠ፡ ​ኢይ​ሁድ</fo:inline>
                              Above <fo:inline id="d1e83589PRS5695John">John</fo:inline> and the cross: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ብካ​የ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e83594PRS5695John">​ዮሐ​ንስ</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
                              Above <fo:inline id="d1e83597PRS6819Mary">Mary</fo:inline>: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ብካ​የ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e83602PRS6819Mary">​ማር​ያም</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(205) Fol. 7r: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e83613PRS9162TaklaHa">Takla Hāymānot</fo:inline>
                              in prayer and wearing a scapular.
                              <fo:inline id="d1e83616PRS4306GabraMa">Gabra Manfas Qǝddus</fo:inline>,
                              with wings and a severed leg, holds a hand cross and a prayer staff.

                              Above the miniature: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​አቡ​ነ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e83621PRS9162TaklaHa">​ተክ​ለ፡ ​ሃይ​ማኖ​ት፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
                              Below the miniature: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​አቡ​ነ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e83626PRS4306GabraMa">​ገብ​ረ፡ ​መን​ፈስ፡ ​ቅዱስ</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(206) Fol. 7v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e83637PRS3894estifano">ʾƎsṭifānos</fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e83640PRS1008Abakaraz">ʾAbakarazun</fo:inline>
                              are shown holding prayer beads.

                              <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                     <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​ነ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e83646PRS3894estifano">​ኤስ​ጢፋ​ኖስ፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​አቡ​ነ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e83651PRS1008Abakaraz">​አበ​ከረ​ዙን</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(207) Fol. 8r: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e83662PRS6951Mazgaba">Mazgaba Śǝllāse</fo:inline>, presumably
                              the abbot of <fo:inline id="d1e83665INS0005Gund">Gunda Gunde</fo:inline>, is shown holding
                                prayer beads; while
                              <fo:inline id="d1e83668PRS8488Samuel">Sāmuʾel</fo:inline>, fourth abbot
                              of the monastery, holds a fly-whisk
                              and a prayer staff.

                              <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​አቡ​ነ፡ ​መዝ​ገበ፡ ​ስላ​ሤ፡</fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​አቡ​ነ፡ ​ሳሙ​ኤል፡ ፬ <fo:inline>ዘ (!)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(208) Fol. 8v: <fo:inline>
                              A figure identified as <fo:inline id="d1e83689PRS3946ezra">ʿƎzrā</fo:inline>,
                              presumably another abbot of <fo:inline id="d1e83692INS0005Gund">Gunda Gunde</fo:inline>, is shown leaning on a prayer
                                staff; while <fo:inline id="d1e83695PRS1852Amdase">ʿAmda Śǝllāse</fo:inline> holds a fly-whisk
                              and a prayer staff.

                              <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​አቡ​ነ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e83700PRS3946ezra">​እዝ​ራ፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​አቡ​ነ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e83705PRS1852Amdase">​አም​ደ፡ ​ስላ​ሤ፡</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline>ዘ (!)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(209) Fol. 9r: <fo:inline>
                              St. <fo:inline/>
                              on horseback with two spears slaying a demon who holds a shield.
                              <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ቴዎ​ድሮ​ስ፡ ​ምስ​ራቃ​ዊ፡</fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሰብ​ድአ​ት፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Headpieces</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(22) Fol. 11r: <fo:inline>
                              A headband with wings at its sides filled with a chain pattern.
                            </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(23) Fols 12rb, 69rb, 72vb: <fo:inline>
                                 Small bands filled with a variety of uncommon decorations.
                               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(24) Fol. 76v: <fo:inline>
                                    A plain band filled with a single small braid.
                                  </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Drawings</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Other</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Few holes from parchment making are present in fols 47, 59.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is good.
                                    Some folios, especially at the beginning of the manuscript, have been severely damaged by water, in particular in the upper outer corner (fols 1–4).
                                    Stains, perhaps of wax, on 15vb–16ra, , 26va–27rb, and fol. . 80vb is stained with dirt.
                                    81 is mutilated.
                                    Traces of the former leather cover are clearly visible on the outer side of the front and back boards.
                                </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>1775–1815</fo:inline>
                            According to the Colophon, the manuscript was written by <fo:inline id="d1e84028PRS12986GabraKr">Gabra Krǝstos</fo:inline> in the monastery of
                            <fo:inline id="d1e84030LOC2297DabraL">Dabra Libānos</fo:inline>, in <fo:inline id="d1e84032LOC5597Sawa">Šawā</fo:inline>, under the patronage of <fo:inline id="d1e84035PRS12983GabraMa">
                  <fo:inline font-style="italic">ʾAbbā</fo:inline> Gabra Māryām</fo:inline>.
                            It was written at the time of
                            <fo:inline id="d1e84040PRS9978Waldase">
                  <fo:inline font-style="italic">Rās</fo:inline> Walda Śǝllāse</fo:inline> (d. 1815).
                            </fo:block>
            <fo:block>
                            The manuscript was brought to <fo:inline id="d1e84048wd:Q21">England</fo:inline> by a British officer after the 1868 expedition by <fo:inline id="d1e84051PRS7484Napier">Napier</fo:inline>, in all likelihood coming
                            from the <fo:inline id="d1e84054INS0101MadhaneAlam">Madḫāne ʿĀlam</fo:inline> collection.
                            It was then sold to the <fo:inline id="d1e84056INS0525Quaritch">Bernard Quaritch Ltd</fo:inline> and in 1897, after failed negotiations with the <fo:inline id="d1e84058INS00001BL">British Library</fo:inline>,
                            it entered the private collection of <fo:inline id="d1e84061PRS9721Valerie">Lady Meux</fo:inline> as ms. Lady Meux 4. The manuscript was inspected and its textual contents edited
                            and translated by <fo:inline id="d1e84064PRS2929Budge">E.A.W. Budge</fo:inline>,
                            who had been asked to examine it by <fo:inline id="d1e84067PRS9721Valerie">Lady
                                Meux</fo:inline>.
                            After <fo:inline id="d1e84070PRS9721Valerie">Lady Meux</fo:inline>’s death, in 1911, the manuscript was probably sold. The subsequent owners are unknown,
                            but the manuscript was eventually purchased by <fo:inline id="d1e84073PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> through the bookseller
                            <fo:inline id="d1e84075PRS13559Thomas">Alan G. Thomas</fo:inline> at a Fine Oriental Manuscripts and Miniatures auction at Sotheby’s
                            on 16 April 1985 (lot 392), according to the auction catalogue. The circumstances of the last acquisition are also described in Juel-Jensen 1987,  218–220.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                      bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e84089PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Bibliography</fo:block>Budge 1900; Budge 1922; Juel-Jensen 1987; Thomas 1990.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethe38">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethe38</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
