      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethe33"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. e. 33</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Juel-Jensen 42)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex179×153 mm (weight: 923g), 131 fols, 21 quires, eighteenth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e84395LIT4957SebhataF">
               <fo:inline>I) Fol. 1r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘‘ Sǝbḥata fǝqur ’ of St George’ (​ስብ​ሐተ፡ ​ፍቁ​ር፡ ​ዘጊ​ዮር​ጊስ፡), incomplete, CAe 4957.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The beginning is missing. The text continues on fol. 1v but is almost completely illegible due to erasure.
                            </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ርዎ ፨ ​ሃሌ  ​እስ​ፍን​ተ፡ ​መጠ​ነ፡ ​ዘአ​መከ​ርዎ፡ ​ከመ፡ 
                                <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ቅ፡ 
                                <fo:inline>በእሰት፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ፈተ​ንዎ፡
                                አ ሃ ​ዝዎ፡ ​ኣሕ​ረጽ​ዎ፡ ​በደብ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ድራ​ስ፡ ​ዘረ​ውዎ ፨
                                ​ሃሌ  ​በማ​ኅፄ፡ ​ወጉ​ድብ፡
                                ​አእፅ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ቲሁ፡ ​ሰበ​ሩ፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ማሰ​ነት፡ ​ሐመ​ሩ፡ ​መድ​ምመ፡ ​ነገ​ሩ፡ ​ለል​ብየ፡ ​ነዳ፡ ​በፍ​ቅሩ ፨
                                ​ሃሌ  ​በእ​ንተ፡
                                ሥ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline> ​ወደ​ሙ፡ ​ለወ​ልደ፡  ፩  ​መም​ለኬ፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ<fo:inline>[​ስ፡]</fo:inline> ​ነአ፡ ​ለቡ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>።  ​ሃሌ 
                                ​ጽድ​ቀ፡ ​ትን​ሣኤ፡  ​ጊዮ​ርጊ<fo:inline>[​ስ፡]</fo:inline> ​ዘአ​ፈድ​ፈደ፡ <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ሔ፡ ​ስነ፡ ​ገድ​ሉ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ኵለ​ሄ፡ ​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ይም​ጻእ፡
                                <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ኅራኄ ፨
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ሃሌ፡ ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡  <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ንተ፡ ​ኮከ​በ፡ ​ልዳ፡ ​ፍቅ​ርከ፡ ​ለል​ብየ፡ ​ዘአ​ንደ​ዳ፡ ​ለሰ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ትየ፡ ​ኢይ​ትዓ​ወዳ፡
                                ​ጸሐ​ፈ፡ ​ወት​ረ፡ ​በሰ​ሌዳ ፨ ​ሃሌ፡ <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline> ​አን​ተ፡ 
                                ​ፍቁ​ርየ፡ ​ሰማ​ዕተ፡ ​አብ፡ ​አቡ​የ፡ ​በጺ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline> ​ኀቤ​የ፡
                                ​አን​ሐሲ፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​ጌጋየ ፨ ​ሃሌ፡  ​እም​ክቡ​ር፡ 
                                <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ቡነ፡  ​ተክ​ለ፡ ​ሃይ​ማኖ​ት፡  ​ማኅ​ቶት፡
                                ​ዘኢ​ትዮ​ጵያ፡ ​ሰዳ​ዴ፡   (fol. 1v) 
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e84507LIT2000Mazmur">
               <fo:inline>II) Fols 2r–130v: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Psalms of David, incomplete, CAe 2000.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">
                                Text corresponding to Pss. 1 and 2 (beginning) is missing. The end
                                of Ps. 151 is missing.
                            </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                 ​ወከ​መ፡ ​ንዋ​የ፡ ​ለብ​ሐ፡ ​ትቀ​ጠቅጦ<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>
                                 ​ወይ​እዜ​ኒ፡ ​ነገ​ሥት፡ ​ለብዉ ፨
                                 ​ወተ​ገሠ​ጹ፡ ​ኵል​ክሙ፡ ​እለ፡ ት<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>፡ ​ለም​ድር ፨
                                 ​ተቀ​ነዩ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​በፍር<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>ት ፨
                                 ​ወተ​ሐሰ​ዩ፡ ​ሎቱ፡ ​በረ​አድ ፨
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                 ​ወቀ​ብአ​ኒ፡ ​ቅብ​አ፡ ​ቅዱሰ ፨
                                 ​አኀ​ውየ​ሰ፡ ​ሠና​ያን፡ ​ወሊ​ሂቃን ፨
                                 ​ወኢ​ሠም​ረ፡ ​ቦሙ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔር ፨
                                 ​ወወ​ጻእ​ኩ፡ ​ለተ​እኅ​ዞቱ፡ ​ለሕ​ዝብ፡ ​ነኪ​ር፡
                                  ​ወረ​ገመ​ኒ፡ ​በአ​ማል​ክቲ​ሁ፡
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Additional notes</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 18r: ‘Protective prayer against the pain’ (​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ሕማ​መ፡ ​ውጋ​ት፡), incomplete, CAe 4625.. The text is crudely written in a pale black ink and is incomplete.
                                        Many words are not fully decipherable. </fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        Incipit: :
                                        <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​ዓት፡ ​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ለገ​ቦከ፡ ​ኵና​ተ፡ ​ለን​ጊኖ​ስ፡ ​ዘወ​ግአ፡ ​እም​አዘ​ቅ፡
                                     ... 
                                    </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Scribal corrections are quite rare: one line is added interlineally on fols 11v, 96r, other small interlinear additions are found, e.g. on
                                        19v, 21v, 34v. Sometimes one sentence or line is added next to the original text of the Psalms, e.g. on 31v, 42v, 62v.
                                        The line is occasionally taken up, e.g. on 22r, 114r.
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Psalms are numbered from Ps 10 onwards.
                                        A word, effaced at a later stage, was written in correspondence of the midpoint of the Psalms of David,
                                        on fol. 70r.
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 19r, 46v, 47r: Scribbles in black ink, partially erased, and pen trials in pencil.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>A white sticker is glued to the inner side of the front board. The name of <fo:inline id="d1e85193PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> is printed on it
                                        (‘<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቤን​ት፡ ​ዩው​ል፡ ​የን​ሰን።</fo:inline>’) and the signature ‘MS. Aeth. e. 33’ is written in pencil.
                                        An additional sticker, with the signature ‘Ms 42’ on it, is glued below it.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                                  The manuscript is bound in wooden boards.
                                
                                  The boards are cut to the same size as the bookblock and are externally bevelled. The grain runs vertically.
                                  Marks left by the previous leather cover turn-ins are still visible on the inner sides of the boards.
                                
                                  The original chainstitch sewing on four sewing stations is for the most part broken but it is preserved in the centre-fold of some quires (e.g. fol. q12),
                                  where, between each pair of sewing stations, there are two lengths of Z-plied thread.
                                  Most folios are now held together by means of overcasting.
                                The manuscript was originally protected in a leather satchel, according to the auction catalogue.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
                                    Pencil foliation in the upper right corner (1–130). Due to an omission in the numbering of one folio before fols 28, ,
                                    the two preceding folios have been foliated as 27a and fol. 27b.
                                </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block white-space-collapse="true">The quire structure is hardly discernible due to the misplacement of some folios.</fo:block>
         <fo:block>21 quires. A<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">0+1 (Fols 1r–1v)</fo:inline> – I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 2r–9v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 10r–17v)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">1 (Fols 18r–18v)</fo:inline> – IV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2 (Fols 19r–20v)</fo:inline> – V<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 21r–27bv)</fo:inline> – VI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 28r–36v)</fo:inline> – VII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">1 (Fols 37r–37v)</fo:inline> – VIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">9 (Fols 38r–48v)</fo:inline> – IX<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 49r–58v)</fo:inline> – X<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">1 (Fols 59r–59v)</fo:inline> – XI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 60r–67v)</fo:inline> – XII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">9+1 (Fols 68r–77v)</fo:inline> – XIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 78r–87v)</fo:inline> – XII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6 (Fols 88r–93v)</fo:inline> – XV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 94r–103v)</fo:inline> – XVI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6+2 (Fols 104r–111v)</fo:inline> – XVII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">1 (Fols 112r–112v)</fo:inline> – XVIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 113r–122v)</fo:inline> – XIX<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">1 (Fols 123r–123v)</fo:inline> – XX<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 124r–131v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 2r–130v: 1
                                    column (18–19 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 60r. The characters per line are 9–23.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            170 × 149 mm (fol. 60r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            112 × 117 mm (fol. 60r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 14 mm, bottom: 33 mm, right: 18 mm, left: 14 mm (fol. 60r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 1r: 1
                                    column (23 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 1r. The characters per line are 22.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            170 × 149 mm (fol. 60r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            127 × 105 mm (fol. 1r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 15 mm, bottom: 16 mm, right: 23 mm (fol. 1r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 1v: 2
                                    columns (23 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 1v. The characters per line are approximately 7–8. The exact number is difficult to ascertain due to faded or erased ink.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            170 × 149 mm (fol. 60r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            128 × 112 mm (fol. 1v)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 15 mm, bottom: 16 mm, left: 25 mm, intercolumn: 11 mm (fol. 1v).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible. Both primary and ruling pricks are visible. The upper and bottom lines are written above the ruling.
                                     Ruling and pricking are visible. Both primary and ruling pricks are visible. The upper and bottom lines are written above the ruling.
                                        The text has been written on one single column although the folio was ruled to accommodate two columns.
                                     Ruling and pricking are visible. Both primary and ruling pricks are visible. The upper and bottom lines are written above the ruling.
                                     Ruling pattern: 1A-1A/0-0/0-0/C.  Ruling pattern: 1A-1A-1A1A/0-0/0-0/C.  Ruling pattern: 1A-1A-1A1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fol. 1r. Eighteenth century.. 
                                    Decent handwriting.
                                <fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: 
                                    The name of <fo:inline id="d1e84983PRS4585Georgeo">St George of Lydda</fo:inline>; the word <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሃሌ፡</fo:inline>; elements of the punctuation signs and numerals.
                                </fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Abbreviations: <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="6mm"
                                             provisional-label-separation="6mm"
                                             start-indent="cm">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>1)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                          <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሃሌ፡</fo:inline>, for
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሃሌ፡ ​ሉያ፡</fo:inline> (fol. 1r).
                                    </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 2:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 2r–130v. Eighteenth century.. 
                                    Small and occasionally irregular handwriting.
                                <fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: 
                                    Numbers and titles of the psalms; holy names (in particular that of <fo:inline id="d1e85021PRS6819Mary">St Mary</fo:inline>);
                                    names, numbers, and traditional interpretation of the Hebrew letters in Ps 118;
                                    elements of the punctuation signs and numerals.
                                </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Decoration</fo:block>
         <fo:block margin-top="3mm" margin-bottom="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">The illuminations belong to a separate and earlier production unit and are 
                                stylistically identical to those found in MS
                                    Munich, Museum Fünf Kontinente, 
                                MfVK 86-307646 to the point that they may even have once belonged to the same manuscript.
                                The painter who created these images was likely responsible for the decoration of several 
                                other manuscripts as discussed in 
                                <inline xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Format">Karlsson et al. 2023</inline>.
                            </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Miniatures</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(210) Fol. 18v: <fo:inline>Saint <fo:inline id="d1e85043PRS6819Mary">Mary</fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                     <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​እሙ ፡
                                        ​ለእ​ግዚ እ ​ነ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(211) Fol. 48r: <fo:inline>Unknown Apostle (possibly Andrew) and
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e85061PRS5662James">James</fo:inline>, son of Zebedee
                                    <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                     <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​ርያ​ስ፡</fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ያዕ​ቆብ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ዘብ ድ ​ዮስ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(212) Fol. 48v: <fo:inline>
                                    Two unknown Apostles, the one to the left is possibly Nathanael
                                    <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ናኤ​ል፡</fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">ማ<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(213) Fol. 104r: <fo:inline>The Apostles <fo:inline id="d1e85096PRS2481Bartholo">Bartholomew</fo:inline> and <fo:inline id="d1e85099PRS5781JudasTh">Thaddeus</fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">በ ​ርተ ​ሎሜ ​ዎስ፡</fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ታዴ ዎ ​ስ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(214) Fol. 104v: <fo:inline>The Apostles <fo:inline id="d1e85122PRS5665James">James</fo:inline>, son of Alphaeus, and <fo:inline id="d1e85125PRS9496Thomas">Thomas</fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ያዕ​ቆብ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​እል​ፍዮስ</fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቶማ ስ ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Headpieces</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Drawings</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Other</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>A hole from parchment making is found on fols 40. Tears have been repaired on 36, 87, 89.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is deficient.
                                    The sewing is badly damaged and has become loose in many places. It was repaired after the misplacement of some folios, which led to severe
                                    perturbations in the textual order (e.g. the original position of fols 19–20 was after 13, ; 74 is misplaced).
                                    Some folios are most probably missing. Since the repair was carried out by stabbing the folios along the inner margin, the complete opening of the quires is prevented.
                                    Losses and tears are present; the latter have been roughly repaired on some occasions by sewing, e.g. on fols 22, 36, 87, 89.
                                    The parchment has been severely damaged by humidity. Most folios are stained with water, especially in the upper part, e.g. 10rv, 17rv, 29rv.
                                    The text is barely legible in some places due to faded ink, e.g. on 10v, 30v, 74r. The red ink is mostly faded out.
                                    Remains of glue and leather are visible on the inner side of both boards, indicating the former presence of a leather cover.
                                    On the inner side of the lower board, a tunnel (possibly created by an insect) opens from the upper edge and crosses the board vertically.
                                    The end of the tunnel inside the board has been closed with a dark substance.
                                </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>eighteenth century</fo:inline>
                            The manuscript can be dated palaeographically to the eighteenth century.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>It was bought by <fo:inline id="d1e85239PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> through the bookseller
                        <fo:inline id="d1e85241PRS13559Thomas">Alan G. Thomas</fo:inline>  at auction at Sotheby’s on 26 November 1985
                        (‘Sotheby’s Western Manuscripts and Miniatures’, lot 172),
                        according to a sale receipt.
                        The circumstances of the acquisition are also described in Juel-Jensen 1987,  220–224.</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                        bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e85254PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Bibliography</fo:block>Juel-Jensen 1987; Karlsson et al. 2023.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethe33">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethe33</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
   <fo:page-sequence initial-page-number="auto-odd" master-reference="Aethiopica-master">
      <fo:static-content flow-name="rest-region-before-odd">
         <fo:block-container height="100%" display-align="center">
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-width="30%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-width="40%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-width="30%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block text-align="right"/>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block text-align="center" font-size="9pt" font-family="Ludolfus">Bodleian Aeth. f. 33</fo:block>
