      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethd23"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. d. 23</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Arch. O. d. 45, Juel-Jensen 44)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm">Gadla Zamikāʾel ʾAragāwi, Gadla Gabra Krǝstos</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex253×229 mm (weight: 1409g), 70 fols (2 p. blank), eighteenth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 5ra–49rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e87611"
                                font-family="Ludolfus"
                                letter-spacing="0.5pt"
                                font-size="0.9em">Hagiographic dossier of Zamikāʾel ʾAragāwi</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e87620LIT1526GadlaZ">
               <fo:inline>I-1) Fols 5ra–44vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Vita of Zamikāʾel ʾAragāwi’ (​ገድ​ለ፡ ​ዘሚ​ካኤ​ል፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ፡), CAe 1526.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​በስ​መ፡ ​አግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​አብ፡ ​ጽኑ​ዕ፡ ​ዘመ​ነ፡ ​መን​ግሥ​ቱ፡ 
                                    ​ዘኢ<fo:inline>...</fo:inline>​ትዌ​ዳዕ፡ ​መል​ዕል​ተ፡ ​ነፋ​ሳት፡ ​ደባ​ትረ፡ ​ማይ፡
                                ​ዘያ​ረግ​ዕ፡ ​በከ​ርሠ፡  ​ደመ​ና፡ ​ማየ፡ ​ባሕ​ር፡ ​ዘያ​መጽ​እ፡ ​ወያ​ዓር​ጎ፡ ​በእ​ደ፡ ​መላ​እክ​ት፡ ​እን​ዘ፡  
                                ​ያጔ​ጕዕ፡ ​በኃ​ይለ፡ ​መላ​እክ​ት፡ ​ወነ​ጐድ​ጓድ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ያጸ​ንዕ፡ ​ድል​ቅል​ቅ፡ ​ወፀ​ዓዕ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ያወ​ክሕ፡ ​እስ​ከነ፡ ​ይስ​ማዕ፡ 
                                ​ማዕ​ዝነ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​ርብዕ ፤
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ወያ​ግብ​ኦ፡ ​ለዘ​ተሐ​ጕለ፡ ​እም​ኔክ​ሙ፡ ​ወይ​ሚጦ​ሙ፡ ​ለነ​ጋድ​ያን፡ ​ኀቤ​ክሙ፡ ​በዳ​ኅና፡
                                ​ወበ​ሰላም ፤ 
                                ​ወየ​ሀብ​ክሙ፡ ​እግ​ዚእ፡ ​ኑዛ​ዜ፡ ​በኀ​ዘና​ት፡ ​እን​ተ፡ ​ትመ​ጽእ፡ ​ላዕ​ሌክ​ሙ፡ ​በኃ​ይለ፡ ​መስ​ቀሉ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​እነ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡
                                ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​ሎቱ፡ ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ወላ​ዕሌ​ነ፡ ​ይኩ​ን፡ ​ሣህ​ል፡ ​ወም​ሕረ​ት፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ለዓ  (b)  ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡
                                ​አሜን ፨
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e87655LIT6842TentaLe">
               <fo:inline>I-2) Fols 44vb–45vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Commencement of the genealogy of the monks’ (​ጥን​ተ፡ ​ልደ​ቶሙ፡ ​ለመ​ነኮ​ሳት፡), CAe 6842.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ዝው​እቱ፡ ​ጥን​ተ፡ ​ልደ​ቶሙ፡ ለ ​መነ​ኮሳ​ት፡ ​እመ​ንገ​ለ፡ ​ጸጋ፡ ​ወሀ​ብት፡
                                    ​እን​ጦን​ዮስ፡ ​ወለ​ዶ፡ ​ለመ​ቃር​ዮስ ፤ 
                                    ​ወመ​ቃር​ዮስ፡ ​ወለ​ዶ፡ ​ለጳ​ኵሚስ ፤ 
                                    ​ወጳ​ኵሚ​ስ፡ ​ወለ​ዶ፡ ​ለዘ​ሚካ​ኤል፡ ​ዘው​እቱ፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ ፤ 
                                    ​ኣረ​ጋዊ፡ ​ወለ​ዶ፡ ​ለማ​ትያስ ፤ 
                                    ​ወማ​ትያ​ስ፡ ​ወለ​ዶ፡ ​ለዮ​ሴፍ ፤
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ወዓ​ጽፈ፡ ​ወል​ድ፡ ​ወለ​ዶ፡ ​ለገ​ብረ፡ ​ክር​ስቶስ ፤ 
                                    ​ወገ​ብረ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​ወለ​ዶ፡ ​ለዘ​ሥላ​ሴ፡ ​እስ​መ፡ ​መፍ​ቀሬ፡ ​ጾም፡ ​ወጸ​ሎት፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡
                                    ​ዘሞ​ተ፡ ​በማ​እከ​ለ፡ ​ዋል​ድባ፡ ​መኒ​ኖ፡ ​ዓለ​መ፡ ​ወኀ​ዲጎ፡ ​ሢመተ ፤ 
                                    ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ይገ​ብር፡ ​ተአ​ምረ፡ ​ወመ​ንክረ ፤ 
                                    ​ወዘ​ሥላ​ሴ፡ ​ወለ​ዶ፡ ​ዳግ​መ፡ ​በመ​ንግ​ሥተ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​ሰገ​ድ፡ ​ለቴ​ዎድ​ሮስ፡ ​ዘጉ​ና፡
                                    ​ዘው​እቱ፡ ​ዞር፡ ​አምባ ፨ 
                                    ​ጸሎ​ቶሙ፡  (b)   ​ወበ​ረከ​ቶሙ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ፍቁ​ሮሙ፡ 
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e87701PRS14798Zaiyasus">​ዘኢ​የሱ​ስ፡</fo:inline> ​ወፍ​ቅር​ቶሙ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e87705PRS14785EhetaMaryam">​እኅ​ተ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                                        ​ወው​ሉዶ​ሙ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e87708PRS15345WaldaG">​ወል​ደ፡ ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e87711PRS15344WalattaTH">​ወለ​ተ፡ ​ተክ​ለ፡ ​ሃይ​ማኖ​ት፡</fo:inline>
                                    ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜን ፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e87724LIT2998RepCh278">
               <fo:inline>I-3) Fols 46ra–49rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Image of ʾAragāwi’ (​መል​ክአ፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ፡), CAe 2998.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​በስ​መ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​እም​ግብ​ጽ፡  ​ፍና​ዋተ፡
                                    ​ግዕ​ዛን፡ ​ዘመ​ርሖ ፤ 
                                    ​ለእ​ግረ፡  ​እስ​ራኤ​ል፡ ​ሙቁ​ሕ፡ ​እማ​ዕሰ​ረ፡ ​ቅን ​የት፡
                                    ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ይፈ​ትሖ ፨
                                    ​አረ​ጋዊ፡  ​ክቡ​ር፡ ​መም​ህረ፡ ​ሰላ​ም፡
                                    ​ወተ​አምኆ ፤ 
                                    ​ከመ፡ ​ይን​ግር፡ ​ዜና፡ ​ጽድ​ቅከ፡ ​ለል​ሳን​የ፡ ​አብሖ ፨ 
                                    ​ወለ​ሕሊ​ናየ፡ ​ካዕ​በ፡ ​እም​ሀኬ​ት፡ ​አን​ቅሖ ፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ሰ፡  ​ለለ​ንብ​ለከ፡ ​ሰላ​መ፡ ​ሰላ​መ፡ ​ዳኅ​ና፡ ​ሀበነ ፤
                                    ​አረ​ጋዊ፡  ​መም​ህርነ ፨ 
                                    ​ወህ​የን​የ፡ ​መል​አክ፡ ​ካዕ​በ፡ ​ዘየ​ዓቅ​በነ ፨ 
                                    ​ጸሎ​ትከ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ሌነ ፨
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e87791LIT4750GadlaGK">
               <fo:inline>II) Fols 50ra–67vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Vita of Gabra Krǝstos’ (​ገድ​ለ፡ ​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡), CAe 4750.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ 
                                ​ቅዱ​ስ፡  ፩ ​ኣም​ላክ፡ ​ንጽ​ሕፍ፡
                                 ​በረ​ድኤ​ተ፡ ​እግ​ዚእ​ነ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ 
                                ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​ዜና​ሁ፡ ​ለቅ​ዱስ፡ ​ብእ​ሴ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡
                                 ​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ 
                                ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ቴዎ​ዶስ​ዮስ፡ ​ንጉ​ሠ፡ ​ቍስ​ጥን​ጥንያ ፨ 
                                ​ወቴ​ዎዶ​ስዮ​ስ፡ ​ንጉ​ሥ፡ ​መፍ​ቀሬ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡
                                ​ወመ​ፍቀ​ሬ፡ ​እን​ግዳ፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ወይ​ገብ​ር፡ ​ብዙ​ኃ፡ ​ምጽ​ዋተ፡ ​ለነ​ዳያ​ን፡ ​ወለ​ምስ​ኪና​ን፡ ​ለእ​ቤራ​ት፡
                                ​ወለ​እጓ​ለ፡ ​ማውታ ፨
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ወቀ​በር​ዎ፡ ​በሣ​ፁን፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡  (b)   ​ወረ​ደ፡ ​ብር​ሃን፡ ​ኀበ፡ ​መቃ​ብሩ፡
                                ​ዘያ​ሐዩ፡ ​ኵሎ፡ ​ድው​ያነ፡ ​ወሕ​ሙማነ ፨ 
                                ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡ ​ወበ​ረከ​ቱ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ፍቁ​ሩ፡ 
                                <fo:inline id="d1e87829PRS14798Zaiyasus">​ዘኢ​የሱ​ስ፡</fo:inline> ​ወም​ስለ፡ ​ፍቅ​ርቱ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e87833PRS14785EhetaMaryam">​እኅ​ተ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                                ​ወወ​ልዶ​ሙ፡  ​ተክ​ለ፡
                                <fo:inline>...</fo:inline>
                                ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜን ፨
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Additional notes</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 67vb–70vb, Fols 1ra–4rb: Excerpts from <fo:inline>“Antiphonary for Lent” (ጾመ፡ ድጓ፡), CAe 2361</fo:inline>,
                                        containing sets of antiphons for Palm Sunday (fols 67vb–69ra),
                                        Good Friday (fols 69ra–69vb),
                                        Holy Saturday (fols 69vb–69vb), and from the
                                        <fo:inline>“Antiphonary (general record for multiple-type collections)” (ድጓ፡), CAe 3178</fo:inline>, containing sets of antiphons for
                                        Easter Sunday and other Easter-related occasions, including
                                        the feast of Adam (fols 1ra–1vb),
                                        for the feasts of Ascension (fols 2ra–2rb),
                                        Pentecost (fols 2rb–2va),
                                        the Transfiguration (fols 2va),
                                        the Assumption of Mary (fol. 2vb),

                                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">ʾAbbā</fo:inline> ʾAragāwi (fols 2vb–3vb),
                                            Christmas (<fo:inline font-style="italic">Lədat</fo:inline>, fols 3vb–4rb),
                                        and, possibly, the Pact of Mercy (<fo:inline font-style="italic">Kidāna məḥrat</fo:inline>, fol. 4rb).
                                        The text is furnished with musical notation (<fo:inline font-style="italic">mələkkət</fo:inline>).

                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 1ra: Amharic note. It is difficult to understand, although most of the letters are legible. It mentions the names
          of several priests (<fo:inline font-style="italic">qes</fo:inline>), the payment of a sum of money, a date, and
      the names of guarantors.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 19va: Amharic reconciliation record mentioning many names.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">​የብ​ላታ፡ ​ክን​ፋ፡ ​ምድ​ር፡ ​ከኖ​ረኀ፡  ​ምክ​ሩ፡ 
                                    ​የታ​ረቍ​በት፡ ​ዕፃ፡ ​ተል​ቅና​ውን፡ ​መሬ​ት፡ ​እኩ​ል፡ ​መሬ​ት፡ ​ታረ​ቁ፡ ​በከ​ብተ​ዎ፡ ​አለ​ዳ፡
                                    ​አለ​ዕን​ግዳ፡  ​ሲበ​ሉ፡  ​አስ​ታራ​ቂዎ​ች፡ ​፭ቱ፡ ​ሸማ​ግሎ​ች፡
                                    ​ነጮ፡ ​ዕን​ቈ፡ ​ሥላ​ሴ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ዮሐ​ንስ፡ ​በው​ቀቱ፡ ​ጕበ​ና፡ ​ኃይ​ሉ፡ ​ብላ​ታ፡ ​ለት​ጹን፡ ​ብላ​ታ፡
                                    ​ገጹ፡ <fo:inline>ናቼው፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​በረ​ምኃ፡ ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡ ​ግብ​ዝና፡ ​በደ​ብረ፡ ​ሲና፡
                                        ​ገበ​ዝ፡  በ ​ባይ​ጠፋ​ኝ፡ ​በ፬​ቱ፡ ​ዕን​ስሳ፡ ​በእ​ብሩ፡
                                    ​ይግ​ዛው፡ ​ግብ​ዝና፡ ​የአ​ቦና፡ ​የጊ​ዮር​ጊስ፡ ​ገበ​ዝ፡ ​ቄስ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ዕ፳​ኤል፡ ​በዕ​ነዚ​ኅ፡
                                    ​ሁሉ፡ ​ፊት፡ ​ተጻ​ፈ፡ ​በዘ​ሚካ​ኤል፡ ​ጭቅ​ነት፡ ​በወ​ልደ፡ ​አብ፡ ​በአ​ስራ​ት፡ ​ጭቅ​ነት፡
                                         በ ​ማት​ያስ፡ ​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡ ​በሊ​ቀላ​ዎስ፡
                                        ​ጭቅ​ነት፡ በ ን ​ዋይ፡ ​ሐፃ​ኑ፡ ​የለ​ባሲ​ት፡ ​ገን​ታ፡
                                        ​ማሞ፡ ​ገብ​ሩ፡ ​ዋሱ፡ ​ለኖ​ረኀ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                        ​ፈን​ታ፡ ​ወለ​ተ፡ ​ሥላ​ሴ፡ ​ነው፡ ​ጸሐ​ፊው፡ ​ደብ​ተራ፡ ​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡
                                        <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>
                                        ​ብላ​ታ፡  ​ደር​ሳኀ፡  ​ነው፡
                                        <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​ስ፡
                                        ​ዕን​ዶይፋ<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>
                        </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 26r: Amharic note written in a careful hand mentioning that the manuscript was written for
                                        <fo:inline id="d1e89036PRS14785EhetaMaryam">ʾƎḫəta Māryām</fo:inline>, the sister of
                                        King <fo:inline id="d1e89039PRS5617IyasuII">ʾIyāsu II</fo:inline>, during his reign, while she was
                                        engaged in the construction of the church of <fo:inline id="d1e89042INS1023BadawoAragawi">Badāwo ʾAbuna ʾAragāwi</fo:inline>.
                                        <!--AMHARIC TO BE DISCUSSED WITH SOMEONE WHO KNOWS IT BETTER-->
                                    </fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">
                           <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዝን​ቱ፡ ​ደብ​ረ፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ፡ ​ዘተ​ተክ​ለ፡</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline id="d1e89054PRS5617IyasuII">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​ባጼ፡</fo:inline> ​ኢያ​ሱ።</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline id="d1e89059PRS2682BerhanM">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​እቴ​ዬ፡</fo:inline> ​ምን​ትዋ​ብ፡</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline id="d1e89064PRS5617IyasuII">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​አጼ፡</fo:inline> ​ኢያ​ሱን​ና፡</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline id="d1e89069PRS9827Walatta">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​ወይ​ዘሮ፡</fo:inline> ​ወለ​ተ፡ ​፳ኤ​ልን፡</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline id="d1e89074PRS14785EhetaMaryam">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​ወይ​ዘሮ፡</fo:inline> ​እኅ​ተ፡ ​ማር​ያም​ን፡</fo:inline>  ​ይወ​ልዳ​ሉ፡
                                        <fo:inline id="d1e89080PRS9827Walatta">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​ወይ​ዘሮ፡</fo:inline> ​ወለ​ተ፡ ​እስራ ​ኤል ​ና፡</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline id="d1e89088PRS14785EhetaMaryam">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​ወይ​ዘሮ፡</fo:inline> ​እኅ​ተ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline> ​ምድ​ር፡ ​ተከ​ፈሉ፡
                                        <fo:inline id="d1e89093PRS14785EhetaMaryam">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​ወይ​ዘሮ፡</fo:inline> ​እኅ​ተ፡ ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline id="d1e89098INS1023BadawoAragawi">​በዳ​ዎ፡ ​አቡ​ነ፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ​ን፡</fo:inline> ​ተከ​ሉ፡ ​ሲተ​ክሉ​ም፡ <fo:inline id="d1e89101PRS14790Qerellos">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​መም​ሕሬ፡</fo:inline> ​ቄር​ሎስ​ና፡</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline id="d1e89106PRS14791Sefani">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​መም​ሕሬ፡</fo:inline> ​ስፋ​ኒ፡</fo:inline>
                                            ​ይሚ​ሏቸ​ው፡ ​መና​ኮስ​ት፡ ​የበ​ቁ፡ ​መጒ​ና፡ ​የሚ​ሉ፡ ​ገዳ​ም፡ ​ነበ​ሩ፡ ​እኔ​ህን፡
                                    ​አስ​ባር​ከው፡ ​ተከ​ሉት፡ ​ሲተ​ክሉ​ም፡ ​በቀ​ይ፡ ​ቀለ​ም፡ ​በን​ጉሥ፡ ​ማኅ​ተም፡ ​ገድ​ለ፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ​ን፡
                                    ​አስ​ጥፈ​ው፡
                                        <fo:inline id="d1e89112PRS5617IyasuII">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​ባጼ፡</fo:inline> ​ኢያ​ሱ፡</fo:inline>
                                    ​መን​ግሥ​ት፡ ​ገድ​ሉ፡ ​ይጠ​በቀ​ው፡ ​ብለ​ው፡ ​በዎ​ጅ፡ ​በቅ​ዳጅ፡ ​ተተ​ከለ፡
                                    ​ሲተ​ክሉ​ም፡ ፫ ​ቄስ፡ ፪ ​ዲያ​ቆን፡ ፭ ​ን፡
                                    ​ልዑክ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>፰  ​ጫን፡
                                        ​የቀ​ዳሽ፡ ፵<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>፰  ​መን​በሯ፡
                                        ​ስን​ዴ፡ ​ግብ​ሩ፡ ​ይህ፡ ​ነው፡ ​ከጨ​ው፡ ​ግማ​ሺ፡ ​ተኽ​ል፡ ​አጋ​ማሽ፡ ​ሌላ፡ ​የለ​በት​ም፡ ​ካቤ​ድብ፡ ​ዠም​ሮ፡ ​እስ​ከ፡
                                        <fo:inline id="d1e89125PRS6723Maredha">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​ራስ፡</fo:inline> ​መር​ድ፡</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ድረ​ስ፡ ​ገድ​ሉ፡ ​ተበ​ቀው፡
                                        <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline id="d1e89134PRS6723Maredha">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​እራስ</fo:inline>
                              <fo:inline> (!)</fo:inline>​ርድ​ም፡</fo:inline>
                                        ​ገድ​ሉን፡ ​አን​ብበ​ው፡
                                        ​አይ​ተው፡ ​ቤተ​ክር​ስቲ​ያኑ​ን፡ ​ስመ​ው፡ ​ጥን​ት፡ ​ይብ​ቃ፡ ​ብለ​ው፡ ​ገድ​ሉ፡ ​ጥብ​ቅ፡ ​ይሁ​ን፡ ​አሉ፡
                                        ከ<fo:inline id="d1e89142PRS6723Maredha">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​ራስ፡</fo:inline> ​መር​ድ፡</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline id="d1e89147PRS4870GugsaMa">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">እ ራ ​ስ፡</fo:inline> ​ጉግ​ሣ፡</fo:inline>
                                        የ<fo:inline id="d1e89155PRS6723Maredha">​መር​ድ፡</fo:inline> የ<fo:inline id="d1e89158PRS14799HaylaIyasus">​ኃይ​ለ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡</fo:inline>
                                        ​ይብ​ቃ፡ ​ገድ​ሉ፡ ​ይጠ​ብቀ​ው፡ ​አሉ፡ ​ከዚ​ያ፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ዛሬ፡ ​ድረ​ስ፡ ​ገድ​ሉ፡ ​ጠብ​ቆት፡ ​ይኖ​ራል፡
                                        ይ ህ ​ነን፡ ​ገጽ፡ ​ያው​ቃል፡ ​ያቦ፡ ​የጊ​ዮር​ጊስ፡
                                         የ ​ማር​ያም፡ ​ገበ​ዝ፡ ​ያው​ቃል፡ ​ይጠ​ይቁ፡ ​ግብ​ር፡
                                        ​የለ​በት​ም፡ እ ​ግዜ ​ር፡ ​ያስ​የዎ፡ ​አም​ላክ፡ ​ያመ​ልክ​ተዎ፡
                                        ​የኔ፡ ​ጌታ፡ ​ከቤ​ቱ፡
                                    </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>5)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 49va: Note in black ink recording the purchase of the land Kok by the

                                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">fitāwrāri</fo:inline>
                        <fo:inline id="d1e89180PRS14793Mahsantu">Māḫḍantu</fo:inline>
                                            for 30 <fo:inline font-style="italic">waqet</fo:inline>.
                                                The creditor (<fo:inline font-style="italic">bālaʿədā</fo:inline>) was <fo:inline id="d1e89188PRS14792WaldaLeul">Walda Lǝʿul Ḫiruta ʾAb</fo:inline>,
                                                    the seller (<fo:inline font-style="italic">šayāč̣</fo:inline>) was <fo:inline id="d1e89194PRS14795Meherka">Walda Lǝʿul Mǝḥǝrkā</fo:inline>,
                                                        the guarantor (<fo:inline font-style="italic">madən</fo:inline>) was <fo:inline id="d1e89199PRS14796Wasan">Wasan</fo:inline>,
                                        and the purchase took place
                                        during the period of office (<fo:inline font-style="italic">gabazənnat</fo:inline>)

                                        of the priest <fo:inline id="d1e89204PRS14797Ramha">Ramḥa</fo:inline>.
                                    </fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">
                                        ​ፊታ​ውራ​ሪ፡ ​ማኅ​ፀን​ቱ፡ ​የገዙ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>፡
                                        ​ምድ​ር፡ ​ኮክ፡ ​ዋጋ​ው፡ ፴ ​ወቄ​ት፡ ​ባለ​ዕዳ​ው፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ልዑ​ል፡ ​ኂሩ​ተ፡ ​አብ፡
                                        ​ሺያ​ጩ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ልዑ​ል፡ ​ምሕ​ርካ፡ ​መድ​ኑ፡ ​ወሰ​ን፡ ​ካህ​ኑ፡ ​በቄ​ስ፡ ​ረም​ሐ፡ ​ገበ​ዝነ​ት፡
                                    </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>6)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 70ra–70rb: Note in blue pen containing four very succinct miracles of

                                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">ʾAbbā</fo:inline> ʾAragāwi.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">
                                    ​ስለ​አቡ​ነ፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ፡ ​የተ​ደረ​ገው፡ ​ተአ​ምር፡ ​አን​ደኛ፡ ​በአ​ጼ፡ ​ዮሐ​ንስ፡ ​ይህ፡ ​ገድ​ል፡ ​እና፡
                                    ​ይህ፡ ​መስ​ቀል<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ትግ​ሬው፡ ​ወስ​ዶት፡
                                    ​ተመ​ለሰ፡ ​፪ተ​ኛ፡ ​ይኽ​ው፡ ​ገድ​ል፡ ​ዲያ​ቆን፡ ​ወስ​ዶ፡ ​ሸጦ​ት፡ ​ያው፡ ​ዲያ​ቆን፡ ​ሲቀ​ድስ፡
                                    ​ጋኔ​ን፡ ​ጥሎ​ት፡ ​በዚ​ያው፡ ​ሞተ፡ ​፫ተ​ኛ፡ ​በጣ​ሊያ​ን፡ ​ጊዜ፡ ​አማ​ሴን፡ ​ይህ​ኑ፡ ​ገድ​ል፡
                                    ​ወስ​ዶ፡ ​አማ​ሴኑ፡ ​ይክ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ገድ​ል፡ ​እን​ደሳ​ት፡
                                        ​ፈጀ​ን፡ ​ሲል፡ ፫  አ ​ጠገ​ራ፡ ​ብር፡ ​ጭም<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>፡
                                        ​መል​ስታ​ል፡ ​፬ኛ፡ ​ጥር፡ ፳<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>፡ ​ቀን፡ ​፶፯ ​ዓመ፡ ​ም፡
                                    ​ይኽ​ን፡  ()   ​ገድ​ልን፡ <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​አን​ድ፡ ​ትል​ቅ፡ ​መስ​ቀል፡
                                    ​፪ተ​ኛ፡ ​አን​ድ፡ ​ሐር፡ ​ካባ፡ ​አን​ድ፡ ​ከፈ​ይ፡ ​ለም​ድ፡ ​ሌባ፡ ​ወስ​ዶት፡ ​ሀገ​ሩ፡ ​በሙ​ሉ፡
                                    ​ተሰ​ብስ​ቦ፡ ​ለአ​ቡነ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​አረ​ጋዊ፡
                                    ​ተስ​ሎ፡ ​እግ​ዚኦ፡ ​ብሎ፡ ​ጸሎ​ተ፡ ​ማር​ያም<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                    ​ደግ​ሞ፡ ​ሄደ፡ ​የካ​ቲት፡ ፮ ​ቀን፡ ​፶፯​ንመ፡ ​ም፡ ​በአ​ስር፡ ​ቀኑ፡ ​መል​ሶ፡ ​ጥሎ​ታል፡ ​የአ​ቡነ፡
                                    ​አረ​ጋዊ፡ ​ገድ​ል፡ ​እን​ደዚ​ሁ፡ ​ሁል፡ ​ጊዜ፡ ​አያ​ቋር​ጥም፡
                                    </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Scribal corrections (e.g. fols 30vb, 38ra)
                                        and erasures (e.g. fols 24rb, 29ra) are rare.
                                        Occasionally, missing characters are written interlineally (e.g. 30ra, 36va: very
                                        thin and small characters).
                                   </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>The name of the commissioner <fo:inline id="d1e89271PRS14785EhetaMaryam">ʾƎḫəta Māryām</fo:inline>
                                    is mentioned in supplications throughout (e.g. fols 5va, 9ra, 15ra). The name 
                                        <fo:inline id="d1e89276PRS14798Zaiyasus">Zaʾiyasus</fo:inline> and of
                                        their children <fo:inline id="d1e89279PRS15344WalattaTH">Walatta Takla
                                            Hāymānot</fo:inline> and <fo:inline id="d1e89282PRS15345WaldaG">Walda Giyorgis</fo:inline> also appears
                                    in supplications throughout (e.g. fol. 45vb), often added interlineally.
                                   </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block> A white sticker with the name of <fo:inline id="d1e89294PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> printed (‘<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቤን​ት፡ ​ዩው​ል፡ ​የን​ሰን።</fo:inline>’), and the signatures ‘MS.
                                        Aeth. d. 23 = Arch. O’ written in pencil is glued onto
                                        the inner side of the front board. Another sticker
                                        with the signature ‘Ms 44’ is glued below it.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 10v, 15v: Stamps belonging to the <fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline id="d1e89307ins"/>
                        </fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                                  The book is bound in wooden boards covered with reddish-brown blind-tooled leather. The inner sides of both boards are decorated with textile <fo:inline id="d1e89330">inlays</fo:inline>.
                                  The textile has a blue horizontal striped pattern with yellow borders on a red background, decorated with yellow rounded flowers.
                                  The manuscript is furnished with a neutral textile chemise and a leather satchel.
                                
                                  The boards are cut to the same size as the bookblock and present both external and internal shallow bevels.
                                
                                  Full reddish-brown leather cover.
                                  The turn-ins have been trimmed out and at the corners they form butt mitres.
                                  An <fo:inline id="d1e89342">additional leather patch</fo:inline> has been added along the inner margin of the boards to fill the gap between the turn-ins.
                                  The portion of leather covering the board attachment sites has been cut and removed to re-sew the manuscript.
                                  The cover shows a fine blind-tooled decoration, identical on both sides of the cover. The turn-ins and the edges are also decorated.
                                  The decoration consists of seven concentric frames surrounding a central rectangular panel featuring a Latin cross.
                                  Frames composed by the repetition of single tools, enclosed between <fo:inline id="d1e89345">triple straight lines</fo:inline>,
                                  alternate with empty ones. <fo:inline id="d1e89348">Double circles</fo:inline> are stamped at the intersections of the straight lines.
                                  Proceeding from the outer to the inner frame, the repeating decoration motifs are <fo:inline id="d1e89351">criss-crosses</fo:inline>,
                                  <fo:inline id="d1e89354">straight strapwork</fo:inline> elements, <fo:inline id="d1e89358">wavy lines</fo:inline>
                                  with <fo:inline id="d1e89361">double circles</fo:inline> between them, and again <fo:inline id="d1e89364">criss-crosses</fo:inline>.
                                  The cross is formed by <fo:inline id="d1e89367">X-form</fo:inline> motifs between triple straight lines.
                                  At the ends of the arms of the cross there are three <fo:inline id="d1e89370">double circles</fo:inline>.
                                  <fo:inline id="d1e89373">Triple straight lines</fo:inline> outline the shape of the cross, dividing the area around it in four panels.
                                  <fo:inline id="d1e89377">Triple straight lines</fo:inline> decorate also the turn-ins, outlining the their margins.
                                  A <fo:inline id="d1e89380">triple straight line</fo:inline> runs along the edges of the boards and is decorated with <fo:inline id="d1e89383">double circles</fo:inline>.
                                
                                  Chainstitch sewing on four sewing stations (two pairs); periodic fold pattern; two Z-plied threads have been used.
                                  Between each pair of sewing stations there are two lengths of thread. The ends of the thread are knotted in the last quire.
                                
                                  The spine, together with the endbands, has been removed to resew the manuscript.
                                  The small holes close to the head and tail of the quires testify to the former presence of endbands.
                                
                                  The manuscript is provided with a one-piece single-walled satchel.
                                  The satchel is equipped with a main flap extending from the back to the front panel to cover the opening of the book compartment.
                                </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block>9 quires. A<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">4 (Fols 1r–4v)</fo:inline> – I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 5r–12v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 13r–20v)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 21r–30v)</fo:inline> – IV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 31r–38v)</fo:inline> – V<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 39r–46v)</fo:inline> – VI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 47r–54v)</fo:inline> – VII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 55r–62v)</fo:inline> – VIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 83r–70v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 5ra–70vb: 2
                                    columns (18 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 21r.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            246 × 227 mm (fol. 21r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            143 × 166 mm (fol. 21r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 38 mm, bottom: 68 mm, right: 41 mm, left: 21 mm, intercolumn: 17 mm (fol. 21r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 1ra–4rb: 2
                                    columns (20–23 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 2r.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            246 × 227 mm (fol. 21r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            171 × 165 mm (fol. 2r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 15 mm, bottom: 60 mm, right: 38 mm, left: 21 mm, intercolumn: 15 mm (fol. 2r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible. Both primary and ruling pricks are visible. The upper line is written above the ruling. The bottom line is written above the ruling. Ruling and pricking are visible. Both primary and ruling pricks are visible. The text is not written on the ruled lines. Ruling pattern: 1A-1A-1A1A/0-0/0-0/C.  Ruling pattern: 1A-1A-1A1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->1700–1799. Fine and regular handwriting. Characters are regularly spaced.<fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: 
                                    Incipits (one word to one or several lines, consecutive or alternating with black lines in different groupings);
                                    captions of miniatures; holy names; the names of individuals related to the production of
                                    the manuscript; elements of the punctuation signs, text dividers, and numerals.
                                </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Decoration</fo:block>
         <fo:block margin-top="3mm" margin-bottom="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">
                                Only the first half of this manuscript, the one that contains the
                                <fo:inline>“Vita of Zamikāʾel ʾAragāwi” (ገድለ፡ ዘሚካኤል፡ አረጋዊ፡), CAe 1526</fo:inline>, 
                                has been illustrated. The second half is unillustrated. The style of
                                the miniatures is similar to
                                works produced between the second half of the seventeenth and early eighteenth centuries, 
                                which is probably when they were executed. Because of the style of the illuminations, the 
                                former owner of this manuscript, <fo:inline id="d1e88106PRS5782JuelJen">Juel-Jensen</fo:inline>, 
                                believed, with reason, that the note added at a 
                                later date to the manuscripts on fol. 26r – which records its donation by two 
                                monks <fo:inline id="d1e88111PRS14790Qerellos">Qerǝllos</fo:inline> and 
                                <fo:inline id="d1e88113PRS14791Sefani">Sǝfāni</fo:inline> to the newly dedicated <fo:inline id="d1e88116INS1023BadawoAragawi">monastery of
                                Zamikāʾel ʾAragāwi in 
                                Badāwo</fo:inline> – references both the reigns of 
                                <fo:inline id="d1e88119PRS5616IyasuI">ʾIyāsu I</fo:inline> and <fo:inline id="d1e88122PRS5617IyasuII">ʾIyāsu II</fo:inline>, 
                                that is that the manuscript was 
                                produced during the former’s reign but donated to <fo:inline id="d1e88125INS1023BadawoAragawi">Zamikāʾel ʾAragāwi in Badāwo</fo:inline> during the 
                                latter’s reign. <!--< -\- some of this info may be transferred to section about date? -\- >-->
                                
                                The palaeography of the rubricated captions that accompany all the illustrations is similar to 
                                that of the main text, indicating that these were executed closely in time and by the same 
                                individual. However, it is worth noting that the illuminator did not always leave enough space 
                                for the rubricated captions to be added – as is most obvious by looking at  the irregular line of 
                                writing above the heads of the Nine Saints on fol. 12r. This, in turn, suggests 
                                that scribe and illuminator were not the same person. We may thus imagine that the 
                                manuscript was first penned by the scribe, who left a series of blank spaces for the miniatures; 
                                after these blank areas were filled by the illuminator, the manuscript was returned to the scribe 
                                who added the captions within what space was left available to him. The fact that several spaces 
                                were left blank by the illuminator, e.g. fol. 25r and fol. 26r, 
                                suggests both a lack of coordination between illuminator and the scribe and that in all 
                                likelihood the latter originally planned for even more miniatures to be included in the 
                                volume that were left out by the artist for unknown reasons. 
                                
                                With regard to these blank spaces, it is likely that the scribe was following an existing exemplar.
                                More specifically, Juel-Jensen believed that MS Aeth. d. 23 was
                                copied at <fo:inline id="d1e88137INS0105DD">Dabra Dāmmo</fo:inline>.  
                                Having visited this monastery on November 13, 1993, he was shown a now-lost eighteenth-century
                                copy of the Gadla Zamikāʾel ʾAragāwi
                                in their collection that included the same 
                                illustrations in the same places as those in his manuscript, with the exception of the military
                                expeditions of King <fo:inline id="d1e88145PRS5841Kaleb">Kāleb</fo:inline> (fols 28r–28v), as well as additional miniatures. In all likelihood both 
                                the copy he was shown and the copy in the Bodleian Libraries were inspired by an earlier 
                                and now lost copy of Gadla Zamikāʾel ʾAragāwi that was either produced or commissioned 
                                by the abbot of <fo:inline id="d1e88154INS0105DD">Dabra Dāmmo</fo:inline>
                                to commemorate his illustrious predecessor. Some of the 
                                miniatures, such as the one on fol. 13r sit awkwardly within the available 
                                blank space on the page. This may be an indication of the fact that the illuminator departed 
                                from the model the scribe was following.
                                
                                Because of the loss of this model, and due to the absence of
                                in-depth studies of the iconography
                                of <fo:inline id="d1e88159PRS10581Zamika">Zamikāʾel ʾAragāwi</fo:inline> or,
                                more generally, of the Nine Saints in Ethiopia 
                                (but see <inline xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Format">Zorzan 2023</inline>), it is not possible to offer a detailed discussion 
                                about this manuscript’s relationship to existing illuminated manuscripts devoted to these 
                                important figures in Ethiopian Christianity or to <fo:inline id="d1e88166PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline> 
                                in particular. Having said that, it is
                                evident that the manuscript draws, at least in part, on more widespread iconographic traditions 
                                relating to the Nine Saints. For example, the images that exemplify some of the miracles 
                                performed by the Nine Saints after their departure from ʾAksum on
                                fols 14v–15r in this 
                                manuscript adopt the same iconographic variants used to represent these miracles in 
                                MS London, British Library Or. 590
                                fols 64r–65r, , though the latter manuscript features additional scenes, 
                                including the one that shows ʾAragāwi using a snake to climb to the top of 
                                Dabra Dāmmo that appears in an expanded version on fol. 22r in MS Aeth. d. 23. 
                                This manuscript is also rich in interesting details inspired by local costume and practice, 
                                such as the book satchel and <fo:inline font-style="italic">tābot</fo:inline> seemingly carried in a basket on
                                fol. 12r, the scapular worn 
                                by <fo:inline id="d1e88184PRS1263Abraha">ʾAbrǝhā</fo:inline> on fols 14v, , the bed on fols 17v, , the prayer-stick on
                                fol. 18r, the veiled <fo:inline font-style="italic">manbara tābot</fo:inline> on 
                                fol. 23v, and the communion before the altar on fol. . The presence of
                                such figures such as 
                                <fo:inline id="d1e88201PRS7696Pachomiu">Pachomius</fo:inline>, <fo:inline id="d1e88204PRS9162TaklaHa">Takla Hāymānot</fo:inline>, 
                                and <fo:inline id="d1e88207PRS10245Yared">Yāred</fo:inline> (who is rarely represented in manuscripts from this 
                                period), is equally noteworthy and aligns with the strategy of the
                                <fo:inline font-style="italic">gadl</fo:inline> to enhance the standing 
                                of ʾAragāwi as a saint and his monastery by associating them to a series of important figures  
                                for Ethiopian Christianity.
                            </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Miniatures</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(215) Fol. 6v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88219PRS7696Pachomiu">Pachomius</fo:inline> ordains
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88222PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline> as a monk.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​አል​በሰ፡ ​አል​ባሰ፡ ​ምን​ኵስ​ና፡ <fo:inline id="d1e88228PRS7696Pachomiu">​አባ፡ 
                                    ​ጳኵ​ሚስ፡</fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88231PRS10581Zamika">​ለአ​ባ፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(216) Fol. 8r: <fo:inline>Seven of the Nine Saints join ʾAragāwi and are ordained as
                                    monks by <fo:inline id="d1e88241PRS7696Pachomiu">Pachomius</fo:inline>.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88246PRS6318Liqanos">​አባ፡ ​ሊቃ​ኖስ፡ </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88249PRS10322Yemata">​አባ፡ ​ይም​አታ፡ </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88252PRS8711sehmas">​አባ፡ ​ጽሕ​ማ፡ </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88255PRS4855Guba">​አባ፡ ​ጕባ፡ </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88258PRS1467Afse">​አባ ​አፍ​ጺ፡ </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88261PRS7720Pantalew">​አባ፡ ​ጰን​ጠሌ​ዎን፡ </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88265PRS1653Alef">​አባ፡ ​አሌ​ፍ፡ </fo:inline>
                                    ​ወአ​ልበ​ሶሙ፡ ​አል​ባሰ፡ ​ምን​ኵስ​ና፡ <fo:inline id="d1e88268PRS7696Pachomiu">​አባ፡
                                        ​ጳኵ​ሚስ።</fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88271PRS10581Zamika">​አባ፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(217) Fol. 10r: <fo:inline>Three scenes: <fo:inline id="d1e88281PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline>, identified by the caption <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​አባ፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ።</fo:inline>, meets his mother; 
                                    Theodore ordains her as a nun; and introduces her to a monastic
                                    group of nuns.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​መጽ​አት፡ ​እሙ፡ ​እድ​ና፡ ​ኀበ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e88290PRS10581Zamika">​አባ፡ 
                                    ​አረ​ጋዊ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ለብ​ሰት፡ ​አል​ባሰ፡ ​ምን​ኵስ​ና፡ ​እም​ኀበ፡ ​ቴዎ​ድሮ​ስ፡ ​ወነ​በረ​ት፡ ​እም​ኀበ፡
                                    ​መነ​ኮሳ​ይያ​ት።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(218) Fol. 11v: <fo:inline>The <fo:inline id="d1e88303PRS7049Michael">Archangel Michael</fo:inline> transports 
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88306PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline>
                                    and his disciples  to <fo:inline id="d1e88309LOC1310Aksum">ʾAksum</fo:inline> where he meets the king and the
                                    metropolitan. Captions: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ንጉ​ሥ፡</fo:inline>, 
                                    <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ጳጳ​ስ፡</fo:inline>,
                                    <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e88320PRS10581Zamika">​አረ​ጋዊ።</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>,
                                    <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em"> ​ዮሴ​ፍ፡ ​ወማ​ትያ​ስ፡ ​አር<fo:inline>[////]</fo:inline>​ዳኢ​ሁ።</fo:inline>.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ጾሮ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e88331PRS7049Michael">​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ሚካ​ኤል፡</fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88334PRS10581Zamika">​ለአ​ረጋ​ዊ፡</fo:inline> ​ወአ​ብጽ​ሖ፡ ​ሀገ​ረ፡
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88337LOC1310Aksum">
                     <fo:inline>አኵስም፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(219) Fol. 12r: <fo:inline>Two scenes: the remaining members of the Nine Saints join
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88349PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline>
                                    in <fo:inline id="d1e88352LOC1310Aksum">ʾAksum</fo:inline> carrying their 
                                    <fo:inline font-style="italic">tabotāt</fo:inline>,
                                    as well as other liturgical implements including censers,
                                    a book in its case, and a chalice; the Nine Saints stand outside the city’s cathedral.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ወጽ​ኡ፡ ፰ ​ቅዱ​ሳን፡ ​አም​ሮም፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ታቦ​ቶሙ፡ ​ወበ​ጽሑ፡ ​ሀገ​ረ፡
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88361LOC1310Aksum">
                     <fo:inline>አኵስም። (!)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(220) Fol. 12v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88370PRS4523Garima">ʾAbbā Garimā</fo:inline> gives up his 
                                    throne in Rome to travel to Ethiopia on the back of the
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88373PRS4377Gabriel">Archangel Gabriel</fo:inline>.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​መነ​ነ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e88379PRS4523Garima">​አባ፡
                                    ​ገሪ​ማ፡</fo:inline> ​መን​ግሥ​ቶ።</fo:inline>
               <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ጾሮ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e88385PRS4377Gabriel">​ገብ​ርኤ​ል፡</fo:inline> 
                                    ​መል​አክ።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(221) Fol. 13r: <fo:inline>Eight of the Nine Saints stand before the Cathedral of
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88396LOC1310Aksum">ʾAksum</fo:inline>.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​አብ​ጽሖ፡ ​ሀገ​ረ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e88402LOC1310Aksum">
                     <fo:inline>አኵስም፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline> ​ኀበ፡ ​ሀለ​ው፡ ​ቅዱ​ሳን፡</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(222) Fol. 13v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88412PRS10581Zamika">ʾAbbā ʾAragāwi</fo:inline> ordains
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88415PRS4523Garima">ʾAbbā Garimā</fo:inline> as a monk.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​አል​በሰ፡ ​አል​ባሰ፡ ​ምን​ኵስ​ና፡ 
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88421PRS10581Zamika">​አባ፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ፡</fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88424PRS4523Garima">​ለአ​ባ፡ ​ገሪ​ማ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(223) Fol. 14r: <fo:inline>Two scenes: one of the Nine Saints moves a mountain with flowers on top of it; 
                                    and then parts the sea.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​አፍ​ለሰ፡ ​ደብ​ረ።</fo:inline>
               <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ከፈ​ለ፡ ​ባሕ​ረ።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(224) Fol. 14v: <fo:inline>Several scenes showing miracles performed by the Nine Saints:
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88447PRS4523Garima">ʾAbbā Garimā</fo:inline> threshes grain he miraculously grew in a day on top of an acacia 
                                    tree with the help of three zebus (sic!) (on this miracle, see
                                    als Zorzan 2023,  150);
                                    his finger tips shine with light during prayer; a saint plants a shrub 
                                    in the morning that turns into a tree by night; <fo:inline id="d1e88455PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline>
                                    is concealed by a cloud; a saint gathers water with a sieve; and a shrouded body of one 
                                    of the Nine Saints is buried by two angels.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88460PRS4523Garima">​አባ፡ ​ገሪ​ማ፡</fo:inline> ​ዘከ​መ፡ ​አኬ​ደ፡ ​ስር​ናየ፡
                                    ​ዲበ፡ ​ዕፀ፡ ​ግራ​ር። 
                                    </fo:inline>
               <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​አብ​ርሃ፡ ​አጸ​ብኢ​ሁ።</fo:inline>
               <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ተሰ​ወረ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e88469PRS10581Zamika">​አባ፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ወዘ​ከመ፡ ​ተክ​ለ፡ ​በነ​ግህ፡ ​ወአ​ብጽ​ሐ፡ ​እፀ፡ ​ለጽ​ንሐ​ሕ፡ ​ጊዜ፡
                                    ​ሰር​ክ።</fo:inline>
               <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​አቁ​ረረ፡ ​ማየ፡ ​በመ​ንፌ፡</fo:inline>
               <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ተገ​ንዘ፡ ​በእ​ደ፡ ​መላ​እክ​ት።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(225) Fol. 15r: <fo:inline>A lamp descends upon the table of the Nine Saints, the miracle
                                    is witnessed by two bystanders (the king’s soldiers?). Captions:
                                    <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ማዕ​ድ።</fo:inline>, <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ማኅ​ቶት።</fo:inline>.
                                </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(226) Fol. 16r: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88503PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline> curses the plants of a village, whose inhabitants had
                                    harmed him, causing them to wither.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ረገ​ማ፡ ​ለሃ​ገር፡ <fo:inline id="d1e88509PRS10581Zamika">​አባ፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ፡</fo:inline> 
                                    ​ወየ​ብሰ፡ ​ዕፀ​ዊሃ።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(227) Fol. 16v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88519PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline> blesses the plants of a village
                                    that had welcomed him
                                    making them bud and bear fruit.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ወለ​ካል​ዕት፡ ​ሀገ​ር፡ ​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ባረ​ካ፡ ​ወኮ​ነ፡ ​ልም​ሉማ​ተ፡ ​ዕፀ​ዊሃ።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(228) Fol. 17r: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88532PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline> exorcises a demon 
                                    from a man.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​አው​ፅአ፡ ​ጋኔ​ነ፡ ​እም​ላእ​ለ፡ ​ብእ​ሲ።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(229) Fol. 17v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88545PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline> blesses a 
                                    sick man with his handcross and heals him in
                                    front of his father.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ባረ​ከ፡ ​በት​እም​ርተ፡ ​መስ​ቀል፡ ​ወፈ​ወሰ፡ ​ድው​የ።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(230) Fol. 18r: <fo:inline>Two scenes: <fo:inline id="d1e88559PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline>
                                    arrives at the foot of the mountain called  Sequrā with his two
                                    disciples; and he climbs the mountain and blesses a loaf of bread on its peak</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ዓር​ገ፡ ​ላዕ​ሌሃ፡ ​ወባ​ረከ፡ ​ኅብ​ስተ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​አር​ዳኢ​ሁ።</fo:inline>
               <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​በጽ​ሐ፡ ​ታሕ​ተ፡ ​እግ​ረ፡ ​ደብ​ር፡ ​እንተ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ስማ፡ ​ሰቍ​ራ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡
                                    ፪ ​አርዳ<fo:inline>[ኢ]</fo:inline>​ሁ።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(231) Fol. 18v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88582PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline> and his disciples pray 
                                    and eat a loaf of blessed bread on the mountain called Məngərgār</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​በጽ​ሐ፡ ​ኀበ፡ ​ካል​ዕ፡ ​ደብ​ር፡ ​ዘስ​ሙ፡ ​ምን​ግር​ጋር፡ ​ወዓ​ርገ፡ ​ዲቤ​ሁ፡ ​ወባ​ረከ፡ ​ኅብ​ስተ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡
                                    ​አር​ዳኢ​ሁ።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(232) Fol. 19r: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88595PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline> and his disciples eat a loaf 
                                    of blessed bread on the
                                    mountain called Muḥaz.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ዓር​ገ፡ ​ኀበ፡ ​ካል​ዕ፡ ​ደብ​ር፡ ​ወባ​ረከ፡ ​ኅብ​ስተ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​አር​ዳኢ​ሁ፡ 
                                    ​እም​ላእ​ለ፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ደብ​ር፡ ​ዘስ​ሙ፡ ​ሙሐ​ዝ።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(233) Fol. 19v: <fo:inline>An impression is miraculously left in the spot near <fo:inline id="d1e88609INS0105DD">Dabra Dāmmo</fo:inline> 
                                    before a lectern where <fo:inline id="d1e88612PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline>’s
                                    disciples layed out of his mat and where 
                                    the saint rested his crosier and his foot. <!--<-\- what do you make of foot impression? 
                                        I believe this is not mentioned in the main text? 
                                        If so, does this depend on a local oral tradition? 
                                        I also don’t understand the reference to a “throne”
                                        in the caption, what’s textual source based on? Is mat the best term for mansefe? -\->-->
                                </fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​በጽ​ሐ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e88620INS0105DD">​ደብ​ረ፡ ​ዳሞ፡</fo:inline> ​ወአ​ንበ​ሩ፡ ​ሎቱ፡ ​መን​ጸፈ፡ ​ዝ፡ ​አር​ዳኢ​ሁ፡ ​ወኮ​ነ፡ ​ስዕ​ልተ፡ ​መል​ዕል​ተ፡
                                    ​ኰኵ​ሕ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​አት​ሮን​ስ፡ ​ወበ​ትረ፡ ​እግ​ሩኒ፡ ​ከነ​ተ፡ ​ስዕ​ልተ፡ ​ህየ።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(234) Fol. 22r: <fo:inline>Two scenes: <fo:inline id="d1e88631PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline> holds 
                                    onto the tail of a horned snake; he
                                    ascends the mountain of <fo:inline id="d1e88634INS0105DD">Dabra Dāmmo</fo:inline>, 
                                    while the <fo:inline id="d1e88637PRS7049Michael">Archangel Michael</fo:inline> pulls out his sword
                                    and remains at his side to prevent it from harming him.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​መጽ​አ፡ ​አር​ዌ፡ ​ወአ​ኀዘ፡ ​ዘነ​ቦ።</fo:inline>
               <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ዓረ​ጎ፡ ​ላዕ​ለ፡ ​ደብ​ር፡ 
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88646PRS7049Michael">​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ሚካ​ኤል፡</fo:inline> ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ይቅ​ውም፡ ​በየ​ማኑ።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(235) Fol. 23v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88656PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline> performs mass in a 
                                    small before a veiled <fo:inline font-style="italic">tābot</fo:inline> with
                                    bread, a chalice, vestments, and a paten brought to him by angels.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​አው​ረዱ፡  ​ሎቱ፡ 
                                    ​መላ​እክ​ት፡ ​ንዋ​ያተ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​መቅ​ድስ፡ ​ወተ​ወከ​ፈ፡
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88668PRS10581Zamika">​አባ፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(236) Fol. 25v: <fo:inline>A man asks <fo:inline id="d1e88678PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline>, who is 
                                    inside a cave, to heal his sick daughter, who waits at the foot
                                    of <fo:inline id="d1e88681INS0105DD">Dabra Dāmmo</fo:inline> since she 
                                    cannot enter the monastery</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ሰአ​ሎ፡ ፩ ​ብእ​ሲ፡ ​የሐ​ዩ፡ ​ወለ​ቶ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ሀለ​ወት፡ ​ታሕ​ተ፡ ​እግ​ረ፡ ​ድብ​ር።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(237) Fol. 26v: <fo:inline>Two scenes: An army general asks 
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88696PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline> who is in his cave to
                                    heal his daughter; he climbs down 
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88699INS0105DD">Dabra Dāmmo</fo:inline> and finds she has been freed 
                                    from the
                                    demon.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ <fo:inline>ወጽአ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​እም​ኔሃ፡  ​ጋኔ​ነ።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(238) Fol. 28r: <fo:inline>Thanks to <fo:inline id="d1e88718PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline> blessing 
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88721PRS5841Kaleb">King Kāleb</fo:inline> marches unseen by his
                                    enemies in an underground passage.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ባረ​ኮ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e88727PRS5841Kaleb">​ለካ​ሌብ፡</fo:inline> ​ንጉ​ሥ፡ ​ወተ​ርኀ​ወት፡ ​ሎቱ፡ ​ምድ​ር።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(239) Fol. 28v: <fo:inline>Two scenes: <fo:inline id="d1e88738PRS5841Kaleb">King Kāleb</fo:inline> on
                                    horseback and his men with shields
                                    and spears kill the sorcerer Finḥas and his soldiers in
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88741LOC4955Najran">Nāǧrān</fo:inline>; and rebuild the destroyed 
                                    church of this country (the structure in the upper left register of the folio in which the king 
                                    and his men are placed, which is similar to that found on the previous page, could represent
                                    either a tunnel use to reach <fo:inline id="d1e88744LOC4955Najran">Nāǧrān</fo:inline> or a trench used to reach the newly constructed church).</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ቀተ​ሎ፡ ​ለፊ​ንሐ​ስ፡ ​አላ​ዊ፡ ​ወለ​ኵሉ፡ ​ሠራ​ዊቱ።
                                    ​ወሐ​ነፀ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​ህየ።
                                </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(240) Fol. 31r: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88757PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline>, flanked by attendants
                                    holdings candles and a chalice, offers the bread of the
                                    communion to the <fo:inline id="d1e88760PRS4327GabraMa">King Gabra Masqal</fo:inline>
                                    and his soldiers (and possibly also the bishop) before a veiled altar in the newly
                                    consecrated church of <fo:inline id="d1e88763INS0105DD">Dabra Dāmmo</fo:inline> commissioned by this ruler</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ወረ​ደ፡ ​ሎቱ፡ ​መን​ፈስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​በጊ​ዜ፡ ​ቍር​ባን፡ ​በአ​ምሳ​ለ፡ ​ርግ​ብ፡ ​ወተ​መጠ​ው፡ 
                                    ​እም​እደ​ዊሁ፡ ​ቍር​ባነ፡ ​ንጉ​ሥ፡ ​ወሠ​ራዊ​ቱ።
                                </fo:inline>
               <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ወዘ​ከመ፡ ​ሐነ​ፀ፡ ​ሎቱ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(241) Fol. 31v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88779PRS5684JesusCh">Jesus Christ</fo:inline> grants a Kidān 
                                    to <fo:inline id="d1e88782PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline> that all that partake
                                    from the Eucharist from his hands will be saved.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ወሀ​ቦ፡ ​ኪዳ​ነ፡ ​እግ​ዚእ​ነ፡ 
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88788PRS5684JesusCh">​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡</fo:inline> ​ከመ፡ ​ይሕ​የው፡ ​ሎቱ፡ ​ኵሎ​ሙ፡ 
                                    ​እለ፡ ​ተመ​ጠው፡ ​ቍር​ባነ፡ ​በእ​ዴሁ።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(242) Fol. 32r: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88798PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline> gives his blessing to 
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88801PRS4327GabraMa">King Gabra Masqal</fo:inline>  who kneels before without his crown on his head</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ከመ፡ ​ባረ​ኮ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e88807PRS10581Zamika">​አባ፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ</fo:inline>፡ 
                                    ​ለን​ጉሥ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e88810PRS4327GabraMa">​ገብ​ረ፡ ​መስ​ቀል።</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(243) Fol. 32v: <fo:inline>The followers of the king are also blessed.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሕዝ​ብኒ፡ ​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ተባ​ረኩ፡ ​ምስ​ሌሁ።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(244) Fol. 35v: <fo:inline>Two scenes: <fo:inline id="d1e88831PRS10245Yared">Yāred</fo:inline> and
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88834PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline>
                                    meet and embrace each other atop
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88837INS0105DD">Dabra Dāmmo</fo:inline>; and
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88840PRS10245Yared">Yāred</fo:inline> sings before the newly 
                                    consecrated church that angels will visit it.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ተራ​ከቦ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e88846PRS10245Yared">​ያሬ​ድ፡</fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88849PRS10581Zamika">​ለአ​ቡነ፡ <fo:inline>አራጋዊ፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline> ​ወይ​ቤ፡ ​ኪያ​ከ፡ ​መሠ​ረተ፡
                                    ​አን​ተ፡ ​ብነ።</fo:inline>
               <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ቦአ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​መቅ​ደስ፡ ​ወይ​ቤ፡ ​ይሔ​ውጽ​ዋ፡ <fo:inline>መለእክት። (!)</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(245) Fol. 38v: <fo:inline>The second Kidān between Jesus Christ and
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88865PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi</fo:inline> that grants
                                    redemption to those who celebrate his commemoration and invoke his name.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ነስ​አ፡ ​ኪዳ​ነ፡ ​እም​ኀበ፡ ​አም​ላኩ፡ 
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88871PRS10581Zamika">​አቡ​ነ፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ፡</fo:inline> ​ከመ፡ ​ይር​ከቡ፡ ​ሕይ​ወተ፡ ​እለ፡ ​ገብ​ሩ፡ 
                                    ​ተዝ​ካሩ፡ ​ወጸ​ውዑ፡ ​ስሞ።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(246) Fol. 40v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88881PRS10581Zamika">ʾAragāwi’s</fo:inline> disciples are blessed 
                                    during a communal meal held
                                    during his commemoration on the top of <fo:inline id="d1e88884INS0105DD">Dabra Dāmmo</fo:inline>.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​በዕ​ለተ፡ <fo:inline>ተዝከሩ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ዐባ​ይ፡ ​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ኮነ፡ ​በረ​ከት፡ ​በጊ​ዜ፡ ​ማዕ​ድ።</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(247) Fol. 43v: <fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline id="d1e88899PRS9162TaklaHa">Takla Hāymānot</fo:inline> ascends with his wings to <fo:inline id="d1e88902INS0105DD">Dabra Dāmmo</fo:inline> where he
                                    meets <fo:inline id="d1e88905PRS10429Yohanni">Yoḥanni</fo:inline>, its seventh abbot, who prays with him and gives his the monastic garb and 
                                    cap.</fo:inline> Legend: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ዓር​ገ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e88911INS0105DD">​ደብ​ረ፡ ​ዳሞ፡</fo:inline>
                                    ​በክ​ንፍ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e88914PRS9162TaklaHa">​አባ፡ ​ተክ​ለ፡ ​ሃይ​ማኖ​ት፡</fo:inline> ​ወነ​ሥአ፡ ​አስ​ኬማ፡ ​ወቆ​ብዓ፡ ​እም​ኀበ፡
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88917PRS10429Yohanni">​አባ፡ ​ዮሐ​ኒ፡</fo:inline> ​ዘው​እቱ፡ ​ስብ​ዕ፡ ​መም​ህር፡ 
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e88920PRS10581Zamika">​እም​አቡ​ነ፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Headpieces</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Drawings</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Other</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>A couple of small tears resulting from parchment making are found on fols 4, 54
                                       and have been repaired by sewing.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is good.
                                     The folios only show slight traces of use on the lower margins
                                  and stains of various origin. Few tears are present, e.g. fols 4, 34, 39.
                                  The manuscript lacks a leather spine and endbands, which have been removed to repair the sewing.
                                  Both the leather cover and the textile chemise are torn at the outer external corners.
                                  The sewing of the satchel has become undone.
                                </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>eighteenth century</fo:inline>
                            According to Additional note 4 
                            <!--check if correct-->, the manuscript was produced
                            for <fo:inline id="d1e89415PRS14785EhetaMaryam">ʾƎḫǝta Māryām</fo:inline>,
                            whose name is mentioned regularly in supplications
                            (see Varia note 2), during the reign of
                            <fo:inline id="d1e89421PRS5617IyasuII">ʾIyāsu II</fo:inline>. It was meant for the church
                            <fo:inline id="d1e89424INS1023BadawoAragawi">Badāwo ʾAbuna ʾAragāwi</fo:inline>, also founded by her.
                            
                           <!-- JG: Date: JJ believed, and I think he was right, that the manuscript’s note mentions Iyasu I and Iyasu II, but that it was produced 
                            in the former’s reign the style of the miniatures is certainly late sixteenth/early seventeenth century and would not align with
                            the reign of Iyasu II 
                            Patron: the name of ʾƎḫəta Māryām appears to have been added at a later date
                           DR:  I don't think the name  is a later addition, see for example 20v or
                           45v.  I understand the note on 26r to mean that ʾƎḫəta Māryām is a
                           daughter of Mentewwab-->
                            
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>
                        The manuscript was sold as lot 143, 23 June 1987, 
                        in a sale of manuscripts at Sotheby’s that included MS
                        Aeth. b. 6, the
                        Synaxarium with the forged miniatures, where the pieces had export licenses,
                        and was purchased by
                        <fo:inline id="d1e89438PRS13559Thomas">Alan Thomas</fo:inline> on behalf of 
                        <fo:inline id="d1e89441PRS5782JuelJen">Juel-Jensen</fo:inline>.
                   </fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                        bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e89447PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Bibliography</fo:block>Thomas 1990.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethd23">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethd23</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
