      <fo:static-content flow-name="xsl-footnote-separator">
         <fo:block space-before="5mm" space-after="5mm">
            <fo:leader leader-length="30%" rule-thickness="0pt"/>
         </fo:block>
      </fo:static-content>
      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethb6"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. b. 6</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Arch. O. b. 23, Juel-Jensen 45)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex, composite393×343 mm, 188 fols.  Unit 1: , 1632–1667. Unit 2: , 1632–1667. </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                                    The book is bound in wooden boards covered with reddish-brown blind-tooled leather. The inner sides of both boards are decorated with red textile <fo:inline id="d1e90661">inlays</fo:inline>.
                                  
                                    The boards are cut to the same size as the bookblock and present both external and internal shallow bevels.
                                  
                                    Full reddish-brown leather cover.
                                    The turn-ins have been trimmed out and at the corners they form butt mitres, which overlap slightly.
                                    An <fo:inline id="d1e90670">additional leather patch</fo:inline> has been added along the inner margin of the boards to fill the gap between the turn-ins
                                    but on the front board it has been removed, presumably to re-sew the bookblock.
                                    The cover shows a fine blind-tooled decoration, identical on both sides of the cover while the turn-ins and the edges are not decorated.
                                    The decoration consists of eleven concentric frames surrounding a central rectangular panel featuring a equal-armed cross with an extended lower stem.
                                    Frames composed by the repetition of single tools, enclosed between <fo:inline id="d1e90673">double straight lines</fo:inline>,
                                    alternate with empty ones.
                                    Proceeding from the outer to the inner frame, the repeating decoration motifs are <fo:inline id="d1e90676">criss-crosses</fo:inline>,
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e90679">curve strapwork</fo:inline> elements, <fo:inline id="d1e90682">straight strapwork</fo:inline> elements, <fo:inline id="d1e90686">mother of water</fo:inline> motifs,
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e90689">wavy lines</fo:inline> with <fo:inline id="d1e90692">double circles</fo:inline> between them, and <fo:inline id="d1e90695">X-form</fo:inline> motifs.
                                    The cross is formed by <fo:inline id="d1e90698">X-form</fo:inline> motifs of smaller dimension between double straight lines.
                                    At the ends of the arms of the cross there are <fo:inline id="d1e90701">corniform</fo:inline>motifs and three <fo:inline id="d1e90705">double circles</fo:inline>.
                                    Double straight lines outline the shape of the cross, dividing the area around it in six panels.
                                    In the panels at the foot of the cross, the triple straight lines form two triangles, each surmounted by four double circles.
                                    Above, they intersect forming in each panel a <fo:inline font-style="italic">crux decussata</fo:inline>.
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e90711">Double circles</fo:inline> are stamped at the intersections of the straight lines and at the corners of the empty frames.
                                  
                                    Chainstitch sewing on four sewing stations (two pairs); periodic fold pattern; S-plied threads.
                                    Between each pair of sewing stations there are two lengths of thread.
                                  
                                    The back of the leather cover, together with the endbands, has been removed to resew the manuscript.
                                    The small holes close to the head and tail of the quires testify to the former presence of endbands.
                                  
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e90727">Leaf string markers</fo:inline> sewn on the upper outer corner of nearly all folios containing larger miniatures, e.g.
                                    fols 1, 102, 187.
                                  </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Pencil foliation in the upper right corner (1–188).</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>1632–1667</fo:inline>
                            This manuscript corresponds to two codicological units, both written by the same hand.
                            Unit 1 consists of one single folio (fol. 1),
                            while Unit 2 is composed of the rest of the text block.
                            The name of <fo:inline id="d1e90751PRS4015Fasilada">Fāsiladas</fo:inline> was originally mentioned in supplications
                            throughout the manuscript, which points to a production date between 1632–1667.
                            Throughout, the name originally mentioned in supplications,
                            still partly legible as <fo:inline id="d1e90754PRS13548AsadaI">ʾAṣada ʾIyasus</fo:inline>,
                            has been erased and that of <fo:inline id="d1e90756PRS13551KidanaW">Kidāna Wald</fo:inline>and more rarely that of
                            <fo:inline id="d1e90758PRS13550WalattaM">Walatta Mikāʾel</fo:inline> added (see Varia note 1).
                            At some point before the manuscript’s sale at Sotheby’s in 1987,  miniatures were
                            added above the text, and several colophon-type notes
                            (see Additional notes 1, 8, 9, and 10)
                            were added in blank spaces and margins. These state that the manuscript was written in 1751/52,
                            at the time of <fo:inline id="d1e90766PRS5617IyasuII">ʾIyāsu II</fo:inline>.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript was sold at Sotheby’s in December 1987,
                            and bought by <fo:inline id="d1e90771PRS13559Thomas">Alan G. Thomas</fo:inline> (see
                            Juel-Jensen 1991,  484–485, where this manuscript is
                            referred to as ‘Synkessar 2’). After <fo:inline id="d1e90779PRS5782JuelJen">Bent
                                Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> exposed the miniatures as recent forgeries,
                            he himself acquired the manuscript, probably either directly from the previous owner or
                            through the intermediary of Sotheby’s.</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e90785PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Bibliography</fo:block>Juel-Jensen 1991.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm">Unit 1</fo:block>
         <fo:block>Parchment, 1 fols (fol. 1 fol. 1), 1 quires.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e90822LIT4035SenkessarDL#Terr">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 1ra–1vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Terr</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Fols 1,  contains the beginning of 1 Ṭǝrr, written by the same hand as
                                the rest of the manuscript,
                                which is also contained in this manuscript on 126. It is unclear
                                whether the folio has been displaced or belonged originally to another manuscript.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e90834LIT4035SenkessarDL#TerrIntroduction">
               <fo:inline>I-1) Fol. 1ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Introduction for Ṭǝrr
                     </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e90841LIT4035SenkessarDL#Terr1">
               <fo:inline>I-2) Fols 1ra–1vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: 
                        1st Ṭǝrr
                        
                     </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e90847LIT4035SenkessarDL#Terr1Estifanos">
               <fo:inline>I-2-1) Fols 1ra–1rc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Commemoration of St Stephen the Protomartyr
                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e90855LIT4035SenkessarDL#Terr1SalStephen">
               <fo:inline>I-2-2) Fol. 1rc: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Salām-hymn to Stephen</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e90863LIT4035SenkessarDL#Terr1Lawdyanos">
               <fo:inline>I-2-3) Fols 1rc–1va: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Commemoration of Lāwdyānos</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e90872LIT4035SenkessarDL#Terr1SalAwendyos">
               <fo:inline>I-2-4) Fol. 1va: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Salām-hymn to ʾAwǝndyos</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e90880LIT4035SenkessarDL#Terr1Maqaryos">
               <fo:inline>I-2-5) Fols 1va–1vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Commemoration of Maqāryos</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block>1 quire. I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">1 (Fols 1r–1v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 1ra–1vb: 3
                                    columns (35 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">The characters per line per column are 16–21.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling is visible; pricking is visible. Primary pricks are partly visible. Ruling pricks are mostly visible. The upper and bottom lines are written above the ruling. Ruling pattern (fols 1ra–1vb): 1A-1A-1A1A-1A1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm">Unit 2</fo:block>
         <fo:block>Parchment, 187 fols (fols 2–188), 26 quires.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e90982LIT4035SenkessarDL#FirstHalf">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 2ra–187vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: First half of the year</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Whenever possible, names are identified in English. All Ethiopic names and unidentifiable names are given
                                in their most common occurrence in the manuscript. Hymns are designated as
                                ‘salām-hymn’ when starting with <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሰላ​ም፡</fo:inline> and as ‘ʿārke-hymn’ when starting
                            with other words.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e90996LIT4035SenkessarDL#MaskIntroduction">
               <fo:inline>I-1) Fol. 2ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Introduction for the first half of the year</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                     (fol. 2ra) 
                                    ​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ ​ስ፡  ​፩፡  ​አም​ላክ ፨ ​ዘቀ​ድሕ​ዎ፡ ​አበ​ዊነ፡
                                    ​ቅዱሳ ​ን፡ ​መም​ህራ​ነ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​አብ፡ ​ክቡ​ር፡ ​አባ፡ ​ሚካ​ኤል፡ ​ኤጲ​ስ፡
                                    ​ቆጶ​ስ፡ ​በሀ​ገረ፡ ​አት​ሪብ፡ ​ወመ​ሊግ ፨  ​ወአ​ብ፡ ​ክቡ​ር፡ ​አባ፡ ​ዮሐ​ንስ፡ ​ኤጲ​ስ፡
                                    ​ቆጶ​ስ፡ ​ዘሀ​ገረ፡ ​ቡር​ልስ፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                     ​ዘጻ​ድቃ​ን፡ ​ወዘ​ሰማ​ዕታት ፤  ​ወሊ​ቃነ፡ ​ጳጳ​ሳት፡ ​ቅዱ​ሳን ፤ 
                                    ​ወገ​ዳማ​ዊያ​ን፡ ​መነ​ኮሳት ፨  ​ከመ፡ ​ይግ​በሩ፡
                                        ​ተዝ​ካሮ​ሙ፡ ​ወያ​ንብ​ቡ፡ ​ገድ​ሎሙ፡ ​ኵሎ፡ ​አሚ​ረ፡ ​እም​ሠር​ቀ፡ ​አሚ​ሩ፡ ​ለመ​ስከ​ረም፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ተፍ​ጻሜ​ተ፡ ​ዓመት ፨  ​ወኮ​ነ፡
                                    ​አስ​ተጋ​ብኦ​ቱ፡ ​ለዝ​ንቱ፡ ​መጽ​ሐፍ፡ በ ​፱፻፡ ​፷ወ​፫፡ 
                                        ​ዓመ​ተ፡ ​ሰማ​ዕታ​ት፡ ​ንጹ​ሐን ፨
                                    ​ጸሎ​ቶሙ፡ ​ወበ​ረከ​ቶሙ፡  ​የሀ​ሉ፡  ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ፍቁ​ሮሙ፡
                                        <fo:inline id="d1e91059PRS4015Fasilada">​ፋሲ​ለደ​ስ፡</fo:inline> ​ንጉሥ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                        ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜን ፨ ​ኦን​ጉሥ​ነ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e91071PRS5617IyasuII">​ኢያ​ሱ፡ ​ብር​ሃን።</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e91081LIT4035SenkessarDL#Maskaram">
               <fo:inline>I-2) Fols 2ra–31vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: 
                     Maskaram
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e91087LIT4035SenkessarDL#Mask1">
               <fo:inline>I-2-1) Fols 2ra–4ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: 
                        1st Maskaram
                        
                     </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e91093LIT4035SenkessarDL#Mask1Beginning">
               <fo:inline>I-2-1-1) Fols 2ra–2rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Synaxarion: Beginning of the year</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ​ዝን​ቱ፡ ​ወር​ኃ፡ ​መስ​ከረ​ም፡ ​ቡሩ​ክ፡
                                            ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ርእ​ሰ፡ ​ዓመ​ታት፡ ​ዘግ​ብጽ፡ ​ወዘ ​ኢት​ዮጵ​ያ፡ ​መዓ​ልቱ፡ ​ወሌ​ሊቱ፡ ​ለዝ​ንቱ፡ ​ወር​ኅ፡
                                            ​ዕሩ​ይ፡  ​፲፡  ወ ​፪፡  ​ሰዓቱ ፨  ​ወእ​ምዝ፡ ​የሐ​ፅፅ፡ ​እም​አሚ​ሩ፡ ​ለወ​ርኃ፡ ​መስ​ከረ​ም፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ርእ​ሰ፡ ​ዓው​ደ፡ ​ዓመ​ት፡ ​ቡር​ክት፡ ​ዘግ​ብጽ፡
                                            ​ወዘ​ኢት​ዮጵያ ፨  ​ወይ​እዜ​ኒ፡ ​ይደ​ልወ​ነ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ንግ​በር፡ ​ባቲ፡ ​በዓ​ለ፡ ​ዓባ​የ፡
                                            ​በኵ​ሉ፡ ​ንጽ​ሕና ፤
                                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ​ወለ​ዕው​ራን፡ ​ይር​አዩ፡ ​ብር​ሃነ ፨ 
                                            ​ወእ​ሱራ​ን፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ይት​ፈትሑ ፨  ​ወእ​ስብ​ክ፡ ​ዓመ​ተ፡
                                            ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ዘም​ሕረት ፨  ​ወይ​ቤ፡ ​ዳዊ​ት፡ ​ነቢ​ይ፡ ​ወት​ባር​ክ፡ ​አክ​ሊለ፡ ​ዓመ​ተ፡ ​ምሕ​ረትከ ፨ 
                                            ​ወይ​ጸግ​ቡ፡ ​ጠላ​ተ፡ ​ገዳ​ም፡ ​እም​በረ​ከትከ ፨
                                            <fo:inline id="d1e91140PRS13550WalattaM">​ወለ​ተ፡ ​ሚካ​ኤል፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
