      <fo:static-content flow-name="xsl-footnote-separator">
         <fo:block space-before="5mm" space-after="5mm">
            <fo:leader leader-length="30%" rule-thickness="0pt"/>
         </fo:block>
      </fo:static-content>
      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethc14"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. c. 14</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Juel-Jensen 46)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex, composite313×265 mm (weight: 3858g), 130 fols.  Unit 1:  sixteenth century. Unit 2:  mid-seventeenth–eighteenth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                              The book is bound in wooden boards which were previously covered with brown blind-tooled leather.
                              A block-printed cotton textile <fo:inline id="d1e104701">inlay</fo:inline> coloured in blue, and
                              red of Indian provenance (see Crill 2026,  169–170) is glued on the inner side of the front board.
                            
                              The boards are cut to the same size as the bookblock and have external shallow bevels. The grain runs vertically.
                            
                                Of the brown leather cover, only the turn-ins are preserved. Concentric frames of blind-tooled <fo:inline id="d1e104716">triple straight lines</fo:inline> outline the borders of straight trimmed turn-ins.
                              The edges of turn-ins meet to form butt mitres.
                            
                              Chainstitch sewing on four sewing stations (two pairs); periodic fold pattern. S-plied threads are used.
                              The ends of the threads are knotted in the centrefold of the last quire.
                          
                              Threads of various colours are inserted in the outer margins for navigating the text.
                              More specifically, a red <fo:inline id="d1e104729">leaf string marker</fo:inline> is inserted in the lower margin of fol. 86 and a
                              uncoloured <fo:inline id="d1e104734">leaf string marker</fo:inline> is inserted in the upper margin of fols 104.
                              Disjoint bifolios have been repaired with overcasting, e.g. fols 51–53 or by sewing parchment <fo:inline id="d1e104742">guards</fo:inline> with <fo:inline id="d1e104745">side stitches</fo:inline>
                              along the <fo:inline id="d1e104748">spine fold</fo:inline> of the quires, e.g. quire 18.
                              The manuscript is wrapped in a modern textile embroidered with two lions and probably purchased by <fo:inline id="d1e104754PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline>.
                          </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Pencil foliation in the upper right corner carried out by the Bodleian Library in January 2020 (1–130).</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
                            The provenance of the manuscript is unknown. According to Additional note 2, Unit 1 was hosted in or linked to the church of
                            <fo:inline id="d1e104770LOC7349DabraMi">Dabra Mikāʾel</fo:inline>. Remarkably,
                            the same place is also mentioned in Colophon 1,
                            which, however, refers to Unit 2.
                            According to Colophon 1, Unit 2 belonged to <fo:inline id="d1e104786LOC7349DabraMi">Dabra Mikāʾel</fo:inline>
                            of the city of <fo:inline id="d1e104789LOC6450Zatta">Zāttā</fo:inline> in <fo:inline id="d1e104792LOC6573NorthWallo">Northern Wallo</fo:inline>.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e104798PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Bibliography</fo:block>Gnisci 2019; Crill 2026; Juel-Jensen 1996.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm">Unit 1</fo:block>
         <fo:block>Parchment, 123 fols (fols 1–123), 18 quires, sixteenth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e104841LIT1560Gospel">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 1ra–123vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Four Gospels, incomplete, CAe 1560.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The introductory materials to the Four Gospels, i.e. the Synopsis of the class, the Letter of Eusebius
                                    to Carpianus and the Eusebian Canons, are missing.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e104849LIT1558Matthew">
               <fo:inline>I-1) Fols 1ra–35ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Gospel of Matthew (Collection), CAe 1558.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e104855LIT1558Matthew#TituliMatthew">
               <fo:inline>I-1-1) Fols 1ra–1va: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Gospel of Matthew (Collection): Tituli of the Gospel of Matthew</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The first three lines are blank, in correspondence of
                                            the first three <fo:inline font-style="italic">tituli</fo:inline>.
                                            The <fo:inline font-style="italic">tituli</fo:inline> are numbered from 1 to 63.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ፩  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ቅዳ​ሜ፡ ​ትም​ህር​ት፡
                                             ፪  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ብፁ​ዓን ፨
                                            ፫  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዘለ​ምጽ ፨
                                            ፬  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​መስ​ፍን ፨
                                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ፷  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ግብ​አቱ፡ ​ለክ​ርስ​ቶስ ፨
                                            ​፷፩  ​በእ​ንተ፡
                                             ​፷፪  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ነስ​ሐ፡ ​ይሁዳ ፨
                                            ​፷፫  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ስእ​ለተ፡ ​ሥጋ​ሁ፡ <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ግዚ​እነ ፨
                                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e104938LIT2709Matthew">
               <fo:inline>I-1-2) Fols 2ra–35ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Gospel of Matthew, CAe 2709.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">
                                            A stichometric note, that states that the Gospel of Matthew has 2700 lines (according to the
                                            meaning of <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቃል፡</fo:inline> in
                                            this context), is added at the end of the text on fol. 35ra: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ወን​ጌል፡ ​ዘማ​ቴዎ​ስ፡ ​ቃሉ፡ ​፳፻​ወ፯​፻።</fo:inline>.
                                        </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ​በስ​መ፡ ​ኣብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​አሐ​ዱ፡ ​አም​ላክ፡  ​ብስ​ራተ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ማቴ​ዎስ፡ ​ሐዋ​ርያ፡ ​ቡሩ​ክ፡ ​ዘዜ​ነወ፡
                                            ​ወን ​ጌለ፡ ​ጸጋ​ሁ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​እነ፡ ​ወመ​ድኃ​ኒነ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​ጸሎ ​ቱ፡ ​ወበ​ረከ​ቱ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ሌነ፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜን ፨
                                            ​ወን​ጌል፡ ​ዘማ​ቴዎስ ፨
                                        </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ​መጽ​ሐፈ፡ ​ልደ​ቱ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​እነ፡ ኢ ​የሱ​ስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ዳዊ​ት፡  ​ወል​ደ፡ ​አብ​ርሃም ፨  ​አብ​ርሃ​ም፡ 
                                            ​ወለ​ዶ፡
                                            ​ለይ​ስሐቅ ፨ 
                                            ​ወይ​ስሐቅ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline> ​ወያ​ዕቆብ ​ኒ፡ ​ወለ​ደ፡ <fo:inline>ይሁዳ፡ ሃ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ወአ​ኃዊሁ ፨
                                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            
                                            ​ወቀ​ረቦ​ሙ፡ ​እግ​ዚእ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ወነ​በቦ​ሙ፡ ​ወይ​ቤሎ​ሙ፡ ​ተው​ህበ፡ ​ሊተ፡ ​ስል​ጣን፡ ​በሰ​ማይ፡ ​ወበ​ምድ​ር፡ ሑ<fo:inline>[ሩ]</fo:inline>​ኬ፡
                                            ​እን​ከ፡ ​ወመ​ሀሩ፡ ​ለኵ​ሉ፡ ​አሕ​ዛብ፡ ​ወአ​ጥም​ቅዎ​ሙ፡ ​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱስ ፨ 
                                            ​ወመ​ሀር​ዎሙ፡ ​ይዕ​ቀቡ፡ ​ኵሎ፡ ​ዘአ​ዘዝ​ኩክ​ሙ፡ ​ወና​ሁ፡ ​አነ፡
                                            ​ሀለ​ውኩ፡ ም  (fol. 35ra)  ​ስሌ​ክሙ፡ ​በኵ​ሉ፡ ​መዋ​ዕል፡ ​እስ​ከ፡
                                            ​ኅል​ቀተ፡ ​ዓለም ​፨=፨
                                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e105026LIT1882MarkGo">
               <fo:inline>I-2) Fols 35rb–60vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Gospel of Mark (Collection), CAe 1882.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e105032LIT1882MarkGo#TituliMark">
               <fo:inline>I-2-1) Fols 35rb–35va: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Gospel of Mark (Collection): Tituli of the Gospel of Mark</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The <fo:inline font-style="italic">tituli</fo:inline> are numbered from 1 to 48.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ፩  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዘጋ​ኔን።
                                             ፪  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ሐማ​ተ፡ ​ጴጥ​ሮስ።
                                             ፫  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​እለ፡ ​ተፈ​ውሱ፡ ​እም​ብዙ​ኅ፡ 
                                            ፬  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዘለ​ምጽ።
                                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ​፵፭  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ፋሲ​ካ።
                                             ​፵፮  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ኣግ​ብኦ፡ ​ይሁ​ዳ።
                                             ​፵፯  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ክሕ​ደ፡ ​ጴጥ​ሮስ።
                                             ​፵፰  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ስእ​ለተ፡ ​ሥጋ​ሁ፡ ​ለእ ​ግዚ ​እነ።
                                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e105098LIT2711Mark">
               <fo:inline>I-2-2) Fols 36ra–60vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Gospel of Mark, CAe 2711.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">
                                            A stichometric note, that states that the Gospel of Mark has 1700 lines, is added at the end of the text on fol. 60vb:
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ወን​ጌል፡ ​ዘማ​ርቆ​ስ፡ ​ቃሉ፡ ​፲፻፡፯፻</fo:inline>.
                                        </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ​ወን​ጌል ፨  ዘ ፨  ​ማር​ቆስ ፨
                                        </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ​ቀዳ​ሚሁ፡ ​ለወ​ንጌ​ል፡ ​እግዚ ​እ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ፡ ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​በከ​መ፡ ጽ ​ሑፍ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ነቢ​ያት፡
                                                ​ናሁ፡ ​አነ፡ ​እፌ​ኑ፡ ​መል​ኣክ​የ፡ ​ቅድ​መ፡  ​ገጽ​ከ፡ ​ዘይ​ጸይ​ሕ፡ ​ፍኖ​ተከ ፨ 
                                            ​ቃለ፡ ​ኣዋ​ዲ፡ ​ዘይ​ሰብ​ክ፡ ​በገዳ ​ም፡ ​ወይ​ብል፡ ​ጺሑ​አ፡ ​ፍኖ​ቶ፡
                                                ​ለእ​ግዚ​አ፡ ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ወዐ​ርዩ፡ መ ​ጽያ​ሕቶ ፨  ​ወሀ​ሎ፡ ​ዮሐ​ንስ፡ ​ያጠ​ምቅ፡ ​በገ​ዳም፡
                                            ​ወይ​ሰብ​ክ፡ ​ጥም​ቀተ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ይነ​ስሑ፡ ​ወይ​ትኀ​ደግ፡ ​ሎሙ፡
                                            ​ኃጢ​ኣቶሙ ፨
                                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            
                                            ​በስ​መ፡ ​ዚኣ​የ፡ ​አጋ​ንን​ት፡ ​ያወ​ፅኡ፡ ​ወበ​ካል​እ፡ ​ልሳ​ን፡ ​ይት​ናገ​ሩ፡ ​ሐዲ​ሰ። ​ወኣ​ራዊ​ተ፡ ​ምድ​ር፡ ​ይእ​ኅዙ፡ ​ወዘ​ሂ፡ ​ይቀ​ትል፡ ​እመ፡ ​ሰት​ዩ፡ ​አል​ቦ፡ ​ዘይ​ነክ​ዮሙ ፨ 
                                            ​ወዲ​በ፡ ​ድዉ​ያን፡ ​እደ​ዊሆ​ሙ፡ ​ያነ​ብሩ፡ ​ወይ​ሜጥኑ ፨  ​ወእ​ግዚ​እነ​ሰ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​እም​ድኅ​ረ፡ ​ተና​ገሮ​ሙ፡
                                            ​ዐር​ገ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ሰማ​ይ፡ ​ወነ​በረ፡ ​በየ​ማነ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ፡
                                            ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ኣቡ​ሁ። ​ወወ​ፂኦ​ሙ፡ ​እም​ህየ፡ ​እሙ​ንቱ፡ ​በኵ​ለሄ፡ ​ሰበ​ኩ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​እግ​ዚእ፡ ​ይረ​ድእ፡ ​ወቃ​ሎ፡ ​ያጸ​ንዕ፡ ​በተ​ኣም​ር፡ ​ዘይ​ተሉ፡ ​አሜን ፨
                                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e105172LIT1812GospelLuke">
               <fo:inline>I-3) Fols 61ra–100rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Gospel of Luke (Collection), CAe 1812.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e105178LIT1812GospelLuke#TituliLuke">
               <fo:inline>I-3-1) Fols 61ra–61vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Gospel of Luke (Collection): Tituli of the Gospel of Luke</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The <fo:inline font-style="italic">tituli</fo:inline> are written over erasure up to 83.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                     <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline> ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ጸሕፍ ፨  ፪ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ኖሎ​ት።
                                            <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline> ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ስም​ዖን ፨ ፬  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ሐና፡ ​ነቢ​ት።
                                            <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline> ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ቃል፡ ​ዘኮ​ነ፡ ​ኃበ፡ ​ዮሐ​ንስ።
                                            <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline> ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ተመ​ከረ፡ ​መድ​ኃኒ​ነ።
                                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ፹  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ኣስ​ተኣ​ከዮ፡ ​ሄሮ​ድስ።
                                              (b) 
                                            ​፹፩  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​እለ፡ ​ይበ​ክያ፡ ​አን​ስት።
                                             ​፹፪  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ነስ​ሐ፡ ​ፈያ​ታዊ።
                                             ​፹፫  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ስእ​ለተ፡ ​ሥጋ​ሁ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​እነ።
                                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e105245LIT2713Luke">
               <fo:inline>I-3-2) Fols 62ra–100rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Gospel of Luke’ (​ብስ​ራተ፡ ​ሉቃ​ስ፡), CAe 2713.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">
                                            A stichometric note, that states that the Gospel of Luke has 2800 lines, is added at the end of the text on fol. 100rb:
                                           <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ወን​ጌል፡ ​ዘሉ​ቃስ፡ ​ቃሉ፡ ​፳፻​፰፻።</fo:inline>.
                                        </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ​ወን​ጌል፡ ​ዘሉ​ቃስ።
                                        </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ​እስ​መ፡ ​ብዙ​ኃን፡ ​እለ፡ ​አኃ​ዙ፡ ወ ​ጠኑ፡ ​ይግ​በሩ፡ ​ወይ​ምሀ​ሩ፡ ​በእ ​ንተ፡ ​ግብ​ር፡ ​ዘኣ​ምኑ፡ ​በላ​ዕሌ​ነ፡  ​በከ​መ፡
                                            ​መሀ​ሩነ፡ ​እለ፡ ​ቀደ​ሙ፡  ​ርእ​ዮቶ፡ ​ወተ​ልእ​ኩዎ፡ ​በቃ​ሉ፡  ​ወረ​ትዓ​ኒ፡ ​ሊተ​ኒ፡ ​እት​ልዎ፡ ​እም ​ጥን​ቱ፡ ​ወእ​ጠይ​ቆ፡
                                                ​ለኵ​ሉ፡ ​በበ፡  ​መት​ልዉ ፨  ​እጽ​ሕፍ፡ ​ለከ፡ ​ዓዚ​ዝ፡  ​ቴዎ​ፍሊ፡ ​ለኣ​ኃዚ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ታእም ​ር፡ ​ጥዩ​ቀ፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​ኃይ​ለ፡ ​ነገ​ር፡
                                            ​ትም​ህር​ተ፡ ​ዘተ​መሀ​ርከ ፨
                                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            
                                            ​ወና​ሁ፡ ​አነ፡ ​እፌ​ኑ፡ ​ተስ​ፋሁ፡ ​ለአ​ቡየ፡ ​ላዕ​ሌክ​ሙ። ​ወአ​ንት​ሙሰ፡ ​ንበ​ሩ፡ ​ሀገ​ረ፡ ​ኢየ​ሩሳ​ሌም፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ትለ​ብሱ፡ ​ኃይ​ለ፡ ​እም​ኣር​ያም ፨ 
                                            ​ወኣ​ውፅ​ኦሙ፡ ​ኣፍ​ኣ፡
                                            ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ቢቲ​ንያ ፨  ​ወአ​ንሥ​አ፡ ​እዴ​ሁ፡ ​ወኣ​ንበ  (b)  ​ረ፡ ​ወባ​ረኮሙ ፨ 
                                            ​ወእ​ንዘ፡ ​ይባ​ርኮ​ሙ፡ ​ተራ​ሐቆ​ሙ፡ ​ወዐ​ርገ፡ ​ሰማ​የ። ​ወእ​ሙን​ቱሰ፡ ​ሰገ​ዱ፡ ​ሎቱ፡
                                            ​ወተ​ሰው​ጡ፡ ​ኢየ​ሩሳ​ሌም፡ ​በዐ​ቢይ፡ ​ፍሥ​ሓ፡ ​ወነ​በሩ፡ ​ቤተ፡ ​መቅ​ደስ፡ ​ዘል​ፈ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ይሴ​ብሕ​ዎ፡ ​ወይ​ባር​ክዎ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​ለዓ​ለም፡ ​ወለ​ዓለ​መ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡
                                            ​ኣሜን ፨
                                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e105319LIT1693John">
               <fo:inline>I-4) Fols 100vb–123vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Gospel of John (Collection), incomplete, CAe 1693.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e105325LIT1693John#TituliJohn">
               <fo:inline>I-4-1) Fol. 100vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Gospel of John (Collection): Tituli of the Gospel of John</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The <fo:inline font-style="italic">tituli</fo:inline> are numbered from 1 to 19.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ፩  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ከብ​ካብ፡ ​ዘቃ​ነ።
                                             ፪  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዘሰ​ደደ፡ ​እም​ኵራ​ብ።
                                             ፫  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ኒቆ​ዲሞ​ስ።
                                             ፬  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​አጥ​ህሮ።
                                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ​፲፮  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​እለ፡ ​መጽ​ኡ፡ ​አረ​ሚይ።
                                             ​፲፯  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዘከ​መ፡ ​ኃፀ​በ፡ ​እግ​ረ፡ ​አር​ዳኢ​ሁ።
                                             ​፲፰  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ጰራ​ቅሊ​ጦስ።
                                             ​፲፱  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ስእ​ለተ፡ ​ሥጋ​ሁ፡ ​ለእ ​ግዚ ​እነ።
                                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e105388LIT2715John">
               <fo:inline>I-4-2) Fols 101ra–123vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Gospel of John, incomplete, CAe 2715.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The text terminates abruptly at John 16:18.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ​ወን​ጌል፡ ​ዘዮ​ሐን​ስ፡
                                        </fo:inline>
                  <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            ​ቀዳ​ሚሁ፡ ​ቃል፡ ​ውእ​ቱ። ​ወውእ ​ቱ፡ ​ቃል፡ ​ኃበ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ፡ ​ብሔ​ር፡  ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ወእ​ግዚ​አ፡ ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ውእ ​ቱ፡
                                            ​ቃል ፨ 
                                            ​ወከ​ማሁ፡ ​ቀዳ​ሚሁ፡ እ ​ምቀ​ዲሙ፡ ​ኃበ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ፡ ​ብሔ​ር፡  ​ውእቱ ፨ 
                                            ​ወኵ​ሉ፡ ​ቦቱ፡ ​ኮነ፡ ​ወዘእ ​ንበ​ሌሁ​ሰ፡
                                                ​አል​ቦ፡ ​ዘኮ​ነ፡ ​ወኢ​ምን ​ትኒ ፨  ​ወዘ​ሂ፡ ​ኮነ፡ ​በእ​ንቲ​ኣሁ፡ ​ቦቱ፡
                                             ​ሕይ​ወት፡ ​ውእ​ቱ። ​ወሕ​ይወ​ትሰ፡  ​ብር​ሃኑ፡ ​ለእ​ጓለ፡ ​እመ፡ ​ሕያ​ው፡
                                            ​ውእቱ ፨
                                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            
                                            ​ኵሎ፡ ​ዘቦ፡ ​አቡ​የ፡ ​ዚአ​የ፡ ​ውእቱ ፨  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዝን​ቱ፡ ​እቤ፡ ​ለክ​ሙ፡ ​እም​ዚአ​የ፡ ​ይነ​ሥእ፡ ​ወይ​ነግ​ረክሙ ፨ 
                                            ​ሕዳ​ጠ፡ ​ወኢ​ትሬ​እዩ​ኒ፡ ​ወካ​ዕበ፡ ​ሕዳ​ጠ፡ ​ወት​ሬእ​ዩኒ ፨ 
                                            ​ወቦ፡ ​እለ፡ ​ይቤ​ሉ፡ ​እም​ኣር​ዳኢ​ሁ፡ ​በበ​ይና​ቲሆ​ሙ፡ ​ምን​ተኑ፡ ​ዘይ​ብለ​ነ፡ ​ሕዳ​ጠ፡ ​ወኢ​ትሬ​እዩ​ኒ፡ ​ወካ​ዕበ፡ ​ሕዳ​ጠ፡ ​ወት​ሬእ​ዩኒ፡ ​ወአ​ሓወ​ር፡ ​ኃበ፡ ​ኣብ ፨ 
                                            ​ወይ​ቤሉ፡ ​ምን​ትኑ፡ ው
                                        </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Additional notes</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 4v: Supplication written in an untrained hand in deep vermilion in the upper margin.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                            Incipit:  :
                                                ​ተዘ​ከር​ነ፡ እ ​ግዚ ​ኦ፡ ​በሣ​ህል​ከ፡ ​ሕዝ​ብከ፡ ​ወተ​ሰሀ​ለነ፡ ​በአ​ድህ​ኖት​ከ፡
                                             ... 
                                        </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 64rb: 
                                            Ownership note written in an untrained hand in the right margin.
                                            The note, written in Amharic, mentions <fo:inline id="d1e106033PRS13183Tasamma">
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">ʾAlaqā</fo:inline> Tasammā</fo:inline>
                                            (possibly a later owner of the manuscript), <fo:inline id="d1e106038PRS13182WaldaSe">
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">ʾAbbā</fo:inline> Walda Śǝllāse</fo:inline>, and the church of <fo:inline id="d1e106043LOC7349DabraMi">Dabra Mikāʾel</fo:inline> (on which see Colophon 1).
                                        </fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">
                                            የ<fo:inline id="d1e106052LOC7349DabraMi">​ደብ​ረ፡ ​ሚካ​ኤል፡</fo:inline> ​ዛፍ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e106055PRS13183Tasamma">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​ያለ​ቃ፡</fo:inline> ​ተሠ​ማ፡</fo:inline> ​ነው፡ ​ዙካ​ው፡ <fo:inline id="d1e106060PRS13182WaldaSe">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​አባ፡</fo:inline> ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ሥላ​ሴ፡</fo:inline> ​ናቸ​ው፡
                                        </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Corrections include letters or words rewritten over erasure (e.g. fols 14rb, 22ra, 51ra), occasionally interlinear
                                            additions (e.g. 4va, 51va) and erasures marked with two thin lines (e.g. fol. 53rb).
                                            The line is sometimes taken down in correspondence of the <fo:inline font-style="italic">tituli</fo:inline>
                                            (e.g. 1rb, 35rb, 62rb, ; it is taken up on 62rb, 62va).
                                        </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>The numbers and titles of the gospel chapters are regularly written in red ink in the upper margin, in correspondence of the beginning of the chapters.
                                            They are sometimes written in the lower margin, e.g. on fols 24va, 29va, 64vb.
                                            Additional titles are written in the upper margin black ink, in the same hand as that of the main text, e.g. on 30v, 59v, 97r.
                                        </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Aids for identifying monthly readings are written in the upper margin, sometimes within a frame:
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘጥ​ር፡</fo:inline> (fol. 4r),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘጥ​ር፡ <fo:inline>ዘጌወርጊስ፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                        </fo:inline> in red ink (fol. 5r),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">Incipit:  ​ዘማ​ቴዎ​ስ፡ ​ምስ​ማክ፡ ​ዘመ​ጋቢ​ት፡ ​ወዘ​ሐም​ሌ፡ ... </fo:inline> (fol. 16v),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘሐ​ምሌ፡ ​ሚካ​ኤል፡ ​እስ​መ፡ ​ለም​ላእ​ክቲ​ሁ፡ ​ይኤ​ዝዞ​ሙ፡ ​በእ​ንቲ​አከ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ይሰ​ቀቡ​ከ፡ ​በኵ​ሉ፡ ​ፍና​ዊከ፡ ​ወበ​እደ​ዊሆ​ሙ፡ ​ያነ​ሥሆ​ሙ፡ ​ፈጸ​ሞ፡</fo:inline> in purple ink in the left margin (fol. 16va),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                           <fo:inline>ዘማዝያ፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                        </fo:inline> (fol. 46va),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘዮ​ሐን​ስ፡ ​ዘታ​ሕሣ​ሥ፡</fo:inline> (fol. 51va),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ምን​ባብ፡ <fo:inline>ዘጌወርጊስ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ዘነ​ሀሴ፡ ​ዘማ​ርቆ​ስ፡</fo:inline> in red ink in the right margin (fol. 54rb),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ወን​ጌል፡ ​ዘማ​ርቆ​ስ፡ ​ምን​ባብ፡ ​ዘመ​ስከ​ረም፡ ​ባህ፡ ​ስር​ቀ፡ <fo:inline>ዘጌወርጊስ፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                        </fo:inline> in red ink in the right margin (fol. 55rb),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘግ​ንቦ​ት፡ <fo:inline>ተፍስሁ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ጻድ​ቃን፡</fo:inline> (fol. 55va),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘኅ​ዳር፡ ​ሚካ​ኤል፡ ​ዓዲ፡ ​ዘይ​ረስ​ዮሙ፡ በ<fo:inline>[ዓ]</fo:inline>​ል፡</fo:inline> (fol. 79va),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                           <fo:inline>ዘጌወርጊስ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ዘሀ​ምሌ፡ ​ወን​ጌል፡ ​ዘሉ​ቃስ፡</fo:inline> crudely written in deep vermilion (fol. 82r),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">Incipit:  ​ወን​ጌል፡ ​ዘሉ​ቃስ፡ ​ዘየ​ካቲ​ት፡ ​ምስ​ማክ፡ ... </fo:inline> (fol. 85r),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">Incipit:  ​ዘመ​ሥከ​ረም፡ ​ምስ​ማክ፡ ​ግነ​ዩ፡ ​ለእ ​ግዚ ​ብሔ​ር፡ ... </fo:inline> (fol. 86rb),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">Incipit:  ​ዘግ​ንቦ​ት። ​ሕቀ፡ ​አህ​በጽ​ኮ፡ ​እመ​ላእ​ክቲ​ከ፡ ​ክብ​ረ፡ ... </fo:inline> (fol. 115r).

                                        </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Aids for identifying liturgical readings concerning the passion of Jesus are written in the upper margin in the main hand:
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ጊዜ፡ ፫ ​ሰዓ​ት፡ ​አኀ​ዝዎ፡ ​ለኢ​የሱ​ስ፡ ​ወወ​ሰድ​ዎ፡ ​ይስ​ቅል​ዎ፡</fo:inline> (fol. 32v),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ጊዜ፡ ፮ ​ሰዓ​ት፡ ​አል​በስ​ዎ፡ ​አል​ባሲ​ሁ፡ ​ወወ​ሰድ​ዎ፡ ​ይስ​ቅል​ዎ፡</fo:inline> (fol. 33r),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ጊዜ፡ ​ተስ​ዓቱ፡ ​ሰዓ​ት፡ ​ጸር​ኀ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​በቃ​ሉ፡ ​ወይ​ቤ፡ ​ኤሎ​ሂ፡ ​ኤሎ​ሂ፡</fo:inline> (fol. 33v),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ጊዜ፡ ፫ ​ሰዓ​ት፡ ​ቀሠ​ፎ፡ ​ጲላ​ጦስ፡ ​ለኢ​የሱ​ስ፡ ​ወወ​ሰድ​ዎ፡ ​ይስ​ቅል​ዎ፡</fo:inline> (fol. 59r),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ጊዜ፡ ፫ ​ሰዓ​ት፡ ​አሕ​የወ፡ ​ሎሙ፡ ​በር​ባን​ሃ፡ ወ  (fol. 98)  ​ወሀ​ቦሙ፡ ኢ<fo:inline>[የ]</fo:inline>​ሱስ​ሃ፡ ​ይስ​ቅል​ዎ፡</fo:inline> (fols 97v–98r),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ጊዜ፡ ፮ ​ሰዓ​ት፡ ​ሰቀ​ልዎ፡ ​ለኢ​የሱ​ስ፡ በ ​መካ​ን፡  ​ቀራ​ንዮ፡</fo:inline> (fol. 98r),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ጊዜ፡ ፱ ​ሰዓ​ት፡ ​ገዓ​ረ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​በቃ​ሉ፡ ​ወወ​ፅአ​ት፡ ​መን​ፈሱ፡ ​ሶቤ​ሃ።</fo:inline> (fol. 98v).
                                        </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>5)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Small writings crudely executed and sometimes poorly legible:
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                           <fo:inline>ክንክሣር፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                        </fo:inline> in blue pen (fol. 27vb),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">ወ<fo:inline>[ን]</fo:inline>​ጌል፡ ​ዘሉ​ቃስ፡</fo:inline> (fol. 27vb),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ጻድ​ቃን፡ ​ይወ​ርስ​ዎ፡ ​ለም​ድር፡</fo:inline> crudely written in deep vermilion in the lower margin (fol. 71r),
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">Incipit:  ​ወን​ጌል፡ ​ዘዮ​ሐን​ስ፡ ​ምስ​ማክ፡ ​ሠረ​ገላ​ቲሁ፡ ​ለእ ​ግዚ ​ብሔ​ር፡ ... </fo:inline> written in a recent hand in the upper margin (fols 119r).
                                            Other poorly legible small writings in blue or vermilion ink are found in the margins, e.g. on fols 46v, 52rb, 82r.
                                        </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>6)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>A white sticker is glued to the inner side of the front board, on the top. The name of <fo:inline id="d1e106286PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> is printed on it
                                            (‘<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቤን​ት፡ ​ዩው​ል፡ ​የን​ሰን።</fo:inline>’) and the signature ‘MS. Aeth. c. 14’ is written in pencil.
                                            An additional sticker, with the signature ‘Ms 46’ on it, is glued on the bottom of the same side.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block white-space-collapse="true">
                                            All quires have been reinforced with parchment guards at a later stage. The original quire structure cannot be reconstructed anymore (see also Condition below).
                                        </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm">
                                            Quire marks were written in the upper inner margin of the first folio and in the upper inner margin of the last folio of most of the original quires.
                                            The position of the signatures no longer coincides with the beginning and end of the current quires.
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">፩</fo:inline> is found in the upper inner margins of fol. 108v;
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">፪</fo:inline> is found in the upper inner margins of fols 69r, 76v, 109r, 115v;
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">፫</fo:inline> is found in the upper inner margins of fols 18r, 25v, 54r, 77r, 116r;
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">፬</fo:inline> is found in the upper inner margins of fols 26r, 68v;
                                            <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">፭</fo:inline> is found  in the upper inner margin of fols 93r, ;
                                            remains of illegible quire marks are found in the upper inner margin of fols 31v, 85r.
                                        </fo:block>
         <fo:block>18 quires. I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">2 (Fols 1r–2v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 3r–10v)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6 (Fols 11r–16v)</fo:inline> – IV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 17r–24v)</fo:inline> – V<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6 (Fols 25r–30v)</fo:inline> – VI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">5 (Fols 31r–35v)</fo:inline> – VII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6+2 (Fols 36r–44v)</fo:inline> – VIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6 (Fols 45r–50v)</fo:inline> – IX<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">3 (Fols 51r–53v)</fo:inline> – X<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8+1 (Fols 54r–62v)</fo:inline> – XI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">4 (Fols 63r–67v)</fo:inline> – XII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">9 (Fols 68r–76v)</fo:inline> – XIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 77r–84v)</fo:inline> – XIV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6+2 (Fols 85r–92v)</fo:inline> – XV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">9 (Fols 93r–101v)</fo:inline> – XVI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">7 (Fols 102r–108v)</fo:inline> – XVII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">5+1 (Fols 109r–114v)</fo:inline> – XVIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">9 (Fols 115r–123v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 1ra–123vb: 2
                                    columns (24 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 45r.There are 14–17 characters per line.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            316 × 267 mm (fol. 45r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 31 mm, bottom: 56 mm, right: 47 mm, left: 15 mm, intercolumn: 15 mm (fol. 45r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible. Both primary and ruling pricks are often visible. The upper and bottom lines are written above the ruling.
                                         Ruling pattern: 1A-1A-1A1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 1ra–123vb. Sixteenth century.. 
                                        Fine and trained hand. Characters are regularly spaced.
                                        The script displays some relatively archaic features: the numeral ፮ has a compressed shape and the open loop;
                                        the letter መ has the loops not completely separated; the letters ፅ and
                                        ዕ and numeral ፬ show “cone-forms”;
                                        the word ​እግ​ዚአ፡ ​ብሔ​ር፡ is sometimes written as two separate words.
                                        The graphemes ግ and ዚ are occasionally written with a ligature in the word ​እግ​ዚእ​ነ፡, e.g. on fols 35va, 100vb.
                                        One bottom ruled line has been left unwritten on fols 24va–25vb.
                                    <fo:block>Ink: Black, red or deep vermilion.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: 
                                        Several groups of lines on the incipit page of each Gospel, alternating with black lines;
                                        the stichometric note at the end of the Gospel of Matthew, on fol. 35ra; holy names;
                                        the captions <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ማር​ቆስ፡</fo:inline> on 35vb, <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ስዕ​ለ፡ ​ሉቃ​ስ፡</fo:inline> (partly illegible)
                                        on 61v, and <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዮሐ​ንስ፡</fo:inline> on 100va;
                                        the numbers of the chapters in the list of the <fo:inline font-style="italic">tituli</fo:inline> at the beginning of each Gospel;
                                        the numbers of the Eusebian Canons to which the Ammonian sections, penned in black ink in the left margins immediately above those numbers, belong;
                                        the numbers and titles of the chapters are written in the upper or lower margin, in correspondence of the beginning of the chapters;
                                        elements of the numerals and of the punctuation signs, including text dividers and caesura signs
                                        (the <fo:inline font-style="italic">crux ansata</fo:inline> is entirely rubricated on 65va; the <fo:inline font-style="italic">coronis</fo:inline> sign is
                                        entirely rubricated on 62vb, 63ra; the word <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቁም፡</fo:inline> is rubricated on e.g. 5rb, 56ra, 97ra.
                                    </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Decoration</fo:block>
         <fo:block margin-top="3mm" margin-bottom="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">The manuscript contains four unframed Evangelist portraits
                                    executed in the Italianate style characteristic of a period between <fo:inline>1480 and 1540</fo:inline>. The miniatures occupy the
                                    full height and the width of one column of text.
                                    <inline xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Format">Juel-Jensen 1996</inline>
                                    believed that these were painted by the Italian artist <fo:inline id="d1e105897 PRS2887Brancale">Nicolò Brancaleone</fo:inline>, but a closer analysis of their
                                    style and iconography (<inline xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Format">Gnisci 2019</inline>) does not support this attribution.
                                    Small ornamental bands with arabesque or interlace patterns mark the end of paragraphs throughout the manuscript.
                                    These fill the empty space left at the end of a paragraph or are placed between columns.
                                    They often cover punctuation marks or chapter divisions and it is difficult to establish when they were added.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Miniatures</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(280) Fol. 1v: <fo:inline> A standing
                                        Evangelist portrait of <fo:inline id="d1e105912PRS6902Matthew">Matthew</fo:inline> with a <fo:inline id="d1e105915">hand cross</fo:inline>
                                        in his right hand and a <fo:inline id="d1e105918">codex</fo:inline> in the other. <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሥዕ​ለ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e105923PRS6902Matthew">​ማቴ​ዎስ፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(281) Fol. 35v: <fo:inline> An
                                        Evangelist portrait of <fo:inline id="d1e105937PRS6751Mark">Mark</fo:inline> seated on a wicker chair under a canopy.
                                        He has a halo and is inscribing a <fo:inline id="d1e105940">codex</fo:inline>. <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e105944PRS6751Mark">​ማር​ቆስ፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(282) Fol. 61v: <fo:inline> A standing
                                        Evangelist portrait of <fo:inline id="d1e105958PRS6387Luke">Luke</fo:inline> with a <fo:inline id="d1e105961">hand cross</fo:inline>
                                        in his right hand and a <fo:inline id="d1e105964">codex</fo:inline> in the other. He wears an unusual tiara. <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሥዕ​ለ፡  <fo:inline id="d1e105969PRS6387Luke">​ሉቃ​ስ።</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(283) Fol. 100v: <fo:inline> A standing
                                        Evangelist portrait of <fo:inline id="d1e105983PRS5695John">John</fo:inline> with a <fo:inline id="d1e105985">hand cross</fo:inline>
                                        in his right hand and a <fo:inline id="d1e105988">codex</fo:inline> in the other.
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e105992PRS5695John">​ዮሐ​ንስ</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Headpieces</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(25) Fols 2r, 36r, 62r, 101r: <fo:inline>Polychrome ornamental bands with arabesque decorations mark the beginning of each gospel.</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Drawings</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Other</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Holes resulting from parchment making are found on e.g. fols 1, 40, 85. Tears on several folios have
                                            been repaired both at the moment of parchment production, e.g. on 106, 118,
                                            and at a later stage, e.g. fol. 2.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is deficient.
                                        The bookblock has been damaged by humidity, especially in the outer margins, and water stains are present (e.g. on fols 37, 104v).
                                        Large tears are present in most of the leaves.
                                        Wax stains are visible on 31v, 72v. The parchment is stained and crumpled on fol. 74.
                                        The bookblock has been resewn together and parchment guards have been placed around all quires.
                                        fols 51r–62v have been stitched together at a later stage.
                                      </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>sixteenth century</fo:inline>
                                Unit 1 can be dated palaeographically to the sixteenth
                                century.
                            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm">Unit 2</fo:block>
         <fo:block>Parchment, 7 fols (fols 124–130), 1 quires, mid-seventeenth–eighteenth century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e106320LIT1693John">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 124ra–130va: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Gospel of John (Collection), incomplete, CAe 1693.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e106326LIT2715John">
               <fo:inline>I-1) Fols 124ra–130va: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Gospel of John, incomplete, CAe 2715.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The text begins abruptly from John 16:20. The stichometric note at the end is missing.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        
                                        ​አማ​ን፡ ​አማ​ን፡ ​እብ​ለክ​ሙ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ትበ​ክዩ፡ ​ወት​ላህ​ዉ፡ ​አን​ትሙ፡ ​ወዓ​ለም​ሰ፡ ​ይት​ፈሣ​ሕ፡ ​ወአ​ንት​ሙሰ፡ ​ተኃ​ዝኑ ፨ 
                                        ​አላ፡ ​ኃዘ​ንክ​ሙ፡ ​ፍሥ​ሐ፡ ​ይከ​ውነ​ክሙ፡
                                        ​ለክ​ሙ። ​በከ​መ፡ ​ብእ​ሲት፡ ​ትቴ​ክዝ፡ ​ሶበ፡ ​አል​ፀቀ​ት፡ ​ትለ​ድ፡ ​እስ​መ፡ ​በጽ​ሐ፡ ​ጊዜሃ ፨ 
                                        ​ወእ​ምከ​መ፡ ​ወለ​ደት፡ ​እጓ​ለ፡ ​ኢት​ዜከ​ሮ፡ ​እን​ከ፡ ​ለሕ​ማማ፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡
                                        ​ፍሥ​ሓሐ፡ ​እስ​መ፡ ​ወለ​ደት፡ ​ብእ​ሴ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​ወአ​ንት​ሙነ፡ ​ትቴ​ክዙ፡ ​ይእ​ዜ።
                                    </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        
                                        ​ወእ​ግዚ​እ፡  ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡  ​ይቤ፡ ​ኢይ​መው​ት፡ ​አላ፡ ​ይቤ​ሎ፡ ​እመ​ኬ፡ ​ፈቀ​ድኩ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ዝን​ቱ፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ሶበ፡ ​እመ​ጽእ፡ ​ሚላ​ዕሌ​ከ፡ ​ወዝ​ንቱ፡
                                        ​ረድ​እ፡ ​ዘኮ​ነ፡ ​ሰማ​ዕተ፡ ​በእ​ንተ​ዝ፡ ​ወጻ​ሐፎ፡ ​ወን​ሕነ፡ ​ነአ​ምር፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ጽድ​ቁ፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ስም​ዑ። ​ወዘ​ንተ፡ ​ገብ​ረ፡ ​እግ​ዚእ፡  ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ 
                                        ​በቅ​ድመ፡ ​አር​ዳኢ​ሁ፡ ​ወባ​ዕደ​ኒ፡ ​ግብ​ራተ፡ ​ብዙኃ ፨ 
                                        ​ወሶ​በ፡ ​ተጽ​ሕፈ፡   (fol. 130va)   ​ኵሉ፡ ​በበ ፩  ​እም​ኢያ​ግመ​ሮ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​ጥቀ፡ ​መጻ​ሕፍ​ቲሁ፡
                                        ​ዘተ​ጽሕ​ፈ፡ ​አሜ​ን፡ ​ወአ​ሜን ፨
                                    </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e106373LIT1693John#Postscript">
               <fo:inline>I-2) Fol. 130va: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Gospel of John (Collection): Colophon of the Gospel of John</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The note includes information on the circumstances of the writing of the Gospel of John, namely the dating and the place of completion.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        ​መል​ዓ፡ <fo:inline>ጽሕፈቱ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​ብስራ ቱ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ለዮ​ሐን​ስ፡ ​ሐዋ​ርያ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ዘ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ዎስ፡
                                         ፩  ​እም ፲ ወ ፪  ​ሰባ​ክያ​ን፡ ​እን​ተ፡ ​ጸሐ​ፎ፡ ​በዮ​ናኒ፡ ​ለሰ​ብአ፡ ​ሀገ​ረ፡ ​ኤፌ​ሶን ፨ 
                                        ​እም​ድኅ​ረ፡ ​ዕር​ገቱ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​እነ፡  ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡  ​በሥ​ጋ፡
                                        ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ሰማ​ይ፡ በ ፴  ​ዓመ​ት፡ በ ፰  ​ዓመ​ተ፡ ​መን​ግሥ​ቱ፡ ​ለጢ​ባር​ዮስ፡ ​ቄሣ​ር፡ ​ወስ​ብሐ​ት፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜን ፨
                                    </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Colophon</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block font-family="Ludolfus">Fol. 130va: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">The colophon is undated. It states that the manuscript belongs to <fo:inline id="d1e106443LOC7349DabraMi">Dabra Mikāʾel</fo:inline>
                                        of the city of <fo:inline id="d1e106446LOC6450Zatta">Zāttā</fo:inline> in <fo:inline id="d1e106449LOC6573NorthWallo">Northern Wallo</fo:inline>.
                                        It also states that the scribe was <fo:inline id="d1e106452PRS13184WaldaHe">Walda Ḥǝḍān</fo:inline> and the patron was
                                        <fo:inline id="d1e106455PRS13185WaldaMi">Walda Mikāʾel</fo:inline>.
                                    </fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                        <fo:block font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዝመ​ጽሐ​ፍ፡ ​ዘቅ​ዱስ፡  ​ሚካ​ኤል፡  ​ዘሀ​ገረ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e106429LOC6450Zatta">​ዛታ፡</fo:inline> ​ተጽ​ሐፈ፡ ​በሢ​መተ፡ ​አካ​ሉ፡ ​ጸሐ​ፊሁ፡
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e106432PRS13184WaldaHe">​ወል​ደ፡ ​ሕፃ​ን፡</fo:inline> ​ወአ​ጽሐ​ፊሁ፡
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e106436PRS13185WaldaMi">​ወል​ደ፡   ​ሚካ​ኤል።</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Corrections are very rare and limited to erasures (fols 130va) or words rewritten over erasure (125va).
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Aids for identifying readings concerning the passion of Jesus are written in the upper margin in deep vermilion ink:
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘአ​ግብ​አ፡  <fo:inline>ተግብር፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                        </fo:inline> (fol. 124va),
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘነ​ግህ፡ ​ወወ​ሰድ​ዎ፡</fo:inline> (fol. 125rb),
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘ፫ ​ሰዓ​ት፡</fo:inline> (fol. 126vb),
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘቀ​ትር፡</fo:inline> (fol. 127rb),
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘሰ​ዓት፡</fo:inline> (fol. 127vb),
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘሰ​ርክ፡</fo:inline> (fol. 128ra),
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዘእ​ሁድ፡ ​ሰን​በት፡</fo:inline> (fol. 128rb).
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block>1 quire. XIX<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6+1 (Fols 124r–130v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 124ra–130va: 2
                                    columns (27 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 124r. There are 12–13 characters per line.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            225 × 206 mm (fol. 124r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 29 mm, bottom: 64 mm, right: 29 mm, left: 13 mm, intercolumn: 16 mm (fol. 124r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible. Both primary and ruling pricks are visible. The upper and bottom lines are written above the ruling. Ruling pattern: 1A-1A-1A1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 2:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 124ra–130va. Mid-seventeenth–eighteenth century. (scribe: Walda Ḥǝḍān) . 
                                    Fine and trained hand, gʷǝlḥ-script. Characters are regularly spaced.
                                    Walda Ḥǝḍān is indicated as the scribe in Colophon 1 (fol. 130va).
                                <fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: 
                                    Incipits of few chapters and of the postscript; holy names; the word <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቁም፡</fo:inline>, written in a later
                                    hand on fol. 127vb; elements of the numerals and of the punctuation signs, including text dividers.
                                </fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Abbreviations: <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="6mm"
                                             provisional-label-separation="6mm"
                                             start-indent="cm">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>1)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                          <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ምዕ፡</fo:inline> for
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ምዕ​ራፍ፡</fo:inline> (e.g. on fols 128ra, 128va).
                                    </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is good.
                                    The unit consists of one quire subsequently sewn to the textblock of the first unit. The unit is in good state of preservation.
                                    Some letters are illegible on fol. 124r due to faded ink. The verso of the last folio displays traces of intensive use and erasures.
                                </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>mid-seventeenth–eighteenth century</fo:inline>
                                Unit 2 can be dated palaeographically to the period between the
                                mid-seventeenth and the eighteenth century.
                            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
