      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethg41"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. g. 41 (R)</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Juel-Jensen 49)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment scroll1648×66–77 mm, 865×66–76 mm, 805×68–77 mm (weight: 28g),  fols, 1779–1800.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e110387LIT5920JohnBeg">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 1r1–1r23: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Beginning of the Gospel of John, CAe 5920.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ወን​ጌል፡ ​ዘዮ​ሐን​ስ፡ ​ቀዳ​ሚሁ፡ ​ቃል፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ቃል፡  ​ወው​እቱ፡ ​ቃል፡ ​ኀበ፡
                            ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ወእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ቃል፡ ​ወከ​ማሁ፡ ​ቀዳ​ሚሁ፡ ​እም​ቀዲ​ሙ፡ ​ኀበ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ወብ​ርሃ​ኑሰ፡ ​ዘው​ስተ፡ ​ጽል​መት፡ ​ያበ​ርህ፡ ​ወያ​ርኢ፡ ​ወጽ​ልመ​ትኒ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                ​ኢይ​ረክ​ቦ፡ ​ወኢ​ይቅ​ርቦ፡ ​ወከ​ማሁ፡ ​ኢይ​ርከ​ብዎ፡
                            ​ወኢ​ይቅ​ረብ ዎ ፡ ​ባር​ያ፡ ​ወለ​ጌዎ​ን፡ ​ወባ​ርያ፡ ​ጸሊ​ማን፡ ​ወባ​ርያ፡ ​ቀይ​ሐን፡ ​ወባ​ርያ፡ ​ጥቁ​ር፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ኢይ​ቅረ​ቡ፡ ​ኀበ፡
                            ​ነፍ<fo:inline> (!)</fo:inline>፡
                                ​ወሥጋ<fo:inline> (!)</fo:inline>፡ ለ ​ገብ​ርከ፡
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e110414PRS13856Elyas">​ኤል​ያስ፡</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e110417PRS13857Baselyos">​ባስ<fo:inline>[ል]</fo:inline>​ዮስ፡</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e110423PRS13858MaryamS">​ማር​ያም፡ ​ስና፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e110431LIT6756PPQwerdat">
               <fo:inline>II) Fols 1r24–1r43: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Prayer against the pain of the stomachache and rheumatism’ (​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ሕማ​መ፡ ​ቍር​ፀት፡ ​ወቅ​ርጥ​ማት፡), CAe 6756.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The entire text is reproduced below.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ሕማ​መ፡ ​ቍር​ፀት፡ ​ወቅ​ርጥ​ማት፡  ​ዝራ​ድም፡ ​ምኩ​ር፡ ​ኤዳ​ሴ፡ ​ፍላ​ኤል፡
                            ​ግጣ​ግላ​ኤል፡ ​ኑዱ​ኤል፡ ​ሱኑ​ኤል፡ ​እም​ላብ​ኤል፡ ​እሉ፡ ​እሙ​ንቱ፡ ​አስ​ማት፡ ​ማእ​ሰሮ​ሙ፡ ​ለአ​ጋን​ንት፡ ​ወለ​ትግ​ርት​ያ፡ ​ለዓ​ይነ​ት፡ ​ወለ​ባር​ያ፡ ​ለቍ​ርፀ​ት፡ ​ወለ​ቅር​ጥማ​ት፡
                            ​ለም​ኙ፡ ​ወለ​ጕሰ​መት፡ ​ለፌ​ራ፡ ​ወለ​ነዳ​ድ፡ ​ለማ​ሪ፡ ​ወለ​ማሪ​ት፡ ​ለዘ​ሪ፡ ​ወለ​ዘሪ​ት፡ ​ለዶ​ቢ፡ ​ወለ​ዶቢ​ት፡ ​ለጋ​ፍ፡ ​ወለ​ጋፋ​ት፡ ​ወእ​ምድ​ንጋ​ፄ፡ ​ዘሌ​ሊት፡ ​ወዘ​መዓ​ልት፡ ​ድድ​ቅ፡
                            ​ወጋ​ኔነ፡ ​ቀት​ር፡ ​ወዘ​ኵሎ​ሙ፡ ​መና​ፍስ​ተ፡ ​ርኩ​ሳን፡ ​አድኅ<fo:inline> (!)</fo:inline>፡
                                ለ ​ገብ​ርከ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e110448PRS13856Elyas">​ኤል​ያስ፡</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e110451PRS13857Baselyos">​ባስ<fo:inline>[ል]</fo:inline>​ዮስ፡</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e110458PRS13858MaryamS">​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e110461PRS13859Nesebbeyo">​ንጽ​በዮ፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e110469LIT4007Salotb">
               <fo:inline>III) Fols 1r44–1r80: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Prayer for undoing charms’ (​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​መፍ​ትሔ፡ ​ሥራ​ይ፡), CAe 4007.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The beginning and further elements of the prayer are close to the one attested in MS London,
                            British Library, Or. 566 (fols 1r–5v).</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​በስመ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡
                                ፩ ​አም​ላክ፡ ​ጸሎ​ት፡  ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ፍት​ሐተ፡ ​ሥራ​ይ፡
                            ​ዘተ​ቀድ​ሐ፡ ​እም​፹ወ፩ ​መጻ​ሕፍ​ት፡ ​በዝ​ንቱ፡ ​ጠል​ሠም፡ ​ተፈ​ትሁ፡ ​መሠ​ርያ​ን፡ ​ብዙ​ኃን፡ ​ወነ​ባብ​ያነ፡ ​ሐሰ​ት፡ ​እለ፡ ​ይገ​ብሩ፡ ​ዕፀ፡ ​ሥራ​ይ፡ ​ወአ​ስማ​ተ፡ ​ዕፀ፡ ​ሰቢ​ሮሙ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ፍታ​ሕ፡ ​ተፈ​ታሕ፡ ​ዘተ​ገብረ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ቅድ​መ፡ ​ወድ​ኅረ፡ ​ዘገ​ብረ፡ ​ፍታ​ሕ፡
                                ​በስ​መ፡ ​ቀን​ተው፡ ​ሰን​ተው፡ ​ቀር​ነለ​ው፡ ​በከ​መ፡ ​አጊ​ገዎ​ኮሙ፡
                            ​ለአ​ዳም፡ ​ወለ​ሄዋ​ን፡ ​ወከ​ማሁ፡ ​አን​ግሣ፡ ​ለዛ​ቲ፡ ​መጽ​ሐፍ፡ ​እም​ላዕ​ለ፡ ​ነፍ<fo:inline> (!)</fo:inline>፡ ​ወሥ​ጋሁ፡ ​ለገ​ብር​ከ፡
                                <fo:inline id="d1e110500PRS13856Elyas">
                        <fo:inline>ኤል፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                     </fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e110503PRS13857Baselyos">​ባስ​ልዮ​ስ፡</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e110507PRS13859Nesebbeyo">​ንጽ​ብዮ፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e110515LIT6757PPUndoing">
               <fo:inline>IV) Fols 1r81–1r122: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Prayer of the names of the charms’ (​ጸሎ​ተ፡ ​አስ​ማተ፡ ​ሥራ​ይ፡), CAe 6757.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ጸሎ​ተ፡ ​አስ​ማተ፡ ​ሥራ​ይ፡ ​ጅር፡ ​ጅር፡ ​ጅር፡ ​አቅ​ዦር፡  ​ፍታ​ሕ፡ ​ሥራ​የ፡ ​ግብ​ጽ፡ ​ወአ​ረብ፡
                                ​ወኢ​ትዮ​ጵያ፡
                                ​ወአ​ንጾ​ኪያ፡ ​ወሶ​ርያ፡ ​ወሮ​ምያ፡ ​ወቢ​ታን​ያ፡ ​ፍታ​ሕ፡ ​ሥራየ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​በቅ​ላ፡ ​ወሐ​ማሴ​ን፡ ​ሶሬ፡ ​ወሰ​ራዌ፡ ​ጋላ፡
                                ​ወሸ​ንቅ​ላ፡ ​በለ​ው፡ ​ወአ​ገው፡ ​ወል​ቃይ​ት፡ ​ወጸ​ገዴ፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ይግ​ባእ፡ ​ሥራ​ዮሙ፡ ​ኅድ​ግ፡ ​ይቤ​ሉከ፡ ​በቃ​ለ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ፍታ​ሕ፡ ​በን​ጉሥ​ነ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e110529PRS9142TaklaGi">​ተክ​ለ፡ ​ጊዮ​ርጊ​ስ፡</fo:inline>
                                ​በጳ​ጳስ​ነ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e110532PRS10450YosabI">​አባ፡ ​ኢዮ​ሳብ፡</fo:inline> ​ፍታ​ሕ፡ ​በአ​ፈ፡ ​ጴጥ​ሮስ፡ ​ወጳ​ውሎ​ስ፡ ​በታ​ቦተ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ዮሐ​ንስ፡ ​ሰማ​ዕት፡
                                ​ፍታ​ሕ፡
                                ​ዘን​ተ፡ ​ሥራ​ዩ፡ ​ወአ​ስማ​ቱ፡ ​ለገ​ብር​ከ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e110535PRS13856Elyas">​ኤል​ያስ፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e110545LIT6758PPSupplications">
               <fo:inline>V) Fols 1r123–1r136: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Prayer of the names of the charms’ (​ጸሎ​ተ፡ ​አስ​ማተ፡ ​ሥራ​ይ፡), CAe 6758.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The entire text is reproduced below.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ጸሎ​ተ፡ ​አስ​ማተ፡ ​ሥራ​ይ፡ ​ድኅ​ድጋ​ሰኒ፡ ​አግ​ማኒ፡ ​አግ​ማኒ፡ ​አቅ​ማኒ፡ ​አግ​ማጅ​ን፡ ​አቅ​ማጅ​ን፡ ​ፍታ​ሕ፡ ​በቃ​ለ፡ ​አ፫​፻፲፰ ​ርቱ​አነ፡ ​ሃይ​ማኖ​ት፡
                                ​በ፲​ወ፭ ​ነቢ​ያት፡ ​በ፲፪ ​ሐዋ​ርያ​ት፡ ​በ፸፪ ​አር​ድእ​ት፡ ​ፍታሕ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​በ፺፱ ​ነገ​ደ፡ ​መላ​እክ​ት፡ ​ወ፬ <fo:inline>እስሳ፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                                ​ወበ​፳ወ፬ ​ካህ​ናተ፡ ​ሰማ​ይ፡ ​ፍታ​ሕ፡ ​በአ​ፈ፡ ​ኵሎ​ሙ፡ ​ቅዱ​ሳን፡
                                ​ወሰ​ማዕ​ት፡ ​አድ​ኅኖ፡ ​ለገ​ብር​ከ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e110558PRS13856Elyas">​ኤል​ያስ፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e110567LIT6759PPGod">
               <fo:inline>VI) Fols 1r137–1r184: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Protective prayer to God containing supplications, CAe 6759.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​አን​ተ፡ ​በሰ​ማይ፡ ​ወአ​ንተ፡ ​በም​ድር፡ ​ሕራ​ስ፡ ​ንዋም ፡ ​ዘኢ​ይመ​ጽአ​ከ፡ ​ወአ​ንተ፡ ​ንጉ​ሠ፡ ​ሰማ​ይ፡
                            ​ወአ​ንተ፡ ​ንጉ​ሠ፡ ​ምድ​ር፡ ​ወአ​ንተ፡ ​ዘሀ​ሎ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ሕሊ​ና፡ ​ወዘ​ሀሎ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ልብ፡ ​ወዘ​ሀሎ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​እድ፡ ​ወዘ​ሀሎ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​በሐ​ውር​ተ፡ ​መለ​ኮቱ፡
                            ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ፍታ​ሕ፡ ​ሥራ​ዩ፡ ​መሠ​ርያ​ን፡ ​ይግ​ባእ፡ ​ዲበ፡ ​ርእ​ሶሙ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ኢይ​ቅረ​ቡ፡ ​ኵሎ​ሙ፡ ​መና​ፍስ​ተ፡ ​ርኩ​ሳን፡ ​አር​ኅቅ፡ ​ወአ​ሰስ​ል፡
                                ​እም​ላዕ​ለ፡ ​ነፍ​ሱ፡
                                ​ወሥ​ጋሁ፡ ​ለገ​ብር​ከ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e110578PRS13856Elyas">​ኤል​ያስ፡</fo:inline>
                                ​ወለ​ዓመ​ትከ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e110582PRS13858MaryamS">​ማር​ያም፡  ​ስና፡</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e110587PRS13857Baselyos">​ባስ​ልዮ​ስ፡</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e110590PRS13856Elyas">​ኤል​ያስ፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e110599LIT4506Salam">
               <fo:inline>VII) Fols 1r185–1r196: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Malkǝʾ-hymn to Mary, CAe 4506.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The entire text is reproduced below.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሰላ​ም፡  ​ለገ​ጽኪ፡ ​ዘጥ​ቀ፡ ​ይል​ይ፡ ​እም​ሥነ፡ ​ከዋ​ክብ​ት፡ ​ወወ​ርኅ፡ ​ወእ​ምሥ​ነ፡ ​ፀሐ​ይ፡ ​መብ​ርሂ፡
                                 ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ድን​ግል፡ ​ፍና​ዋት​የ፡ ​ሠር​ሂ፡ ​በመ​ዓል​ት፡ ​ወበ​ሌሊ​ት፡ ​ኢይ​ርከ​በኒ፡ ​ጸና​ሂ፡ ​መሥ​ገር​ተ፡ ​አበ​ሳ፡ ​ዘይ​ጽፍ​ር፡
                                ​ወግ​በ፡ ​ዘይ​ድኂ፡ ​አድ​ኅኖ፡ ​ለገ​ብር​ከ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e110615PRS13856Elyas">​ኤል​ያስ፡</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e110619PRS13858MaryamS">​ማር​ያም፡  ​ስና፡</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e110624PRS13857Baselyos">​ባስ​ልዮ​ስ፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e110633LIT6761PPUndoing">
               <fo:inline>VIII) Fols 1r196–1r224: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Protective prayer for the undoing of charms, CAe 6761.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ፍታ​ሕ፡ ​ሥራ​የ፡ ​ሴዋ፡  ​ወአ​ምሐ​ራ፡ ​በጌ፡
                                ​ምድር<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ወዳ​ሞት፡ ​ወላ​ስታ፡ ​ወጐ​ንደ​ር፡ ​ሥራ​የ፡ ​ወሰ​ራዌ፡
                            ​ወሥ​ራየ፡ ​ደጕ​ዓ፡ ​ወበ​ለው፡ ​ወአ​ገው፡ ​ፍታ​ሕ፡ ​ሥራ​ዮሙ፡ ​ወአ​ስማ​ቶሙ፡ ​እመ​ሂ፡ ​በው​ሉዱ፡ ​ወበ​ንብ​ርታ፡ ​ዘገ​ብሩ፡ ​ዘገ​ዘቱ፡ ​ወዘ​ደገ​ሙ፡ ​ወዘ​አስ​ተኃ​ደሩ፡ ​መሠ​ርያ​ን፡</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​አድ​ኅኖ፡ ​እም​ፀር፡ ​ሳዶ​ር፡ ​አላ​ዶር፡ ​ዳና​ት፡ ​አዴ​ራ፡ ​ሮዳ​ስ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​ሊቀ፡ ​ካህ​ናት፡ ​ዘላ​ዕለ፡ ​ኵሉ፡ ​አዴ​ራ፡ ​ይጸ​ሐፍ፡
                            ​በመ​ሰን​የ፡ ​በው​ዳሴ​ከ፡ ​ፊደ​ሉ፡ ​ዳና​ት፡ ​ይት​ኃደ​ግ፡ ​ዲበ፡ ​ምድ​ር፡ ​ንባ​ቡ፡ ​ወቃ​ሉ፡ ​በዝ​ንቱ፡ ​በቃ​ልከ፡ ​አድ​ኅኖ፡ ​ለገ​ብር​ከ፡ <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>The verso is empty.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>The manuscript contains no scribal corrections other than the adaptation of the supplications
                                        to the gender of the owner.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Spaces for the name of the owner(s) had been left empty by the scribe and were
                                       filled subsequently, possibly also by the main hand. In the upper
                                   part of the scroll, the words introducing the supplications (<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ነፍሳ</fo:inline>,
                                       <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሥጋሃ</fo:inline>, <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​አድ​ኅና</fo:inline>)
                                       are used with their feminine form, which was
                                   then corrected to the masculine form.
                                   The names of the owners, mentioned in supplications throughout, were
                                       <fo:inline id="d1e110937PRS13856Elyas">ʾElyās</fo:inline>, <fo:inline id="d1e110939PRS13857Baselyos">Bāsǝlyos</fo:inline>, <fo:inline id="d1e110942PRS13858MaryamS">Māryām Sǝnā</fo:inline>,
                                       and <fo:inline id="d1e110944PRS13859Nesebbeyo">Nǝṣǝbbǝyo</fo:inline>.
                                   </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Order of textual units and miniatures: Miniature 1, Textual units I–IV
                                        (beginning),
                                        Miniature 2, Textual units IV (end)–V, Miniature 3, Textual
                                        unit VI, Miniature 4, Textual units VII–VIII.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>The two strips are slightly overlapping and are
                                    sewn together with a running stitch using two narrow parchment strips.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>1
                                    column (107 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Number of characters per line: 14–15.The left margin is delimited by a black line.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            485 × 64–70 mm ()</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            right: 1–3 mm, left: 1–3 mm, top: 1–2 mm, bottom: 1–2 mm ().
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>1
                                    column (43 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Number of characters per line: 14–15.The left margin is delimited by a black line.The six last written lines extent into the painted area d3.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            209 × 60–68 mm ()</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            right: 1–3 mm, left: 1–3 mm, top: 1–2 mm, bottom: 1–2 mm ().
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>1
                                    column (48 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Number of characters per line: 13–16.The left margin is delimited by a black line.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            281 × 72 mm ()</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            right: 1–3 mm, left: 1–3 mm, top: 1–2 mm, bottom: 1–2 mm ().
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>1
                                    column (40 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Number of characters per line: 13 –14.The left margin is delimited by a black line.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            260 × 70 mm ()</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            right: 1–3 mm, left: 1–3 mm, top: 1–2 mm, bottom: 1–2 mm ().
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Pricking and ruling are not visible. Pricking and ruling are not visible. Pricking and ruling are not visible. Pricking and ruling are not visible.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->1779–1800. Relatively regular hand. The script is bulky, characters are broadly spaced.
                                    The word separator is often placed at the beginning of the next line.<fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: Incipits of texts and sections; holy names; occasionally the name of the owners.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Decoration</fo:block>
         <fo:block margin-top="3mm" margin-bottom="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">
                                The scroll features four illustrated panels decorated with earthy shades of ochre, brown, 
                                and red. The images appear to be coeval with the text. 
                            </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Miniatures</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(287) <fo:inline>A cross element decorated with a black and brown harlequin
                                 pattern and with a face at its centre.</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(288) <fo:inline>A highly stylized pair of figures, one much larger than the
                                    other; the visually unusual pair (the larger figure has long blade like fingers and a cross emerging from its head; the smaller had a body made out of circles)
                                    could represent the Virgin and Child seated on a chequered throne, since the Virgin is 
                                    mentioned in one of the scroll’s hymns.</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(289) <fo:inline>A cross element with foliated arms similar to the one at the top; the eight curlicue
                                    elements that sprout from its arms feature eyes at their centre.</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(290) <fo:inline>An empty Golgotha-type cross. The name of the donor, <fo:inline id="d1e110897PRS13856Elyas">ʾElyās</fo:inline>, is inscribed next to these latter 
                                    two motifs.</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Headpieces</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Drawings</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Other</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is good.Small areas of loss are present in the upper part of the scroll. The lower part has been crumpled by rolling,
                                the last line is not legible anymore.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>1779–1800</fo:inline>
               <fo:inline id="d1e110972PRS9142TaklaGi">Takla Giyorgis I</fo:inline> and <fo:inline id="d1e110974PRS10450YosabI">Yosāb II</fo:inline>, who were
                            active simultaneously in 1779–1800 (with interruptions),
                            are mentioned in Textual unit IV.
                            Supplications are introduced by feminine grammatical forms, which indicates that the manuscript might have been
                           intended for a female owner. However, the names added inside the space left empty for supplications,
                           possibly by the main hand, were those of <fo:inline id="d1e110979PRS13856Elyas">ʾElyās</fo:inline>,
                            <fo:inline id="d1e110982PRS13857Baselyos">Bāsǝlyos</fo:inline>,
                            <fo:inline id="d1e110984PRS13858MaryamS">Māryām Sǝnā</fo:inline>,
                            and <fo:inline id="d1e110986PRS13859Nesebbeyo">Nǝṣǝbbǝyo</fo:inline> (see Varia note 3).
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>One of the names mentioned in the supplications, <fo:inline id="d1e110994PRS13859Nesebbeyo">Nǝṣǝbbǝyo</fo:inline>,
                        points to a Tigrinya-speaking area as place of production.</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e110999PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethg41">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethg41</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
