      </fo:static-content>
      <fo:static-content flow-name="xsl-footnote-separator">
         <fo:block space-before="5mm" space-after="5mm">
            <fo:leader leader-length="30%" rule-thickness="0pt"/>
         </fo:block>
      </fo:static-content>
      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethd22"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. d. 22</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Juel-Jensen 51)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Paper leaf178×220 mm (weight: 2g), 1 fols, 1855–1868.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true" font-family="Ludolfus" space-after="3mm" id="">
               <fo:inline>I) Fol. 1r: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">
                     <fo:inline id="d1e113495" font-family="Ludolfus">Letter from King Tewodros II to military officials</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">After a greeting to <fo:inline id="d1e113502PRS13884Bisawwer">Bisawwǝr</fo:inline> and other
                                military leaders identified by their titles, King <fo:inline id="d1e113504PRS9430Tewodros">Tewodros II</fo:inline> informs 
                                the recipients of the arrival of a cannon in <!--or from?--> <fo:inline id="d1e113508LOC2449Dalant">Dalāntā</fo:inline>. It might be related to the events leading up to the siege of
                                <fo:inline id="d1e113510LOC4547Maqdal">Maqdalā</fo:inline>, especially the cannon (<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">​ቡም​ባ፡</fo:inline>) brought there, as related in
                                Mondon-Vidailhet 1904,  46–47, where a
                            <fo:inline>Rās</fo:inline> Bisawwǝr is also mentioned as <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">​የመ​ቅደ​ላ፡ ​ጠባ​ቂ፡</fo:inline>
                                (Mondon-Vidailhet 1904,  50).
                                The following is the entire text. </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ፩ ​አም​ላክ፡
                                <fo:inline id="d1e113536PRS9430Tewodros">
                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">​ንጉ​ሠ፡ ​ነገ​ሥት፡</fo:inline> ​ቴዎ​ድሮ​ስ፡</fo:inline> ​ይድ​ረስ፡
                                ከ<fo:inline id="d1e113541PRS13884Bisawwer">
                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">​ራስ፡</fo:inline> ​ቢሰ​ውር፡</fo:inline> ​ከቢ​ትወ​ደዶ​ች፡ ​ከደ​ጃዝ​ማቾ​ች፡ ​ካም​በሎ​ች፡ ​ከ፻ ​አለ​ቆች፡ ​ካ፶ ​አለ​ቆች፡ ​ካ፲ ​አለ​ቆች፡
                                ​ካ፭ ​አለ​ቆች፡ ​እን​ዴት፡
                                ​ሰነ​በታ​ችሁ፡ ​እኔ፡
                                ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ይመ​ስገ​ን፡ ​ደኅ​ና፡ ​ነኝ። ​በእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​ኃይ​ል፡ ​የም​ስራ​ች፡ ​ቡም​ባው​ም፡ ​መድ​ፉም፡ ​ወጣ​ልኝ፡
                                <fo:inline id="d1e113546LOC2449Dalant">​ደላ​ንታ፡</fo:inline> ​ከሜ​ዳው። ​ደግ​ሞም፡ ​ሁለ​ንት​ናው​ን፡ ​ተጫ​ውተ​ን፡ ​እል​ክባ​ችሁ፡ ​አለ​ሁ፡
                            ፫ ​ጊዜ፡ ​መድ​ፍ፡ ​ተኩ​ሱ። ​ባሩ​ዱን፡ ​ተጠ​ንቅ​ቃች​ሁ።</fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>There are no scribal corrections.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 1r: Stamp of King <fo:inline id="d1e113660PRS9430Tewodros">Tewodros II</fo:inline>, a lion surrounded by writing in Gǝʿǝz and Arabic.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ንጉ​ሠ፡ ​ነገ​ሥት፡ ​ቴዎ​ድሮ​ስ፡ ​ዘኢ​ትዮ​ጵያ፡</fo:inline>
                        <fo:inline baseline-shift="2pt"
                                   font-size="14pt"
                                   font-family="Scheherazade"
                                   writing-mode="rl">
                           <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>تاودروس ملك الحبشة</fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 1v: Written on the verso, possibly by the main hand.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">ከ<fo:inline id="d1e113679PRS13884Bisawwer">
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">​ራስ፡</fo:inline> ​ቢሰ​ውር፡</fo:inline>
                        </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Traces of printed text, maybe on the remainder of a paper sticker, are visible on the verso.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>5)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 1v: The shelfmark ‘Ms. Aeth. d. 21’ is written in pencil on the verso (the current shelfmark of the manuscript is Aeth. d. 22).</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>6)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>A white sticker, with the name of <fo:inline id="d1e113702PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> (‘<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ቤን​ት፡
                                            ​ዩው​ል፡ ​የን​ሰን።</fo:inline>’) printed on it, and the signature
                                        ‘Ms. Aeth. d. 22’ written in pencil, is glued
                                        on the inside of the folder in which the letter is kept. Another sticker with estimated dating, ‘[109]’ (possibly an inventory number), and a brief content description signature printed on
                                        it is glued below it. In pencil, the content description has been corrected and ‘£ 30’, presumably the price of the manuscript, been added.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The leaf is not foliated. In this description, the recto is referred to as
                                    fols 1r, , the verso as 1v.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 1: 1
                                    column (8 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 1r.There are 12–13 characters per line.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            80 × 200 mm (fol. 1r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 15 mm, bottom: 88 mm, right: 9 mm, left: 11 mm (fol. 1r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->1855–1868. Regular hand, bulky script.<fo:block>Ink: Black.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is good.Creases show where the leaf had been folded. There are a few small tears along the border of the leaf.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>1855–1868</fo:inline>
                            The letter can be dated to the reign of King <fo:inline id="d1e113719PRS9430Tewodros">Tewodros II</fo:inline>
                            (1855–1868). It seems likely that it was written towards the end of his reign, possibly in
                            <fo:inline>1867–1868</fo:inline>, shortly before
                            the fall of <fo:inline id="d1e113723LOC4547Maqdal">Maqdalā</fo:inline>.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>The provenance of the manuscript is unknown.</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e113730PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethd22">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethd22</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
   <fo:page-sequence initial-page-number="auto-odd" master-reference="Aethiopica-master">
