      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethf28"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. f. 28</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Juel-Jensen 53)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm">Maṣḥafa tārik</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex167×119 mm (weight: 424g),  fols, nineteenth–twenty-first century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e114453LIT6557Mashafat">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 1–122: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Book of History’ (​መጽ​ሐፈ፡ ​ታሪ​ክ፡), incomplete, CAe 6557, in Amharic and Gǝʿǝz.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">A long historiographical work in Amharic which contains various genealogies
                                and chronologies of Biblical figures, Ethiopian kings and Church history, accounts of the rule of Ethiopian kings and further sections
                                dealing with the hierarchies of Ethiopian notables and other topics.
                                A relation to <fo:inline>“Chronicle of the kings” (ታሪከ፡ ነገሥት፡), CAe 2422</fo:inline> is possible.The text on fol. 58, which is the end of Quire 3, breaks off in the middle of the sentence
                                (<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">​ልጁ፡ ​ገላ​ውዴ​ዎስ፡ ​ነገ​ሠ፡ ​ስመ፡ ​መን​ግስ​ቱ፡ ​አጽ​ናፍ፡ ​ሰገ​ድ፡ ​ይባ​ል፡ ​ነበ​ር፡ ​እር​ሱም፡ ​ከሰ​ራዩ፡ ​ተነ​ሥተ፡ ​፫፻ ​ነፍ​ጠኞ​ች፡ ​አስ​ከተ​ሉ፡ ​በት​ግሬ፡
                                ​ያሉ፡ ​ሰራ​ዊቱ​ን፡ ​ሁሉ፡ ​ሰብ​ስባ፡ ​ተከ​ዜን፡ ​ተሻ​ግሮ፡ ​ስና​ር፡ ​በኵ​ሳ፡ ​በሚ​ባል፡ ​አገ​ር፡ ​ሰፈ​ረ። ​በዚ​ያ፡ ​ቦታ፡ ​ከግ​ራኝ፡ ​ጋራ፡ ​ገጠ​መ፡ ​ድል፡ ​ነሳ​ው፡ ​ግራ</fo:inline>),
                                with a new section beginning on
                            59 (<fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">​የግ​ራኝ​ም፡ ​ነገ​ር፡ ​እን​ዲህ፡ ​ነው፡ ​በግ​ራኝ፡ ​ዘመ​ን፡ ​የሞ​ተት​ም፡ ​የተ​ለደ​ዱት​ም፡ ​ሰማ​ዕታ​ት፡ ​፺፪፼ ​ከ፫ ​ሽህ፡ ​ከ፰​፻፡
                            ​ከ፺፭ ​ናቸ​ው።</fo:inline>).</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">
                     <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ፩ ​አም​ላክ፡ ​ንዌ​ጥን፡ ​መጽ​ሐፈ፡ ​ታሪ​ክ፡</fo:inline> ​አን​ድ፡ ​አም​ላክ፡ ​በሚ​ሆኑ፡ ​በአ​ብ፡ ​በወ​ልድ፡
                                ​በመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስም፡ ​አም​ነን፡ ​የነ​ገሥ​ታት​ን፡ ​የት​ውል​ዳቸ​ውን፡ ​ነገ​ር፡ ​ታሪ​ክ፡ ​እን​ጽፋ​ለን፡ ​ማለ​ት፡ ​ነው።
                                <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​ዓለ​ም፡ ​ሰይ​ፈጠ​ር፡ ​ባን​ድነ​ት፡ ​በሶ​ስት​ነት፡ ​ያለ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>
                                ​መን​ግሥ​ት፡ ​ካሂ<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline> ​አስ​ቀድ​ሞ፡ ​መኖ​ሩ፡ <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline> ​ታወ​ቀ፡
                                ​ዓለ​ምን፡ <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​ፍጠ​ር፡ ​ብሎ፡ ​አሰ​በ፡ ​አስ​ቦም፡
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">
                                
                                ​ተሰ​ብሰ​በው፡ ​አገ​ኛቸ​ው፡ ​በሰ​ይፍ፡ ​ፈተ​ው፡ ​ብዙ​ዎች፡ ​በሰ​ይፍ፡ ​ሞቱ፡ ​ይኸ​መም፡ ​ሐሰ​ተሶ፡ ​መም​ህር፡ ​ዝክ​ረ፡ ​ስሙ፡ ​ካዚ​ህ፡ ​አለ​ም፡ ​ጠፋ፡ ​አባ​ቱም፡ ​ሰይ​ጣን፡ ​የፈ​ሰት፡ ​መገ​ኛ፡ ​ነው​ና፡ ​በው​ነት፡ ​አፈ​ረ። ። ። <!-- Amharic text should be double-checked by a native speaker -->
                                <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ተፈ​ጸመ፡ ​መጽ​ሐፈ፡ ​ታሪ​ክ፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Additional notes</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 38: ‘No. 19’ written in Amharic in the upper margin. The number presumably refers to the foliation of the manuscript.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">​ቁጥ​ር፡ <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline> ​፲፱</fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 60: ‘No. 29’ written in Amharic in the upper margin. The number presumably refers to the foliation of the manuscript.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">​ቁጥ​ር፡ ​፳፱</fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Omitted words or characters are occasionally inserted interlineally (e.g. on fols 10, 81, 94).
                                        Some words are scratched out (e.g. on 26), striked through (e.g. on 55),
                                        sometimes with a blue pen (e.g. on 36, 121), or marked for deletion by lines surrounding the words (e.g. on 83, 100, 121).
                                        Rarely, text is written over erasures (e.g. on 81).</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Spaces intended for rubricated words have occasionally been left blank (fols 9, 56).</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Amharic scribbles and notes, often hardly legible, in the margins throughout (e.g. fols 9, 65, 98).</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>On most pages starting from fols 37,
                                        small dots or strokes (e.g. 12, 38, 58), often in red ink, are placed in either the left or in both margins on each written line.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>5)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Paper slips on which the content of sections of the work is indicated summarily in English are placed inside the textblock throughout.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                                The book is bound in modern wooden boards.
                              
                                The boards are flush with the bookblock and have square edges.
                                The grain runs vertically. Both inner and outer surfaces are finely polished.
                              
                                Chainstitch sewing on four sewing stations (two pairs); periodic fold pattern. The original Z-plied thread has been repaired with a modern S-plied thread to reattach
                                the bookblock to the boards.
                            
                              Parchment tackets are still extant at head and tail of q1 #q2.
                            </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Pencil pagination in the middle of the upper margin
                                    (1–122). On fols 29–94, a numeral had been skipped in the original pagination. The mistaken numeral has either been corrected
                                    into the right one, or striked through, with the correct numeral written next to it.
                                See also Additional notes 1 and 2, which might constitute a foliation system.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block>7 quires. I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 1–20)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 21–40)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8+1 (Fols 41–58)</fo:inline> – IV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 59–78)</fo:inline> – V<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 79–98)</fo:inline> – VI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 99–114)</fo:inline> – VII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 115–122)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 1r–122: 1
                                    column (24 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 60.The number of characters per line is c. 24–26.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            162 × 107 mm (fol. 60).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            104 × 70 mm (fol. 60)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 19 mm, bottom: 28 mm, right: 25 mm, left: 12 mm (fol. 60).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Primary and ruling pricks are visible. The upper and bottom lines are written above the
                                        ruling. Ruling pattern: 1A-1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->1800–2006. At least two hands were involved in the writing of the manuscript, possibly more.
                                    The script changes repeatedly throughout, often within the same page (e.g. fols 35, 90, 115),
                                    leading to an overall impression of irregularity. All hands belong to the nineteenth–twenty-first century.<fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: Holy names; elements of numerals and punctuation signs.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Holes from the parchment making process (e.g. fols 3, 27, 85).
                                   The hole on 47 has been repaired at the moment of parchment production by sewing. </fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is good.
                                 The bookblock has been damaged by humidity, especially in the outer margins.
                                 Insect droppings are present on fols 31, 32. The blunt edge used for ruling has perforated on 22.
                                 Creases and losses are present, especially on the first and last folios.
                               </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>nineteenth–twenty-first century</fo:inline>
                            The manuscript can be dated palaeographically to the period between the
                            nineteenth and the twenty-first century.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>The provenance of the manuscript is unknown.</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the
                            bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e114829PRS5782JuelJen">Bent Juel-Jensen</fo:inline> after his death in 2006.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethf28">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethf28</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
