         </fo:table>
      </fo:static-content>
      <fo:static-content flow-name="xsl-footnote-separator">
         <fo:block space-before="5mm" space-after="5mm">
            <fo:leader leader-length="30%" rule-thickness="0pt"/>
         </fo:block>
      </fo:static-content>
      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLeu6"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. g. 50</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Bodleian Ullendorff 6)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex121×102 mm (weight: 213g), 69 fols, 8 quires, eighteenth
                       century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e120844LIT1526GadlaZ">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 9ra–68ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Vita of Zamikāʾel ʾAragāwi’ (​ገድ​ለ፡ ​ዘሚ​ካኤ​ል፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ፡), CAe 1526.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​በስ​መ፡ ​አግ​ዚአብ ​ሔር፡ ​ጽኑ​ዕ፡ ​ዘመ​ነ፡  ​መን​ግሥ​ቱ፡ <fo:inline>[​ዘኢይ]</fo:inline>​ትዌ​ዳእ
                                 ፤  ​መል​ዕል​ተ፡ ​ነፋ​ሳት፡ ​ደባ<fo:inline>[ት]</fo:inline>​ረ፡ ​ማይ፡
                                ​ዘያ​ረግዕ  ፤  ​በከ​ርሠ፡ ​ደመ​ና፡ ​ማየ፡ ​ባሕ​ር፡ ​ዘያ​መጽእ  ፨ 
                                ​ወያ​ዓር​ጎ፡ ​በእ ​ደ፡ ​መላ​እክ​ት፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ያጔ​ጕዕ፡  ​መባ​ርቅ​ት፡ ​ወነ​ጐድ​ጓድ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ይጼ​ንዕ።
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ወያ​ግብ​ኦ፡ ​ኀበ፡ ​ንስ​ሐ፡ ​ለዘ​ተኃ​ጕለ፡ ​እም​ኔክሙ ፤  ​ወይ​ሚጦ​ሙ፡ 
                                ​ለነ​ጋድ​ያን ፤  ​ኀቤ​ክሙ፡ ​በዳ​ኅን፡ ​ወበ​ሰላም ፨ 
                                ​ወየ​ሀብ​ክሙ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ኑዛዜ ፤  ​ለኅ​ዙና​ን፡ ​እንተ ፤ 
                                ​ትመ​ጽእ፡   (fol. 68ra)   ​ላዕ​ሌክ​ሙ፡ ​በኃ​ይለ፡ ​መስ​ቀሉ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​እነ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡
                                ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​ሎቱ ፤  ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ወላ​ዕሌ​ነ፡ ​ይኩ​ን፡ ​ምሕ​ረት፡ ​እስ​ከ፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ 
                                ​አሜን ፨
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e120911LIT6842TentaLe">
               <fo:inline>II) Fols 68ra–68vb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Commencement of the genealogy of the monks’ (​ጥን​ተ፡ ​ልደ​ቶሙ፡ ​ለመ​ነኮ​ሳት፡), CAe 6842.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ዝው​እቱ፡  ​ጥን​ተ፡ ​ልደ​ቶሙ፡ ​ለመ​ነኮ​ሳት ፤  ​እን​ጦን​ዮስ፡ ​ወለ​ዶ፡ 
                                ​ለመ​ቃር​ዮስ ፤  ​መቃ​ርዮ​ስ፡ ​ወለ​ዶ፡ ​ለጳ​ኵሚስ ፤ 
                                ​ጳኵ​ሚስ፡ ​ወለዶ ፤ 
                                ​ለዘሚ  (b)  ​ካኤ​ል፡ ​ዝው​እቱ፡ ​አቡ​ነ፡ ​አረ​ጋዊ ፤  ​አረ​ጋዊ፡ ​ወለ​ዶ፡ 
                                ​ለማ​ትያስ ፤  ​ማት​ያስ፡ ​ወለ​ዶ፡ ​ለዮ​ሴፍ ፤
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ወአ​ባ፡ ​ዓፅ​ፈ፡ ​ወልድ ፤  ​ወአ​ባ፡ ​ገብ​ረ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ ​ወአ​ባ፡ 
                                ​ተወ​ልደ ፤  ​መድ​ኅን፡ ​ወአ​ባ፡ ​ዘሥ​ላሴ፡ ​ጸሎ​ቶሙ ፤ 
                                ​ወረ​ድኤ​ተ፡ ​ትዕ​ግሥ​ቶሙ፡ ​ይዕ​ቀቦ፡ ​ለፍ​ቁሮ​ሙ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e120958PRS14037Zamaryam">​ዘማ​ርያ​ም፡</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline id="d1e120962PRS14039Enzira">​እን​ዚራ፡ ​ድን<fo:inline>[ግ]</fo:inline>​ል፡</fo:inline> ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን፡
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Additional notes</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 1v–7v: Malkǝʾ-hymn to Raphael, CAe 2849..
                                        The note, written by Hand 2, contains several corrections and additions in the margins, referenced in the body of the text by
                                        means of <fo:inline font-style="italic">tamallas</fo:inline>-signs (fols 1v, 6r).
                                    </fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                        Incipit: :
                                            ​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ለዝ​ክረ፡ ​ስም​ከ፡  ​ተጽ​ውዖ፡ ​ዘቀ​ደመ፡ ​በአ​ፈ፡ ​አም​ላክ፡ ​አዳ​ም፡ ​እን​በለ፡ ​ይሰ​መይ፡ ​ስመ፡
                                             ​ሩፋ​ኤል፡  ​ምል​ዓኒ፡ ​ወወ​ስከ​ኒ፡ ​ዳግ​መ፡ ​መን​ፈስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ሳዌ፡ ​አእ​ምሮ፡ ​እን​ተ፡ ​ይፈ​ሪ፡ ​ሰላ​መ፡
                                         ... 
                                   </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                                        Inventory note written in Arabic on the inner side of the back board. It mentions the textual contents of the book. Few words are not easily readable.
                                    </fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline baseline-shift="2pt"
                                   font-size="14pt"
                                   font-family="Scheherazade"
                                   writing-mode="rl">
                                        مديح... لمار روفايل الملاك
                                        سيرة الانبا اراݣاڨى... الرهبنة
                                        الانطونية في الحبشة وجدول
                                        تسلسل الرهبان
                                    </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Scribal corrections are rare: omitted letters or words added above the line (e.g. fols 10va, 20rb, 61rb), and erasures
                                        (e.g. fol. 10va). The text on 68vb has been written in condensed script to accommodate the end of the column.
                                        Pen trial on 1r.
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>The names of the original owners, mentioned in supplications throughout, have been erased and replaced with those of
                                        <fo:inline id="d1e121386PRS14037Zamaryam">Zamāryām</fo:inline> (e.g. on fols 15va, 48ra, 66va) and
                                        <fo:inline id="d1e121390PRS14039Enzira">ʾƎnzirā Dǝngǝl</fo:inline> (fols 64ra, 66va, 68vb),
                                        introduced by the epithet <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ፍቁ​ሮሙ፡</fo:inline> ‘their beloved’.
                                    </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>A white sticker is glued to the inner side of the front board. The signature ‘MS. Eth. E.U. VI’ and the title ‘Za-Mikael Aragawi’ are printed on it.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                                       The book is bound in cardboard boards fully covered with parchment.
                                     
                                       The boards have squares and are larger than the book block.
                                     
                                         Full parchment cover undecorated.
                                       
                                         Stuck-on endbands obtained from a cord of neutral colour.
                                       
                                         The manuscript is sewn continuously on two cord sewing supports, which indicate the Western origin of the binding.
                                       
                                       The quires do not present holes close to the head and tail which may indicate the former presence of quire tackets.
                                       The titles of the texts in the manuscript are tooled in gold on the spine of the cover.
                                     </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Pencil foliation in the upper right corner (1–69).</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block>8 quires. I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">8 (Fols 1r–8v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 9r–18v)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 19r–28v)</fo:inline> – IV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 29r–38v)</fo:inline> – V<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 39r–48v)</fo:inline> – VI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 49r–58v)</fo:inline> – VII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 59r–68v)</fo:inline> – B<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">0+1 (Fols 69r–69v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 9ra–68vb: 2
                                    columns (14 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 43r.The characters per line are 8–9.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            113 × 100 mm (fol. 43r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            75 × 78 mm (fol. 43r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 13 mm, bottom: 26 mm, right: 13 mm, left: 8 mm, intercolumn: 8 mm (fol. 43r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 1v–7v: 1
                                    column (13 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 5r.The characters per line are 12–18.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            113 × 100 mm (fol. 43r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            93 × 82 mm (fol. 5r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 8 mm, bottom: 10 mm, right: 11 mm, left: 8 mm (fol. 5r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Ruling and pricking are visible. Both primary and ruling pricks are visible. The upper and bottom lines are written above the ruling. The quire is unruled. Ruling pattern: 1A-1A-1A1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 9ra–68vb. Eighteenth century.. Fine and regular handwriting. The ligature ​ግዚ is used e.g. on fol. 1r.
                                <fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: 
                                    Few lines on the incipit page of the Vita of Zamikāʾel ʾAragāwi, alternating with black lines;
                                    the incipits of the sections of the Vita of Zamikāʾel ʾAragāwi; the first word of the Monastic genealogy of
                                        Dabra Dāmmo; holy names, included that of the saint; elements of the punctuation, including text dividers, and numerals.
                                </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 2:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 1v–7v. Eighteenth–nineteenth century.. 
                                    This hand wrote the Malkǝʾ-hymn to the Archangel Raphael.
                                    The handwriting is irregular due to the lack of ruling. Characters are executed in a very angular manner.
                                    The ligature ​ግዚ is used e.g. on fol. 2r.<fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: The incipit of the text; the name of Rufāʾel; the word <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሰላ​ም፡</fo:inline> (in full or in abbreviated
                                    form); elements of the numerals and of the punctuation.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Abbreviations: <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="6mm"
                                             provisional-label-separation="6mm"
                                             start-indent="cm">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>1)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                          <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሰላ</fo:inline> for <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሰላ​ም፡</fo:inline> (fols 1v–6r);
                                    </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:inline>2)</fo:inline>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block hyphenate="true">
                                          <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሩፋ</fo:inline> or <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሩፋኤ</fo:inline> for <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሩፋ​ኤል፡</fo:inline> (fols 3r–6r).
                                    </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Small holes from the parchment making process, e.g. on fols 45, 61, 66.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is good.
                                    Some folios are stained or slightly darkened by use (e.g. fols 1r, 39v).
                                    Stains are present on 63, 64 and on fol. 8v.
                                </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>eighteenth
                       century</fo:inline>
                   The manuscript can be dated palaeographically to the eighteenth century.
                   The names of the original owners have been erased and replaced with those of <fo:inline id="d1e121450PRS14037Zamaryam">Zamāryām</fo:inline> and
                   <fo:inline id="d1e121452PRS14039Enzira">ʾƎnzirā Dǝngǝl</fo:inline> (the two names might also possibly refer to one
                   single person, see Varia note 3).
               </fo:block>
            <fo:block>
                   No information is available on the provenance and early history of the
                   manuscript, except for the presence of a summary of the book
                   contents written in Arabic on the back board (cp. Additional note 2),
                   which might suggest that the manuscript was produced or circulated at some time in an Arabic-speaking country.
                   The manuscript was then acquired by <fo:inline id="d1e121463PRS9622Ullendor">Edward Ullendorff</fo:inline>.
                  </fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e121468PRS9622Ullendor">Edward Ullendorff</fo:inline> after his death in 2011.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLeu6">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLeu6</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
