            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Pricking and ruling are not visible. Pricking and ruling are not visible. Pricking and ruling are not visible.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Nineteenth–twenty-first century.. Fine handwriting. Characters are regular.
                                    The ligature ​ግዚ is occasionally used e.g. on fol. 1r18.
                                  <fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: Few lines of the incipits and other lines within the text; the name of Mary and of the owner in the supplications;
                                    the refrain <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ሰላ​ም፡ ​ለኪ፡</fo:inline>; captions of the miniatures.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Decoration</fo:block>
         <fo:block margin-top="3mm" margin-bottom="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Two illustrations survive from the scroll’s original decoration. They are painted
                                with rich earthy shades of brown, ochre, and red and were painted by a professional hand. 
                                They appear to belong to the nineteenth century based on style.
                            </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Miniatures</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(312) <fo:inline>Unidentified standing angel with an unsheathed sword.</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(313) <fo:inline>A cross with volutes at its ends (rather than the usual eyes)
                                    and a face at its centre.</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Headpieces</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Drawings</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Other</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is deficient.
                              The parchment is crumpled from rolling and darkened toward the lower border, rendering the text barely legible.
                              It exhibits small areas of loss and tears, especially along the upper and lower margins.
                              Some letters are illegible due to material damage. The right margin of the third strip has been damaged by pests,
                              with consequent loss of letters. The stitching in the lower margin of the first and second strips has become partially undone.
                            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>nineteenth century</fo:inline>
                            The manuscript can be dated palaeographically and by the style of the
                            miniatures to the nineteenth century.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>The provenance and circumstances of production of the manuscript are unknown.
                         The original owner, indicated in the supplication formulas as <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ዓመ​ትከ፡</fo:inline> ‘your maid’, was
                             <fo:inline id="d1e122084PRS14045WalattaKi">Walatta Kidān</fo:inline>.
                         The scroll was acquired at some point by <fo:inline id="d1e122086PRS9622Ullendor">Edward Ullendorff</fo:inline>.
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e122091PRS9622Ullendor">Edward Ullendorff</fo:inline> after his death in 2011.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLeu7">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLeu7</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
