      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLeu9"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. g. 53 (R)</fo:block>
            <fo:block>(Bodleian Ullendorff 9)</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment scroll1431×81–84 mm, 720×81–83 mm, 725×84 mm (weight: 28g),  fols, nineteenth–twenty-first century.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e123103LIT6829PPAyna">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 1r1–1r25: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Prayer against the evil eye, the possession, the Bāryā and the Legewon’ (​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዓይ​ነ፡ ​ጽላ፡ ​ወነ​ገር​ጋር፡ ​ወባ​ርያ፡ ​ወሌ​ጌዎ​ን፡), CAe 6829.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The entire text is reproduced below.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ቅ ​ዱስ፡ ፩ ​አም​ላክ፡ ​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዓይ ይ ​ነ፡ ​ጽላ ፨  ​ወነ​ገር​ጋር ፨  ​ወባ​ርያ፡ ​ወሌ​ጌዎን ፨ 
                                ​ወጠ​ር፡ ​ቀለም ፨  ​ወእ​ምድ​ኅረዝ ፨  ​ፀውዑ ፨  ​ህዝብ ፨  ​አስ​ማተ ፨ ​ሥላሴ ፨  ​ያሮክ ፨  ​ሣሮክ ፨  ​አዳ​ሮሰ፡
                                አ<fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​ዊን ፨  ​ጢት​ሮስ ፨
                                <fo:inline>&lt;...&gt;</fo:inline>​ሮፎሮ ​ድሩ​ኤል፡ ይ ​መትር ፨  ​የሐ​ር፡ ​አዝ​ራዊ ፨  ​ደላዊ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                ​ቀተ​ናዊ ፨  ለ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ተና​ዊ፡ ​አሰ​ኮራ​ላጵስ ፨  ​አስ​ከራ​ፋጲስ ፨  ​አረ​ጋዎን ፨  ​ፈሐ​ዝር፡ ​አት​ናውጲ ፨ 
                                ​ስዕሉ ፨
                                ​አድ​ኅና፡ ​ወዕ ቀ ባ ፨  ​ለአ​መትከ ፨ <fo:inline id="d1e123210PRS14023WalattaM">​ወለ​ተ፡ ​ሚካ​ኤል፡
                                    ​በተ​ሐ።  ​በተ​ሐ፡ ​በተሃ</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e123221LIT6830PPAyna">
               <fo:inline>II) Fols 1r26–1r41: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Prayer against the evil eye, the eye of the Zār and the Šotalāy’ (​ጸሎ​ት። ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዓይ​ነ፡ ​ጥላ፡ ​ወዓ​ይነ፡ ​ዛር፡ ​ወሾ​ተላ​ይ፡), CAe 6830.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The entire text is reproduced below.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡  ፩ ​አም​ላክ፡ ​ጸሎ​ት። ​በእ​ንተ ፨  ​ዓይ​ነ፡ ​ጥላ፡ ​ወዓ​ይነ፡ ​ዛር፡ ​ወሾ​ተላ​ይ፡
                                 ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡  ​ናዝ​ራዊ ፨ <fo:inline>በትምርተ (!)</fo:inline> ​መስ​ቀል ፨ 
                                ​መር​አዊ፡ ​ጸረ፡ ​ፈውስ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ሲቃ ፨  ​ጳጢቃ ፨  ​ኢዮ​ሎን ፨  ​አኽ​ያ፡ ​ሾራ​ኽያ ፨  ​አል​ሸይ ፨  ​ኢማ​ኑኤል ፨ 
                                ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር ፨
                                ​አድ​ኅና ፨  ​ለአ​መት​ከ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e123280PRS14023WalattaM">​ወለ​ተ፡ ​ሚካ​ኤል፡ ​በተ​ሐ፡  ​በተ​ሐ፨</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e123291LIT5920JohnBeg">
               <fo:inline>III) Fols 1r41–1r76: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Beginning of the Gospel of John, CAe 5920.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The entire text is reproduced below.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                     <fo:inline>ቀ (!)</fo:inline> ​በስ​መ፡ <fo:inline>[​አብ፡]</fo:inline>
                                    ወ ​ወል​ድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡
                                 ፩  ​አም​ላክ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዓይ​ነ፡ ​ጥላ፡ ​ወባ​ርያ፡ ​ወሌ​ጌዎ​ን፡ ​ርኩ​ስ፡  ​ቀዳ​ሚሁ፡ ​ቃል፡  ​ውእ​ቱ፡
                                ​ቃል፡ ​ቃለ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር። ​ውእቱ ፨  ​ቃል፡
                                ወ እ ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፨ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ቃል፡ ​ወከ​ማሁ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                ​እም​ቀዲሙ ፨  ​ኀበ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔር ፨  ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ቃል፡
                                <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline> ​ወኵሉ ፨  ​ኮነ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                ​ወዘ​እን​በሌ​ሁሰ ፨  ​ዘኮ​ነ፡ ​ወኢ​ምን​ትኒ፡
                                ​እም​ዘኮነ ፨  ​ወዘ​ሂ፡ ​በእ​ንቲ​አሁ ፨ 
                                ​ቦቱ ፨ 
                                ​ሕይ​ወት፡ ​ውእቱ ፨  ​ወሕ​ይዎ​ሰ፡ ​ብር​ሃኑ ፨  ​ለእ​ጓለ፡ ​እመሕ ያ ​ው፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ወብ​ርሃ​ነ፡
                                ​ጽድ​ቅሰ ፨  ​ዘው​ስተ ፨  ​ጽል​መት፡ ​ወያ​ርኢ ፨ 
                                ​ወያ​በርህ ፨  ​ወያ​ርኢ ፨ <fo:inline>ወጽመትኒ (!)</fo:inline>
                                ​ኢረ​ከቦ ፨  ​ወኢ​ይቀ​ርከቦ ፨  ​ሰማ​ይ፡ <fo:inline>ወምምድር (!)</fo:inline> ​የሐ​ልፍ ፨ 
                                ​ወቃ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ልየ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ሰ፨ ​ኢየ​ሐል​ፍ፡ ​ለዓ​ለም፨ ​ዓለ​ም፨ ​አሜ​ን፨
                                 ​አድ​ኅና፡
                                   ​ለአ​መትከ ፨ <fo:inline id="d1e123415PRS14023WalattaM">​ወለ​ተ፡ ​ሚካ​ኤል፡ ​በተሐ</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e123424LIT5690MagicPrayer">
               <fo:inline>IV) Fols 1r77–1r109: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Protective prayer against eye disease’ (​ጸሎ​ተ፡ ​ነደ​ራ፡), CAe 5690.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">The entire text is reproduced below.</fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​በስ​መ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ወወ​ልድ፡ ​ወመ​ንፈ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡
                                    ፩  ​አም​ላክ፡ ​ጸሎ​ት፡ ​በእ​ንተ፡ ​ዓይነ ፨  ​ባር​ያ፡ ​ወሌ​ጌዎን ፨ 
                                ​ርኩ​ስ፡ ​ጸሎ​ተ፡ ​ነደራ ፨  ​ወእ​ንዘ ።  ​የሐ​ልፍ፡ ​እግ​ዚእነ ፨
                                ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡  ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​አር​ዳኢ​ሁ፡ ​ርዕ​ዩ፡ ​መል​ክ፡ ​ብእ​ሲት፡ ​አረ​ጊት፡ ​መፍ​ርህ​ት፡ ​ወመ​ጸን​ግፅ​ት፡ ​ወእ​ንዘ፡ ​ይበ​ርቅ፡ ​ዓይ​ና፡ ​ከመ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                ​ወር​ቅ፡ ​ቀይ​ህ፡ ​አዕ​ዳዊ​ሃኒ። ​ወአ​ዕጋ​ሪሃኒ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ከመ፡ ​ሰረ​ገላ፡ ​እሳ​ት፡ ​መጠ​ናሂ፡ ​ወቆ​ማ፡ ​ከመ፡ ​በቀ​ልት፡ ​ወይ​ቤልዎ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                ​አር​ዳኢ​ሁ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​እነ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ምን​ት፡ ​ይእ​ቲ፡ ​ዓይ​ነ፡ ​እኪ​ት፡ ​ወር​ግም​ት፡ ​በም​ንት፡ <fo:inline>ናጥፋአጥፍዕዋ፡ (!)</fo:inline> ​በእ​ሳት፡
                                ​ወዝ​ርዕ​ዋ፡ ​በነ​ፋስ። ​ምስ​ራቀ፡ ​ወም​ዕራ​በ።
                                ​ሰሜ​ነ፡ ​ወደ​ቡበ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ቦር። ​ፎሪ​ኮን፡ ​አት​ሪክ​ን። ​አተ​ርዋ​ን፡ ​ቶሪ​ፍ። ​ቶራ​ኒቆ፡ ​ቶሲ​ሰ። ​ጉሄ​ል፡ ​አማ​ኑኤ​ል።
                                 ​አድ​ኅና፡ ​ወዕ​ቀባ። ​ለአ​መት​ከ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e123474PRS14023WalattaM">​በተ​ሐ፡ ​ወለ​ተ፡ ​ሚካ​ኤል፡</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>The verso is blank except for the modern sticker e3.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Occasionally, omitted characters are added interlineally and erroneous characters are marked for deletion by dashes or lines above and below.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>White printed, probably typewritten, sticker glued to the verso, containing a brief description of the scroll, its provenance and price in Francs:
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus">‘Rouleau éthiopien de la ville de <fo:inline id="d1e123673LOC4244Laliba">Lalibela</fo:inline>. (Kitab) XIXè siècle avec une
                                            miniature. Fr. 150.–’</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Each prayer ends with a supplication for the owner, who is introduced by the epithet
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​አመ​ትከ፡</fo:inline> ‘your maid’, after which a space had originally been left blank. Following the blank space, the
                                        word <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​በተ​ሐ፡</fo:inline> / <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​በተ​ሃ፡</fo:inline>, sometimes repeated several times, is written in the main hand and script.
                                        Inside the space originally left
                                        blank, the name <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ወለ​ተ፡ ​ሚካ​ኤል፡</fo:inline> / <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ወለ​ተ፡ ​ሚካ​ኤል፡ ​በተ​ሐ፡</fo:inline> has been written,
                                        probably also by the main hand, but in a smaller script. It seems likely that both names are the given and baptismal name of the owner,
                                        <fo:inline id="d1e123699PRS14023WalattaM">Walatta Mikāʾel</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>5)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Order of textual units and miniatures: Miniature 1, Textual units I–IV.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>The two parchment strips that compose the scroll are sewn together with a running stitch.The manuscript is kept in a pipe case.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>1
                                    column (25 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Number of characters per line: 10–11.The outer margins are delimited by a black line.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            215 × 55–65 mm ()</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            right: 5–15 mm, left: 5–15 mm ().
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>1
                                    column (51 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Number of characters per line: 9–10.The outer margins are delimited by a black line.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            413 × 55–65 mm ()</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            right: 5–15 mm, left: 5–15 mm ().
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>1
                                    column (33 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">Number of characters per line: 10–13.The outer margins are delimited by a black line.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            229 × 60–65 mm ()</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            right: 5–15 mm, left: 5–15 mm ().
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Pricking and ruling are not visible. Pricking and ruling are not visible. Pricking and ruling are not visible.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Nineteenth–twenty-first century.. Modern bulky script, somewhat irregular. The nine-dot asterisk is used often as word separator, and the word separator is often omitted when the end of a word
                                    coincides with the end of the line.<fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: Beginnings of prayers; holy names; elements of numerals and punctuation marks. Towards the end of the scroll, rubrication in
                                    punctuation marks is omitted.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Decoration</fo:block>
         <fo:block margin-top="3mm" margin-bottom="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Bands filled with irregular elements mark the beginning and ending of the scroll’s 
                                three textual sections. Two monochrome images are located at its top.
                            </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Miniatures</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
            <fo:inline>(320) <fo:inline>A 3 x 6 grid filled with faces and surmounted by a pattern of small accents. These are 
                                    perhaps deliberately rendered in a way that creates an ambiguous connection with the writing
                                    (e.g. the eyes look like a <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">ወ</fo:inline>).</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
            <fo:inline>(321) <fo:inline>An unidentified angel with an unsheathed sword.</fo:inline>
            </fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Headpieces</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Drawings</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Other</fo:block>
         <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                   provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Several holes from parchment making.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is good.The verso is darkened, and the upper and lower margins are slightly crumpled.
                                A small hole and a tear are present near the upper margin.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>nineteenth–twenty-first century</fo:inline>
                            The manuscript can be dated palaeographically to the period between the
                            nineteenth and the twenty-first century.
                            The probably original owner was <fo:inline id="d1e123730PRS14023WalattaM">Walatta Mikāʾel</fo:inline> (see
                            Varia note 4).
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>According to the sticker on the backside, the scroll came from <fo:inline id="d1e123738LOC4244Laliba">Lālibalā (town)</fo:inline>. The same sticker, typewritten
                            in French and indicating the scroll’s price in francs, suggests that the scroll was offered for sale before 2002 in France (unless the currency refers to Swiss francs,
                            in which case 2002 would not constitute a terminus ante quem).</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The manuscript entered the Bodleian Libraries as part of the bequest of <fo:inline id="d1e123743PRS9622Ullendor">Edward Ullendorff</fo:inline> after his death in 2011.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLeu9">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLeu9</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
