      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body"
               font-size="10.5pt"
               line-height="12.5pt"
               font-family="Ludolfus"
               text-align="justify"
               hyphenate="true"><!-- CATALOGUE     -->
         <fo:block id="BDLaethf35"
                   text-align="center"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid"
                   space-before="3mm">
            <fo:block font-weight="800">Bodleian Aeth. f. 35</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block text-align="center" space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm"/>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" space-after="3mm" white-space-collapse="true">Parchment codex155×110 mm (weight: 418g), 114 fols (17 p. blank), 12 quires, 1889–1926.</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Main Contents</fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e126837LIT2715John">
               <fo:inline>I) Fols 1r–79va: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Gospel of John, CAe 2715.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​ብስ​ራተ፡ ​አብ፡ ​ትሩ​ፍ፡ ​ረድ​እ፡ ​ተና​ጋሪ፡ ​በመ​ለኮ​ት፡ ​ዮሐ​ንስ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ዘብ​ዴዎ​ስ፡ ​ፍቁ​ረ፡ እ ​ግዚ​እነ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡  ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡
                                ​ወበ​ረከ​ቱ፡
                                ​የሃ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ገብ​ሩ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e126850PRS14002WaldaS">​ወል​ደ፡
                                    ​ሥላ​ሴ፡</fo:inline> ​መስ​ለ፡
                                 ​ጸሐ​ፊሁ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e126856PRS14003FereS">​ፍሬ፡ ​ሰን​በት፡</fo:inline> ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡
                                       (a)   ​አሜን
                                ፨
                                ​ቀዳ​ሚሁ፡ ቃ ​ል፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡  ​ቃል፡  ​ወው​እቱ፡ ​ቃል፡ ​ኀበ፡ ​አብ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ወእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ቃል፡
                                ​ወከ​ማሁ፡
                                ቀ ​ዳሚ​ሁ፡ ​እም​ቀዲሙ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ኀበ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡  ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ወኵ​ሉ፡
                                ​ቦቱ፡ ​ኮኑ፡
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ወዝ​ንቱ፡ ​ረድ​እ፡ ​ዘኮ​ነ፡ ​ሰማ​ዕተ፡ ​በእ​ንተ​ዝ፡ ​ወዘ​ሂ፡ ​ጸሐ​ፈ፡ ​ዘን​ተ፡ ​ንሕ​ነ፡ ​ነአ​ምር፡ ​ከመ፡ ​ጽድ​ቅ፡ ​ውእ​ቱ፡ ​ስም​ዑ። ​ወዘ​ንተ፡ ​ገብ​ረ፡ ​እግ​ዚእ፡
                                 ​ኢየ​ሱስ ፡ ​ወቦ፡ ​ባዕ​ድኒ፡ ​ብዙ​ኅ፡ ​ዘገ​ብረ፡ ​እግ​ዚእ፡  ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡  ​ወሶ​በ፡
                                ተ  (b)  ​ጽሕ​ፈ፡ ​በበ​፩ዱ፡ ​እም​ኢያ​ገመ​ሮ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​ጥቀ፡ ​እመ​ጻሕ​ፍቲ​ሁ፡ <fo:inline>ዝተጽሕፈ፡ (!)</fo:inline>
                                ​አሜን ፨ ፨ ፨
                                ​መል​ዓ፡ ​ስብ​ከተ፡ ​ዮሐ​ንስ፡ ​ሐዋር ​ያ፡ ​ወል​ደ፡ ​ዘብ​ዴዎ​ስ፡ ፩ ​እም​፲ወ​፪ቱ፡ ​ሐዋ​ርያ​ት። ​ወጸ​ሐፎ፡ ​በዮ​ናኒ፡
                                ​ለሰ​ብአ፡ ​ሀገ​ረ፡ ​ኤፌ​ሶን። ​እም​ድኅ​ረ፡ ​ዕር​ገቱ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​እነ፡  ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ክር​ስቶ​ስ፡ 
                                ​በሥ  (fol. 79va)  ​ጋ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ሰማ​ያት። ​በ፴ ​ዓመ​ት፡ ​ወ፰ ​ዓመ​ተ፡ ​መን​ግሥ​ቱ፡ ​ለኔ​ሮን፡ ​ቄሣ​ር፡
                                ​ንጉሠ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                     <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ሮሜ፡ ​ወስ​ብሐ​ት፡ ​ለእ ​ግዚ ​አብ​ሔር፡
                                ​ወም​ሕረ​ቱ፡ ​ይኩ​ን፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ገብ​ሩ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e126921PRS14002WaldaS">​ወል​ደ፡
                                 ​ሥላ​ሴ፡</fo:inline> ​ወም​ስለ፡ ​ጸሐ​ፊሁ፡
                                <fo:inline id="d1e126926PRS14003FereS">​ፍሬ፡  ​ሰን​በት፡</fo:inline> ​ለዓ​ለመ፡ ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን።
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e126937LIT1099Anapho">
               <fo:inline>II) Fols 81ra–99va: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">Anaphora of Our Lady Mary by Cyriacus of Behnesa, CAe 1099.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                ​አኰ​ቴተ፡ ​ቍር​ባን፡ ​ዘእ​ግዝእ ​ትነ፡  ​ማር​ያም፡  ​ወላ​ዲተ፡
                                ​አም ​ላክ፡ ጽ ​ርደ​ት፡
                                 ​ዘነ​በበ፡ ​በመ​ንፈ ​ስ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​አባ፡ ​ህር​ያቆ​ስ፡ ​ኤጲ​ስ፡ ​ቆጶ​ስ፡ ​ዘሀ​ገረ፡ ​ብህ​ንሳ፡ ​ጸሎ​ቱ፡ ​ወበ​ረከ​ቱ፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡
                                 ​ምስ​ለ፡  ​ገብ​ሩ፡
                                    <fo:inline id="d1e126960PRS14002WaldaS">​ወል​ደ፡ ​ሥላ​ሴ፡</fo:inline> ​ለዓ​ለመ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline>
                                ​ዓለ​ም፡ ​አሜ​ን፡
                                ​ጐሥ​ዓ፡ ​ልብ  (b)  ​የ፡ ​ቃለ፡ ​ሠና​የ፡ ​ጐሥ​ዓ፡ ​ልብ​የ፡  ​ቃለ፡ ​ሠና​የ፡ ​ወአ​ነ፡ ​አየ​ድዕ፡
                                ​ቅዳ ​ሴሃ፡ ​ለማ​ርያም<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​አኮ፡
                                    ​በአ​ብዝ​ኆ፡  ​አላ፡ ​በአ​ውህዶ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ወአ​ነ፡ ​አየ​ድዕ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ውዳ​ሴሃ፡ ​ለድ​ንግ​ል።
                            </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                
                                ​ኦእ​ግዝ​እት​የ፡ ​ቅድ​ስት፡ ​ድን​ግል፡ ​በ፪​ኤ፡  ​ማር​ያም<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ወላ​ዲተ፡ ​አም​ላክ፡ ​በጸ​ሎት​ኪ፡ ​ወበ​ስእ​ለት​ኪ፡
                                ​ወበ​ምሕ​ረተ፡ ​ፍቁ​ር፡ ​ወል​ድኪ፡ ​የሃ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ኃጥ​እ፡ ​ገብ​ርኪ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e126992PRS14002WaldaS">​ወል​ደ፡
                                     ​ሥላ​ሴ፡</fo:inline> ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ጸሐ​ፊሁ፡ ​ኃጥ​እ፡ ​ወአ​ባሲ፡ <fo:inline id="d1e126997PRS14003FereS">​ፍሬ፡
                                         ​ሰን​በት። ።</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e127008LIT2260salota">
               <fo:inline>III) Fols 99va–107ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Prayer of the Covenant’ (​ጸሎ​ተ፡ ​ኪዳ​ን፡), CAe 2260.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e127016LIT1716Kidanz">
               <fo:inline>III-1) Fols 99va–105rb: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘Covenant of the Morning’ (​ኪዳ​ን፡ ​ዘነ​ግህ፡), CAe 1716.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    ​ኪዳ​ን፡ ​ዘነ​ግህ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ ​ር፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ኃያ​ል፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ሕያ​ው፡   (b)   ​ዘኢ​ይመ​ውት፡ ​ዘተ​ወል​ደ፡
                                    እ ​ማር​ያም፡  ​እም​ቅድ​ስት፡ ​ድን​ግል፡ ​ተሠ​ሃለ​ነ፡ ​እግ​ዚኦ፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​እግ​ዚአ​ብሔ​ር፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ኃያ​ል፡ ​ቅዱ​ስ፡ ​ሕያ​ው፡ ​ዘኢ​ይመ​ውት፡
                                    ​ዘተ​ጠም​ቀ፡ ​በዮ​ርዳ​ኖስ፡ ​ወተ​ሰቅ​ለ፡ ​ዲበ፡ ​ዕፀ፡ ​መስ​ቀል፡ ​ተሠ​ሃለ​ነ፡
                                 </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                     <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ናዝ​ዝ፡ ​እጓ​ለ፡ ​ማው​ታ፡ ​ተወ​ከፍ፡ ​ሲሩ​ያነ፡ ​በም​ሕረ​ትከ፡ ​አን​ጽሕ፡ ​አብ​ዳነ፡ ​አጥ​ብብ፡ ​ወኅ​ጉላ​ነ፡ ​ሚጥ፡
                                    ​እለ፡ ​ውስ​ተ፡ ​ሞቅ​ሕ፡ ​አድ​ኅን፡ ​ወለ​ኵል​ነ፡ ​ኩን፡ ​ፀወ​ነ፡ ​እስ​መ፡ ​ለከ፡ ​እግ​ዚኦ፡ ​አም​ላክ​ነ፡ ​መን​ግሥ​ት፡ ​ቡሩ​ክ።  <fo:inline>[////]</fo:inline>
                                    ​አሜ​ን።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block hyphenate="true"
                      font-family="Ludolfus"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      id="d1e127048LIT1717Kidanz">
               <fo:inline>III-2) Fols 105rb–107ra: <fo:inline xml:lang="en" hyphenate="true">‘’ (​ኪዳ​ን፡ ​ዘሠ​ርክ፡), CAe 1717.</fo:inline>
               </fo:inline>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Incipit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                     <fo:inline>[////]</fo:inline> ​ጸጋ​ሁ፡ ​ለእ​ግዚ​አብ​ሔር፡ ​የሀ​ሉ፡ ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​ኵል​ሙ።   (fol. 105va)   ​ምስ​ለ፡ ​መን​ፈስ​ከ።
                                    <fo:inline>[////]</fo:inline> ​አእ​ኵት​ዎ፡ ​ለአ​ምላ​ክነ። <fo:inline>[////]</fo:inline> ​ርቱ​ዕ፡ ​ይደ​ሉ።
                                    <fo:inline>[////]</fo:inline> ​ለከ፡ ​ለአ​ብ፡ ​ዘኢ​ይማ​ስን፡ ​መድ​ኃኔ፡ ​ነፍ​ስነ፡ ​ወመ​ሠረ​ተ፡ ​ጥበ​ባት፡ ​አቃ​ቤ፡ ​አል​ባቢ​ነ፡ ​ዘእ​ንተ፡ ​ውስ​ጥ፡ ​አደ​ነነ፡ ​አብ​ራኅ​ከ፡
                                    ​ወጽ​ልመ​ተ፡ ​ህሊ<fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>​ናነ፡ ​በዘ​ዚአ​ከ፡ ​አእ​ምሮ፡ ​ከለ​ልከ​ነ፡
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block start-indent="10mm">Explicit: <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                                    
                                    ​ዘይ​ሁብ፡ ​መርሐ ​ርቱ​አ፡ ​ለቤ​ተ፡ ​ክር​ስቲ​ያን፡ ​ዘተ​ከላ፡ ​ላቲ፡ ​ምዕ​ራፈ፡ <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>፡ ​ስብ​ሐተ፡ ​ሐይ​ማኖ​ት፡ ​ጉባ​ኤ፡ ​መን​ፈሰ፡ ​ሀብ​ተ፡
                                    ​ጸጋ፡ ​ወኃ​ይል፡
                                    ​ለከ፡ ​እን​ዘ፡ ​ንዌ​ድሶ፡ ​ወኢና  (fol. 107ra)  ​ዕር​ፍ፡ ​ለዝ​ሉፉ፡ ​በአ​ልባ​ቢነ፡ ​ናስ​ተማ​ሰል፡ ​አም​ሳለ፡
                                    ​መን​ግሥ​ትከ፡ ​ቦቱ፡ ​በእ​ንቲ​አከ፡ ​ወበ​እን​ተ፡ ​ፍቁ​ር፡ ​ወል​ድከ፡ ​እግ​ዚእ​ነ፡ ​ኢየ​ሱስ፡ ​ዘቦ​ቱ፡ ​ለከ፡ ​ስብ​ሐት፡ ​ወእ​ሒዝ፡ ​ለዓ​ለመ፡
                                    ​ዓለ​ም። ​አሜ​ን። ።
                                </fo:inline>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Additional notes</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 108v: List of names of individuals. Each person’s name is probably given next to their baptismal name.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">
                           <fo:inline id="d1e127380PRS14004Berhane">​ብር​ሃኔ፡ ​ወለተ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ጻዴ​ቅ፡</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline>[...]</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline id="d1e127391PRS14005Baqqala">​በቀ​ለ፡ ​ገብ​ረ፡ ​እዚ​አር</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline id="d1e127394PRS14006Ballata">​በለ​ጠ፡ ​ወልደ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ገብ​ርኤ​ል፡</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline id="d1e127400PRS14007Alamayyahu">​አለ​ማየ​ሁ፡ ​ወል​ደአ​ብ፡</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline id="d1e127404PRS14008Taddas">​ጠዳ​ሽ፡ ​አሥ​ካለ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ማር​ያም፡</fo:inline>
                           <fo:inline id="d1e127410PRS14009Amalawarq">​አመ​ለወ​ርቅ፡ ​ወለተ<fo:inline>[፡]</fo:inline> ​ክዳ​ን፡</fo:inline>
                        </fo:inline>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      space-before="2mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Varia</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em"
                           white-space-collapse="true">
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>The part written by Hand 1 contains no scribal corrections.
                                    The part written by Hand 2 contains an erasure on fol. 105ra
                                        and fols 106va.
                                        Spaces intended for rubrication have been left empty on fols 105ra–107ra.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. 82rb: A supplication within the main text of ms_i2 mentions
                                        <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​አባ፡ ​ቄር​ሎስ፡ ​ዘሀ​ገር፡ ​ዓባ​ይ፡ ​እለ፡ ​እስ​ክን​ድር​ያ፡</fo:inline>
                                        and <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">​ብፁ​ዕ፡ ​ጳጳ​ስነ፡ ​አባ፡ ​ማቴ​ዎስ፡</fo:inline>.
                                        These can probably be identified with <fo:inline id="d1e127450PRS3259CyrilV">Cyril V</fo:inline> and
                                        <fo:inline id="d1e127452PRS6876Matewos">Mātewos X</fo:inline>, simultaneously in tenure in
                                        <fo:inline>1889–1926</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:inline id="d1e127462PRS14002WaldaS">Walda Śǝllāse</fo:inline>, probably the owner or commissioner, and the scribe
                                        <fo:inline id="d1e127464PRS14003FereS">Fǝre Sanbat</fo:inline> are mentioned in supplications, e.g. on fol. 79va.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>The first words of the Gospel of John are written in pencil in a untrained hand on fol. 109v.
                                        It is probably a probably a pen trial.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>5)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Scribbles in pencil on both inner boards.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>6)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fol. ir: The shelfmark ‘MS Aeth. f. 35’ is written in pencil at the bottom of the page.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Binding</fo:block>
                                     The book is bound in wooden boards.
                                   
                                     The boards are flush with the bookblock. The grain runs vertically.
                                     The inner surface and the edges of the boards are rough while the outer surface is polished.
                                   
                                     Chainstitch sewing on four sewing stations (two pairs); Z-plied thread.
                                     In the first quire, between the sewing stations, there is one length of thread. In the rest of the quires there are double lengths.
                                     The sewing is closed in the last quire with knots.
                                   </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Foliation</fo:block>
            <fo:block>Pencil foliation in the upper right corner (i–iv+1–110).</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block font-style="italic"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   space-before="2mm"
                   page-break-inside="avoid"
                   page-break-after="avoid">Quire structure</fo:block>
         <fo:block space-after="3mm">
                                        Undecorated quire marks are written in the middle of the upper margin of the first folio of the third and eighth quires,
                                        respectively indicated as <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">፪</fo:inline> and <fo:inline font-family="Ludolfus" letter-spacing="0.5pt" font-size="0.9em">፯</fo:inline>.
                                      </fo:block>
         <fo:block>12 quires. A<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">4 (Fols ir–ivv)</fo:inline> – I<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 1r–10v)</fo:inline> – II<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 11r–20v)</fo:inline> – III<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 21r–30v)</fo:inline> – IV<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 31r–40v)</fo:inline> – V<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 41r–50v)</fo:inline> – VI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 51r–60v)</fo:inline> – VII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 61r–70v)</fo:inline> – VIII<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 71r–80v)</fo:inline> – IX<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">14 (Fols 81r–94v)</fo:inline> – X<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">10 (Fols 95r–104v)</fo:inline> – XI<fo:inline font-size="7pt" vertical-align="text-top">6 (Fols 105r–110v)</fo:inline>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Layout</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:list-item space-after="3mm">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1)</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>Fols 1ra–107ra1–110: 2
                                    columns (18 written lines)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block start-indent="10mm" space-before="3mm" space-after="3mm">There are 11–12 characters per line per column in the part
                                        written by Hand 1 and 9–11 in the part written by Hand 2.Data on text area and margin dimensions taken from fol. 11r.</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Leaf dimensions:
                                            156 × 112 mm (fol. 11r).
                                            </fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Text area:
                                            101 × 85 mm (fol. 11r)</fo:block>
                     <fo:block page-break-after="avoid"
                               start-indent="10mm"
                               space-before="3mm"
                               space-after="3mm">Margins: 
                                            top: 13 mm, bottom: 41 mm, right: 17 mm, left: 11 mm (fol. 11r).
                                            </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm">
            <fo:block page-break-after="avoid" font-style="italic" space-after="3mm">Ruling and pricking</fo:block>
            <fo:block provisional-label-separation="1em"
                      provisional-distance-between-starts="2em">
               <fo:inline>Primary and ruling pricks are visible. The upper and bottom lines are written above the ruling. Ruling pattern: 1A-1A-1A1A/0-0/0-0/C.</fo:inline>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Palaeography</fo:block>
            <fo:table>
               <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="15%"/>
               <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="85%"/>
               <fo:table-body>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 1:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 1ra–104vb. 1889–1926 (scribe: Fǝre Sanbat) . Modern bulky, slightly condensed script. The characters are of somewhat irregular height, but the hand is trained.
                                    The vowel markers of the third and fifth orders are hardly distinguishable. The word separator is often omitted at the
                                    end of a line.
                                Fǝre Sanbat is indicated as the scribe in the supplication formulas throughout.
                                <fo:block>Ink: Black, red.</fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Rubrication: Incipits (groups of red lines alternating with black lines) and single words; holy names; the names
                                    of persons involved in the manuscript production; elements of the punctuation marks.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
                  <fo:table-row space-after="2mm">
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline>Hand 2:</fo:inline>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                     <fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:block hyphenate="true"><!-- {fo:tei2fo($handnote/tei:seg[@type='script'])}{' '}-->Fols 105ra–107ra. 1889–1926. Hand of the last quire. Modern, slightly cursive script, somewhat irregular. The letter ሠ
                                    has an archaising form.<fo:block>Ink: Black.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:table-cell>
                  </fo:table-row>
               </fo:table-body>
            </fo:table>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Other details</fo:block>
            <fo:block>A long tear has been repaired by sewing on fol. ii.</fo:block>
            <fo:block/>
            <fo:block/>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">Condition</fo:block>
            <fo:block>The condition is good.The manuscript shows traces of use in the lower external corners
                                  and the back cover is split vertically in half. The two parts are held together by threads passing through pairs of holes
                                  drilled through the board.
                                </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm" white-space-collapse="true">
            <fo:block font-style="italic"
                      space-after="3mm"
                      page-break-inside="avoid"
                      page-break-after="avoid">History</fo:block>
            <fo:block>
               <fo:inline>1889–1926</fo:inline>
                            The manuscript was written by two hands (one of which is that of
                            <fo:inline id="d1e127524PRS14003FereS">Fǝre Sanbat</fo:inline>, see
                            Varia note 3), but the continuities in layout and content point to a single production process.
                            <fo:inline id="d1e127529PRS14002WaldaS">Walda Śǝllāse</fo:inline> was the original owner or
                            commissioner (see
                            Varia note 3).
                            A supplication mentions ‘<fo:inline font-style="italic">ʾAbbā Qerǝllos za-hagara ʿābbāy ʾƎlla ʾƎskǝndǝryā</fo:inline>’ and ‘<fo:inline font-style="italic">ṗāṗāsǝna ʾAbbā Mātewos</fo:inline>’
                            (fol. 82rb), likely to be identified with
                            <fo:inline id="d1e127543PRS3259CyrilV">Cyril V</fo:inline> (in tenure 1874–1927) and
                            <fo:inline id="d1e127545PRS6876Matewos">Mātewos X</fo:inline> (in tenure 1889–1926), which would date the production of the manuscript to
                            1889–1926 (see Varia note 2).
                        </fo:block>
            <fo:block>The provenance of the manuscript is not known.</fo:block>
            <fo:block>It was acquired by the Bodleian Library in 2012.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block space-before="2mm"
                   space-after="3mm"
                   margin-bottom="16.25pt"
                   page-break-before="avoid">URL: <fo:basic-link external-destination="https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethf35">https://betamasaheft.eu/BDLaethf35</fo:basic-link>
         </fo:block>
         <!--  break  after Catalogue -->
         <fo:block page-break-after="always"/>
      </fo:flow>
   </fo:page-sequence>
